rl":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/ae92ba5026978b5fe9afe1f6e387abd68e4897ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T15:49:38Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T15:49:38Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(examples): meridian-monolith, the reference subject for decomposition\n\nmeridian-station rebuilt as one React SPA (webpack, React 18, React\nRouter) on the same three backends, written the way a real team would\nhave: mixed folder conventions, a global store, one API client\nnormalizing all three backend conventions, cross-domain reads, a\nlife-support badge in the console nav, and two route tables that must\nagree. All seven domains are ported, including the three Angular MFEs\n(docking, life support, cargo) rewritten in React and the Babylon/Havok\ndocking simulator carried over as-is.\n\nThe test suite is deliberately poor, as real monoliths'' are: 29% line\ncoverage, snapshots, implementation-coupled tests, brittle selectors, a\nskipped test, commented-out tests, a flaky timing test, a file excluded\nfrom Jest that asserts behavior the app no longer has, mocks that never\nexercise real API shapes, and two happy-path e2e specs with fixed sleeps.\n\nanswer-key.yaml is the score target for decompose:score: the seven\nmeridian-station MFEs with capabilities, placements and backends, every\nsource file''s owning domain, shared files and expected handling,\ncouplings, route-to-state-key map, latent bugs parity must preserve\n(dockings default page of 10, favicon 404), keep/rewrite/discard triage\nfor every test, untested behaviors, and per-domain \"before\" coverage.\n\nRepo Jest and ESLint already exclude examples/**. System map regenerated\nfor the new test files.\n\nRefs #412\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Q1KNQo47PteVV6NFx722DV","tree":{"sha":"e81d9f5d5e12f309d887cb8b222928915bc2871b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/e81d9f5d5e12f309d887cb8b222928915bc2871b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/ae92ba5026978b5fe9afe1f6e387abd68e4897ab","verification":{"payload":"tree e81d9f5d5e12f309d887cb8b222928915bc2871b\nparent 79a8788c97d448c95a0dfdcd155a21581b05354e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791042578 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791042578 +0000\n\nfeat(examples): meridian-monolith, the reference subject for decomposition\n\nmeridian-station rebuilt as one React SPA (webpack, React 18, React\nRouter) on the same three backends, written the way a real team would\nhave: mixed folder conventions, a global store, one API client\nnormalizing all three backend conventions, cross-domain reads, a\nlife-support badge in the console nav, and two route tables that must\nagree. All seven domains are ported, including the three Angular MFEs\n(docking, life support, cargo) rewritten in React and the Babylon/Havok\ndocking simulator carried over as-is.\n\nThe test suite is deliberately poor, as real monoliths'' are: 29% line\ncoverage, snapshots, implementation-coupled tests, brittle selectors, a\nskipped test, commented-out tests, a flaky timing test, a file excluded\nfrom Jest that asserts behavior the app no longer has, mocks that never\nexercise real API shapes, and two happy-path e2e specs with fixed sleeps.\n\nanswer-key.yaml is the score target for decompose:score: the seven\nmeridian-station MFEs with capabilities, placements and backends, every\nsource file''s owning domain, shared files and expected handling,\ncouplings, route-to-state-key map, latent bugs parity must preserve\n(dockings default page of 10, favicon 404), keep/rewrite/discard triage\nfor every test, untested behaviors, and per-domain \"before\" coverage.\n\nRepo Jest and ESLint already exclude examples/**. System map regenerated\nfor the new test files.\n\nRefs #412\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Q1KNQo47PteVV6NFx722DV\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHJgGGI1\n/XhzTx0lBbnfpa2+RUsQJ2a6AcnOYw2w46MBq14O4295e1E94OVpg9UfhEMBvUE77xmmSsSIoRmn\n6Ag=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T15:49:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"