PDR-011\n\n- ADR-110 §1a: the first decomposition.yaml is produced by deterministic\n  clustering; the operating agent''s judgment (naming, merging, splitting)\n  is applied as edits. No model runs inside the CLI on this path\n  (PDR-010''s split).\n- ADR-110 §3: agreement is a merged proposal PR; any later approval\n  surface writes to the same document on the same PR (#425).\n- PDR-011: the same two decisions, and the approval UI for\n  non-engineers noted as a later phase.\n\nRefs #411\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Q1KNQo47PteVV6NFx722DV","tree":{"sha":"09a06aa18fcf5eed5c9e3be2a1e978495274ba6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/09a06aa18fcf5eed5c9e3be2a1e978495274ba6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/de94504cfda1ea1b389a83a5cc5c5d2f625954b3","verification":{"payload":"tree 09a06aa18fcf5eed5c9e3be2a1e978495274ba6d\nparent 0f04edf1353878f092de74769dc2c5b298b3c22a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791037407 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791037407 +0000\n\ndocs(adr): record propose and agreement decisions in ADR-110 and PDR-011\n\n- ADR-110 §1a: the first decomposition.yaml is produced by deterministic\n  clustering; the operating agent''s judgment (naming, merging, splitting)\n  is applied as edits. No model runs inside the CLI on this path\n  (PDR-010''s split).\n- ADR-110 §3: agreement is a merged proposal PR; any later approval\n  surface writes to the same document on the same PR (#425).\n- PDR-011: the same two decisions, and the approval UI for\n  non-engineers noted as a later phase.\n\nRefs #411\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Q1KNQo47PteVV6NFx722DV\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0