/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/0f04edf1353878f092de74769dc2c5b298b3c22a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T13:53:30Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T13:53:30Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs(adr): PDR-011 and ADR-109–113 for agent-driven monolith decomposition\n\nDraft the product decision and the five architecture decisions the\ndecomposition epic needs, all Proposed:\n\n- PDR-011: an agent decomposes a running monolith into SMT MFEs from\n  observed evidence and proves the result behaves the same\n- ADR-109: the evidence bundle (capture keyed by region and interaction,\n  joined to source)\n- ADR-110: decomposition.yaml is the agreed artifact; manifests and\n  composition are derived from it\n- ADR-111: the monolith runs as one generated MFE via Module Federation\n  wrap; strangling is composition\n- ADR-112: OpenAPI inferred from recorded traffic and client code\n- ADR-113: the parity gate; captured behavior, not the old suite, is the\n  baseline\n\nADR-108 is reserved for #407. Regenerated the ADR index, PDR map and\nsystem map; PDR register updated by hand.\n\nRefs #411\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Q1KNQo47PteVV6NFx722DV","tree":{"sha":"e3d92856435773d98e789e64e3dffb7e1590f800","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/e3d92856435773d98e789e64e3dffb7e1590f800"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/0f04edf1353878f092de74769dc2c5b298b3c22a","verification":{"payload":"tree e3d92856435773d98e789e64e3dffb7e1590f800\nparent 79a8788c97d448c95a0dfdcd155a21581b05354e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791035610 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1791035610 +0000\n\ndocs(adr): PDR-011 and ADR-109–113 for agent-driven monolith decomposition\n\nDraft the product decision and the five architecture decisions the\ndecomposition epic needs, all Proposed:\n\n- PDR-011: an agent decomposes a running monolith into SMT MFEs from\n  observed evidence and proves the result behaves the same\n- ADR-109: the evidence bundle (capture keyed by region and interaction,\n  joined to source)\n- ADR-110: decomposition.yaml is the agreed artifact; manifests and\n  composition are derived from it\n- ADR-111: the monolith runs as one generated MFE via Module Federation\n  wrap; strangling is composition\n- ADR-112: OpenAPI inferred from recorded traffic and client code\n- ADR-113: the parity gate; captured behavior, not the old suite, is the\n  baseline\n\nADR-108 is reserved for #407. Regenerated the ADR index, PDR map and\nsystem map; PDR register updated by hand.\n\nRefs #411\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Q1KNQo47PteVV6NFx722DV\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEmwzC7E\nkH7K+bCiVbChQyYvv2Rid802yrjVLX72+vLtSNh0zw7fuoRaRMVj61PcYGddA+90qgVOfriWsz7B\nsQw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T13:53:32Z"}},"commi