nd the\nADR index are regenerated.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JMMwTTDxGkC9WKKaT9bvQY","tree":{"sha":"360d04cfd7b53df601a7dcc6f84b3349180d54bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/360d04cfd7b53df601a7dcc6f84b3349180d54bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/6d2d183dc60820d1812ab784dbc4f5f79b5267df","verification":{"payload":"tree 360d04cfd7b53df601a7dcc6f84b3349180d54bc\nparent d832885c89f06d59ae79a0850c653d7e07453949\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790743309 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790743309 +0000\n\nchore(examples): declare hosts on every example MFE, regenerate (ADR-107)\n\nEvery abc-kids MFE declares `abc`, every meridian MFE `meridian`, and\nabc-kids-flappy declares both — meridian composes it since #400, and\nthat is now the owner''s stated claim rather than a fact only meridian''s\ncontrol-plane.yaml knew.\n\nThe manifest is inlined into generator-owned files (bootstrap.ts, the\nSwift and Rust manifest mirrors), so check:mfe-drift regenerated 23 of\nthem. docs/api, the manifest field reference, the system map and the\nADR index are regenerated.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JMMwTTDxGkC9WKKaT9bvQY\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGNfY8iE\nZL8T40nKCQZaPFA/JNUEqfvUhGf3QDHDL4Z8Ne95dtljOjNQhoYvtjkId9VTNCevTFiDQJQ0IHvE\ndQ0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T04:42:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/6d2d183dc60820d1812ab784dbc4f5f79b5267df","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDZkMmQxODNkYzYwODIwZDE4MTJhYjc4NGRiYzRmNWY3OWI1MjY3ZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/d832885c89f06d59ae79a0850c653d7e07453949","sha":"d832885c89f06d59ae79a0850c653d7e07453949","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/d832885c89f06d59ae79a0850c653d7e07453949"}],"sha":"6d2d183dc60820d1812ab784dbc4f5f79b5267df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/6d2d183dc60820d1812ab784dbc4f5f79b5267df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/d832885c89f06d59ae79a0850c653d7e07453949/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:41:49Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:41:49Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(dsl): an MFE''s manifest declares the hosts it works in (ADR-107)\n\n`hosts:` is a non-empty list of `{ id }` entries, each naming a host\nproject by its control-plane namespace. Strict: the compose compiler\nreports `undeclared-host` (fatal) for any fleet member that does not\nname the composing namespace, and mfe:validate reports `hosts-declared`\nfor a manifest with none. The parser keeps the field optional so every\nloader still reads an older manifest; the gates name the gap and the fix.\n\nHost entries are `.strict()` objects: the slot for a host''s own identity\nand access scheme is reserved, and an `auth:` written before that\ndecision is rejected rather than silently stripped.\n\n`remote:init --host <namespace>` (repeatable) writes the list.\n`NAMESPACE_PATTERN` is now the single namespace grammar, shared by\ncontrol-plane.yaml and hosts[].id.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JMMwTTDxGkC9WKKaT9bvQY","tree":{"sha":"002538254e9b103889f17806a6f589e5130e2a35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/002538254e9b103889f17806a6f589e5130e2a35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/d832885c89f06d59ae79a0850c653d7e07453949","verification":{"payload":"tree 002538254e9b103889f17806a6f589e5130e2a35\nparent 3ec4b896b0f2fe93f74e4bf3b26b90563198f461\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790743309 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790743309 +0000\n\nfeat(dsl): an MFE''s manifest declares the hosts it works in (ADR-107)\n\n`hosts:` is a non-empty list of `{ id }` entries, each naming a host\nproject by its control-plane namespace. Strict: the compose compiler\nreports `undeclared-host` (fatal) for any fleet member that does not\nname the composing namespace, and mfe:validate reports `hosts-declared`\nfor a manifest with none. The parser keeps the field optional so every\nloader still reads an older manifest; the gates name the gap and the fix.\n\nHost entries are `.strict()` objects: the slot for a host''s own identity\nand access scheme is reserved, and an `auth:` written before that\ndecision is rejected rather than silently stripped.\n\n`remote:init --host <namespace>` (repeatable) writes the list.\n`NAMESPACE_PATTERN` is now the single namespace grammar, shared by\ncontrol-plane.yaml and hosts[].id.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JMMwTTDxGkC9WKKaT9bvQY\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOWeMIjV\njPklZgtIaqSJomXURLtaGsNDlbpY8G6uShMejHil40m1P0Hz1WnqVVa5FJsCSnldizxF2R4nCe23\nMAU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T04:42:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_ur