//api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/196dca1535bcf142782fbf0fa6b4f81751e3babf","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDE5NmRjYTE1MzViY2YxNDI3ODJmYmYwZmE2YjRmODE3NTFlM2JhYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/b409ca64094028cf9db8bf83646904e916548dc4","sha":"b409ca64094028cf9db8bf83646904e916548dc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/b409ca64094028cf9db8bf83646904e916548dc4"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/5f0b63e0607763385d75fd8c589e7d816d6a36a4","sha":"5f0b63e0607763385d75fd8c589e7d816d6a36a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/5f0b63e0607763385d75fd8c589e7d816d6a36a4"}],"sha":"196dca1535bcf142782fbf0fa6b4f81751e3babf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/196dca1535bcf142782fbf0fa6b4f81751e3babf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/b409ca64094028cf9db8bf83646904e916548dc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T03:53:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T03:53:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(runtime): stub container exposes nothing, so a caught render error shows the fallback\n\nBaseRemoteMFE.fetchContainer''s stub answered every get() with a placeholder\nclass. RemoteMFE.resolveMfeFallback took that for an MFE-provided\n./ErrorBoundary, and React cannot call a class without `new` — so once a\nremote had loaded, a render throw made the boundary throw inside its own\ncatch and blanked the slot. Every composed React remote was affected; the\ncross-app composition spec caught it in a real page.\n\nThe stub now rejects with BusinessError MODULE_NOT_EXPOSED, as a real\ncontainer does for a module it lacks, and resolveMfeFallback''s existing\nswallow selects the built-in boundary. Components never came through\nget(); they load via loadDomainComponent().\n\nNo PLATFORM_MIGRATIONS entry: runtime-internal, and no generated or\ndeveloper-owned code overrides fetchContainer or reads container.get.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"7e281d874d45dc100bd37160db25aabc3273875c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/7e281d874d45dc100bd37160db25aabc3273875c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/b409ca64094028cf9db8bf83646904e916548dc4","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e281d874d45dc100bd37160db25aabc3273875c\nparent 8b8839980689edc9c030e98c6ff79bfa0b01c99c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790481234 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790481234 +0000\n\nfix(runtime): stub container exposes nothing, so a caught render error shows the fallback\n\nBaseRemoteMFE.fetchContainer''s stub answered every get() with a placeholder\nclass. RemoteMFE.resolveMfeFallback took that for an MFE-provided\n./ErrorBoundary, and React cannot call a class without `new` — so once a\nremote had loaded, a render throw made the boundary throw inside its own\ncatch and blanked the slot. Every composed React remote was affected; the\ncross-app composition spec caught it in a real page.\n\nThe stub now rejects with BusinessError MODULE_NOT_EXPOSED, as a real\ncontainer does for a module it lacks, and resolveMfeFallback''s existing\nswallow selects the built-in boundary. Components never came through\nget(); they load via loadDomainComponent().\n\nNo PLATFORM_MIGRATIONS entry: runtime-internal, and no generated or\ndeveloper-owned code overrides fetchContainer or reads container.get.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBIInz96\nXpyJ2CO72l3ROXN6FvTDY5Hq+TLba2lewk78SRWiDeB/mQJBPMD32GDjy0LeQyIx22iq/y0sSrXq\nZAo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T03:53:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url"