42589e9428e6d05fc5fefe2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:44:35Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:44:35Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"test(composition): scope the slot check; make the fallback probe explain itself\n\nSecond real run: the cross-app composition works. meridian.root composed\nthe console, and meridian.off-shift mounted abc-kids'' flappy into\nmeridian-console/main with content and no error boundary. Two failures\nremained:\n\n- \"no slot in error\" was page-wide, and found six. They are the console''s\n  berth strip: it fires meridian.berth.b1..b6 on mount, which resolve to\n  docking-control, deliberately absent from this minimal stack. The test\n  now checks the slots this composition owns, `root` and `main`.\n- The render-throw probe mounted, but no .mfe-error-boundary appeared,\n  although the same probe renders one against flappy on its own. Rather\n  than guess at the difference (host share scope, a React copy), the\n  failure now reports the probe''s rendered HTML and the page''s errors.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"e7c449f3a1f131bc109c9a5019bc9b2d775182a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/e7c449f3a1f131bc109c9a5019bc9b2d775182a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/d1ef944de05a3df9f42589e9428e6d05fc5fefe2","verification":{"payload":"tree e7c449f3a1f131bc109c9a5019bc9b2d775182a5\nparent 3993e4b42f95505f6388767146cdecd6e7765d22\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790462675 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790462675 +0000\n\ntest(composition): scope the slot check; make the fallback probe explain itself\n\nSecond real run: the cross-app composition works. meridian.root composed\nthe console, and meridian.off-shift mounted abc-kids'' flappy into\nmeridian-console/main with content and no error boundary. Two failures\nremained:\n\n- \"no slot in error\" was page-wide, and found six. They are the console''s\n  berth strip: it fires meridian.berth.b1..b6 on mount, which resolve to\n  docking-control, deliberately absent from this minimal stack. The test\n  now checks the slots this composition owns, `root` and `main`.\n- The render-throw probe mounted, but no .mfe-error-boundary appeared,\n  although the same probe renders one against flappy on its own. Rather\n  than guess at the difference (host share scope, a React copy), the\n  failure now reports the probe''s rendered HTML and the page''s errors.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH5Zq2o+\n3xFv0Q9Xvir2KxZaw+r971BBiJHdpIncI92DxBrO1Zy9I5ecgCVrb0cjBEKO1JqYrRrqIzQYk/gE\nsww=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:44:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/d1ef944de05a3df9f42589e9428e6d05fc5fefe2","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKGQxZWY5NDRkZTA1YTNkZjlmNDI1ODllOTQyOGU2ZDA1ZmM1ZmVmZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/3993e4b42f95505f6388767146cdecd6e7765d22","sha":"3993e4b42f95505f6388767146cdecd6e7765d22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/3993e4b42f95505f6388767146cdecd6e7765d22"}],"sha":"d1ef944de05a3df9f42589e9428e6d05fc5fefe2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/d1ef944de05a3df9f42589e9428e6d05fc5fefe2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/3993e4b42f95505f6388767146cdecd6e7765d22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:38:24Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:38:24Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"ci(composition): meridian composes abc-kids'' flappy on a context change\n\nA better test of the platform''s claim than one fleet composing its own\nMFEs: Meridian Station places an MFE it did not build. abc-kids owns\nand builds flappy; meridian''s control-plane.yaml references it\n(`../abc-kids/flappy`) and places PlayGame into meridian-console/main on\n`meridian.off-shift`. The compiler needed no change: the new registration\nserves from flappy''s own deployment (:3001), the route stays in\nmeridian''s namespace, and slots:validate resolves the target against the\nconsole''s declared `main`.\n\n- docker-compose.yaml and build-station.sh gain abc-kids-flappy, built\n  from ../abc-kids/flappy (no port overlap with meridian''s 4500-5103).\n- e2e/cross-app-composition.spec.ts: shell connects; meridian.root\n  composes the console; meridian.off-shift mounts flappy into\n  meridian-console/main (ready, with content, no error boundary, and\n  flappy''s own container on window); the render-throw fallback probe.\n- The Composition workflow now builds only registry, daemon, shell,\n  meridian-console and abc-kids-flappy, starts them --no-deps, runs\n  register-station.sh, and runs that spec. It is cheaper than the abc-kids\n  version (no game base, no home) and a stronger claim.\n- The abc-kids composition.spec.ts this PR had added is removed; the\n  abc-kids.spec.ts selector fix stays, and that suite is #402''s.\n- STATION-DEMO.md documents the off-shift action.\n\ncompose:validate --check and slots:validate pass for both fleets.\n\nRefs #345, #402\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"e21c86a9f1a9b4c0fdf61e19234952810a513749","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/e21c86a9f1a9b4c0fdf61e19234952810a513749"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/3993e4b42f95505f6388767146cdecd6e7765d22","verification":{"payload":"tree e21c86a9f1a9b4c0fdf61e19234952810a513749\nparent bb1eea8dc36d1ad800724cf8ab456d2f15f10230\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790462304 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790462304 +0000\n\nci(composition): meridian composes abc-kids'' flappy on a context change\n\nA better test of the platform''s claim than one fleet composing its own\nMFEs: Meridian Station places an MFE it did not build. abc-kids owns\nand builds flappy; meridian''s control-plane.yaml references it\n(`../abc-kids/flappy`) and places PlayGame into meridian-console/main on\n`meridian.off-shift`. The compiler needed no change: the new registration\nserves from flappy''s own deployment (:3001), the route stays in\nmeridian''s namespace, and slots:validate resolves the target against the\nconsole''s declared `main`.\n\n- docker-compose.yaml and build-station.sh gain abc-kids-flappy, built\n  from ../abc-kids/flappy (no port overlap with meridian''s 4500-5103).\n- e2e/cross-app-composition.spec.ts: shell connects; meridian.root\n  composes the console; meridian.off-shift mounts flappy into\n  meridian-console/main (ready, with content, no error boundary, and\n  flappy''s own container on window); the render-throw fallback probe.\n- The Composition workflow now builds only registry, daemon, shell,\n  meridian-console and abc-kids-flappy, starts them --no-deps, runs\n  register-station.sh, and runs that spec. It is cheaper than the abc-kids\n  version (no game base, no home) and a stronger claim.\n- The abc-kids composition.spec.ts this PR had added is removed; the\n  abc-kids.spec.ts selector fix stays, and that suite is #402''s.\n- STATION-DEMO.md documents the off-shift action.\n\ncompose:validate --check and slots:validate pass for both fleets.\n\nRefs #345, #402\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAz4S6T3\nH0bayufoPyd/jAaEpUq0JMe4w+ltDQxYVij36OOZgAQCWzbxndDgfL7n2I6GmOP5evLDtHXTjMxU\nMwQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:38:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/3993e4b42f95505f6388767146cdecd6e7765d22","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDM5OTNlNGI0MmY5NTUwNWY2Mzg4NzY3MTQ2Y2RlY2Q2ZTc3NjVkMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/bb1eea8dc36d1ad800724cf8ab456d2f15f10230","sha":"bb1eea8dc36d1ad800724cf8ab456d2f15f10230","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/bb1eea8dc36d1ad800724cf8ab456d2f15f10230"}],"sha":"3993e4b42f95505f6388767146cdecd6e7765d22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/3993e4b42f95505f6388767146cdecd6e7765d22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/bb1eea8dc36d1ad800724cf8ab456d2f15f10230/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:31:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:31:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"ci(composition): compose through the control plane, as a session does\n\nThe first real run built and started the fleet, and all three remotes\nserved their containers. Every UI test then timed out: they drove the\npre-ADR-055 static shell UI, which App.tsx no longer renders, and the job\nnever composed anything. The daemon-driven shell stays empty until the\nregistry holds rules and a state action resolves against them.\n\n- Build abc-kids-game-base and the home launcher too. Games mount into\n  abc-kids-home/main, a slot the home provides, so a real composition\n  needs it.\n- Register control-plane/rules.json (scripts/register-games.sh) after\n  the stack is up.\n- composition.spec.ts drives the real path: wait for \"control plane:\n  connected\", send abc.root then abc.play.flappy through the daemon''s\n  sendMessage (as play.sh does), and assert [data-layout-slot] reaches\n  data-slot-state=\"ready\" with content and no error boundary. Keeps the\n  remoteEntry checks (now including home) and the render-throw fallback\n  probe.\n- Run composition.spec.ts only. abc-kids.spec.ts tests UI that no longer\n  ships; tracked in #402, named in the workflow rather than silently\n  excluded.\n\nRefs #345, #402\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"410050ef4caf45581122d27c4921c02bbe617fde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/410050ef4caf45581122d27c4921c02bbe617fde"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/bb1eea8dc36d1ad800724cf8ab456d2f15f10230","verification":{"payload":"tree 410050ef4caf45581122d27c4921c02bbe617fde\nparent f4060056c67ac1343958b4f89987ed6e0940b3ab\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790461867 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790461867 +0000\n\nci(composition): compose through the control plane, as a session does\n\nThe first real run built and started the fleet, and all three remotes\nserved their containers. Every UI test then timed out: they drove the\npre-ADR-055 static shell UI, which App.tsx no longer renders, and the job\nnever composed anything. The daemon-driven shell stays empty until the\nregistry holds rules and a state action resolves against them.\n\n- Build abc-kids-game-base and the home launcher too. Games mount into\n  abc-kids-home/main, a slot the home provides, so a real composition\n  needs it.\n- Register control-plane/rules.json (scripts/register-games.sh) after\n  the stack is up.\n- composition.spec.ts drives the real path: wait for \"control plane:\n  connected\", send abc.root then abc.play.flappy through the daemon''s\n  sendMessage (as play.sh does), and assert [data-layout-slot] reaches\n  data-slot-state=\"ready\" with content and no error boundary. Keeps the\n  remoteEntry checks (now including home) and the render-throw fallback\n  probe.\n- Run composition.spec.ts only. abc-kids.spec.ts tests UI that no longer\n  ships; tracked in #402, named in the workflow rather than silently\n  excluded.\n\nRefs #345, #402\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGeKY6M6\nEO3JI3fxf+sWXphpHVQl1ZzPetq+dkmGc7uOUpZTeE5EQyjQ5XFZ4tXMRi0ipn8lm+o7g4yx87uL\n9As=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:31:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/bb1eea8dc36d1ad800724cf8ab456d2f15f10230","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKGJiMWVlYThkYzM2ZDFhZDgwMDcyNGNmOGFiNDU2ZDJmMTVmMTAyMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/f4060056c67ac1343958b4f89987ed6e0940b3ab","sha":"f4060056c67ac1343958b4f89987ed6e0940b3ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/f4060056c67ac1343958b4f89987ed6e0940b3ab"}],"sha":"bb1eea8dc36d1ad800724cf8ab456d2f15f10230","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/bb1eea8dc36d1ad800724cf8ab456d2f15f10230"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/04f22b423de4b4d19488ed362b95ee3033d65e10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:21:50Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:21:50Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs(api): regenerate with source links for http-outcome\n\nThe api-docs gate failed: build:docs ran before http-outcome.ts was\ncommitted, and TypeDoc only links a source file git knows about, so the\nfour new pages had bare ''Defined in'' lines where CI expects links.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"b77cb460c98aa5945837b2641dc5551c25d45e1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/b77cb460c98aa5945837b2641dc5551c25d45e1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/04f22b423de4b4d19488ed362b95ee3033d65e10","verification":{"payload":"tree b77cb460c98aa5945837b2641dc5551c25d45e1f\nparent 020cb8ad6d9a8a8c42448f0b4357bf550ec76edc\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790461310 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790461310 +0000\n\ndocs(api): regenerate with source links for http-outcome\n\nThe api-docs gate failed: build:docs ran before http-outcome.ts was\ncommitted, and TypeDoc only links a source file git knows about, so the\nfour new pages had bare ''Defined in'' lines where CI expects links.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQASLe/Eu\n33WWQ8GtTkS1IgVzMi4Yu9DvE4pp6WtRvj/ZY2quE30Qfd7bJS9Fh7xxIX2F9SGGrGJ95MPg1wYg\nzQM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:21:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/04f22b423de4b4d19488ed362b95ee3033d65e10","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDA0ZjIyYjQyM2RlNGI0ZDE5NDg4ZWQzNjJiOTVlZTMwMzNkNjVlMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/020cb8ad6d9a8a8c42448f0b4357bf550ec76edc","sha":"020cb8ad6d9a8a8c42448f0b4357bf550ec76edc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/020cb8ad6d9a8a8c42448f0b4357bf550ec76edc"}],"sha":"04f22b423de4b4d19488ed362b95ee3033d65e10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/04f22b423de4b4d19488ed362b95ee3033d65e10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/020cb8ad6d9a8a8c42448f0b4357bf550ec76edc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:20:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:20:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs(adr): correct ADR-106''s evidence; drop the dead-code worked example\n\nADR-106 cited the abc-kids shell''s GameLauncher.fetchPets as a live\nmfe.query() caller, and this PR \"updated the shell to look\" there.\nGameLauncher is dead: it belongs to the shell''s pre-ADR-055 static UI and\nis imported by nothing but its own test. The daemon-driven shell never\ncalls query(). Found by the first real run of the composition job\n(#400), whose shell never rendered that UI.\n\nThe decision is unchanged. BaseMFE.doQuery (and the Swift and Rust\ncapabilities) did return untyped transport errors, which the tests here\nshow. Only the evidence and the example were wrong. Reverted the\nGameLauncher edit, rewrote the Context to say no example exercises the\ncapability at runtime today, and fixed a leftover `SystemError` that\nshould read `BusinessError` after the table correction.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"39c71ddf3bdd65a482b577df0e6a980df1e06a71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/39c71ddf3bdd65a482b577df0e6a980df1e06a71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/020cb8ad6d9a8a8c42448f0b4357bf550ec76edc","verification":{"payload":"tree 39c71ddf3bdd65a482b577df0e6a980df1e06a71\nparent fde5287e768c6619eda35bba6e9f6aebe3ab6a8f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790461240 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790461240 +0000\n\ndocs(adr): correct ADR-106''s evidence; drop the dead-code worked example\n\nADR-106 cited the abc-kids shell''s GameLauncher.fetchPets as a live\nmfe.query() caller, and this PR \"updated the shell to look\" there.\nGameLauncher is dead: it belongs to the shell''s pre-ADR-055 static UI and\nis imported by nothing but its own test. The daemon-driven shell never\ncalls query(). Found by the first real run of the composition job\n(#400), whose shell never rendered that UI.\n\nThe decision is unchanged. BaseMFE.doQuery (and the Swift and Rust\ncapabilities) did return untyped transport errors, which the tests here\nshow. Only the evidence and the example were wrong. Reverted the\nGameLauncher edit, rewrote the Context to say no example exercises the\ncapability at runtime today, and fixed a leftover `SystemError` that\nshould read `BusinessError` after the table correction.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKjMmKrn\n7SDLZUG4CaaYhffL3co3cho6bcnc9UU5/ZytgJM6riTRRyOf8ophYcByeW4ti3dNJYRIsKehlquR\ngg8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:20:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/020cb8ad6d9a8a8c42448f0b4357bf550ec76edc","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDAyMGNiOGFkNmQ5YThhOGM0MjQ0OGYwYjQzNTdiZjU1MGVjNzZlZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/fde5287e768c6619eda35bba6e9f6aebe3ab6a8f","sha":"fde5287e768c6619eda35bba6e9f6aebe3ab6a8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/fde5287e768c6619eda35bba6e9f6aebe3ab6a8f"}],"sha":"020cb8ad6d9a8a8c42448f0b4357bf550ec76edc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/020cb8ad6d9a8a8c42448f0b4357bf550ec76edc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/fde5287e768c6619eda35bba6e9f6aebe3ab6a8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:18:24Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:18:24Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(runtime): type the query capability''s transport errors (ADR-106)\n\nImplements ADR-106, now Implemented.\n\n- contracts: `classifyHttpOutcome(status)` and `httpOutcomeError(msg,\n  status)`, one table from an HTTP outcome to an error type; re-exported\n  by the runtime barrel. Frozen-literal test.\n- runtime: `QueryError` gains `type`, `retryable`, `status`.\n  `BaseMFE.doQuery` fills them for a non-2xx and, newly, for a fetch that\n  got no response, which used to escape as a raw TypeError. GraphQL\n  errors in a 2xx stay `{ message, path }`. It also sends `X-Request-ID`\n  from `context.requestId`, lifted from the Angular override below so the\n  BFF keeps its correlation id.\n- bff.ts template: throws the class the status maps to, so a 404 or 401\n  no longer claims to be retryable; no-response throws NetworkError(0).\n- Angular template: drops its doQuery override, as ADR-053 did for React.\n  It flattened the typed error to `{ message }` and ignored the\n  `inputs.bffUrl` its own comment offered.\n- Rust and Swift: same fields and table. A literal copy of the table in\n  each generated test runs against the lane''s own function, and a\n  TypeScript pin checks those rows against `classifyHttpOutcome`. A\n  missing Rust transport is `business`, not the no-response row.\n- PLATFORM_MIGRATIONS: `bff-4xx-no-longer-network-error` (advice) for\n  developer code that narrows on NetworkError.\n- abc-kids shell: fetchPets retries once, only when the error says so.\n\nADR corrected before implementing: the \"other 4xx\" row is `business`,\nnot `system`. SystemError.retryable is `true`, so a thrown 404 would have\ndisagreed with the envelope.\n\nRegenerated: 8 bff.ts (+ tests), 4 Angular mfe.ts, the Rust and Swift\nexample packages, the codegen snapshot, docs/api, PLATFORM-CONTRACT.md,\nthe ADR index and the system map.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"bb55fc3b9bcc294b65e6a080b1c5a7333f6c8057","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/bb55fc3b9bcc294b65e6a080b1c5a7333f6c8057"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/fde5287e768c6619eda35bba6e9f6aebe3ab6a8f","verification":{"payload":"tree bb55fc3b9bcc294b65e6a080b1c5a7333f6c8057\nparent af70f01100d689214a451d7d18f1364e333ad667\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790461104 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790461104 +0000\n\nfeat(runtime): type the query capability''s transport errors (ADR-106)\n\nImplements ADR-106, now Implemented.\n\n- contracts: `classifyHttpOutcome(status)` and `httpOutcomeError(msg,\n  status)`, one table from an HTTP outcome to an error type; re-exported\n  by the runtime barrel. Frozen-literal test.\n- runtime: `QueryError` gains `type`, `retryable`, `status`.\n  `BaseMFE.doQuery` fills them for a non-2xx and, newly, for a fetch that\n  got no response, which used to escape as a raw TypeError. GraphQL\n  errors in a 2xx stay `{ message, path }`. It also sends `X-Request-ID`\n  from `context.requestId`, lifted from the Angular override below so the\n  BFF keeps its correlation id.\n- bff.ts template: throws the class the status maps to, so a 404 or 401\n  no longer claims to be retryable; no-response throws NetworkError(0).\n- Angular template: drops its doQuery override, as ADR-053 did for React.\n  It flattened the typed error to `{ message }` and ignored the\n  `inputs.bffUrl` its own comment offered.\n- Rust and Swift: same fields and table. A literal copy of the table in\n  each generated test runs against the lane''s own function, and a\n  TypeScript pin checks those rows against `classifyHttpOutcome`. A\n  missing Rust transport is `business`, not the no-response row.\n- PLATFORM_MIGRATIONS: `bff-4xx-no-longer-network-error` (advice) for\n  developer code that narrows on NetworkError.\n- abc-kids shell: fetchPets retries once, only when the error says so.\n\nADR corrected before implementing: the \"other 4xx\" row is `business`,\nnot `system`. SystemError.retryable is `true`, so a thrown 404 would have\ndisagreed with the envelope.\n\nRegenerated: 8 bff.ts (+ tests), 4 Angular mfe.ts, the Rust and Swift\nexample packages, the codegen snapshot, docs/api, PLATFORM-CONTRACT.md,\nthe ADR index and the system map.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGhs3QdR\nS4J9zy7Nn9W+HZInju0SpTb1Zki0ai5hncbV6rdtn/WJZPufIX0sRA1CmE+PZdb8kmnK2LasYTOx\nOwQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:18:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/fde5287e768c6619eda35bba6e9f6aebe3ab6a8f","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKGZkZTUyODdlNzY4YzY2MTllZGEzNWJiYTZlOWY2YWViZTNhYjZhOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/af70f01100d689214a451d7d18f1364e333ad667","sha":"af70f01100d689214a451d7d18f1364e333ad667","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/af70f01100d689214a451d7d18f1364e333ad667"}],"sha":"fde5287e768c6619eda35bba6e9f6aebe3ab6a8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/fde5287e768c6619eda35bba6e9f6aebe3ab6a8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/af70f01100d689214a451d7d18f1364e333ad667/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:03:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:03:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs(adr): ADR-106 — the query capability''s transport errors are typed\n\nProposed. The composition smoke job (#345) found that on the path the\ncomposed fleet actually runs, `mfe.query()` -> `BaseMFE.doQuery`, a BFF\n5xx comes back as an untyped `{ message }`. #342 typed the generated\nbff.ts connector, which no game UI imports.\n\nDecision: keep the envelope policy that ADR-053 §3 and ADR-096 set, and\nthat all three targets share, but type the transport errors inside it\n(`type`, `retryable`, `status`). One status-to-type mapping, shared by\nthe capability and the generated connector, which stops calling a 404\nretryable. The Angular template stops overriding doQuery. Swift and Rust\ncarry the same fields and table (ADR-102). Throwing was considered and\nrejected: it reverses a shared policy and breaks every existing caller.\n\nReplaces ADR-053 §3 only. ADR-053 is not edited.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"09eb7ace01830701c2b9dfe82dfa248d83eeb421","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/09eb7ace01830701c2b9dfe82dfa248d83eeb421"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/af70f01100d689214a451d7d18f1364e333ad667","verification":{"payload":"tree 09eb7ace01830701c2b9dfe82dfa248d83eeb421\nparent a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790460206 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790460206 +0000\n\ndocs(adr): ADR-106 — the query capability''s transport errors are typed\n\nProposed. The composition smoke job (#345) found that on the path the\ncomposed fleet actually runs, `mfe.query()` -> `BaseMFE.doQuery`, a BFF\n5xx comes back as an untyped `{ message }`. #342 typed the generated\nbff.ts connector, which no game UI imports.\n\nDecision: keep the envelope policy that ADR-053 §3 and ADR-096 set, and\nthat all three targets share, but type the transport errors inside it\n(`type`, `retryable`, `status`). One status-to-type mapping, shared by\nthe capability and the generated connector, which stops calling a 404\nretryable. The Angular template stops overriding doQuery. Swift and Rust\ncarry the same fields and table (ADR-102). Throwing was considered and\nrejected: it reverses a shared policy and breaks every existing caller.\n\nReplaces ADR-053 §3 only. ADR-053 is not edited.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBrF3Gsa\njrYOEJfl04uEWEhxefLqvTDgDJLcShEapu93acEDTsBH/3Zi+p2Nu/TRV34SJU9VCboxOAjQ/+ps\niA0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:03:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/af70f01100d689214a451d7d18f1364e333ad667","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKGFmNzBmMDExMDBkNjg5MjE0YTQ1MWQ3ZDE4ZjEzNjRlMzMzYWQ2Njc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e","sha":"a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e"}],"sha":"af70f01100d689214a451d7d18f1364e333ad667","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/af70f01100d689214a451d7d18f1364e333ad667"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/f4060056c67ac1343958b4f89987ed6e0940b3ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:57:34Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:57:34Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"ci: compose the abc-kids fleet and drive it in Chromium\n\nNothing in CI composed a fleet. Every gate is static, and the root\nPlaywright suite runs against a hand-written fixture. A new Composition\nworkflow builds the abc-kids base stack (registry, daemon, API, flappy,\nhockey, multiplication-quiz, shell) one service at a time, starts it,\nwaits on the endpoints the suite uses, and runs the abc-kids Playwright\nsuite that already existed but never ran in CI.\n\n- composition.spec.ts: each remote serves its federation container; the\n  shell mounts a remote into a non-empty host; and a remote component\n  that throws is contained by the runtime''s ErrorBoundary instead of\n  leaving an empty host (#247). That last probe was run locally against\n  flappy''s real built remote in Chromium; it renders\n  `<div role=\"alert\" class=\"mfe-error-boundary\">`.\n- abc-kids.spec.ts: the \"Error boundary\" tests asserted that\n  [data-testid=\"mfe-error-fallback\"] was absent, and nothing emits that\n  test id, so they could not fail. They now use the selector the runtime\n  renders, which composition.spec.ts proves appears on a render throw.\n- Advisory: path-filtered, not a required check yet.\n- Wrote down why the examples/ jest exclusion stays, and which\n  Playwright suite tests the contract''s description and which tests an\n  implementation.\n\nNot included: the in-browser 5xx -> network/retryable assertion. The\nlive query path (BaseMFE.doQuery) returns a 5xx in-band, untyped, so\nthat assertion needs a decision first.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"f8737e96a2569f80e72d50fde464090444090686","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/f8737e96a2569f80e72d50fde464090444090686"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/f4060056c67ac1343958b4f89987ed6e0940b3ab","verification":{"payload":"tree f8737e96a2569f80e72d50fde464090444090686\nparent a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790459854 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790459854 +0000\n\nci: compose the abc-kids fleet and drive it in Chromium\n\nNothing in CI composed a fleet. Every gate is static, and the root\nPlaywright suite runs against a hand-written fixture. A new Composition\nworkflow builds the abc-kids base stack (registry, daemon, API, flappy,\nhockey, multiplication-quiz, shell) one service at a time, starts it,\nwaits on the endpoints the suite uses, and runs the abc-kids Playwright\nsuite that already existed but never ran in CI.\n\n- composition.spec.ts: each remote serves its federation container; the\n  shell mounts a remote into a non-empty host; and a remote component\n  that throws is contained by the runtime''s ErrorBoundary instead of\n  leaving an empty host (#247). That last probe was run locally against\n  flappy''s real built remote in Chromium; it renders\n  `<div role=\"alert\" class=\"mfe-error-boundary\">`.\n- abc-kids.spec.ts: the \"Error boundary\" tests asserted that\n  [data-testid=\"mfe-error-fallback\"] was absent, and nothing emits that\n  test id, so they could not fail. They now use the selector the runtime\n  renders, which composition.spec.ts proves appears on a render throw.\n- Advisory: path-filtered, not a required check yet.\n- Wrote down why the examples/ jest exclusion stays, and which\n  Playwright suite tests the contract''s description and which tests an\n  implementation.\n\nNot included: the in-browser 5xx -> network/retryable assertion. The\nlive query path (BaseMFE.doQuery) returns a 5xx in-band, untyped, so\nthat assertion needs a decision first.\n\nRefs #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBjdnHRQ\n9TecyrPs7MVXRQbYMAF1d9KIgPvu0uqbLsbseJ+T3R8O4le0XXNGvBQu2o8fGfk90Gmi4Ijim8JQ\nRQs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T21:57:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/f4060056c67ac1343958b4f89987ed6e0940b3ab","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKGY0MDYwMDU2YzY3YWMxMzQzOTU4YjRmODk5ODdlZDZlMDk0MGIzYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e","sha":"a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e"}],"sha":"f4060056c67ac1343958b4f89987ed6e0940b3ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/f4060056c67ac1343958b4f89987ed6e0940b3ab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/8e17e08ea63da14663f64426a7648721a232f2ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:55:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:55:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(docker): leave hockey and multiplication-quiz on npm install\n\nTheir lockfiles do not record the Linux native binaries their builds\nneed, so `npm ci` would install none and the image build would fail:\n\n- multiplication-quiz (node:20-slim, Angular): no linux-x64 build of\n  esbuild, rollup, lmdb, @parcel/watcher, msgpackr-extract or\n  @napi-rs/nice.\n- hockey (node:20-alpine): no Linux build of @rspack/binding at all, and\n  its builder needs the musl one.\n\nThis is npm/cli#4828: a lockfile regenerated on macOS over an existing\nnode_modules records only that machine''s platform binaries. `npm install`\nre-resolved around it; `npm ci` installs exactly what is recorded. The\nearlier verification ran the install and counted packages but never\nchecked that a build tool''s native binary was among them.\n\nChecked the other 7 migrated MFEs the way that matters: after `npm ci`\non Linux x64/glibc (their builder), every installed package that declares\nlinux-x64 optional dependencies has one present. All 7 pass.\n\nBoth files go back to main''s version and keep their migration warning,\nwhich is accurate. The migration''s fix text and the template comment now\nsay to check the lockfile for Linux binaries before switching, and how to\nregenerate it.\n\nRefs #346\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"4936724e55b96367ea5cba032d0b0d664b05e8b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/4936724e55b96367ea5cba032d0b0d664b05e8b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/8e17e08ea63da14663f64426a7648721a232f2ba","verification":{"payload":"tree 4936724e55b96367ea5cba032d0b0d664b05e8b1\nparent cf167bb921b5ed7cc62c6e85f7b6ba6d48315ef4\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790459729 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790459729 +0000\n\nfix(docker): leave hockey and multiplication-quiz on npm install\n\nTheir lockfiles do not record the Linux native binaries their builds\nneed, so `npm ci` would install none and the image build would fail:\n\n- multiplication-quiz (node:20-slim, Angular): no linux-x64 build of\n  esbuild, rollup, lmdb, @parcel/watcher, msgpackr-extract or\n  @napi-rs/nice.\n- hockey (node:20-alpine): no Linux build of @rspack/binding at all, and\n  its builder needs the musl one.\n\nThis is npm/cli#4828: a lockfile regenerated on macOS over an existing\nnode_modules records only that machine''s platform binaries. `npm install`\nre-resolved around it; `npm ci` installs exactly what is recorded. The\nearlier verification ran the install and counted packages but never\nchecked that a build tool''s native binary was among them.\n\nChecked the other 7 migrated MFEs the way that matters: after `npm ci`\non Linux x64/glibc (their builder), every installed package that declares\nlinux-x64 optional dependencies has one present. All 7 pass.\n\nBoth files go back to main''s version and keep their migration warning,\nwhich is accurate. The migration''s fix text and the template comment now\nsay to check the lockfile for Linux binaries before switching, and how to\nregenerate it.\n\nRefs #346\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIH3MCuJ\nSKXI0eWZkHXHRwVSDpO+870DuOnin7dYJrFvqS+gcp5BytqyL1LEXa6+mt8lpwGOt9ML30pixtxX\nmgM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T21:55:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/8e17e08ea63da14663f64426a7648721a232f2ba","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDhlMTdlMDhlYTYzZGExNDY2M2Y2NDQyNmE3NjQ4NzIxYTIzMmYyYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/cf167bb921b5ed7cc62c6e85f7b6ba6d48315ef4","sha":"cf167bb921b5ed7cc62c6e85f7b6ba6d48315ef4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/cf167bb921b5ed7cc62c6e85f7b6ba6d48315ef4"}],"sha":"8e17e08ea63da14663f64426a7648721a232f2ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/8e17e08ea63da14663f64426a7648721a232f2ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/cf167bb921b5ed7cc62c6e85f7b6ba6d48315ef4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:42:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:42:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(docker): install from the committed lockfile with npm ci\n\nThe generated Dockerfile copied package.json alone and ran `npm install`,\nso the committed package-lock.json reached the image several layers after\nthe install that should have used it. Two builds of one commit could\nresolve different trees.\n\nTemplate (packages/plugin-bff/templates/Dockerfile.ejs):\n- `COPY package*.json ./`, then\n  `npm uninstall @seans-mfe-tool/runtime --package-lock-only && npm ci`.\n- The runtime is staged from the CLI image, not installed, so it has to\n  come out first. `npm pkg delete` edited package.json only, and `npm ci`\n  rejects a lockfile that disagrees with it: reproduced here, ENOENT on the\n  lockfile''s `../../../dist/runtime` link. The uninstall edits both\n  together, with npm''s own tooling rather than a hand-edited lockfile.\n- With no lockfile the uninstall resolves one from the registry, which is\n  what `npm install` did, so the 11 lockfile-less MFEs keep building on\n  one code path with no conditional.\n\nMigration (ADR-082): the Dockerfile is developer-owned, so regeneration\ncannot reach it.\n- New PLATFORM_MIGRATIONS entry `dockerfile-installs-from-lockfile`\n  (advice, no failsAt: an old Dockerfile still builds).\n- `collectSources` now reads the MFE''s root Dockerfile. It only scanned\n  src/, swift/ and rust/ code, so no Dockerfile entry could ever fire.\n\nFleet: migrated the 9 MFE Dockerfiles with the template''s delete-then-copy\nshape (7 meridian, abc-kids hockey and multiplication-quiz), keeping each\nfile''s own flags. Each migrated command was run against that MFE''s real\npackage.json + lockfile with no ../../../dist/runtime present: all 9\n`npm ci` cleanly. Explicitly left:\n- abc-kids/flappy: repoints the runtime to a file: link via `npm pkg\n  set`, a different mechanism; it keeps its migration warning.\n- the two shells: same `npm pkg set` shape, not template-generated, and\n  not validated as MFEs.\n- abc-kids/game-base: no lockfile to pin, not an MFE.\n\nRegenerated the codegen characterization baseline (only Dockerfile hashes\nchanged), docs/api line anchors, and the system map (new test file).\n\nCloses #346\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"1a21874a640d4117fe802c7dccb45e3459dfbbf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/1a21874a640d4117fe802c7dccb45e3459dfbbf3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/cf167bb921b5ed7cc62c6e85f7b6ba6d48315ef4","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a21874a640d4117fe802c7dccb45e3459dfbbf3\nparent a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790458961 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790458961 +0000\n\nfix(docker): install from the committed lockfile with npm ci\n\nThe generated Dockerfile copied package.json alone and ran `npm install`,\nso the committed package-lock.json reached the image several layers after\nthe install that should have used it. Two builds of one commit could\nresolve different trees.\n\nTemplate (packages/plugin-bff/templates/Dockerfile.ejs):\n- `COPY package*.json ./`, then\n  `npm uninstall @seans-mfe-tool/runtime --package-lock-only && npm ci`.\n- The runtime is staged from the CLI image, not installed, so it has to\n  come out first. `npm pkg delete` edited package.json only, and `npm ci`\n  rejects a lockfile that disagrees with it: reproduced here, ENOENT on the\n  lockfile''s `../../../dist/runtime` link. The uninstall edits both\n  together, with npm''s own tooling rather than a hand-edited lockfile.\n- With no lockfile the uninstall resolves one from the registry, which is\n  what `npm install` did, so the 11 lockfile-less MFEs keep building on\n  one code path with no conditional.\n\nMigration (ADR-082): the Dockerfile is developer-owned, so regeneration\ncannot reach it.\n- New PLATFORM_MIGRATIONS entry `dockerfile-installs-from-lockfile`\n  (advice, no failsAt: an old Dockerfile still builds).\n- `collectSources` now reads the MFE''s root Dockerfile. It only scanned\n  src/, swift/ and rust/ code, so no Dockerfile entry could ever fire.\n\nFleet: migrated the 9 MFE Dockerfiles with the template''s delete-then-copy\nshape (7 meridian, abc-kids hockey and multiplication-quiz), keeping each\nfile''s own flags. Each migrated command was run against that MFE''s real\npackage.json + lockfile with no ../../../dist/runtime present: all 9\n`npm ci` cleanly. Explicitly left:\n- abc-kids/flappy: repoints the runtime to a file: link via `npm pkg\n  set`, a different mechanism; it keeps its migration warning.\n- the two shells: same `npm pkg set` shape, not template-generated, and\n  not validated as MFEs.\n- abc-kids/game-base: no lockfile to pin, not an MFE.\n\nRegenerated the codegen characterization baseline (only Dockerfile hashes\nchanged), docs/api line anchors, and the system map (new test file).\n\nCloses #346\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAKtyh4U\nakyiMT5G/d1BVwxt2c64a5Ls5Vn2g6kakdfotkIeFcC4pQXTAPLeMMrxu7cLqNSFgHJj1D8pZiaw\nBA4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T21:42:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/cf167bb921b5ed7cc62c6e85f7b6ba6d48315ef4","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKGNmMTY3YmI5MjFiNWVkN2NjNjJjNmU4NWY3YjZiYTZkNDgzMTVlZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e","sha":"a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e"}],"sha":"cf167bb921b5ed7cc62c6e85f7b6ba6d48315ef4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/cf167bb921b5ed7cc62c6e85f7b6ba6d48315ef4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/e68de60a4c21a71a4b3b9d014156e2d9da6ac608/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:23:02Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:23:02Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"refactor(codegen): drop the options generateAllFiles ignores; pin BFF packaging\n\n1. `generateAllFiles` accepted `force` and `dryRun` and read neither. It\n   plans and renders; nothing in it writes, so both belong to\n   `writeGeneratedFiles`, which honours them. They are removed from the\n   signature and from every caller (2 source, 1 script, 13 test files).\n   A test reads the declared options type through the TypeScript checker,\n   since test files are not typechecked and an ordinary call could not\n   prove the signature.\n\n2. BFF template resolution was already moved inside the BFF package by\n   the file-contributor seam (ADR-094), the injection option the issue\n   preferred. What was missing is the acceptance test: the template root\n   sits inside a directory the package publishes, every required template\n   exists there, generateAllFiles renders from it, and no codegen source\n   reaches into a sibling package by path.\n\nRegenerated docs/api (generateAllFiles) and the system map (two new test\nfiles).\n\nADR-061, ADR-094.\n\nCloses #332\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"4c53ee405a24d46d26ad45ada343130db2655c3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/4c53ee405a24d46d26ad45ada343130db2655c3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/e68de60a4c21a71a4b3b9d014156e2d9da6ac608","verification":{"payload":"tree 4c53ee405a24d46d26ad45ada343130db2655c3b\nparent a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790457782 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790457782 +0000\n\nrefactor(codegen): drop the options generateAllFiles ignores; pin BFF packaging\n\n1. `generateAllFiles` accepted `force` and `dryRun` and read neither. It\n   plans and renders; nothing in it writes, so both belong to\n   `writeGeneratedFiles`, which honours them. They are removed from the\n   signature and from every caller (2 source, 1 script, 13 test files).\n   A test reads the declared options type through the TypeScript checker,\n   since test files are not typechecked and an ordinary call could not\n   prove the signature.\n\n2. BFF template resolution was already moved inside the BFF package by\n   the file-contributor seam (ADR-094), the injection option the issue\n   preferred. What was missing is the acceptance test: the template root\n   sits inside a directory the package publishes, every required template\n   exists there, generateAllFiles renders from it, and no codegen source\n   reaches into a sibling package by path.\n\nRegenerated docs/api (generateAllFiles) and the system map (two new test\nfiles).\n\nADR-061, ADR-094.\n\nCloses #332\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKk6vVI8\nnJa+ltpadr0prnOEad1UCMLBHh0s/qH8LwIsuL4po8zSqLaWlyrO7Gz6pr8cW7Na4hxD/wj/vcCQ\n4wE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T21:23:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/e68de60a4c21a71a4b3b9d014156e2d9da6ac608","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKGU2OGRlNjBhNGMyMWE3MWE0YjNiOWQwMTQxNTZlMmQ5ZGE2YWM2MDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e","sha":"a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e"}],"sha":"e68de60a4c21a71a4b3b9d014156e2d9da6ac608","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/e68de60a4c21a71a4b3b9d014156e2d9da6ac608"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/042a49a9bd7360395d775962b4cd69f96eafd53f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:16:00Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:16:00Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"chore(docs): regenerate system map for the new dsl test file\n\nThe quality job''s build:system-map:check failed: this PR adds\nschema.dependencies.test.ts, so the generated test-file count moved\n278 -> 279.\n\nRefs #373\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"35fbb22546e63c15835db70adbdfe681b468be46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/35fbb22546e63c15835db70adbdfe681b468be46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/042a49a9bd7360395d775962b4cd69f96eafd53f","verification":{"payload":"tree 35fbb22546e63c15835db70adbdfe681b468be46\nparent 5f0e4549196c833ddcd90d1b308ba1218d78