com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/5f0e4549196c833ddcd90d1b308ba1218d784f60","sha":"5f0e4549196c833ddcd90d1b308ba1218d784f60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/5f0e4549196c833ddcd90d1b308ba1218d784f60"}],"sha":"042a49a9bd7360395d775962b4cd69f96eafd53f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/042a49a9bd7360395d775962b4cd69f96eafd53f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/caa1f27519d89849c42cb5b2ffdc2a2a6d42cd4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:15:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:15:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(cli): CLI/MCP contract hygiene — tool names, exit-code guard, not-found envelope\n\n1. `mfe:mfe:validate` -> `mfe:validate`. A local MCP tool now carries the\n   command it runs (`command`, from the schema''s `title`), and buildArgv\n   uses it before falling back to stripping the source prefix. Renaming\n   alone would have broken dispatch: `mfe:validate` minus its prefix is\n   `validate`, which does not exist. Commands already in the `mfe:` topic\n   keep their own id; everything else is unchanged (`mfe:bff:init`, ...).\n\n2. EXIT_CODES: generate-schemas.ts already imports the contracts table.\n   Added the missing regression guard: the conformance sweep fails if any\n   published schema''s errorCodes diverges from it.\n\n3. command-not-found under --json now emits a real CommandResult\n   (ok/error/warnings/telemetry) via formatError, reusing the init hook''s\n   correlation id, and exits with exitCodeFor(type) — 64, matching\n   error.code — instead of a literal 2. Suggestions survive in\n   error.details, and are now actual nearest command ids; the old field\n   echoed argv.\n\nThe conformance sweep also covers the tool-name rule across the real\nschemas/ catalog, including that each tool dispatches to its command.\n\nADR-018, ADR-019, ADR-077.\n\nCloses #331\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"e4259979f351fb70b95a8a1b2702fd11892e80fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/e4259979f351fb70b95a8a1b2702fd11892e80fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/caa1f27519d89849c42cb5b2ffdc2a2a6d42cd4b","verification":{"payload":"tree e4259979f351fb70b95a8a1b2702fd11892e80fe\nparent a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790457307 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790457307 +0000\n\nfix(cli): CLI/MCP contract hygiene — tool names, exit-code guard, not-found envelope\n\n1. `mfe:mfe:validate` -> `mfe:validate`. A local MCP tool now carries the\n   command it runs (`command`, from the schema''s `title`), and buildArgv\n   uses it before falling back to stripping the source prefix. Renaming\n   alone would have broken dispatch: `mfe:validate` minus its prefix is\n   `validate`, which does not exist. Commands already in the `mfe:` topic\n   keep their own id; everything else is unchanged (`mfe:bff:init`, ...).\n\n2. EXIT_CODES: generate-schemas.ts already imports the contracts table.\n   Added the missing regression guard: the conformance sweep fails if any\n   published schema''s errorCodes diverges from it.\n\n3. command-not-found under --json now emits a real CommandResult\n   (ok/error/warnings/telemetry) via formatError, reusing the init hook''s\n   correlation id, and exits with exitCodeFor(type) — 64, matching\n   error.code — instead of a literal 2. Suggestions survive in\n   error.details, and are now actual nearest command ids; the old field\n   echoed argv.\n\nThe conformance sweep also covers the tool-name rule across the real\nschemas/ catalog, including that each tool dispatches to its command.\n\nADR-018, ADR-019, ADR-077.\n\nCloses #331\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQExizc7a\n1plrCJGtMhFfwQI94LcwrVGKwZgA2h317JBUrAyRo54MrSTpwp7yIJKvTCPR0fHn3OCMdM6gXMgo\nTQo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T21:15:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/caa1f27519d89849c42cb5b2ffdc2a2a6d42cd4b","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKGNhYTFmMjc1MTlkODk4NDljNDJjYjViMmZmZGMyYTJhNmQ0MmNkNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e","sha":"a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e"}],"sha":"caa1f27519d89849c42cb5b2ffdc2a2a6d42cd4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/caa1f27519d89849c42cb5b2ffdc2a2a6d42cd4b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/5f0e4549196c833ddcd90d1b308ba1218d784f60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:09:27Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T21:09:27Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(dsl): reject unknown keys under manifest dependencies\n\n`DependenciesSchema` was a plain Zod object, which strips an unknown key\ninstead of rejecting it. `dependencies.devDependencies` in\nmeridian-docking-simulation therefore passed `mfe:validate`, was silently\ndropped, and was never read by codegen, while the JSON Schema generated\nfrom the same source (ADR-065) rejects it with additionalProperties:false.\n\n- `DependenciesSchema` is now a strict object; an unknown section fails\n  with a message naming it, the allowed keys, and that dev-only deps go\n  in package.json.\n- Drop the inert key from the meridian manifest. Its package.json already\n  carries @types/styled-components, so nothing is lost.\n- Regenerated docs/api ($strip -> $strict, shifted line anchors). The\n  committed JSON Schema is byte-identical: it already said this.\n\nNo PLATFORM_MIGRATIONS entry (ADR-082): the migration matcher scans\ndeveloper-owned source, not manifests, and manifest validation already\nreports this with the fix.\n\nCloses #373\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2","tree":{"sha":"05dfab7760a4b20409c486c25870163902210cc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/05dfab7760a4b20409c486c25870163902210cc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/5f0e4549196c833ddcd90d1b308ba1218d784f60","verification":{"payload":"tree 05dfab7760a4b20409c486c25870163902210cc7\nparent a81564a43a7d5cc1bb7b19c7cd9870c8549b794e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790456967 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790456967 +0000\n\nfix(dsl): reject unknown keys under manifest dependencies\n\n`DependenciesSchema` was a plain Zod object, which strips an unknown key\ninstead of rejecting it. `dependencies.devDependencies` in\nmeridian-docking-simulation therefore passed `mfe:validate`, was silently\ndropped, and was never read by codegen, while the JSON Schema generated\nfrom the same source (ADR-065) rejects it with additionalProperties:false.\n\n- `DependenciesSchema` is now a strict object; an unknown section fails\n  with a message naming it, the allowed keys, and that dev-only deps go\n  in package.json.\n- Drop the inert key from the meridian manifest. Its package.json already\n  carries @types/styled-components, so nothing is lost.\n- Regenerated docs/api ($strip -> $strict, shifted line anchors). The\n  committed JSON Schema is byte-identical: it already said this.\n\nNo PLATFORM_MIGRATIONS entry (ADR-082): the migration matcher scans\ndeveloper-owned source, not manifests, and manifest validation already\nreports this with the fix.\n\nCloses #373\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaBtNmWafs9ZcQQWMbdmy2\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCo90WoJ\npwUDghgPGzPnoPEnqIX664ULasmY4cVsG9CQ59Sq3o1tADqL6+rSyJcLxkwgyBaSujig415Fv4jj\nOww=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T21:09:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://a