b6e420a8152666257bb7023db30a0449061","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/29453b6e420a8152666257bb7023db30a0449061"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/71343ac9088fca70de043cd7159ae4a44b12c1c0","verification":{"payload":"tree 29453b6e420a8152666257bb7023db30a0449061\nparent 7b7c73e5c25eddca4280bbfb30cba4bb8c67844f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351798 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351798 +0000\n\ndocs: regenerate API reference and system map\n\nGenerated by npm run build:docs (ADR-065) and npm run build:system-map\nafter the retry/timeout wiring, BaseControlPlane retirement,\nsentinel:validate and contract-guard changes.\n\nRefs #383 #384 #385 #391 #393\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhvYhXezqjQ6frNzWcpm4j\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGQiPOra\ndQ81y+Eux2rIzS/vtBwebamZsT/S3LeKhYijfilyKwhWWKvywQFhart9GSaJtTxuuOOQw4kRBbMG\nHA8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T15:58:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/71343ac9088fca70de043cd7159ae4a44b12c1c0","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDcxMzQzYWM5MDg4ZmNhNzBkZTA0M2NkNzE1OWFlNGE0NGIxMmMxYzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/7b7c73e5c25eddca4280bbfb30cba4bb8c67844f","sha":"7b7c73e5c25eddca4280bbfb30cba4bb8c67844f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/7b7c73e5c25eddca4280bbfb30cba4bb8c67844f"}],"sha":"71343ac9088fca70de043cd7159ae4a44b12c1c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/71343ac9088fca70de043cd7159ae4a44b12c1c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/7b7c73e5c25eddca4280bbfb30cba4bb8c67844f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:54:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:54:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(runtime): route the platform contract''s guards through their consumers (ADR-054, ADR-080)\n\nThe contracts published predicates that only their tests called, while\nthe code that needed them restated them inline. Now:\n\n- layout-manager: an EXPERIENCE payload from the daemon was cast to\n  RenderedExperience unchecked. isRenderedExperience now vouches for it,\n  and a malformed payload is reported through onError instead of being\n  handed to an adaptor. New test.\n- layout-adaptors: the module-federation adaptor re-declared the output\n  shape inline. It now uses ModuleFederationExperienceOutput and\n  isModuleFederationOutput (still rejecting empty strings, and now\n  rejecting early with the INCOMPLETE_PLACEMENT_RULE BusinessError that\n  names the missing fields). defaultAdaptors is keyed by\n  EXPERIENCE_CONTENT_TYPES instead of three string literals.\n- BaseMFE.transitionState uses isValidLifecycleTransition.\n- The generator''s hook-shadowing check uses isPlatformCapability; the\n  widened PLATFORM_CAPABILITY_NAMES copy is gone.\n\nKept, deliberately: isMfeLifecycleState, MFE_LIFECYCLE_TERMINAL_STATE,\nisResolution, isActionRecord and DaemonConfig. They are the published\nwire-protocol surface ADR-054/080 enumerate; the in-repo daemon and\nregistry are plain JavaScript images that cannot import them, so their\nconsumers are TypeScript hosts outside this repo.\n\nCloses #391\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhvYhXezqjQ6frNzWcpm4j","tree":{"sha":"934b141dd8f84f191790a7d04493544278ce9f7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/934b141dd8f84f191790a7d04493544278ce9f7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/7b7c73e5c25eddca4280bbfb30cba4bb8c67844f","verification":{"payload":"tree 934b141dd8f84f191790a7d04493544278ce9f7b\nparent 33328b0a0aa8592e4bb9f249c0d9eb52544ba323\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351650 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351650 +0000\n\nfix(runtime): route the platform contract''s guards through their consumers (ADR-054, ADR-080)\n\nThe contracts published predicates that only their tests called, while\nthe code that needed them restated them inline. Now:\n\n- layout-manager: an EXPERIENCE payload from the daemon was cast to\n  RenderedExperience unchecked. isRenderedExperience now vouches for it,\n  and a malformed payload is reported through onError instead of being\n  handed to an adaptor. New test.\n- layout-adaptors: the module-federation adaptor re-declared the output\n  shape inline. It now uses ModuleFederationExperienceOutput and\n  isModuleFederationOutput (still rejecting empty strings, and now\n  rejecting early with the INCOMPLETE_PLACEMENT_RULE BusinessError that\n  names the missing fields). defaultAdaptors is keyed by\n  EXPERIENCE_CONTENT_TYPES instead of three string literals.\n- BaseMFE.transitionState uses isValidLifecycleTransition.\n- The generator''s hook-shadowing check uses isPlatformCapability; the\n  widened PLATFORM_CAPABILITY_NAMES copy is gone.\n\nKept, deliberately: isMfeLifecycleState, MFE_LIFECYCLE_TERMINAL_STATE,\nisResolution, isActionRecord and DaemonConfig. They are the published\nwire-protocol surface ADR-054/080 enumerate; the in-repo daemon and\nregistry are plain JavaScript images that cannot import them, so their\nconsumers are TypeScript hosts outside this repo.\n\nCloses #391\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhvYhXezqjQ6frNzWcpm4j\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCigN8x9\nilRuF+pKSSoMdNscDdoyb3rkjnYJOjG/WZ7nfG9xl3PSJ9HDlYHpD7mVHvtTf5LmBwSkA1gyv9Bl\nKQw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T15:58:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/7b7c73e5c25eddca4280bbfb30cba4bb8c67844f","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDdiN2M3M2U1YzI1ZWRkY2E0MjgwYmJmYjMwY2JhNGJiOGM2Nzg0NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/33328b0a0aa8592e4bb9f249c0d9eb52544ba323","sha":"33328b0a0aa8592e4bb9f249c0d9eb52544ba323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/33328b0a0aa8592e4bb9f249c0d9eb52544ba323"}],"sha":"7b7c73e5c25eddca4280bbfb30cba4bb8c67844f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/7b7c73e5c25eddca4280bbfb30cba4bb8c67844f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/33328b0a0aa8592e4bb9f249c0d9eb52544ba323/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:54:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:54:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"refactor(codegen): drop ownershipOf; ownership is already one column\n\nownershipOf(plan) claimed to be the single source of the generator /\ndeveloper split for check:mfe-drift, mfe:validate and the dry-run\nplanner. None of them called it, and they could not have: they need the\nresolved plan (when-filtered, dynamic contributor specs expanded, paths\njoined), which a raw FileSpec list is not.\n\nThey do share one source already. FileSpec.owner becomes `overwrite` in\nexactly one place, resolveFilePlan, and every consumer reads that; the\nexisting test \"maps owner onto the overwrite flag, which is the\nownership map\" pins it. ADR-093 §4''s decision therefore holds without\nthe helper. The rationale that lived on ownershipOf moves to that line.\n\nCloses #393\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhvYhXezqjQ6frNzWcpm4j","tree":{"sha":"18742cf5c733deda0cb98f5351c4d2bfb2eb866d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/18742cf5c733deda0cb98f5351c4d2bfb2eb866d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/33328b0a0aa8592e4bb9f249c0d9eb52544ba323","verification":{"payload":"tree 18742cf5c733deda0cb98f5351c4d2bfb2eb866d\nparent 24e4102e81f3e3f5878cde6e99e59d09a38e4645\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351650 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351650 +0000\n\nrefactor(codegen): drop ownershipOf; ownership is already one column\n\nownershipOf(plan) claimed to be the single source of the generator /\ndeveloper split for check:mfe-drift, mfe:validate and the dry-run\nplanner. None of them called it, and they could not have: they need the\nresolved plan (when-filtered, dynamic contributor specs expanded, paths\njoined), which a raw FileSpec list is not.\n\nThey do share one source already. FileSpec.owner becomes `overwrite` in\nexactly one place, resolveFilePlan, and every consumer reads that; the\nexisting test \"maps owner onto the overwrite flag, which is the\nownership map\" pins it. ADR-093 §4''s decision therefore holds without\nthe helper. The rationale that lived on ownershipOf moves to that line.\n\nCloses #393\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhvYhXezqjQ6frNzWcpm4j\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHc4nJLh\nADt2x23ZYc3XOfW7vmtuRne1kZtUu8KcDefV3ktuHn6wLhr4KLo2RS4jDSG38Rc81c11BWOeIjpF\nlAU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T15:58:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/33328b0a0aa8592e4bb9f249c0d9eb52544ba323","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDMzMzI4YjBhMGFhODU5MmU0YmI5ZjI0OWMwZDllYjUyNTQ0YmEzMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/24e4102e81f3e3f5878cde6e99e59d09a38e4645","sha":"24e4102e81f3e3f5878cde6e99e59d09a38e4645","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/24e4102e81f3e3f5878cde6e99e59d09a38e4645"}],"sha":"33328b0a0aa8592e4bb9f249c0d9eb52544ba323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/33328b0a0aa8592e4bb9f249c0d9eb52544ba323"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/24e4102e81f3e3f5878cde6e99e59d09a38e4645/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:51:06Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:51:06Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(sentinel): add sentinel:validate — the kernel on a production path\n\nThe PDR-010/ADR-089 kernel and SMT''s port adapters were exercised only by\nthe n=1 proof test. sentinel:validate runs all four ports the way a host\nwould:\n\n  locateArtifacts(dir) → validate(manifest) → materialize(manifest)\n    → verify(check, source) for every HardenedCheck\n\nmaterialize is the ownership oracle: files the generator would stamp\nwith overwrite:true are excluded, so checks run only over developer-owned\ncode (ADR-082), the same split mfe:validate draws but reached through\nthe port. An invalid manifest exits non-zero; check hits are reported\nwith file, line and fix, mirrored into the envelope''s warnings, and do\nnot fail the run.\n\nThe orchestration (src/sentinel/validate.ts) takes ports and checks as\nparameters defaulting to smtPorts / smtHardenedChecks, so it names\nnothing MFE-shaped. mfe:validate''s collectSources is exported and reused\nso both commands scan the same roots.\n\nAdds the sentinel oclif topic, SentinelValidateResult, the generated\nschemas/sentinel-validate.json, and an output-schema conformance case.\n\nCloses #384\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhvYhXezqjQ6frNzWcpm4j","tree":{"sha":"2656315b3779ea064e98637e9a1165b2ae3c638c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/2656315b3779ea064e98637e9a1165b2ae3c638c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/24e4102e81f3e3f5878cde6e99e59d09a38e4645","verification":{"payload":"tree 2656315b3779ea064e98637e9a1165b2ae3c638c\nparent e678a9ffd27d62eb23c139826232705b1b3a8999\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351466 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351466 +0000\n\nfeat(sentinel): add sentinel:validate — the kernel on a production path\n\nThe PDR-010/ADR-089 kernel and SMT''s port adapters were exercised only by\nthe n=1 proof test. sentinel:validate runs all four ports the way a host\nwould:\n\n  locateArtifacts(dir) → validate(manifest) → materialize(manifest)\n    → verify(check, source) for every HardenedCheck\n\nmaterialize is the ownership oracle: files the generator would stamp\nwith overwrite:true are excluded, so checks run only over developer-owned\ncode (ADR-082), the same split mfe:validate draws but reached through\nthe port. An invalid manifest exits non-zero; check hits are reported\nwith file, line and fix, mirrored into the envelope''s warnings, and do\nnot fail the run.\n\nThe orchestration (src/sentinel/validate.ts) takes ports and checks as\nparameters defaulting to smtPorts / smtHardenedChecks, so it names\nnothing MFE-shaped. mfe:validate''s collectSources is exported and reused\nso both commands scan the same roots.\n\nAdds the sentinel oclif topic, SentinelValidateResult, the generated\nschemas/sentinel-validate.json, and an output-schema conformance case.\n\nCloses #384\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhvYhXezqjQ6frNzWcpm4j\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCPxNBh3\nXvz1F38+k5git7cySc2QxWGeK10xq4SILA3KksHig0+O+1O6+oq3tzbZHPnMabDfs/AFWVm/1AKJ\nCgY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T15:58:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/24e4102e81f3e3f5878cde6e99e59d09a38e4645","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDI0ZTQxMDJlODFmM2UzZjU4NzhjZGU2ZTk5ZTU5ZDA5YTM4ZTQ2NDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/e678a9ffd27d62eb23c139826232705b1b3a8999","sha":"e678a9ffd27d62eb23c139826232705b1b3a8999","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/e678a9ffd27d62eb23c139826232705b1b3a8999"}],"sha":"24e4102e81f3e3f5878cde6e99e59d09a38e4645","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/24e4102e81f3e3f5878cde6e99e59d09a38e4645"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/e678a9ffd27d62eb23c139826232705b1b3a8999/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:50:53Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:50:53Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(runtime): classify invokeGuarded for the Swift surface; move NO_RETRY beside withRetry\n\nThe Swift lane''s BaseMFE-surface test requires every BaseMFE member to be\nrendered natively or knowingly absent. invokeGuarded (hook timeout and\nretry) is absent: a native hook runs once, untimed. The test''s member\nscanner also read NO_RETRY''s fields as members, so the constant moves to\nretry-wrapper.ts, where the policy it defaults belongs anyway.\n\nRefs #383\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhvYhXezqjQ6frNzWcpm4j","tree":{"sha":"b1ccd47a160f0fbe03d0209563351a713ec372f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/b1ccd47a160f0fbe03d0209563351a713ec372f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/e678a9ffd27d62eb23c139826232705b1b3a8999","verification":{"payload":"tree b1ccd47a160f0fbe03d0209563351a713ec372f5\nparent f95f0ea5bd1cd4e94f40fd8ace9560549c3f1f6b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351453 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351453 +0000\n\nfix(runtime): classify invokeGuarded for the Swift surface; move NO_RETRY beside withRetry\n\nThe Swift lane''s BaseMFE-surface test requires every BaseMFE member to be\nrendered natively or knowingly absent. invokeGuarded (hook timeout and\nretry) is absent: a native hook runs once, untimed. The test''s member\nscanner also read NO_RETRY''s fields as members, so the constant moves to\nretry-wrapper.ts, where the policy it defaults belongs anyway.\n\nRefs #383\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhvYhXezqjQ6frNzWcpm4j\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK3WXchH\nZdbMapXj8iFR52b4Y/OkUFs8ifWseZlTl5PoX4GDPqZKNO28AG09+ygZ2Asg1t7jqyOyXStVCxYa\n7wY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T15:58:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/e678a9ffd27d62eb23c139826232705b1b3a8999","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKGU2NzhhOWZmZDI3ZDYyZWIyM2MxMzk4MjYyMzI3MDViMWIzYTg5OTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/f95f0ea5bd1cd4e94f40fd8ace9560549c3f1f6b","sha":"f95f0ea5bd1cd4e94f40fd8ace9560549c3f1f6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/f95f0ea5bd1cd4e94f40fd8ace9560549c3f1f6b"}],"sha":"e678a9ffd27d62eb23c139826232705b1b3a8999","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/e678a9ffd27d62eb23c139826232705b1b3a8999"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/f95f0ea5bd1cd4e94f40fd8ace9560549c3f1f6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:47:06Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:47:06Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"refactor(runtime): retire BaseControlPlane (ADR-105, supersedes ADR-059)\n\nADR-059 made the control plane an abstract base so independent Node and\nRust implementations in other repos could be swapped. PDR-008/ADR-078\nthen brought the control plane into this repo as one implementation\n(packages/control-plane, plain JS services), and nothing ever subclassed\nthe class: its only subclass was its own test double.\n\n- Delete BaseControlPlane, isBaseControlPlane, ControlPlaneConfig,\n  ControlPlaneStatus, ControlPlaneHealth and the conformance test; drop\n  them from the runtime barrel and the boundary test''s file list.\n- A host connects with LayoutManager over a\n  GraphQLTransportWsDaemonTransport, which is what start() did inside.\n- ADR-082: new base-control-plane-removed platform migration names any\n  developer-owned use and gives that replacement.\n- ADR-105 records the decision; ADR-059 marked Superseded (the\n  supersession link is required in both directions by check:adr).\n- docs/schemas/control-plane.md rewritten around the real host API;\n  whitepaper, slides, runtime-platform, class-hierarchy, status,\n  comparison and the runtime-architecture page updated to match.\n- Drop the stale graphql-ws-client.ts coverage threshold (interface-only\n  since #387).\n\nCloses #385\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhvYhXezqjQ6frNzWcpm4j","tree":{"sha":"dc7b35b839fe0d37f74c6fa0d94085b96f1f6708","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/dc7b35b839fe0d37f74c6fa0d94085b96f1f6708"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/f95f0ea5bd1cd4e94f40fd8ace9560549c3f1f6b","verification":{"payload":"tree dc7b35b839fe0d37f74c6fa0d94085b96f1f6708\nparent 3b54992466a02cb60b26c8b3173bd725238b468c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351226 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351226 +0000\n\nrefactor(runtime): retire BaseControlPlane (ADR-105, supersedes ADR-059)\n\nADR-059 made the control plane an abstract base so independent Node and\nRust implementations in other repos could be swapped. PDR-008/ADR-078\nthen brought the control plane into this repo as one implementation\n(packages/control-plane, plain JS services), and nothing ever subclassed\nthe class: its only subclass was its own test double.\n\n- Delete BaseControlPlane, isBaseControlPlane, ControlPlaneConfig,\n  ControlPlaneStatus, ControlPlaneHealth and the conformance test; drop\n  them from the runtime barrel and the boundary test''s file list.\n- A host connects with LayoutManager over a\n  GraphQLTransportWsDaemonTransport, which is what start() did inside.\n- ADR-082: new base-control-plane-removed platform migration names any\n  developer-owned use and gives that replacement.\n- ADR-105 records the decision; ADR-059 marked Superseded (the\n  supersession link is required in both directions by check:adr).\n- docs/schemas/control-plane.md rewritten around the real host API;\n  whitepaper, slides, runtime-platform, class-hierarchy, status,\n  comparison and the runtime-architecture page updated to match.\n- Drop the stale graphql-ws-client.ts coverage threshold (interface-only\n  since #387).\n\nCloses #385\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhvYhXezqjQ6frNzWcpm4j\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCPQWzBV\nBVFelCsdzyb+DnlNHgbphWk80XoBEbQ02lNYCl9DHUATKjGFOCA5j9mkxyC9ZAbQX1v3qDGgql2H\ndww=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T15:58:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/f95f0ea5bd1cd4e94f40fd8ace9560549c3f1f6b","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKGY5NWYwZWE1YmQxY2Q0ZTk0ZjQwZmQ4YWNlOTU2MDU0OWMzZjFmNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/3b54992466a02cb60b26c8b3173bd725238b468c","sha":"3b54992466a02cb60b26c8b3173bd725238b468c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/3b54992466a02cb60b26c8b3173bd725238b468c"}],"sha":"f95f0ea5bd1cd4e94f40fd8ace9560549c3f1f6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/f95f0ea5bd1cd4e94f40fd8ace9560549c3f1f6b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/3b54992466a02cb60b26c8b3173bd725238b468c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:43:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:43:22Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(runtime): wire hook-level timeout and retry into BaseMFE (ADR-029, ADR-030)\n\nwithTimeout and withRetry were implemented and unit-tested but nothing\ncalled them, while a base-mfe.ts comment claimed they were already in\nthe pipeline. They now run around every lifecycle handler call, via\nBaseMFE.invokeGuarded inside executeHook, so ADR-002''s containment,\nmain-phase propagation and failure telemetry apply to whatever comes\nout of them.\n\nManifest (LifecycleHookSchema), in the shapes ADR-029/030 specify:\n  timeout: <ms>                      no timer at all when omitted\n  onTimeout: error | warn | skip     default error\n  errorHandling:\n    types: [{ type, pattern?, retryable, maxRetries?, backoff?,\n              baseDelay?, maxDelay?, jitter?, onRetry?, fallbackHandler? }]\n\nSemantics:\n- Retry wraps timeout: each attempt gets a fresh timer, and a timeout\n  is itself a classifiable (retryable) failure.\n- Opt-in per error type: a failure is retried only when it classifies\n  as retryable AND its type has an entry with maxRetries. A manifest\n  declaring neither field behaves exactly as before.\n- withRetry now resolves the policy per classified type (ADR-030 puts\n  maxRetries/backoff per type) and resolves onRetry/fallback names\n  through BaseMFE.invokeHandler, so they resolve like any hook handler.\n- The timeout''s AbortSignal reaches the handler as context.signal, not\n  a second argument: platform handlers already use that position\n  (checkPermissions(context, requiredRoles)).\n\nAlso corrects the false comments in base-mfe.ts, handlers/error-handling.ts\nand the ADR-026 test. ADR-026''s capability-wide\nerrorHandling.retry.maxAttempts shape is not adopted; retrying doLoad\nitself remains open under #318.\n\nCloses #383\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhvYhXezqjQ6frNzWcpm4j","tree":{"sha":"5560795d3cb027ca04a2b5aefc0f44fe2dd7dcdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/5560795d3cb027ca04a2b5aefc0f44fe2dd7dcdd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/3b54992466a02cb60b26c8b3173bd725238b468c","verification":{"payload":"tree 5560795d3cb027ca04a2b5aefc0f44fe2dd7dcdd\nparent bc6895559b9687418e2d66e6219449c6472fb5f0\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351002 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790351002 +0000\n\nfeat(runtime): wire hook-level timeout and retry into BaseMFE (ADR-029, ADR-030)\n\nwithTimeout and withRetry were implemented and unit-tested but nothing\ncalled them, while a base-mfe.ts comment claimed they were already in\nthe pipeline. They now run around every lifecycle handler call, via\nBaseMFE.invokeGuarded inside executeHook, so ADR-002''s containment,\nmain-phase propagation and failure telemetry apply to whatever comes\nout of them.\n\nManifest (LifecycleHookSchema), in the shapes ADR-029/030 specify:\n  timeout: <ms>                      no timer at all when omitted\n  onTimeout: error | warn | skip     default error\n  errorHandling:\n    types: [{ type, pattern?, retryable, maxRetries?, backoff?,\n              baseDelay?, maxDelay?, jitter?, onRetry?, fallbackHandler? }]\n\nSemantics:\n- Retry wraps timeout: each attempt gets a fresh timer, and a timeout\n  is itself a classifiable (retryable) failure.\n- Opt-in per error type: a failure is retried only when it classifies\n  as retryable AND its type has an entry with maxRetries. A manifest\n  declaring neither field behaves exactly as before.\n- withRetry now resolves the policy per classified type (ADR-030 puts\n  maxRetries/backoff per type) and resolves onRetry/fallback names\n  through BaseMFE.invokeHandler, so they resolve like any hook handler.\n- The timeout''s AbortSignal reaches the handler as context.signal, not\n  a second argument: platform handlers already use that position\n  (checkPermissions(context, requiredRoles)).\n\nAlso corrects the false comments in base-mfe.ts, handlers/error-handling.ts\nand the ADR-026 test. ADR-026''s capability-wide\nerrorHandling.retry.maxAttempts shape is not adopted; retrying doLoad\nitself remains open under #318.\n\nCloses #383\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JhvYhXezqjQ6frNzWcpm4j\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEMV0x6e\nYbeLvJFnzTuvVzFIufAUZOWZ/GzL1QKn7n1DBLkBE+hSdGr9Tn5lUJ9OA8dG1KVyDjMvxkS6rmKn\nGwU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T15:58:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/3b54992466a02cb60b26c8b3173bd725238b468c","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDNiNTQ5OTI0NjZhMDJjYjYwYjI2YzhiMzE3M2JkNzI1MjM4YjQ2OGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/bc6895559b9687418e2d66e6219449c6472fb5f0","sha":"bc6895559b9