tml_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/c059e51540b4ef6bde1d361b1dd7677850de52ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T01:39:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T01:40:03Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs: base-class reference generated from the contract; BaseRemoteMFE in the API reference\n\ndocs/PLATFORM-CONTRACT.md is rewritten as the single base-class reference\nfor every build (ADR-102): the class ladder, what a developer writes versus\ninherits, the pipeline, lifecycle, result shapes, and per-language names.\nIts tables are generated from PLATFORM_CAPABILITY_SPECS,\nMFE_LIFECYCLE_TRANSITIONS and capability-results.ts (ADR-080) by\nscripts/generate-platform-contract.ts, gated in the quality job.\n\nThe HTML API reference (ADR-104) now opens on that document, with a small\nstylesheet so wide tables scroll instead of overlapping the sidebar.\nBaseRemoteMFE is added as a TypeDoc entry point: without it RemoteMFE''s\nhierarchy stopped short and BaseMFE was unreachable by navigation.\n\nFour capability descriptions in the contract were wrong (schema as SDL,\nauthorizeAccess as a daemon gate check, describe as self-registration);\ncorrected, and the generated Swift/Rust comments regenerated. Only\ngenerator-owned text changes, so no PLATFORM_MIGRATIONS entry (ADR-082).\n\nRefs ADR-080, ADR-102, ADR-104.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS","tree":{"sha":"e84a32da59d82d8e4f1b0bc6a178e52e75202be2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/e84a32da59d82d8e4f1b0bc6a178e52e75202be2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/c059e51540b4ef6bde1d361b1dd7677850de52ba","verification":{"payload":"tree e84a32da59d82d8e4f1b0bc6a178e52e75202be2\nparent 7dac431ab86cc302b4842c5281f4d563d15a2c4f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790300347 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790300403 +0000\n\ndocs: base-class reference generated from the contract; BaseRemoteMFE in the API reference\n\ndocs/PLATFORM-CONTRACT.md is rewritten as the single base-class reference\nfor every build (ADR-102): the class ladder, what a developer writes versus\ninherits, the pipeline, lifecycle, result shapes, and per-language names.\nIts tables are generated from PLATFORM_CAPABILITY_SPECS,\nMFE_LIFECYCLE_TRANSITIONS and capability-results.ts (ADR-080) by\nscripts/generate-platform-contract.ts, gated in the quality job.\n\nThe HTML API reference (ADR-104) now opens on that document, with a small\nstylesheet so wide tables scroll instead of overlapping the sidebar.\nBaseRemoteMFE is added as a TypeDoc entry point: without it RemoteMFE''s\nhierarchy stopped short and BaseMFE was unreachable by navigation.\n\nFour capability descriptions in the contract were wrong (schema as SDL,\nauthorizeAccess as a daemon gate check, describe as self-registration);\ncorrected, and the generated Swift/Rust comments regenerated. Only\ngenerator-owned text changes, so no PLATFORM_MIGRATIONS entry (ADR-082).\n\nRefs ADR-080, ADR-102, ADR-104.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAA