riptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/732a7cdf34ed4625609dc75dec0db10175a1320a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T00:25:34Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T00:25:34Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs: embed the 79-second overview reel on the landing page and system map\n\nA self-hosted WebM (720p, 4 MB) and poster under docs/media/, embedded as a\nclick-to-play <video> with a text caption on docs/index.html (under the\nheadline) and docs/system-map.html (in the header). Styled with each page''s\nown tokens, so it follows light and dark themes; no autoplay.\n\n- assemble-site.js copies docs/media/ into the site; check-site.js already\n  resolves every local src/href, so a missing file fails the publish.\n- pages.yml republishes on docs/media/** changes.\n- The caption dates the figures shown (25 September 2026) — unlike the\n  system map''s counts, the reel''s are not regenerated.\n\nVerified: assemble-site + check-site (6 pages, 0 problems); the video plays\nin Chromium on both pages, light/dark, and at 390px with no horizontal\nscroll; build:system-map:check, docs:check-links, docs:check-paths green.\n\nRefs #379.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS","tree":{"sha":"4593bf0c307566164fe42353e0af61176da71b29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/4593bf0c307566164fe42353e0af61176da71b29"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/732a7cdf34ed4625609dc75dec0db10175a1320a","verification":{"payload":"tree 4593bf0c307566164fe42353e0af61176da71b29\nparent 46c338a5421a879971583eb323462e938baff69e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790295934 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790295934 +0000\n\ndocs: embed the 79-second overview reel on the landing page and system map\n\nA self-hosted WebM (720p, 4 MB) and poster under docs/media/, embedded as a\nclick-to-play <video> with a text caption on docs/index.html (under the\nheadline) and docs/system-map.html (in the header). Styled with each page''s\nown tokens, so it follows light and dark themes; no autoplay.\n\n- assemble-site.js copies docs/media/ into the site; check-site.js already\n  resolves every local src/href, so a missing file fails the publish.\n- pages.yml republishes on docs/media/** changes.\n- The caption dates the figures shown (25 September 2026) — unlike the\n  system map''s counts, the reel''s are not regenerated.\n\nVerified: assemble-site + check-site (6 pages, 0 problems); the video plays\nin Chromium on both pages, light/dark, and at 390px with no horizontal\nscroll; build:system-map:check, docs:check-links, docs:check-paths green.\n\nRefs #379.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGuCwKoQ\nVojeOjmxKgD1tLyZTYzBCp0pq8X9KhXrrj9STWvJFIE3pPblvgiggidplfksStAFBsZzr7UDwHyu\n3Qc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T00:25:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/732a7cdf34ed4625609dc75dec0db10175a1320a","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDczMmE3Y2RmMzRlZDQ2MjU2MDlkYzc1ZGVjMGRiMTAxNzVhMTMyMGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/46c338a5421a879971583eb323462e938baff69e","sha":"46c338a5421a879971583eb323462e938baff69e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/46c338a5421a879971583eb323462e938baff69e"}],"sha":"732a7cdf34ed4625609dc75dec0db10175a1320a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/732a7cdf34ed4625609dc75dec0db10175a1320a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/46c338a5421a879971583eb323462e938baff69e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:22:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:22:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(meridian): Rust PayStatus and CrewRoster with live data; place PayStatus from the WASM build\n\nThe browser build''s renderers were seeded placeholders. Both now fetch\nthrough the build''s own query capability (ADR-101) and draw what the React\ncomponents draw — PayStatus''s held/scheduled exceptions, CrewRoster''s\nthree-list join — with the same query documents in *_query.rs.\n\n- rust/src/crew.rs: the crew.ts glue (crew refs, cents, colours), unit-tested\n  by cargo test; rust/web/src/crew.rs: query + DOM helpers. Any GraphQL\n  error fails the query, as the web lane''s query() throws, so a partial\n  `payroll: null` never reads as \"all settled\".\n- control-plane.yaml places PayStatus `from: meridian-crew-services-wasm`\n  beside the React roster; rules.json recompiled.\n- Dockerfile builds the browser build; dev-up.sh builds it on the host.\n- e2e: the status rail is the Rust build, with live HELD rows.\n\nRefs ADR-103.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS","tree":{"sha":"18d19be7d2901570003db02c9c3964f73233d842","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/18d19be7d2901570003db02c9c3964f73233d842"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/46c338a5421a879971583eb323462e938baff69e","verification":{"payload":"tree 18d19be7d2901570003db02c9c3964f73233d842\nparent ba01a24ce08d59f308f9d117f21084923dc70c86\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790274160 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790274160 +0000\n\nfeat(meridian): Rust PayStatus and CrewRoster with live data; place PayStatus from the WASM build\n\nThe browser build''s renderers were seeded placeholders. Both now fetch\nthrough the build''s own query capability (ADR-101) and draw what the React\ncomponents draw — PayStatus''s held/scheduled exceptions, CrewRoster''s\nthree-list join — with the same query documents in *_query.rs.\n\n- rust/src/crew.rs: the crew.ts glue (crew refs, cents, colours), unit-tested\n  by cargo test; rust/web/src/crew.rs: query + DOM helpers. Any GraphQL\n  error fails the query, as the web lane''s query() throws, so a partial\n  `payroll: null` never reads as \"all settled\".\n- control-plane.yaml places PayStatus `from: meridian-crew-services-wasm`\n  beside the React roster; rules.json recompiled.\n- Dockerfile builds the browser build; dev-up.sh builds it on the host.\n- e2e: the status rail is the Rust build, with live HELD rows.\n\nRefs ADR-103.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA9L/wzO\nGvTV9uImYFHNLI84x7CELUHy0d3VIPj10lCRlmb/MQX+eAMtz05A1ZGXNiOeYnf0+epG8Z3d4yyD\nzgg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T18:22:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/46c338a5421a879971583eb323462e938baff69e","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDQ2YzMzOGE1NDIxYTg3OTk3MTU4M2ViMzIzNDYyZTkzOGJhZmY2OWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/ba01a24ce08d59f308f9d117f21084923dc70c86","sha":"ba01a24ce08d59f308f9d117f21084923dc70c86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/ba01a24ce08d59f308f9d117f21084923dc70c86"}],"sha":"46c338a5421a879971583eb323462e938baff69e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/46c338a5421a879971583eb323462e938baff69e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/ba01a24ce08d59f308f9d117f21084923dc70c86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:22:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T18:22:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(control-plane): compose a manifest''s browser build as <name>-wasm (ADR-103)\n\nADR-100 left the Rust browser build unplaceable: one registration per\nmanifest, and \"which build serves PayStatus\" unanswered. The compiler now\nderives a second registration for targets.rust.wasm — <name>-wasm, scope\n<crate>_wasm, <endpoint>/wasm/remoteEntry.js, no slots. An unqualified\nplacement stays on the web build; `from: <name>-wasm` opts in.\n\n- dsl: browser-build.ts holds rustCrateName / rustWasmScope / browserBuildOf,\n  read by the compiler and (via codegen) by the Rust codegen, so rules.json\n  and remoteEntry.js cannot disagree on the scope.\n- plugin-bff: server.ts serves rust/web/www at /wasm before the SPA fallback;\n  the seeded Dockerfile gains a wasm-builder stage (wasm-bindgen CLI version\n  read from the lockfile). .dockerignore excludes Cargo output. All three\n  are conditional: MFEs without the build generate byte-identical files.\n- check-rust-wasm-mount asserts the renderer''s data-capability stamp, not\n  its heading text, which is developer-owned.\n\nGenerator-owned files only (server.ts, .dockerignore); no developer-owned\nfile names anything changed, so no PLATFORM_MIGRATIONS entry (ADR-082).\n\nRefs ADR-103.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS","tree":{"sha":"0501dc2f28b4cfc6c40bd6899a9c56d54bbcffdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/0501dc2f28b4cfc6c40bd6899a9c56d54bbcffdc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/ba01a24ce08d59f308f9d117f21084923dc70c86","verification":{"payload":"tree 0501dc2f28b4cfc6c40bd6899a9c56d54bbcffdc\nparent 7695f8a2254f3133c45447787da13396faa36ebe\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790274160 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790274160 +0000\n\nfeat(control-plane): compose a manifest''s browser build as <name>-wasm (ADR-103)\n\nADR-100 left the Rust browser build unplaceable: one registration per\nmanifest, and \"which build serves PayStatus\" unanswered. The compiler now\nderives a second registration for targets.rust.wasm — <name>-wasm, scope\n<crate>_wasm, <endpoint>/wasm/remoteEntry.js, no slots. An unqualified\nplacement stays on the web build; `from: <name>-wasm` opts in.\n\n- dsl: browser-build.ts holds rustCrateName / rustWasmScope / browserBuildOf,\n  read by the compiler and (via codegen) by the Rust codegen, so rules.json\n  and remoteEntry.js cannot disagree on the scope.\n- plugin-bff: server.ts serves rust/web/www at /wasm before the SPA fallback;\n  the seeded Dockerfile gains a wasm-builder stage (wasm-bindgen CLI version\n  read from the lockfile). .dockerignore excludes Cargo output. All three\n  are conditional: MFEs without the build generate byte-identical files.\n- check-rust-wasm-mount asserts the renderer''s data-capability stamp, not\n  its heading text, which is developer-owned.\n\nGenerator-owned files only (server.ts, .dockerignore); no developer-owned\nfile names anything changed, so no PLATFORM_MIGRATIONS entry (ADR-082).\n\nRefs ADR-103.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCm1g/2M\n/zzB3CxjFOWXWjTeGyHKiZvPdt0VjV4tdgvW6BfH0Jo3ct/nwSTxAlZ4OKx5OPx675qkSUZGhKsb\ndAM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T18:22:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followe