","tree":{"sha":"f3f0254cee88001b8b11a59cdf5328586ec4f938","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/f3f0254cee88001b8b11a59cdf5328586ec4f938"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/270f3d31e6c139e09c0bab45c33ac13db83abfa6","verification":{"payload":"tree f3f0254cee88001b8b11a59cdf5328586ec4f938\nparent 11372632c4e2b387063c25f28dcb071e3917733b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790249563 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790249563 +0000\n\nfeat(examples): drive all ten Rust capabilities in the browser gate\n\ncheck:rust-wasm now also lints the core crate for wasm32, and the mount\ncheck drives every capability through the remote''s mfe object in Chromium:\nquery reaches a stub BFF over fetch with the bearer token, emit reaches an\nattached telemetry function, and updateControlPlaneState sends its\nSTATE_UPDATE envelope over the daemon channel the SHELL''S ADAPTOR handed\nover. Breaking that hand-over fails exactly those two checks.\n\nmeridian-crew-services'' Rust crate regenerated; its developer-owned web\nCargo.toml and READMEs re-seeded (seeded by this same unmerged PR).\n\nRefs ADR-101.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEJovdOH\n50ZWMCrETwfD0NxFUKHsZ5bNlYEY36Lw25olNYpRWC2Gim4xl6olpfQNZPO8YyRrVfoHE2XQKoLL\nRAw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T11:32:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/270f3d31e6c139e09c0bab45c33ac13db83abfa6","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDI3MGYzZDMxZTZjMTM5ZTA5YzBiYWI0NWMzM2FjMTNkYjgzYWJmYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/11372632c4e2b387063c25f28dcb071e3917733b","sha":"11372632c4e2b387063c25f28dcb071e3917733b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/11372632c4e2b387063c25f28dcb071e3917733b"}],"sha":"270f3d31e6c139e09c0bab45c33ac13db83abfa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/270f3d31e6c139e09c0bab45c33ac13db83abfa6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/11372632c4e2b387063c25f28dcb071e3917733b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T11:32:43Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T11:32:43Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(framework-rust): implement all ten capabilities against the runtime result contract\n\nThe Rust lane now implements every capability BaseRemoteMFE implements and\nreturns the shapes in packages/runtime/src/capability-results.ts (camelCase,\nlowercase enums, ISO-8601 timestamps) instead of the Swift lane''s.\n\n- schema: the manifest as JSON (embedded at generation), format json\n- describe: adds type and the manifest\n- health: status + checks (state, capability-table, transport with a BFF)\n- emit: forwards inputs.event to deps.telemetry; emitted:false otherwise\n- updateControlPlaneState: validates stateKey/stateData/correlationId,\n  builds the ADR-057 STATE_UPDATE envelope, sends the daemon''s sendMessage\n  mutation through an injected MfeControlPlaneClient (the analogue of\n  deps.wsClient); acknowledged:false when disconnected; timeout mapped\n- MfeTelemetryEvent now mirrors the runtime''s TelemetryEvent\n- futures/traits are Send natively and not on wasm32 (MaybeSendSync), so\n  the browser build can use fetch and the shell''s daemon channel\n- browser build: fetch transport, adaptor-attached daemon channel,\n  attachable telemetry, and all ten exposed on the remote entry''s mfe object\n\nrust-result-contract.test.ts compares capability-results.ts (read with the\nTS compiler) to the generated types.rs — not circular. 15 new generated\ncargo tests run each capability.\n\nRefs ADR-101.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS","tree":{"sha":"16ed537a5db892ab456e38420cc9f3b69144c45b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/16ed537a5db892ab456e38420cc9f3b69144c45b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/11372632c4e2b387063c25f28dcb071e3917733b","verification":{"payload":"tree 16ed537a5db892ab456e38420cc9f3b69144c45b\nparent 02fbf221e9f87ca3cbeb3ff1e21d93b284f1055c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790249563 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790249563 +0000\n\nfeat(framework-rust): implement all ten capabilities against the runtime result contract\n\nThe Rust lane now implements every capability BaseRemoteMFE implements and\nreturns the shapes in packages/runtime/src/capability-results.ts (camelCase,\nlowercase enums, ISO-8601 timestamps) instead of the Swift lane''s.\n\n- schema: the manifest as JSON (embedded at generation), format json\n- describe: adds type and the manifest\n- health: status + checks (state, capability-table, transport with a BFF)\n- emit: forwards inputs.event to deps.telemetry; emitted:false otherwise\n- updateControlPlaneState: validates stateKey/stateData/correlationId,\n  builds the ADR-057 STATE_UPDATE envelope, sends the daemon''s sendMessage\n  mutation through an injected MfeControlPlaneClient (the analogue of\n  deps.wsClient); acknowledged:false when disconnected; timeout mapped\n- MfeTelemetryEvent now mirrors the runtime''s TelemetryEvent\n- futures/traits are Send natively and not on wasm32 (MaybeSendSync), so\n  the browser build can use fetch and the shell''s daemon channel\n- browser build: fetch transport, adaptor-attached daemon channel,\n  attachable telemetry, and all ten exposed on the remote entry''s mfe object\n\nrust-result-contract.test.ts compares capability-results.ts (read with the\nTS compiler) to the generated types.rs — not circular. 15 new generated\ncargo tests run each capability.\n\nRefs ADR-101.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKyhxz0z\nXW7k32OIU/ueXRyPXZiWDmS5awdT6RivnhhVE1TWw7HjQvztQVU1jQInmnxou+wz/UNJWK+vf2Fl\nXwc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T11:32:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/11372632c4e2b387063c25f28dcb071e3917733b","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDExMzcyNjMyYzRlMmIzODcwNjNjMjVmMjhkY2IwNzFlMzkxNzczM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/02fbf221e9f87ca3cbeb3ff1e21d93b284f1055c","sha":"02fbf221e9f87ca3cbeb3ff1e21d93b284f1055c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/02fbf221e9f87ca3cbeb3ff1e21d93b284f1055c"}],"sha":"11372632c4e2b387063c25f28dcb071e3917733b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/11372632c4e2b3