c30f6e3a791194d8f27"}],"sha":"02fbf221e9f87ca3cbeb3ff1e21d93b284f1055c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/02fbf221e9f87ca3cbeb3ff1e21d93b284f1055c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/c545900bdc3ca6ade300bc30f6e3a791194d8f27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T03:10:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T03:10:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(examples): crew-services builds its Rust crate for the browser; check:rust-wasm gate\n\nmeridian-crew-services sets targets.rust.wasm and commits rust/web/.\ncheck:rust-wasm builds every browser crate for wasm32 (clippy, fmt,\nbuild.sh), then check-rust-wasm-mount.mjs loads the COMPILED\ndist/runtime/layout-adaptors.js into Chromium and mounts each capability\nthrough moduleFederationAdaptor: drawn, side by side, unmount empties the\nslot, unknown capability rejected. A broken scope fails it with the\nshell''s own ''Remote container not found''.\n\nNew rust-wasm CI job runs it with --require and builds on Rust 1.77, the\nweb crate''s declared MSRV (wasm-bindgen 0.2.128 needs 1.77).\n\nRefs ADR-100.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS","tree":{"sha":"d4fba07c370824da340a37fcad64b8cdee2b6750","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/d4fba07c370824da340a37fcad64b8cdee2b6750"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/c545900bdc3ca6ade300bc30f6e3a791194d8f27","verification":{"payload":"tree d4fba07c370824da340a37fcad64b8cdee2b6750\nparent 66d3aea3628134bd20bb6eaf3a96ea83fb728ea4\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790219413 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790219413 +0000\n\nfeat(examples): crew-services builds its Rust crate for the browser; check:rust-wasm gate\n\nmeridian-crew-services sets targets.rust.wasm and commits rust/web/.\ncheck:rust-wasm builds every browser crate for wasm32 (clippy, fmt,\nbuild.sh), then check-rust-wasm-mount.mjs loads the COMPILED\ndist/runtime/layout-adaptors.js into Chromium and mounts each capability\nthrough moduleFederationAdaptor: drawn, side by side, unmount empties the\nslot, unknown capability rejected. A broken scope fails it with the\nshell''s own ''Remote container not found''.\n\nNew rust-wasm CI job runs it with --require and builds on Rust 1.77, the\nweb crate''s declared MSRV (wasm-bindgen 0.2.128 needs 1.77).\n\nRefs ADR-100.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDcYqI1/\nqH0qoMDKL1dGAg+W2xkFjyhjNF/FRGUnGh6mB9cAbXvKNhfYX+n9cBjRe5YQqyGFKQ7XmJmmt+eT\nzAI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T03:10:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/c545900bdc3ca6ade300bc30f6e3a791194d8f27","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKGM1NDU5MDBiZGMzY2E2YWRlMzAwYmMzMGY2ZTNhNzkxMTk0ZDhmMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/66d3aea3628134bd20bb6eaf3a96ea83fb728ea4","sha":"66d3aea3628134bd20bb6eaf3a96ea83fb728ea4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/66d3aea3628134bd20bb6eaf3a96ea83fb728ea4"}],"sha":"c545900bdc3ca6ade300bc30f6e3a791194d8f27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/c545900bdc3ca6ade300bc30f6e3a791194d8f27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/66d3aea3628134bd20bb6eaf3a96ea83fb728ea4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T03:10:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T03:10:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(framework-rust): targets.rust.wasm builds the crate as a browser remote\n\ntargets.rust.wasm: true adds rust/web/, a cdylib compiled to WebAssembly\nand shipped with a hand-written remoteEntry.js: a Module Federation\ncontainer under its own scope (<lib>_wasm) exposing ./App as the ADR-056\nimperative handle. The shell''s existing moduleFederationAdaptor mounts it\nlike any React remote — no runtime, shell or control-plane change.\n\n- mount() runs load then render through the contract (guards, hooks),\n  then the capability''s developer-owned web-sys render(element, props)\n- a second crate, so enabling it changes no developer-owned Cargo.toml\n- core crate is wasm32-safe: no SystemTime/Instant::now() on wasm32\n  (StateTransition.at is Option<SystemTime>)\n- wasm-bindgen pinned exactly; build.sh checks the CLI matches\n- mfe:validate: rust-capability-view backstop for a deleted renderer;\n  source scan skips rust/web/www/pkg and Cargo target dirs\n- plugin buildProduction also builds the browser remote when wasm is on\n- drift gate''s maximal manifest forces wasm on for orphan detection\n\nRefs ADR-100.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS","tree":{"sha":"2ce86fb45b65411ce9070d661c8fafc40c2e6d9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/2ce86fb45b65411ce9070d661c8fafc40c2e6d9c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/66d3aea3628134bd20bb6eaf3a96ea83fb728ea4","verification":{"payload":"tree 2ce86fb45b65411ce9070d661c8fafc40c2e6d9c\nparent d8c6aefbcfa697bd2c89aa66f7c3a2cb5ea4858c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790219413 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790219413 +0000\n\nfeat(framework-rust): targets.rust.wasm builds the crate as a browser remote\n\ntargets.rust.wasm: true adds rust/web/, a cdylib compiled to WebAssembly\nand shipped with a hand-written remoteEntry.js: a Module Federation\ncontainer under its own scope (<lib>_wasm) exposing ./App as the ADR-056\nimperative handle. The shell''s existing moduleFederationAdaptor mounts it\nlike any React remote — no runtime, shell or control-plane change.\n\n- mount() runs load then render through the contract (guards, hooks),\n  then the capability''s developer-owned web-sys render(element, props)\n- a second crate, so enabling it changes no developer-owned Cargo.toml\n- core crate is wasm32-safe: no SystemTime/Instant::now() on wasm32\n  (StateTransition.at is Option<SystemTime>)\n- wasm-bindgen pinned exactly; build.sh checks the CLI matches\n- mfe:validate: rust-capability-view backstop for a deleted renderer;\n  source scan skips rust/web/www/pkg and Cargo target dirs\n- plugin buildProduction also builds the browser remote when wasm is on\n- drift gate''s maximal manifest forces wasm on for orphan detection\n\nRefs ADR-100.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLu7PgQZ\nTdUzRUnqD6WwUOwXracoWPtu+wGI2WgWnl7AroQQhavOvuSS9uzQZdKk3eNHWNVdJ0QnAnJqU93D\naw8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T03:10:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/66d3aea3628134bd20bb6eaf3a96ea83fb728ea4","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDY2ZDNhZWEzNjI4MTM0YmQyMGJiNmVhZjNhOTZlYTgzZmI3MjhlYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/d8c6aefbcfa697bd2c89aa66f7c3a2cb5ea4858c","sha":"d8c6aefbcfa697bd2c89aa66f7c3a2cb5ea4858c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/d8c6aefbcfa697bd2c89aa66f7c3a2cb5ea4858c"}],"sha":"66d3aea3628134bd20bb6eaf3a96ea83fb728ea4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/66d3aea3628134bd20bb6eaf3a96ea83fb728ea4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/d8c6aefbcfa697bd2c89aa66f7c3a2cb5ea4858c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T02:50:34Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T02:50:34Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs: prompt audit — fix drifted agent instructions and under-described MCP tools\n\nInstruction files had drifted from the code and from each other:\n- src/runtime/ (does not exist) -> packages/runtime/src/ in CLAUDE.md,\n  execute-issue.md and copilot-instructions.md, so runtime edits now\n  trigger test:ci and the CLI image rebuild as intended\n- execute-issue.md: defer to CLAUDE.md''s gate list instead of a 5-gate\n  copy that ran build:schemas alone (which CLAUDE.md §5 says is wrong);\n  drop a dead src/utils/ path and harness-duplicating tooling hints\n- copilot-instructions.md: replace an ADR table whose every number was\n  wrong with a pointer to the generated index; correct template paths,\n  schema layout, class hierarchy, load() semantics and the framework\n  plugin rule\n- CLAUDE.md: correct template and schema paths and the framework rule;\n  replace the dated status snapshot and backlog with a pointer to\n  docs/PROJECT-STATUS.md; stop calling session-prompt.md the current\n  session; keep gate 8''s reasons, drop its archaeology\n- meridian skill: no machine-specific Chrome path\n\nMCP tools: deploy, remote:generate and mfe:validate descriptions now\nstate what they do, their side effects, and what they are not for.\nSchemas regenerated with npm run build.\n\nRefs ADR-036, ADR-096.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS","tree":{"sha":"17278e5192f20e0e58efc528c9ca33e60d9e035e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/17278e5192f20e0e58efc528c9ca33e60d9e035e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/d8c6aefbcfa697bd2c89aa66f7c3a2cb5ea4858c","verification":{"payload":"tree 17278e5192f20e0e58efc528c9ca33e60d9e035e\nparent 7d0ea286c0baa0de5f419d351b6fad501372f30b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790218234 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790218234 +0000\n\ndocs: prompt audit — fix drifted agent instructions and under-described MCP tools\n\nInstruction files had drifted from the code and from each other:\n- src/runtime/ (does not exist) -> packages/runtime/src/ in CLAUDE.md,\n  execute-issue.md and copilot-instructions.md, so runtime edits now\n  trigger test:ci and the CLI image rebuild as intended\n- execute-issue.md: defer to CLAUDE.md''s gate list instead of a 5-gate\n  copy that ran build:schemas alone (which CLAUDE.md §5 says is wrong);\n  drop a dead src/utils/ path and harness-duplicating tooling hints\n- copilot-instructions.md: replace an ADR table whose every number was\n  wrong with a pointer to the generated index; correct template paths,\n  schema layout, class hierarchy, load() semantics and the framework\n  plugin rule\n- CLAUDE.md: correct template and schema paths and the framework rule;\n  replace the dated status snapshot and backlog with a pointer to\n  docs/PROJECT-STATUS.md; stop calling session-prompt.md the current\n  session; keep gate 8''s reasons, drop its archaeology\n- meridian skill: no machine-specific Chrome path\n\nMCP tools: deploy, remote:generate and mfe:validate descriptions now\nstate what they do, their side effects, and what they are not for.\nSchemas regenerated with npm run build.\n\nRefs ADR-036, ADR-096.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QLsKAxwc9YVsKab1o1cvJS\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOGfcx4g\nVKE2RMAnH5FqMIok9N6utIOu6xDi5aQIywUTkPP+uOaTizjchu8L87TNOabhobiRAYHLJxVfetri\nsAc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T02:50:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/d8c6aefbcfa697bd2c89aa66f7c3a2cb5ea4858c","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKGQ4YzZhZWZiY2ZhNjk3YmQyYzg5YWE2NmY3YzNhMmNiNWVhNDg1OGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/c