false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/28e6a2252751622584a42095d54e001040e8a268","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDI4ZTZhMjI1Mjc1MTYyMjU4NGE0MjA5NWQ1NGUwMDEwNDBlOGEyNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/d7e9b88eb57c1468015f8e3a99d4391360731904","sha":"d7e9b88eb57c1468015f8e3a99d4391360731904","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/d7e9b88eb57c1468015f8e3a99d4391360731904"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/51928c9ae0933b49300b6a0f3f32a454c78f63fa","sha":"51928c9ae0933b49300b6a0f3f32a454c78f63fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/51928c9ae0933b49300b6a0f3f32a454c78f63fa"}],"sha":"28e6a2252751622584a42095d54e001040e8a268","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/28e6a2252751622584a42095d54e001040e8a268"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/51928c9ae0933b49300b6a0f3f32a454c78f63fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T02:46:15Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T02:46:15Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(framework-swift): the generated test file never imported Foundation\n\nThe `swift` job failed on 44b10c6. Three errors, one cause:\n\n  LifecycleTests.swift:191: error: cannot find ''URL'' in scope\n  LifecycleTests.swift:166: error: ''nil'' requires a contextual type   (x2)\n\n`import Testing` and `@testable import <Module>` do not bring Foundation into\nscope, and the transport tests I added are the first thing in this file to name\n`URL`, `HTTPURLResponse` and `URLRequest`. On Linux HTTPURLResponse is in\nFoundationNetworking, so the import is guarded the same way the platform files\nguard theirs.\n\nAlso replaced `await #expect(throws: BFFError.self) { ... }`, which resolved to\nthe synchronous overload and warned \"no ''async'' operations occur within ''await''\nexpression\", with an explicit do/catch and `#expect(thrown is BFFError)`. Same\nassertion, no dependence on macro overload resolution.\n\nAnd a self-inflicted one worth recording, caught by reading the generated file\nrather than by a gate: my first attempt anchored the new imports on the string\n`import Testing`, which occurs EARLIER in the header comment — \"Swift Testing\n(`import Testing`, `@Test`, …)\" — so the imports were spliced into the middle of\na sentence and the rest of it fell outside the comment. Templates are prose plus\ncode; a string anchor has to be a line, not a word.\n\nRefs ADR-096\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZJjm3UBS7bRDSC4stk6wD","tree":{"sha":"490b257892d0496dbcab741e361a88d0269e4f09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/490b257892d0496dbcab741e361a88d0269e4f09"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/51928c9ae0933b49300b6a0f3f32a454c78f63fa","verification":{"payload":"tree 490b257892d0496dbcab741e361a88d0269e4f09\nparent 44b10c6b1d4ac40aa2d5331dfe0b38fdce303618\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789699575 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789699575 +0000\n\nfix(framework-swift): the generated test file never imported Foundation\n\nThe `swift` job failed on 44b10c6. Three errors, one cause:\n\n  LifecycleTests.swift:191: error: cannot find ''URL'' in scope\n  LifecycleTests.swift:166: error: ''nil'' requires a contextual type   (x2)\n\n`import Testing` and `@testable import <Module>` do not bring Foundation into\nscope, and the transport tests I added are the first thing in this file to name\n`URL`, `HTTPURLResponse` and `URLRequest`. On Linux HTTPURLResponse is in\nFoundationNetworking, so the import is guarded the same way the platform files\nguard theirs.\n\nAlso replaced `await #expect(throws: BFFError.self) { ... }`, which resolved to\nthe synchronous overload and warned \"no ''async'' operations occur within ''await''\nexpression\", with an explicit do/catch and `#expect(thrown is BFFError)`. Same\nassertion, no dependence on macro overload resolution.\n\nAnd a self-inflicted one worth recording, caught by reading the generated file\nrather than by a gate: my first attempt anchored the new imports on the string\n`import Testing`, which occurs EARLIER in the header comment — \"Swift Testing\n(`import Testing`, `@Test`, …)\" — so the imports were spliced into the middle of\na sentence and the rest of it fell outside the comment. Templates are prose plus\ncode; a string anchor has to be a line, not a word.\n\nRefs ADR-096\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZJjm3UBS7bRDSC4stk6wD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIfPIde+\n8SvT0IxX1q0Y77dICnCuOktNf1waLW94q7BO9bO7VFBeGrSlt1i5yFjN3mTS9bB/KlU4V8DMkudr\nxQE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T02:46:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/51928c9ae0933b49300b6a0f3f32a454c78f63fa","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDUxOTI4YzlhZTA5MzNiNDkzMDBiNmEwZjNmMzJhNDU0Yzc4ZjYzZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/44b10c6b1d4ac40aa2d5331dfe0b38fdce303618","sha":"44b10c6b1d4ac40aa2d5331dfe0b38fdce303618","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/44b10c6b1d4ac40aa2d5331dfe0b38fdce303618"}],"sha":"51928c9ae0933b49300b6a0f3f32a454c78f63fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/51928c9ae0933b49300b6a0f3f32a454c78f63fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/44b10c6b1d4ac40aa2d5331dfe0b38fdce303618/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T02:05:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T02:05:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"refactor(framework-swift): one HTTP path for query, and a seam that makes it testable\n\n`MFEBase.doQuery` and `BFFClient` each built a URLRequest, set the same\nContent-Type, checked the same 200..<300 range and reached for URLSession. I\njustified that as mirroring TypeScript. It was a rationalisation — I copied a\nstructure without checking whether its reason carries.\n\nThe web lane duplicates because `BaseMFE` ships in the published\n`packages/runtime` and cannot import the `bff.ts` generated into an MFE later:\na dependency inversion across a package boundary, structurally forced. Swift has\nno such boundary. Both files are generator-owned, emitted in the same commit,\ninto the same directory, in the same module. The real constraint was only that\nBFFClient is gated on `hasBff` while MFEBase is not — solved by putting the\nshared transport in MFEBase and having the gated file depend on it, rather than\nthe reverse. No gating changes.\n\n`GraphQLPost.send` is now the one HTTP path. Pinned: exactly one\n`URLRequest(url:)` and one `URLSession.shared` in the generated package, and\nBFFClient contains neither.\n\n**What is deliberately NOT shared is error policy**, and the distinction is the\npart worth keeping. On a partial GraphQL response — `data` AND `errors`, a\nnormal outcome — `doQuery` returns both because the capability answers with an\nenvelope, and `query<T>` throws because a caller decoding into a type should not\nsilently receive half a response. TypeScript splits them identically\n(base-mfe.ts:780 returns the envelope, bff.ts throws). Consolidating the\ntransport had to preserve that, which is why this shares `perform`-level\nplumbing and not `queryRaw` — delegating to `queryRaw` would have thrown away\npartial data.\n\n**Why it mattered more than tidiness.** Nothing could observe the divergence.\ncheck:mfe-drift compares generated bytes to the template, so both files stay\n\"correct\" however far apart they drift, and no test touched either path —\ndoQuery hardcoded `URLSession.shared`, so the `query` capability was untestable\nwhile BFFClient already took an injectable session. That is the same shape as\nthe hook engine shipping inert: correct-looking code with nothing executing it.\n\nSo `MFEDependencies.transport` is the seam (TypeScript needs no analogue — its\ntests stub the global `fetch`; Swift has no global to stub), and the generated\nLifecycleTests now RUN both policies over the same stubbed bytes:\n\n  queryReturnsPartialDataAndErrorsTogether     envelope keeps both halves\n  bffClientThrowsOnTheSamePartialResponse      same bytes, throws\n  queryReturnsErrorsRatherThanThrowing         non-2xx stays an envelope\n  queryForwardsTheBearerTokenAndHeaders        jwt + headers + Content-Type\n\nA closure rather than a protocol for the transport: `URLSession` is not declared\n`Sendable` on every platform, so a `Sendable` protocol it had to conform to\nwould compile on Darwin and fail on Linux — where this CI job runs.\n\nVerified the pin bites by reintroducing a second `URLRequest` in BFFClient.\nChecked the bare manifest too: no hooks, no BFF, and the emitted suite is still\ncoherent — the stub-transport actor is ungated because its test is, the\nBFFClient case is gated because its type is.\n\nRefs ADR-053, ADR-070, ADR-096\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZJjm3UBS7bRDSC4stk6wD","tree":{"sha":"89ff161cc03b64be55916088105e1de0471375f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/89ff161cc03b64be55916088105e1de0471375f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/44b10c6b1d4ac40aa2d5331dfe0b38fdce303618","verification":{"payload":"tree 89ff161cc03b64be55916088105e1de0471375f0\nparent 0dd413bad95498b9f582d0460b02be7dd3691c6b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789697141 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789697141 +0000\n\nrefactor(framework-swift): one HTTP path for query, and a seam that makes it testable\n\n`MFEBase.doQuery` and `BFFClient` each built a URLRequest, set the same\nContent-Type, checked the same 200..<300 range and reached for URLSession. I\njustified that as mirroring TypeScript. It was a rationalisation — I copied a\nstructure without checking whether its reason carries.\n\nThe web lane duplicates because `BaseMFE` ships in the published\n`packages/runtime` and cannot import the `bff.ts` generated into an MFE later:\na dependency inversion across a package boundary, structurally forced. Swift has\nno such boundary. Both files are generator-owned, emitted in the same commit,\ninto the same directory, in the same module. The real constraint was only that\nBFFClient is gated on `hasBff` while MFEBase is not — solved by putting the\nshared transport in MFEBase and having the gated file depend on it, rather than\nthe reverse. No gating changes.\n\n`GraphQLPost.send` is now the one HTTP path. Pinned: exactly one\n`URLRequest(url:)` and one `URLSession.shared` in the generated package, and\nBFFClient contains neither.\n\n**What is deliberately NOT shared is error policy**, and the distinction is the\npart worth keeping. On a partial GraphQL response — `data` AND `errors`, a\nnormal outcome — `doQuery` returns both because the capability answers with an\nenvelope, and `query<T>` throws because a caller decoding into a type should not\nsilently receive half a response. TypeScript splits them identically\n(base-mfe.ts:780 returns the envelope, bff.ts throws). Consolidating the\ntransport had to preserve that, which is why this shares `perform`-level\nplumbing and not `queryRaw` — delegating to `queryRaw` would have thrown away\npartial data.\n\n**Why it mattered more than tidiness.** Nothing could observe the divergence.\ncheck:mfe-drift compares generated bytes to the template, so both files stay\n\"correct\" however far apart they drift, and no test touched either path —\ndoQuery hardcoded `URLSession.shared`, so the `query` capability was untestable\nwhile BFFClient already took an injectable session. That is the same shape as\nthe hook engine shipping inert: correct-looking code with nothing executing it.\n\nSo `MFEDependencies.transport` is the seam (TypeScript needs no analogue — its\ntests stub the global `fetch`; Swift has no global to stub), and the generated\nLifecycleTests now RUN both policies over the same stubbed bytes:\n\n  queryReturnsPartialDataAndErrorsTogether     envelope keeps both halves\n  bffClientThrowsOnTheSamePartialResponse      same bytes, throws\n  queryReturnsErrorsRatherThanThrowing         non-2xx stays an envelope\n  queryForwardsTheBearerTokenAndHeaders        jwt + headers + Content-Type\n\nA closure rather than a protocol for the transport: `URLSession` is not declared\n`Sendable` on every platform, so a `Sendable` protocol it had to conform to\nwould compile on Darwin and fail on Linux — where this CI job runs.\n\nVerified the pin bites by reintroducing a second `URLRequest` in BFFClient.\nChecked the bare manifest too: no hooks, no BFF, and the emitted suite is still\ncoherent — the stub-transport actor is ungated because its test is, the\nBFFClient case is gated because its type is.\n\nRefs ADR-053, ADR-070, ADR-096\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZJjm3UBS7bRDSC4stk6wD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPT05d0H\n4vB22qMgfNOVMJw+eTt7OvGc30363PHKlatN1aucIzrQlb1ARRDiEGoji9+q5yc/rY/RyOR2vs/P\nuwA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T02:05:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/44b10c6b1d4ac40aa2d5331dfe0b38fdce303618","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDQ0YjEwYzZiMWQ0YWM0MGFhMmQ1MzMxZGZlMGIzOGZkY2UzMDM2MTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/0dd413bad95498b9f582d0460b02be7dd3691c6b","sha":"0dd413bad95498b9f582d0460b02be7dd3691c6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/0dd413bad95498b9f582d0460b02be7dd3691c6b"}],"sha":"44b10c6b1d4ac40aa2d5331dfe0b38fdce303618","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/44b10c6b1d4ac40aa2d5331dfe0b38fdce303618"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/0dd413bad95498b9f582d0460b02be7dd3691c6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:14:56Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:14:56Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(framework-swift): descriptions reached the iOS UI as HTML entities\n\nA capability described as `Crew & payroll <all>` generated\n\n    Text(\"Crew &amp; payroll &lt;all&gt;\")\n\nand that string is what an iOS user would have read on screen.\n\nEJS `<%=` escapes for HTML. The whole codebase uses it for descriptions and it\nhas always been harmless, because the web lane renders through a browser that\ndecodes the entities back — `&amp;` in JSX text is `&` on screen. Swift has\nnothing to decode them. The same idiom that is invisibly correct in\nfeature.tsx.ejs is user-visible garbage in a SwiftUI `Text`.\n\nThe Swift templates now use `<%-` with a `swiftText()` helper: no HTML escaping,\nand the escaping Swift actually needs (backslash, quote, newline). Three sites —\nthe view''s `Text`, the view''s doc comment, and the platform capability doc\ncomments in MFEBase. It also replaces an inline `.replace(/\"/g, …)` in the\ntemplate, which handled quotes but not the entity problem underneath.\n\nFound while reviewing the concurrent view-wiring change, by generating against a\ndescription containing `&`, `<` and `\"` rather than the tame ones every example\nhappens to use. Verified the regression test bites by restoring the old\nexpression: it fails naming the entity.\n\nRefs ADR-095, ADR-096\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZJjm3UBS7bRDSC4stk6wD","tree":{"sha":"17811eb0462be2a3b731f8b89dccddefe55b3a2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/17811eb0462be2a3b731f8b89dccddefe55b3a2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/0dd413bad95498b9f582d0460b02be7dd3691c6b","verification":{"payload":"tree 17811eb0462be2a3b731f8b89dccddefe55b3a2c\nparent 598188890da09500d4f5da2d29e717598d1b7355\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789668896 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789668896 +0000\n\nfix(framework-swift): descriptions reached the iOS UI as HTML entities\n\nA capability described as `Crew & payroll <all>` generated\n\n    Text(\"Crew &amp; payroll &lt;all&gt;\")\n\nand that string is what an iOS user would have read on screen.\n\nEJS `<%=` escapes for HTML. The whole codebase uses it for descriptions and it\nhas always been harmless, because the web lane renders through a browser that\ndecodes the entities back — `&amp;` in JSX text is `&` on screen. Swift has\nnothing to decode them. The same idiom that is invisibly correct in\nfeature.tsx.ejs is user-visible garbage in a SwiftUI `Text`.\n\nThe Swift templates now use `<%-` with a `swiftText()` helper: no HTML escaping,\nand the escaping Swift actually needs (backslash, quote, newline). Three sites —\nthe view''s `Text`, the view''s doc comment, and the platform capability doc\ncomments in MFEBase. It also replaces an inline `.replace(/\"/g, …)` in the\ntemplate, which handled quotes but not the entity problem underneath.\n\nFound while reviewing the concurrent view-wiring change, by generating against a\ndescription containing `&`, `<` and `\"` rather than the tame ones every example\nhappens to use. Verified the regression test bites by restoring the old\nexpression: it fails naming the entity.\n\nRefs ADR-095, ADR-096\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZJjm3UBS7bRDSC4stk6wD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCQgeeWY\ns9kxZiycNNOv3vWZTUzkETmxK0phPj5GlJBpMuY2w8DU2jhMrIfZDTQGs8VQtC+YCQRQmhK0qlqn\nkgg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T18:14:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/0dd413bad95498b9f582d0460b02be7dd3691c6b","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDBkZDQxM2JhZDk1NDk4YjlmNTgyZDA0NjBiMDJiZTdkZDM2OTFjNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/598188890da09500d4f5da2d29e717598d1b7355","sha":"598188890da09500d4f5da2d29e717598d1b7355","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/598188890da09500d4f5da2d29e717598d1b7355"}],"sha":"0dd413bad95498b9f582d0460b02be7dd3691c6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/0dd413bad95498b9f582d0460b02be7dd3691c6b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9287957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/falese","id":9287957,"login":"falese","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODc5NTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/598188890da09500d4f5da2d29e717598d1b7355/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:09:12Z","email":"falese@gmail.com","name":"Sean Falese"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:09:12Z","email":"falese@gmail.com","name":"Sean Falese"},"message":"feat(framework-swift): generated views fetch through the injected provider\n\nThe transport was generated end to end (BFFClient → BFF<Module>DataProvider\n→ <cap>()) and the view scaffold used none of it. The seeded view now takes\n`any <Module>DataProvider`, calls `provider.<cap>()` in `.task`, and renders\nloading / error / loaded — the web lane''s feature-scaffold level of readiness.\n\nThe provider is threaded, not re-made: `NativeMFEBase.provider` is public,\n`CapabilityViewRegistry.view(for:provider:)` passes it, and\n`GeneratedMFE.view(for:)` hands over the instance the MFE was constructed\nwith (ADR-096) — a host''s stub reaches the view too. The BFF-backed default\non the view''s init is emitted only when the manifest has a BFF. Previews use\na canned per-file provider so the canvas renders without a BFF.\n\nViews are developer-owned; the meridian example was re-seeded by hand.\n\nRefs #378\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"fa5e146d02a239826d9929698a9a71219db3c3fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/fa5e146d02a239826d9929698a9a71219db3c3fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/598188890da09500d4f5da2d29e717598d1b7355","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9287957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/falese","id":9287957,"login":"falese","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODc5NTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/598188890da09500d4f5da2d29e717598d1b7355","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDU5ODE4ODg5MGRhMDk1MDBkNGY1ZGEyZDI5ZTcxNzU5OGQxYjczNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/0992802d5d5a8c5f7aadcb36b0f8c522e8ae795e","sha":"0992802d5d5a8c5f7aadcb36b0f8c522e8ae795e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/0992802d5d5a8c5f7aadcb36b0f8c522e8ae795e"}],"sha":"598188890da09500d4f5da2d29e717598d1b7355","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/598188890da09500d4f5da2d29e717598d1b7355"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9287957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/falese","id":9287957,"login":"falese","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODc5NTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/0992802d5d5a8c5f7aadcb36b0f8c522e8ae795e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T14:21:26Z","email":"falese@gmail.com","name":"Sean Falese"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T14:21:26Z","email":"falese@gmail.com","name":"Sean Falese"},"message":"fix(framework-swift): Swift Testing, a real unknown-capability error, no force unwraps\n\nAddresses the generated-output review on #378 (Xcode + simulator run).\n\n- `LifecycleTests.swift.ejs` emits Swift Testing (`import Testing`, `@Suite`,\n  `@Test`, `#expect`) instead of XCTest. The swift:6.0 CI container already\n  links the Testing library (`swift test` reported \"0 tests\" from it), so the\n  same job now runs these. Adds `mountRejectsUnknownCapability`.\n- `GeneratedMFE.mount(_:)` throws `MFEUnknownCapabilityError(capabilityId:,\n  declared:)` for an id the manifest does not declare, instead of an\n  `MFEStateError` whose description claims a state violation that did not\n  happen.\n- `BFFClient.defaultEndpoint` is a `guard let` with a message naming the\n  manifest; `MFEBase` handler fallback is `split(...).last.map(String.init)\n  ?? name`. No force unwraps remain in generator-owned Swift; pinned.\n- `view(for:)` documents the `AnyView` trade-off and when to bypass it.\n- Seeded `Features/<Cap>View.swift` gains a `PreviewProvider` — not\n  `#Preview`, which needs Xcode''s PreviewsMacros and breaks `swift build`\n  on the command line.\n- README: embedding the package in an Xcode app (Frameworks, Libraries, and\n  Embedded Content) and how to get the package test target into a scheme.\n  The example''s developer-owned README and views are updated by hand to\n  match the new seed.\n\nRefs ADR-096, ADR-098\n\nCo-Authored-By: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"92ea8f1e742810705a8bc8e248d7d549eaf8e718","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/92ea8f1e742810705a8bc8e248d7d549eaf8e718"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/0992802d5d5a8c5f7aadcb36b0f8c522e8ae795e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9287957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/falese","id":9287957,"login":"falese","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODc5NTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/falese","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/0992802d5d5a8c5f7aadcb36b0f8c522e8ae795e","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDA5OTI4MDJkNWQ1YThjNWY3YWFkY2IzNmIwZjhjNTIyZThhZTc5NWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/55490e55e287ed6f19d1c4544f340369ebf8b8b7","sha":"55490e55e287ed6f19d1c4544f340369ebf8b8b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/55490e55e287ed6f19d1c4544f340369ebf8b8b7"}],"sha":"0992802d5d5a8c5f7aadcb36b0f8c522e8ae795e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/0992802d5d5a8c5f7aadcb36b0f8c522e8ae795e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/55490e55e287ed6f19d1c4544f340369ebf8b8b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T00:52:23Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T00:52:23Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs(framework-swift): the view registry described behaviour it no longer has\n\n`CapabilityViewRegistry.swift` told every generated MFE that views live in a\nsingle developer-owned `Features/CapabilityViews.swift` and that adding a\ncapability \"fails the Swift build until the author writes the matching view,\"\ncalling that failure the ADR-082 migration notice.\n\nNone of that has been true since the per-capability split: each view is its own\n`Features/<Capability>View.swift`, regeneration seeds a new one because it does\nnot exist yet, and the build keeps working. The comment described the workaround\nthe split removed.\n\nFound while writing the Mac test runbook — the same class as the stale\n`mount()` comment fixed in 23b24f8. Generated prose is shipped to every MFE and\nno gate reads it.\n\nRefs ADR-082, ADR-095, ADR-096\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZJjm3UBS7bRDSC4stk6wD","tree":{"sha":"b831f218f5fc1aaaf8606ae3407fe5c1eb1b2864","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/b831f218f5fc1aaaf8606ae3407fe5c1eb1b2864"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/55490e55e287ed6f19d1c4544f340369ebf8b8b7","verification":{"payload":"tree b831f218f5fc1aaaf8606ae3407fe5c1eb1b2864\nparent 08ca880d463fb0c79215791bbd40a0e83de5852b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789519943 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789519943 +0000\n\ndocs(framework-swift): the view registry described behaviour it no longer has\n\n`CapabilityViewRegistry.swift` told every generated MFE that views live in a\nsingle developer-owned `Features/CapabilityViews.swift` and that adding a\ncapability \"fails the Swift build until the author writes the matching view,\"\ncalling that failure the ADR-082 migration notice.\n\nNone of that has been true since the per-capability split: each view is its own\n`Features/<Capability>View.swift`, regeneration seeds a new one because it does\nnot exist yet, and the build keeps working. The comment described the workaround\nthe split removed.\n\nFound while writing the Mac test runbook — the same class as the stale\n`mount()` comment fixed in 23b24f8. Generated prose is shipped to every MFE and\nno gate reads it.\n\nRefs ADR-082, ADR-095, ADR-096\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZJjm3UBS7bRDSC4stk6wD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMDsgdKa\nXcK0rt3B5sTeiTDSxPTUGvQvHPPzUIe0rN06cnoO9BnVCo9Ha4mfIMyoKwrU4d+r07oNl0aBfiX9\n+QI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T00:52:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/55490e55e287ed6f19d1c4544f340369ebf8b8b7","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDU1NDkwZTU1ZTI4N2VkNmYxOWQxYzQ1NDRmMzQwMzY5ZWJmOGI4Yjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/08ca880d463fb0c79215791bbd40a0e83de5852b","sha":"08ca880d463fb0c79215791bbd40a0e83de5852b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/08ca880d463fb0c79215791bbd40a0e83de5852b"}],"sha":"55490e55e287ed6f19d1c4544f340369ebf8b8b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/55490e55e287ed6f19d1c4544f340369ebf8b8b7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/08ca880d463fb0c79215791bbd40a0e83de5852b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T00:00:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T00:00:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(framework-swift): manifest hooks never fired — the lookup compared two spellings exactly\n\nDevin found it by writing a throwaway XCTest against the committed package and\nwatching zero handlers run. ADR-098 shipped inert.\n\n    ManifestMetadata.hooks.filter { $0.capability == capability && ... }\n\n`MFECapability.load.rawValue` is \"load\" — the platform contract''s spelling. A\nmanifest writes `Load:`, and the projection preserves it because `describe`\nreports what the manifest declared. Exact compare, zero matches, every hook\ndead. `BaseMFE.findCapabilityConfig` lowercases both sides (base-mfe.ts:437)\nprecisely because the two spellings have always differed; the Swift rendering\ndid not. It does now.\n\nThe fix is in the comparison, not the data — normalising the projection would\nhave made `describe` report a capability name the manifest never wrote.\n\n**What this says about the last three commits.** The \"regression I nearly\nshipped\" in ce3015a — a handler-not-found throwing on load() — could never have\nreproduced, because the lookup returned empty before resolution was reached. The\ngenerated stub handlers are still right, and now they are actually load-bearing,\nbut my account of why was untestable at the time I wrote it. 141 text assertions\nand a clean `swift build` both passed with the whole feature wired to nothing.\n\n**So the generated test now runs the hooks instead of reading for them.**\n`LifecycleTests.swift.ejs` gains testManifestHooksFire and\ntestHostHandlerOverridesGeneratedStub, gated on the manifest declaring hooks at\nall. They execute in the `swift` CI job, so \"the engine is rendered correctly\nand connected to nothing\" fails a gate rather than surviving a review. That is\nthe second thing the Linux gate has bought in a day, and the first one it could\nnot have caught by compiling alone.\n\nTwo smaller ones from the same review:\n\n  - `manifest-metadata-gen` escaped only `\\` and `\"`. A `description:` written\n    with a YAML literal block keeps its newlines, and a raw newline in a Swift\n    string literal is an unterminated-string error in a file nobody hand-wrote.\n    Now escapes \\n \\r \\t \\0 and emits \\u{...} for anything else non-printable.\n  - `transition(to:)` reported every invalid transition as an attempted `load`,\n    whatever capability was running — harmless until deps.errorHandler started\n    receiving them two commits ago. Now takes `for capability:`, threaded from\n    the pipeline.\n\nNot acted on, and Devin agrees they are pre-existing: the `swift` job uses\nactions/checkout@v3 like every other job in the workflow, and `build:schemas`\ndeleting 12 stale `schemas/*.json` reproduces on main.\n\nRefs ADR-002, ADR-040, ADR-096, ADR-098\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZJjm3UBS7bRDSC4stk6wD","tree":{"sha":"7f2357132d6c6cc6f7dc1199e826ad12523163b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/7f2357132d6c6cc6f7dc1199e826ad12523163b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/08ca880d463fb0c79215791bbd40a0e83de5852b","verification":{"payload":"tree 7f2357132d6c6cc6f7dc1199e826ad12523163b3\nparent f0b066bd60d74863100b915d5852830d8fdf78d0\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789516805 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789516805 +0000\n\nfix(framework-swift): manifest hooks never fired — the lookup compared two spellings exactly\n\nDevin found it by writing a throwaway XCTest against the committed package and\nwatching zero handlers run. ADR-098 shipped inert.\n\n    ManifestMetadata.hooks.filter { $0.capability == capability && ... }\n\n`MFECapability.load.rawValue` is \"load\" — the platform contract''s spelling. A\nmanifest writes `Load:`, and the projection preserves it because `describe`\nreports what the manifest declared. Exact compare, zero matches, every hook\ndead. `BaseMFE.findCapabilityConfig` lowercases both sides (base-mfe.ts:437)\nprecisely because the two spellings have always differed; the Swift rendering\ndid not. It does now.\n\nThe fix is in the comparison, not the data — normalising the projection would\nhave made `describe` report a capability name the manifest never wrote.\n\n**What this says about the last three commits.** The \"regression I nearly\nshipped\" in ce3015a — a handler-not-found throwing on load() — could never have\nreproduced, because the lookup returned empty before resolution was reached. The\ngenerated stub handlers are still right, and now they are actually load-bearing,\nbut my account of why was untestable at the time I wrote it. 141 text assertions\nand a clean `swift build` both passed with the whole feature wired to nothing.\n\n**So the generated test now runs the hooks instead of reading for them.**\n`LifecycleTests.swift.ejs` gains testManifestHooksFire and\ntestHostHandlerOverridesGeneratedStub, gated on the manifest declaring hooks at\nall. They execute in the `swift` CI job, so \"the engine is rendered correctly\nand connected to nothing\" fails a gate rather than surviving a review. That is\nthe second thing the Linux gate has bought in a day, and the first one it could\nnot have caught by compiling alone.\n\nTwo smaller ones from the same review:\n\n  - `manifest-metadata-gen` escaped only `\\` and `\"`. A `description:` written\n    with a YAML literal block keeps its newlines, and a raw newline in a Swift\n    string literal is an unterminated-string error in a file nobody hand-wrote.\n    Now escapes \\n \\r \\t \\0 and emits \\u{...} for anything else non-printable.\n  - `transition(to:)` reported every invalid transition as an attempted `load`,\n    whatever capability was running — harmless until deps.errorHandler started\n    receiving them two commits ago. Now takes `for capability:`, threaded from\n    the pipeline.\n\nNot acted on, and Devin agrees they are pre-existing: the `swift` job uses\nactions/checkout@v3 like every other job in the workflow, and `build:schemas`\ndeleting 12 stale `schemas/*.json` reproduces on main.\n\nRefs ADR-002, ADR-040, ADR-096, ADR-098\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZJjm3UBS7bRDSC4stk6wD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJsCXPH4\nFNwgRzyA/wAgqeVQ/3DN5az1u5SR6Dte83AFU9NcQDDeZ+L7kr19IjybAgWNs0xWJcBDuKTO78Zn\nwA4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T00:00:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/08ca880d463fb0c79215791bbd40a0e83de5852b","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKDA4Y2E4ODBkNDYzZmIwYzc5MjE1NzkxYmJkNDBhMGU4M2RlNTg1MmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/f0b066bd60d74863100b915d5852830d8fdf78d0","sha":"f0b066bd60d74863100b915d5852830d8fdf78d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/f0b066bd60d74863100b915d5852830d8fdf78d0"}],"sha":"08ca880d463fb0c79215791bbd40a0e83de5852b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/08ca880d463fb0c79215791bbd40a0e83de5852b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/f0b066bd60d74863100b915d5852830d8fdf78d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T21:38:02Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T21:38:02Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(framework-swift): the two compile errors the new Linux gate found on its first run\n\nThe `swift` job failed on 919be5c, which is the job doing its job. Swift 6.0.3,\n`x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`, two distinct errors:\n\n  GeneratedMFE.swift:66: error: overriding declaration requires an ''override''\n                         keyword\n    <Module>MFE.init(provider:identity:deps:) has the same signature as\n    NativeMFEBase''s designated init — a default value on `provider:` does not\n    change that — so Swift requires `override`. Added.\n\n  MFEBase.swift:251,259: error: missing argument label ''context:'' in call\n    The protocol I wrote three commits ago is\n    `handle(_ error: Error, context: MFEContext)`; both call sites passed the\n    context positionally.\n\nEverything else compiled, which is the part worth recording: the middleware\npipeline, the hook engine, JSONValue, MFEContext, BFFClient behind the\nFoundationNetworking guard, the BFF provider, and the SPM build-tool plugin\nactually running — \"Generating ManifestMetadata.swift from mfe-manifest.json\" —\nwhich is the half no Node-side gate can reach.\n\nFour type errors have now been found by compiling rather than by reading: two\nbefore the first CI run and these two on it. All four were in generated Swift\nthat 136 passing text assertions were happy with, because a text assertion\ncannot see a type. That is the entire argument for the gate, and it did not\ntake long to make it.\n\nThe `override` is pinned by a test — it is a structural relationship between\nthe generated subclass and its base, so it is worth asserting where the failure\nis cheap to read. The argument label is not: the compiler owns that, and a\nstring assertion for it would be ceremony.\n\nRefs ADR-096, ADR-098\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZJjm3UBS7bRDSC4stk6wD","tree":{"sha":"78928614df38c06391c93d6e83e9b6770c92e15f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/trees/78928614df38c06391c93d6e83e9b6770c92e15f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/git/commits/f0b066bd60d74863100b915d5852830d8fdf78d0","verification":{"payload":"tree 78928614df38c06391c93d6e83e9b6770c92e15f\nparent 919be5ccf40546636c2a3484148c6e8e7d18c9f7\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789508282 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789508282 +0000\n\nfix(framework-swift): the two compile errors the new Linux gate found on its first run\n\nThe `swift` job failed on 919be5c, which is the job doing its job. Swift 6.0.3,\n`x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`, two distinct errors:\n\n  GeneratedMFE.swift:66: error: overriding declaration requires an ''override''\n                         keyword\n    <Module>MFE.init(provider:identity:deps:) has the same signature as\n    NativeMFEBase''s designated init — a default value on `provider:` does not\n    change that — so Swift requires `override`. Added.\n\n  MFEBase.swift:251,259: error: missing argument label ''context:'' in call\n    The protocol I wrote three commits ago is\n    `handle(_ error: Error, context: MFEContext)`; both call sites passed the\n    context positionally.\n\nEverything else compiled, which is the part worth recording: the middleware\npipeline, the hook engine, JSONValue, MFEContext, BFFClient behind the\nFoundationNetworking guard, the BFF provider, and the SPM build-tool plugin\nactually running — \"Generating ManifestMetadata.swift from mfe-manifest.json\" —\nwhich is the half no Node-side gate can reach.\n\nFour type errors have now been found by compiling rather than by reading: two\nbefore the first CI run and these two on it. All four were in generated Swift\nthat 136 passing text assertions were happy with, because a text assertion\ncannot see a type. That is the entire argument for the gate, and it did not\ntake long to make it.\n\nThe `override` is pinned by a test — it is a structural relationship between\nthe generated subclass and its base, so it is worth asserting where the failure\nis cheap to read. The argument label is not: the compiler owns that, and a\nstring assertion for it would be ceremony.\n\nRefs ADR-096, ADR-098\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZJjm3UBS7bRDSC4stk6wD\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIpogdek\nZG2WXnj+WpDT2xn7EoJybF/Oo6FCnQ7dpQGQfwErNF0uHvuZMlSD7IV3HPjIAlOAB2gfeWlxURJK\npws=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T21:38:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/f0b066bd60d74863100b915d5852830d8fdf78d0","node_id":"C_kwDONNw3XdoAKGYwYjA2NmJkNjBkNzQ4NjMxMDBiOTE1ZDU4NTI4MzBkOGZkZjc4ZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commit/919be5ccf40546636c2a3484148c6e8e7d18c9f7","sha":"919be5ccf40546636c2a3484148c6e8e7d18c9f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/919be5ccf40546636c2a3484148c6e8e7d18c9f7"}],"sha":"f0b066bd60d74863100b915d5852830d8fdf78d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits/f0b066bd60d74863100b915d5852830d8fdf78d0"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/falese/seans-mfe-tool/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=96742d45c350afac7ca68b8eae25583ee4173332&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T15%3A53%3A33.424Z"}');
