received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/commits/5dab2b13a9d4ed3053b509f62670250670b102eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:03:22Z","email":"wells.scot@gmail.com","name":"Scot Wells"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:03:22Z","email":"wells.scot@gmail.com","name":"Scot Wells"},"message":"fix: keep wildcard certs through quota errors\n\nA failed read of the project''s wildcard entitlement was treated as a\ndenial, so a Milo root outage or an expired token would delete the\nTLSCertificate and mirrored Secret of every entitled wildcard hostname\nwithin a minute, and re-issuing is blocked while the outage lasts.\n\nTreat the read as three outcomes: entitled, denied, unknown. Only a\ndefinite denial (no bucket, or nothing available) withdraws a\ncertificate. When the read fails, existing certificates and Secrets are\nleft as they are, no new certificate is requested, and the listener\nreports the usual \"couldn''t request a certificate just now\" status\nuntil the next check.\n\nTests cover an error while a certificate is serving, an error before one\nexists, and a denial arriving after an outage.","tree":{"sha":"5be99590324e85865914615130a31066cf2baae1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/git/trees/5be99590324e85865914615130a31066cf2baae1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/git/commits/5dab2b13a9d4ed3053b509f62670250670b102eb","verification":{"payload":"tree 5be99590324e85865914615130a31066cf2baae1\nparent f91c8dab0711dcd9455895b77afae982c1169e3b\nauthor Scot Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1791299002 -0500\ncommitter Scot Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1791299002 -0500\n\nfix: keep wildcard certs through quota errors\n\nA failed read of the project''s wildcard entitlement was treated as a\ndenial, so a Milo root outage or an expired token would delete the\nTLSCertificate and mirrored Secret of every entitled wildcard hostname\nwithin a minute, and re-issuing is blocked while the outage lasts.\n\nTreat the read as three outcomes: entitled, denied, unknown. Only a\ndefinite denial (no bucket, or nothing available) withdraws a\ncertificate. When the read fails, existing certificates and Secrets are\nleft as they are, no new certificate is requested, and the listener\nreports the usual \"couldn''t request a certificate just now\" status\nuntil the next check.\n\nTests cover an error while a certificate is serving, an error before one\nexists, and a denial arriving after an outage.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQR/ozPp/oJ2P+NplhUmONarzn3cYgUCasUNugAKCRAmONarzn3c\nYnsqAQCFvv+mueOSbEjCU4fgOkPgDFFtyUVmJO/HKguv/HW4zgEA3V7tk8dUPVYH\nCjodlmGXwwhk/X7av0U89BYOutzmFQw=\n=iuSO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T15:03:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6007097?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/scotwells","id":6007097,"login":"scotwells","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDcwOTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/repos","site_admin":fa