/users/mattdjenkinson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/commits/1076a7f7405af7e895a69c59cbc42242e50c5d2f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:01:27Z","email":"75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matt Jenkinson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:01:27Z","email":"75292329+mattdjenkinson@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matt Jenkinson"},"message":"feat: Export the load balancer agent tools\n\ndatum-mcp runs on a customer''s own machine, so it cannot reach the\nin-cluster alb-mcp, and it cannot import internal/agent. Without an\nimportable surface its only option is to copy the diagnosis walk and the\nreason catalog, which is the drift the agent design exists to prevent.\n\nKey changes:\n- Add pkg/albagent, a re-export of internal/agent with no logic of its own\n- Re-export the scheme and namespace a caller needs to build a Reader\n- Test that every named tool registers through the facade\n- Point to it from the agent docs\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a0927cf1e325c7b7453b36a1e4fe884f477c89e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/git/trees/a0927cf1e325c7b7453b36a1e4fe884f477c89e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/git/commits/1076a7f7405af7e895a69c59cbc42242e50c5d2f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75292329?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mattdjenkinson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mattdjenkinson","id":752923