cation\n\nThe DNS operator won''t provision a DNSZone until its Domain is verified,\nso the zone never becomes Programmed. Requiring Programmed for DNSZone\nverification deadlocked every domain delegated to Datum nameservers.\n\nattemptDNSZoneVerification now also accepts a zone that is\nAccepted=False with reason PendingDomainVerification. It does so only\nfor the registered apex: all zones share nameservers, and a subdomain\nwith no delegation of its own reports its parent''s, so accepting one\nwould let any tenant verify sub.example.com once example.com was on\nDatum. A waiting subdomain zone falls through to TXT or HTTP\nverification.","tree":{"sha":"c53387b83c4c60b95b1a4b87508d886308a3f269","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/git/trees/c53387b83c4c60b95b1a4b87508d886308a3f269"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/git/commits/6d91bd5c8cbbe0ee034d8d52fcd986e239205d8c","verification":{"payload":"tree c53387b83c4c60b95b1a4b87508d886308a3f269\nparent 595c9a2c7813ff10a9f315b8bf2154c0a8d8b1f8\nauthor Kevin Williams <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790686491 -0700\ncommitter Kevin Williams <kwilliams@datum.net> 1790686491 -0700\n\nfix: verify a domain against a DNSZone waiting on its verification\n\nThe DNS operator won''t provision a DNSZone until its Domain is verified,\nso the zone never becomes Programmed. Requiring Programmed for DNSZone\nverification deadlocked every domain delegated to Datum nameservers.\n\nattemptDNSZoneVerification now also accepts a zone that is\nAccepted=False with reason PendingDomainVerification. It does so only\nfor the registered apex: all zones share nameservers, and a subdomain\nwith no delegation of its own reports its parent''s, so accepting one\nwould let any tenant verify sub.example.com once example.com was on\nDatum. A waiting subdomain zone falls through to TXT or HTTP\nverification.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiE