network-services-operator/commits/4ce0bcb963bb40ef29c8fa6861970ef9afb93118"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/commit/fc5198556a910cc61742dd8dc9ddb35ad44df110","sha":"fc5198556a910cc61742dd8dc9ddb35ad44df110","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/commits/fc5198556a910cc61742dd8dc9ddb35ad44df110"}],"sha":"0e9ed66aa58411233966ddb229998072e09e8e07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/commits/0e9ed66aa58411233966ddb229998072e09e8e07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6007097?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/scotwells","id":6007097,"login":"scotwells","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDcwOTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/commits/fc5198556a910cc61742dd8dc9ddb35ad44df110/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T01:52:00Z","email":"wells.scot@gmail.com","name":"Scot Wells"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T01:52:00Z","email":"wells.scot@gmail.com","name":"Scot Wells"},"message":"feat(agent): register the ALB agent with the service catalog\n\nThe load balancer capabilities this repo publishes — the knowledge document,\nfive read-only ALB tools and ten triage guides — were registered from raw JSON\nin the infra repository, mounted into the assistant as a fixture file. This\nteam''s provider content sat where it neither reviewed nor versioned it, and\nadding a guide under docs/agent/skills/ meant a second change in a repository\nits author probably did not have open.\n\nThe fixture also could not be scoped: it named no project, so every project\nreaching the staging assistant got these tools whether entitled or not.\n\nRegisters instead what a provider owns: a ServiceAgent for the agent itself and\na ServiceAgentConfiguration for the content it offers. The service catalog copies\nthat content into each entitled project, as the object the assistant reads there\n(milo-os/service-catalog#110).\n\nContent is byte-identical to the fixture it replaces, and both objects validate\nclosed-world against the catalog''s CRDs.\n\nThe MCP endpoint is still alb-mcp''s in-cluster address, which is what staging\ndials. Production needs it pointed at the AI gateway.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cd68cf0f1df10a81899a0c48c6f8806aa7a721e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/git/trees/cd68cf0f1df10a81899a0c48c6f8806aa7a721e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/network-services-operator/git/commits/fc5198556a910cc61742dd8dc9ddb35ad44df110","verification":{"payload":"tree cd68cf0f1df10a81899a0c48c6f8806aa7a721e4\nparent 4ce0bcb963bb40ef29c8fa6861970ef9afb93118\nauthor Scot Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1790646720 -0500\ncommitter Scot Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1790646720 -0500\n\nfeat(agent): register the ALB agent with the service catalog\n\nThe load balancer capabilities this repo publishes — the knowledge document,\nfive read-only ALB tools and ten triage guides — were registered from raw JSON\nin the infra repository, mounted into the assistant as a fixture file. This\nteam''s provider content sat where it neither reviewed nor versioned it, and\nadding a guide under docs/agent/skills/ meant a second change in a repository\nits author probably did not have open.\n\nThe fixture also could not be scoped: it named no project, so every project\nreaching the staging assistant got these tools whether entitled or not.\n\nRegisters instead what a provider owns: a ServiceAgent for the agent itself and\na ServiceAgentConfiguration for the content it offers. The service catalog copies\nthat content into each entitled project, as the object the assistant reads there\n(milo-os/service-catalog#110).\n\nContent is byte-identical to the fixture it replaces, and both objects validate\nclosed-world against the catalog''s CRDs.\n\nThe MCP endpoint is still alb-mcp''s in-cluster address, which is what staging\ndials. Production needs it pointed at the AI gateway.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQR/ozPp/oJ2P+NplhUmONarzn3cYgUCarsZwAAKCRAmONarzn3c\nYkszAP4y0+44KOO8J6JyDNkm3OQIhWKA8I9j76jAIht1jk0y/QEAiTSvmsj7zH5B\ncTqXNkCozlAkhKh1xCHj+ROARwF4kwg=\n=TCUH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T01:52:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6007097?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/scotwells","id":6007097,"login":"scotwells","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDcwOTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"h