expand POSTGRES_USER on the wrong side\n\nLeft to the host shell it expands to nothing, psql falls back to the OS user of\nthe exec — root — and the server answers `role \"root\" does not exist`. sh -c with\nsingle quotes hands the expansion to the container, which is what the compose\nhealthcheck already does a layer up with $$POSTGRES_USER.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f963eec569f8b55b8cabbc6e0fdc0d59b79aac10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/f963eec569f8b55b8cabbc6e0fdc0d59b79aac10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/928bad52769dbba2f18f9c2e6df9d6079fc31ab8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/928bad52769dbba2f18f9c2e6df9d6079fc31ab8","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDkyOGJhZDUyNzY5ZGJiYTJmMThmOWMyZTZkZjlkNjA3OWZjMzFhYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/ec38712c813d9d11707d54c4c05da6ab5dcd75ea","sha":"ec38712c813d9d11707d54c4c05da6ab5dcd75ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/ec38712c813d9d11707d54c4c05da6ab5dcd75ea"}],"sha":"928bad52769dbba2f18f9c2e6df9d6079fc31ab8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/928bad52769dbba2f18f9c2e6df9d6079fc31ab8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/ec38712c813d9d11707d54c4c05da6ab5dcd75ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T04:36:12Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T04:36:12Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The desk, in akira-ng: two queues and the steps beside the report\n\n/desk is the queue, waiting first and oldest first inside that — a queue read\nnewest-first starves its own bottom, and the bottom of this one is whoever has\nwaited longest to hear anything. Held reports sit in their own group with the\ndate the year runs out, and the page counts the ones that have passed it.\n\nA report opens with what the reporter wrote, what the app could prove, how to\nreach them, and then the steps for its category in order, pulled from the\nservice so there is one copy of the routing rather than two. The sentence above\nthe button changes with the case, because the button''s consequence does: a\nreport nobody can be told about is deleted straight away, one that can be is\ndeleted only after the mail goes, and a mandatory one is not deleted at all.\n\nThe nav entry appears only for an account carrying COMMS_DESK. Everyone else\nwould get a link that 403s, and a link into somebody else''s abuse reports is not\nsomething to advertise to a realm full of card players.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6bc7f9e119c1f80e0cd8de243c051f6bf9b52499","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/6bc7f9e119c1f80e0cd8de243c051f6bf9b52499"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/ec38712c813d9d11707d54c4c05da6ab5dcd75ea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/ec38712c813d9d11707d54c4c05da6ab5dcd75ea","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGVjMzg3MTJjODEzZDlkMTE3MDdkNTRjNGMwNWRhNmFiNWRjZDc1ZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/cda4f9271e73a29b5759dc591aac65819cd5c0ac","sha":"cda4f9271e73a29b5759dc591aac65819cd5c0ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/cda4f9271e73a29b5759dc591aac65819cd5c0ac"}],"sha":"ec38712c813d9d11707d54c4c05da6ab5dcd75ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/ec38712c813d9d11707d54c4c05da6ab5dcd75ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/cda4f9271e73a29b5759dc591aac65819cd5c0ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T04:25:14Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T04:25:14Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The desk: read a report, say what was done, and only then delete it\n\n/desk is the read side, behind the COMMS_DESK realm role rather than merely\nbehind a login — the realm has users who are here for a card game, and this is\nwhat somebody was sent plus how to reach them. The intake endpoints still have\nno GET.\n\nThe order of the handling is the promise the site makes, in the order it makes\nit: tell the reporter, then delete the copy. Never the other way, and never the\ndelete without the telling — a mail server that is down leaves the row standing,\nbecause \"we no longer hold it\" has to be true when it is read rather than\nmerely intended. handled_record is what is left: category, outcome, times, and\nnothing else. Its id is the report''s id, so a reference somebody kept still\nresolves after the report itself is gone.\n\nThe child-sexual category sets hold_until a year out and the delete path refuses\nwhile it stands. Releasing it is a separate manual call: a year is long enough\nthat a scheduled job quietly deleting evidence is the worse failure.\n\nCategoryGuides is the operator''s copy of the routing — what to do, in order, so\na report at two in the morning does not depend on remembering. Deliberately not\nthe same text /resources publishes, which tells a reporter who they can contact\nthemselves.\n\nThe BFF gains a cms route beside the other four. Its public intake never comes\nthrough there; this is only the desk.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c05ca683267f1f06e6db56ceecb48e71968ddd78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/c05ca683267f1f06e6db56ceecb48e71968ddd78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/cda4f9271e73a29b5759dc591aac65819cd5c0ac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/cda4f9271e73a29b5759dc591aac65819cd5c0ac","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGNkYTRmOTI3MWU3M2EyOWI1NzU5ZGM1OTFhYWM2NTgxOWNkNWMwYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/b590db44a3d4c48731a09b57270a58d93634f2da","sha":"b590db44a3d4c48731a09b57270a58d93634f2da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/b590db44a3d4c48731a09b57270a58d93634f2da"}],"sha":"cda4f9271e73a29b5759dc591aac65819cd5c0ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/cda4f9271e73a29b5759dc591aac65819cd5c0ac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/b590db44a3d4c48731a09b57270a58d93634f2da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T03:21:28Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T03:21:28Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Two intakes, a category on each, and a weekly note about the backups\n\nThe site publishes no address now, so this service is the whole contact surface.\n/reports takes the report as pasted text rather than an uploaded file — the app\ncopies it and opens the form, so there is no file input left to hand a photograph\nto — and every report carries a category, which is the only thing that decides\nwhere it is taken. /messages is new: product, category, title, description, and an\nemail address that is optional because somebody who leaves none has said they do\nnot want an answer.\n\nreporter_description is gone. The reporter''s account is written in the app, where\nthey can still see the message, and it arrives inside the report they paste. Two\nboxes asking one question collected two answers and nothing said which was meant.\n\nCategoryTest pins both slug lists, because outpost-site posts them and no compiler\njoins the two repositories.\n\npg-backup-report mails once a week saying whether the nightly dumps happened —\nnames, sizes, checksums, and a subject that shouts when the newest is over 26h\nold. It does not attach the dump: pg_dumpall carries every role password, and\nsince this service exists it also carries every abuse report and every reporter''s\naddress, which is exactly what should not be sitting in an inbox.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8f443fb565e5f7a1921a021358e92389acd04fb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/8f443fb565e5f7a1921a021358e92389acd04fb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/b590db44a3d4c48731a09b57270a58d93634f2da","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/b590db44a3d4c48731a09b57270a58d93634f2da","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGI1OTBkYjQ0YTNkNGM0ODczMWEwOWI1NzI3MGE1OGQ5MzYzNGYyZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/eadd5e279ad54a6fb0ce8a7a3c51d312535d30d7","sha":"eadd5e279ad54a6fb0ce8a7a3c51d312535d30d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/eadd5e279ad54a6fb0ce8a7a3c51d312535d30d7"}],"sha":"b590db44a3d4c48731a09b57270a58d93634f2da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/b590db44a3d4c48731a09b57270a58d93634f2da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/eadd5e279ad54a6fb0ce8a7a3c51d312535d30d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T23:28:35Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T23:28:35Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Add microgpt-comms: abuse intake that refuses anything but a report\n\noutpostmessaging.com publishes an abuse address, and a published address can be\nsent a picture. The app''s own report is text with no field for media, so the one\nway media could arrive was somebody mailing it — which would leave the operator\nholding material they are not equipped to hold.\n\nA form and a service replace that. POST /reports takes the report the app wrote\nand the reporter''s own words, verifies the upload, stores it in cms-db and mails\nabuse@outpostmessaging.com.\n\nThe verification is over the bytes, not the content type or the extension, because\nboth of those are whatever the browser was told. ReportParser decodes strict UTF-8\nand refuses control characters, which is where a JPEG, a PNG, a PDF, a zip and a\nvideo all die — a PDF opens with readable ASCII, so a check on the first bytes\nalone would have let one through. What survives that must then carry the app''s\nlabelled lines with a 64-hex fingerprint, a 6-hex short code, two parseable\ntimestamps and one of exactly two kind phrases. Eighteen tests, written from\nAbuseReport.body in the app rather than from the regexes, so a change to the app''s\nwording fails them rather than quietly widening what is accepted.\n\nAt least one contact field is required. Which one is the reporter''s choice: a\nphone suits somebody who does not want to write, an address somebody with no\nphone, and insisting on email would turn a safety form into an account.\n\nMail is best-effort and outside the transaction — a relay that is down must not\ncost somebody their report. notified_at stays null when it fails, which is what\nmakes an unsent one findable.\n\nPOST is open to anyone; there is no GET at all. Somebody reporting abuse is often\nsomebody who wants less to do with this app rather than more, and a sign-in in\nfront of that screen is a barrier where there must not be one.\n\nDEPLOY.md has the psql for the database — init-db.sh only runs on an empty volume\n— the env vars to fill in, the nginx block and a curl that proves an image is\nrefused before the service is trusted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6fe8a2be911002490e08355077cea4e32a8ce270","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/6fe8a2be911002490e08355077cea4e32a8ce270"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/eadd5e279ad54a6fb0ce8a7a3c51d312535d30d7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/eadd5e279ad54a6fb0ce8a7a3c51d312535d30d7","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGVhZGQ1ZTI3OWFkNTRhNmZiMGNlOGE3YTNjNTFkMzEyNTM1ZDMwZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/764e432cee8d0b337205eeb3f438eebe1bddf0e0","sha":"764e432cee8d0b337205eeb3f438eebe1bddf0e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/764e432cee8d0b337205eeb3f438eebe1bddf0e0"}],"sha":"eadd5e279ad54a6fb0ce8a7a3c51d312535d30d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/eadd5e279ad54a6fb0ce8a7a3c51d312535d30d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/764e432cee8d0b337205eeb3f438eebe1bddf0e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:14:46Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:14:46Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Phase 5 on the page, and the defaults settled\n\n4.1: the board opens on temporal aa only, render scale 100%, fast grass\noff — which is where it already was, because the two switches that buy\nframes are the two you said to leave alone, and everything else spends\none. 60 fps is not reachable at 100% with PBR grass; 27.9 ms is the\nfloor, and the levers that move it are in the menu for whoever wants\nthem.\n\nBOARD-PLAN, PLAN and BOARD-HANDOFF gain Phase 5 and the two findings\nworth carrying: pcf-at-low-quality emits invalid WGSL on 9.26, and a\npage-side console hook cannot see WebGPU validation errors at all.\nboard-plan.html gains the phase and three new asks — FSR1, IBL shadows,\ndepth peeling. Version 22.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c541cb5b614cc3564d718e6d632569f5fbcee08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/9c541cb5b614cc3564d718e6d632569f5fbcee08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/764e432cee8d0b337205eeb3f438eebe1bddf0e0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/764e432cee8d0b337205eeb3f438eebe1bddf0e0","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDc2NGU0MzJjZWU4ZDBiMzM3MjA1ZWViM2Y0MzhlZWJlMWJkZGYwZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/bc570fa1094bd3fe8880f443fabc9d0800b4de56","sha":"bc570fa1094bd3fe8880f443fabc9d0800b4de56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/bc570fa1094bd3fe8880f443fabc9d0800b4de56"}],"sha":"764e432cee8d0b337205eeb3f438eebe1bddf0e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/764e432cee8d0b337205eeb3f438eebe1bddf0e0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/bc570fa1094bd3fe8880f443fabc9d0800b4de56/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:12:21Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T02:12:28Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"A capability document, and every knob it found put on the panel\n\nGRAPHICS.md is the survey the work was missing: what the meadow actually\ndraws pass by pass, every knob the board already exposes, every constant\nit hardcodes that could be one, and what Babylon 9.26 has that this board\ndoes not use — each checked against node_modules and cited by path, so\nthe next reader can check it rather than believe it. It ends with seven\nordered batches.\n\nBatches A and B are in. The graphics menu is now a declarative table in\ngraphics.ts: six banks, 53 settings, each a switch, a pick or a dial with\nits own note saying what it does and what it breaks, persisted per key,\nwith a reset. Nothing new is on by default — the board opens exactly as\nit did.\n\n  edges          temporal aa + samples + blend + while-moving, msaa, fxaa\n  light and shade  occlusion, god rays, grass shadows, shadow map size,\n                   cascades, filter, filter quality, cascade blend,\n                   darkness, depth-fitted cascades, sky light\n  the grade      tone mapping (none/standard/aces/neutral), exposure,\n                 contrast, vignette, white balance + temperature + tint,\n                 dither, bloom + threshold + strength + spread, glow\n                 layer + strength, grain, sharpen, chromatic aberration\n  air and lens   fog (linear/exp/exp2) + density, depth of field +\n                 quality + focus + aperture + lens size\n  the field      fast grass + lit, leaf cut-out, leaf roughness, ground\n                 relief, anisotropy\n  resolution     render scale\n\nStage stops owning the grade: exposure, contrast and vignette are trims\nthe menu writes and regrade() applies, so the clock and the sliders stop\nfighting over the same three numbers.\n\nEvery one of the 106 reachable knob values was swept on a fresh browser\nwith the board''s triangle count read after each, and one is broken:\n**pcf at low quality emits invalid WGSL** on Babylon 9.26 —\ncomputeShadowWithCSMPCF1 is called with an empty argument where\nshadowTexture0 should be. It is guarded to medium and the control says\nso. Nothing else faulted and the board never stopped drawing.\n\nThe instrument that found it matters as much: a console.warn wrapper\ninstalled in the page sees none of this and reported all 53 clean. WebGPU\nuncaptured errors reach the CDP console and not the page''s console\nobject, so the sweep marks each knob with a console.log and attributes\nfaults from the raw CDP stream between marks. tools/chrome-probe.mjs\ngains RAW_LOGS for that.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"032d839f245297b6416a2cb658256f504f631b95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/032d839f245297b6416a2cb658256f504f631b95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/bc570fa1094bd3fe8880f443fabc9d0800b4de56","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/bc570fa1094bd3fe8880f443fabc9d0800b4de56","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGJjNTcwZmExMDk0YmQzZmU4ODgwZjQ0M2ZhYmM5ZDA4MDBiNGRlNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/d26e92aad71547051db2688eb86f4fb83b36adee","sha":"d26e92aad71547051db2688eb86f4fb83b36adee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/d26e92aad71547051db2688eb86f4fb83b36adee"}],"sha":"bc570fa1094bd3fe8880f443fabc9d0800b4de56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/bc570fa1094bd3fe8880f443fabc9d0800b4de56"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/d26e92aad71547051db2688eb86f4fb83b36adee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:42:26Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:42:26Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The docs and the page follow 2.1 and 2.2 into the menu\n\nPhase 2 closes with them. BOARD-PLAN''s Next now says what is actually\nopen — the defaults, where render scale starts to look soft, and the\nshadowProxy threshold that still misses the searsia parts. PLAN.md\ncarries the full record for both: the three passes it took to match PBR''s\nlook and the instrument that found each gap, the two traps (ShaderMaterial\npushing world0..3 itself, and half being a WGSL reserved word), and the\nrender-scale table with the finding that resolution is not linear in\npixels here, which corrects an older note that said it was.\n\nboard-plan.html gets both as settings, a 2.2b for the flora work that had\nbeen filed under 2.2 by mistake, and an ask that is now a real choice\nrather than a question: fast grass matched, no sheen, or off. Version 21.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5e5433484519c300c369174645d2f328d44b807e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/5e5433484519c300c369174645d2f328d44b807e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/d26e92aad71547051db2688eb86f4fb83b36adee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/d26e92aad71547051db2688eb86f4fb83b36adee","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGQyNmU5MmFhZDcxNTQ3MDUxZGIyNjg4ZWI4NmY0ZmI4M2IzNmFkZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/eecbbfc2ae4c9cd3f50cc3168f85bca396c4af0b","sha":"eecbbfc2ae4c9cd3f50cc3168f85bca396c4af0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/eecbbfc2ae4c9cd3f50cc3168f85bca396c4af0b"}],"sha":"d26e92aad71547051db2688eb86f4fb83b36adee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/d26e92aad71547051db2688eb86f4fb83b36adee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/eecbbfc2ae4c9cd3f50cc3168f85bca396c4af0b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:39:37Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:39:37Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"2.2 passes: a grass shader written for the grass gives 3.2 ms back\n\nThe only switch in the menu that returns a frame instead of spending\none. grass-fast.ts swaps the four grass materials off PBR onto a\nShaderMaterial that does exactly what the grass needs: one texture read,\nan alpha test, a sun, a bounce, a hemisphere and one GGX highlight. The\nwind, the leaf-normal blend, the per-plant tint and the base-to-tip ramp\nare the plugin''s WGSL carried over verbatim, so the geometry and the\nmotion are the same field.\n\nMeasured at 3600 x 2026, play camera, noon, wind stopped, fresh browser,\nbracketed either side, two passes over a 27.9 ms frame:\n\n  PBR                   27.9 ms\n  fast, matched         24.5 / 25.0   -3.0 to -3.4\n  fast, no sheen        24.0 / 24.4   -3.6 to -4.0\n\nThe bar was 1.5 ms saved. The old note in PLAN.md put the ceiling for any\ncheaper grass material at 2.0 ms, measured as unlit PBR — that measured\nPBR''s fragment shader short-circuiting while its vertex shader and every\nvarying stayed. This board runs about 40M vertex invocations a frame on\nthe grass alone, and that is where most of the 3.2 comes from.\n\nMatching the look took three passes and the pixel instrument found each\ngap. Diffuse-only was right in red and green and missing 40% of the blue:\nPBR''s specular is where the sky''s blue reaches a green field, and\nspecularIntensity = 0 on the PBR arm reproduced the fast arm exactly\n(blue 12.6 to 7.3 against 7.7). A Blinn lobe recovered a third of it; the\nreal GGX with Smith visibility and a Schlick rim closed it to R 0.996 /\nG 1.019 / B 0.887. The sheen is 1.7 ms of the 4.8, so it is a select.\n\nIt cannot receive the shadow map, so fast grass and grass shadows now\nturn each other off rather than one silently doing nothing.\n\nAlso 2.1: render scale is measured across its five steps, and it is not\nlinear in pixels. 7.29 MP 27.9 ms, 5.27 25.3, 4.10 23.1, 2.62 20.9,\n1.82 19.1 — a quarter of the pixels for 31% of the frame, because the\nvertex work, the culling and the shadow map do not scale with resolution.\n\nwgsl-lint gains the reserved words it was missing, half among them, which\nis what this shader tripped over first. The other trap was Babylon''s own:\nShaderMaterial pushes world0..world3 itself when instances are on, so\nlisting them in options.attributes duplicates shader location 4 and the\npipeline is refused as a warning while the board reads 60 fps drawing no\ngrass at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"533b18a5d80bf154541b14e9fdf1cd7f1003eda6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/533b18a5d80bf154541b14e9fdf1cd7f1003eda6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/eecbbfc2ae4c9cd3f50cc3168f85bca396c4af0b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/eecbbfc2ae4c9cd3f50cc3168f85bca396c4af0b","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGVlY2JiZmMyYWU0YzljZDNmNTBjYzMxNjhmODViY2EzOTZjNGFmMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/e79409552856d71ba21f861728a6b39a9b3d9ca9","sha":"e79409552856d71ba21f861728a6b39a9b3d9ca9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/e79409552856d71ba21f861728a6b39a9b3d9ca9"}],"sha":"eecbbfc2ae4c9cd3f50cc3168f85bca396c4af0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/eecbbfc2ae4c9cd3f50cc3168f85bca396c4af0b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/e79409552856d71ba21f861728a6b39a9b3d9ca9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:38:54Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:38:54Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Phase 3 closed as settings, Phase 4 is the menu, and the docs say so\n\nThe instruction was to stop rejecting and build a menu instead, so the\nplan now carries that as a standing rule and the refused table is the\npriced table: priced is not refused, and anything that works and only\ncosts too much for this machine is a switch with its number beside it.\n\nBOARD-PLAN.md gains a Next line at the top and a Phase 4 for the menu,\nand its Phase 3 rows are rewritten with what each one actually cost.\nPLAN.md gains the full record — the sky NaN and where the patch has to\ngo, the excludedMeshes answer (18.5 of 26.9 ms), the god-ray render list,\nthe proxy that was the acne, and the two instrument faults found on the\nway: a g-buffer that outlives its pipeline, and a probe that reached past\nthe UI and measured something the UI does not do. BOARD-HANDOFF.md''s 4g\nand its plan section are settled.\n\nboard-plan.html moves with them: Phase 4, a setting state, and three new\nasks in Next up — which switches the board should open with, where render\nscale starts to soften, and whether 2.2 is worth taking. Published as\nVersion 20.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c35478d20a7e3556ef10b5e67325cbee03434ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/6c35478d20a7e3556ef10b5e67325cbee03434ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/e79409552856d71ba21f861728a6b39a9b3d9ca9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/e79409552856d71ba21f861728a6b39a9b3d9ca9","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGU3OTQwOTU1Mjg1NmQ3MWJhMjFmODYxNzI4YTZiMzlhOWIzZDljYTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/6995839a66b780adeda397fd7f5a61775ddd1aa3","sha":"6995839a66b780adeda397fd7f5a61775ddd1aa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/6995839a66b780adeda397fd7f5a61775ddd1aa3"}],"sha":"e79409552856d71ba21f861728a6b39a9b3d9ca9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/e79409552856d71ba21f861728a6b39a9b3d9ca9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/6995839a66b780adeda397fd7f5a61775ddd1aa3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:32:41Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:32:41Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"A graphics menu, and the three refused effects built as settings in it\n\nNothing is refused any more. SSAO2, god rays and grass shadows all work,\nall cost more than a frame can spare on this machine, and all three are\nnow toggles in a graphics menu with their measured price beside them.\n\neffects.ts holds the three. SSAO2 gets the sky mask the forum fix calls\nfor, patched into the WGSL at the shader store rather than worked around:\nthe prepass normal is (0,0,0) on the sky, normalize() of that is NaN, and\nWGSL propagates it where WebGL drivers did not. The g-buffer takes an\nexplicit render list, which is the excludedMeshes question the handoff\nleft untested — measured, the grass in that buffer is 18.5 ms of the\n26.9, and leaving it out takes most of what you can see with it, so the\nchoice is a select rather than a decision.\n\nGod rays get a real sun disc on a hidden layer plus an occluder render\nlist of the disc, the terrain, the trees and the stone. That is the whole\ndifference from the attempt that flooded white: the sky box was standing\nin for the light, and a sky is not an object.\n\nGrass shadows: the acne was never the depth bias, it was the lifted proxy\nstanding at grass height shadowing every blade beneath it. Dropped from\nthe casters while the grass receives, the field takes tree shadows\ncleanly and gives up its own shadow on the road; that too is a select.\n\nMeasured at 3600 x 2026, play camera, noon, wind stopped, over a 28.1 ms\nframe, two passes each:\n\n  temporal aa                     +1.8 ms   (the only thing on by default)\n  msaa x2                         +4.6\n  ambient occlusion, ground only  +8.4\n  ambient occlusion, grass too    +26.9\n  god rays                        +4.6\n  grass shadows                   +8.3\n  bloom                           +1.6\n\nRender scale joins them at 100 / 85 / 75 / 60 / 50, and split frame now\nmeasures whichever of these are on, so the numbers above are this\nmachine''s rather than the answer.\n\ntaa and bloom moved out of the show row into the menu, where they belong.\nThe g-buffer is disposed when occlusion goes off — left alive it renders\nevery frame for nothing, which is what made the first reading say 4.4 ms.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f3eba7090c743daaabea8ee7791482ab74c3e7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/4f3eba7090c743daaabea8ee7791482ab74c3e7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/6995839a66b780adeda397fd7f5a61775ddd1aa3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/6995839a66b780adeda397fd7f5a61775ddd1aa3","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDY5OTU4MzlhNjZiNzgwYWRlZGEzOTdmZDdmNWE2MTc3NWRkZDFhYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/d49a4ee5ebcf453b8cab2df4cc67d330497f8a44","sha":"d49a4ee5ebcf453b8cab2df4cc67d330497f8a44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/d49a4ee5ebcf453b8cab2df4cc67d330497f8a44"}],"sha":"6995839a66b780adeda397fd7f5a61775ddd1aa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/6995839a66b780adeda397fd7f5a61775ddd1aa3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/d49a4ee5ebcf453b8cab2df4cc67d330497f8a44/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T22:38:42Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T22:38:42Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"3.1 refused: MSAA costs 9.4 ms, and it only exists through TAA\n\nSwept taa.msaaSamples live, camera static, wind stopped, play camera, 7.29 MP.\nedge is mean neighbour difference in green — lower is smoother; crawl is mean\npixel change between consecutive frames.\n\n                        frame     edge    crawl\n  TAA on,  samples 1    31.1 ms   17.96   0.962\n  TAA on,  samples 2    40.5      17.66   0.696\n  TAA on,  samples 4    40.5      17.50   0.625\n  TAA off, samples 1    29.4      22.35   0\n  TAA off, samples 2    29.5      22.35   0\n  TAA off, samples 4    29.3      22.35   0\n\nTwo samples costs 9.4 ms against a 2 ms bar. Four is no worse than two, so the\ncost is the multisampled target, not the resolve.\n\nAnd the mechanism is not what I claimed when researching this. taa.msaaSamples\nis not the modern spelling of pipeline.samples: it sets the sample count on the\nTAA post-process''s target, so with TAA disabled it does nothing whatsoever —\nsamples 1, 2 and 4 give a byte-identical frame and an identical 22.35 edge.\nMSAA on this board exists only through the TAA pass.\n\nWhat it buys where it works is small: edge 17.96 to 17.66 and 0.89 mean out of\n255 across the frame, barely above the 0.5 TAA noise floor. Crawl does fall\n0.962 to 0.696, so it helps temporal stability — not by nine milliseconds.\n\n3.2 is therefore blocked on cost rather than on capability:\nengine.setAlphaToCoverage(true) exists on the WebGPU engine, but the only route\nto samples above 1 here is 3.1''s 9.4 ms.\n\nTAA is carrying the anti-aliasing: turning it off raises edge contrast from\n17.96 to 22.35.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87406368bb258cb55392575dca6f29850e0ee494","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/87406368bb258cb55392575dca6f29850e0ee494"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/d49a4ee5ebcf453b8cab2df4cc67d330497f8a44","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/d49a4ee5ebcf453b8cab2df4cc67d330497f8a44","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGQ0OWE0ZWU1ZWJjZjQ1M2I4Y2FiMmRmNGNjNjdkMzMwNDk3ZjhhNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/62470e6eb896b6aa4c6e6654cca238e736ff7f39","sha":"62470e6eb896b6aa4c6e6654cca238e736ff7f39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/62470e6eb896b6aa4c6e6654cca238e736ff7f39"}],"sha":"d49a4ee5ebcf453b8cab2df4cc67d330497f8a44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/d49a4ee5ebcf453b8cab2df4cc67d330497f8a44"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/62470e6eb896b6aa4c6e6654cca238e736ff7f39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:38:10Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:38:10Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Pull the quiver trees down and look at them: a different plant, not a cheaper tree\n\nBoth downloaded and judged in the Assets panel, which grew a candidates shelf\nfor the purpose — an asset listed with count: 0, previewable from all four\nstops, placed nowhere.\n\n  quiver_tree_01   2.72 m   150,124 tris   a bare pole with a small tuft on top\n  quiver_tree_02   1.47 m    82,074 tris   a squat aloe, reads as a palm\n  island_tree_02   3.41 m 1,072,213 tris   a broadleaf with a spreading canopy\n\nAloidendron dichotomum is a succulent: smooth pale trunk, dichotomous fork,\naloe rosettes where a canopy would be. In a green meadow they read as desert\npalms. Refused on the look, as expected.\n\nTwo useful facts from the trip: neither has an alpha map — only diff, arm and\nnor, with an OPAQUE glTF material, because the rosettes are real geometry and\nnot cut-out cards, which is also why 82k triangles covers a whole plant. And\nPoly Haven''s download URLs answer urllib with a 403 and want a browser user\nagent; curl -L -A \"Mozilla/5.0\" works.\n\nFiles kept under assets/board/models (6.3 MB the pair) so the judgement can be\nre-run without downloading again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6723897883fc5681e74e3df4788ee67e7632a7f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/6723897883fc5681e74e3df4788ee67e7632a7f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/62470e6eb896b6aa4c6e6654cca238e736ff7f39","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/62470e6eb896b6aa4c6e6654cca238e736ff7f39","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDYyNDcwZTZlYjg5NmI2YWE0YzZlNjY1NGNjYTIzOGU3MzZmZjdmMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/26c6c8602c1439bfd38d3e2849572e49ddb3f2da","sha":"26c6c8602c1439bfd38d3e2849572e49ddb3f2da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/26c6c8602c1439bfd38d3e2849572e49ddb3f2da"}],"sha":"62470e6eb896b6aa4c6e6654cca238e736ff7f39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/62470e6eb896b6aa4c6e6654cca238e736ff7f39"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/26c6c8602c1439bfd38d3e2849572e49ddb3f2da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:13:05Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:13:05Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Research: there is no lighter version of this tree at Poly Haven\n\nTheir 1k/2k/4k/8k tiers are texture resolution only — all four glTF entries\nshare one 40.7 MB geometry binary — and the file is a single LOD0 node with no\nLOD chain.\n\nTriangle counts read from the glTF accessors:\n\n  quiver_tree_02          82,074   13x lighter than the board''s tree\n  othonna_cerarioides    118,149   but that is seven plants, ~17k each\n  quiver_tree_01         150,124\n  island_tree_02       1,072,213   current: trunk 27k, leaves 715k, branches 330k\n  island_tree_01       1,599,403\n  island_tree_03            ~2.1M\n  jacaranda_tree            ~5.5M\n  fir_tree_01              ~12.6M\n  pine_tree_01               ~25M\n\nSo the only light trees they have are quiver trees, which are desert\nsucculents — a different plant, not a cheaper version of the same one.\n\nOff Poly Haven, CC0 at low triangle counts is stylised low-poly, which is the\nwrong object on a board whose grass is photographs.\n\nThe route that keeps this tree is offline QEM decimation of the branches\nprimitive alone — 330,171 triangles of solid twig geometry, which QEM handles\nwell — leaving the leaf cards untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bf6fd6305dff558a584d81c0c654854bcc9a7f0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/bf6fd6305dff558a584d81c0c654854bcc9a7f0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/26c6c8602c1439bfd38d3e2849572e49ddb3f2da","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/26c6c8602c1439bfd38d3e2849572e49ddb3f2da","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDI2YzZjODYwMmMxNDM5YmZkMzhkM2UyODQ5NTcyZTQ5ZGRiM2YyZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/80c24268be09d5dccba78287e9c049fb062e5634","sha":"80c24268be09d5dccba78287e9c049fb062e5634","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/80c24268be09d5dccba78287e9c049fb062e5634"}],"sha":"26c6c8602c1439bfd38d3e2849572e49ddb3f2da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/26c6c8602c1439bfd38d3e2849572e49ddb3f2da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/80c24268be09d5dccba78287e9c049fb062e5634/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:02:16Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:02:16Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"2.5 closed: refused to the asset, with every renderer lever measured\n\nThe scans cost 4.2 ms at the play camera, split by swapping the shadow caster\nlist and the meshes independently: shadow pass 1.1, camera pass 3.6.\n\nFour levers tried, none of them the answer:\n\n  Not fill. At a camera where the whole board is 3.75% of the view and the\n  scans are a few dozen pixels, they still cost 2.4 ms. At the play camera they\n  draw 0.4% of the screen — green 35.58 with, 35.95 without.\n\n  Not the material. One-sided lighting 33.0, back-face culling on 32.8, against\n  32.9. material.freeze() is 2.4 ms worse.\n\n  Only half is triangle count. Thinning the indices 7x, 4,224,480 to 620,023,\n  recovers 1.9 ms of the 3.6.\n\n  And thinning destroys the tree: at 25% kept it has lost most of its leaves,\n  at 12% it is a bare skeleton. On a photogrammetry canopy the leaves are the\n  triangles, so hash-thinning removes foliage rather than detail. Refused on\n  the picture, not the number.\n\nisland_tree_02.gltf is a single LOD0 node with no LOD chain: trunk 27,298,\nleaves 714,744, branches 330,171 — 1,072,213 triangles for a 3.4 m plant that\ncovers a few hundred pixels here. Same conclusion as the pale rosette: the fix\nbelongs in the asset.\n\nLeft open and untested: shadowProxy only fires over 200,000 triangles and the\nsearsia parts are 113,405, 77,603 and 27,701, so all the scrub still casts at\nfull resolution.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5eeeecad3ecfe916f3e875cc4c1559aadae1ff36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/5eeeecad3ecfe916f3e875cc4c1559aadae1ff36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/80c24268be09d5dccba78287e9c049fb062e5634","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/80c24268be09d5dccba78287e9c049fb062e5634","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDgwYzI0MjY4YmUwOWQ1ZGNjYmE3ODI4N2U5YzA0OWZiMDYyZTU2MzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/a437257c0b6173b33e188b14ef8d74098b058c08","sha":"a437257c0b6173b33e188b14ef8d74098b058c08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a437257c0b6173b33e188b14ef8d74098b058c08"}],"sha":"80c24268be09d5dccba78287e9c049fb062e5634","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/80c24268be09d5dccba78287e9c049fb062e5634"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a437257c0b6173b33e188b14ef8d74098b058c08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T18:53:23Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T18:53:23Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"2.5 and 3.1: the findings, before either is touched\n\n2.5 — trees and scrub are vertex-bound, not fill-bound. Split by switching each\ngroup out, wind stopped, green coverage reported for every arm:\n\n                        play (r300)   far (r900)\n  everything              30.8 ms       20.7 ms\n  without the big tree    28.2          19.1\n  without the scrub       29.6          20.0\n  neither                 26.8          18.3\n  the scans cost          4.0           2.4\n\nThe far camera is the decisive one: the whole board is 3.75% of that view and\nthe scans are a few dozen pixels, yet they still cost 2.4 ms — sixty per cent\nof their play-camera cost. Green moves 35.58 to 35.95 with every scan removed,\nso at the play camera they draw 0.4% of the screen for 4.0 ms.\n\nThey submit 4,224,480 triangles a frame: island_tree_02 is 1,072,213 x 3, the\nsearsia parts 113,405 x 4, 77,603 x 5, 27,701 x 6.\n\n3.1 — MSAA is one line, not new plumbing. TAARenderingPipeline exposes\nmsaaSamples (default 1), which sets the TAA post process''s samples; that is the\nmodern spelling of pipeline.samples, and stage.ts already sets it to 1. The\n24 ms that refused MSAA came from antialias: true on the engine, which is\nswapchain MSAA over the whole chain. engine.setAlphaToCoverage(true) exists on\nthe WebGPU engine, so 3.2 unblocks as soon as samples go above 1.\n\nNeither is implemented; both plans are on the page for the call.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ca313ee1ad46448c0050add14103f81fc969a0ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/ca313ee1ad46448c0050add14103f81fc969a0ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/a437257c0b6173b33e188b14ef8d74098b058c08","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/a437257c0b6173b33e188b14ef8d74098b058c08","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGE0MzcyNTdjMGI2MTczYjMzZTE4OGIxNGVmOGQ3NDA5OGIwNThjMDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/80c31344c7a71683e6e862de5ba438da716daf60","sha":"80c31344c7a71683e6e862de5ba438da716daf60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/80c31344c7a71683e6e862de5ba438da716daf60"}],"sha":"a437257c0b6173b33e188b14ef8d74098b058c08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a437257c0b6173b33e188b14ef8d74098b058c08"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/80c31344c7a71683e6e862de5ba438da716daf60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T18:06:52Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T18:06:52Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The bald ground was the species lottery; a survey tool that reads the buffers\n\nI guessed twice and was wrong twice — first the wear field, then 1.4''s stature.\ntools/board-survey.mjs reads every species'' instance matrices out of the\nstorage buffers, bins them across the board, prints a density map, and takes\neight top-down tiles with bab.shot(). It answered in one run:\n\n  95 bins with no plants at all — every one wear 254 or 255. That is the road.\n  97 bins with no grass but other species present — every one wear 0.\n\ndriftAt clamps with (raw - 0.5) * 1.9 + 0.5, so any noise value under 0.237\nbecomes exactly zero — about a quarter of the board. A species'' weight is\nshare * drift^clumping * (clumping + 1), so where grass''s drift clamps to zero\nits weight is zero, relative is zero, and no grass is placed at all, while\nclover and plantain carry on from their own noise fields. Grass''s patch of\n0.012 is an 83 half-foot wavelength, so each of those regions is enormous.\n\nFixed with a per-species `hold`: the least of its slots a species keeps however\nthe competition goes, carried in the spare w of the kinds uniform. Grass holds\n0.72 as the matrix species, clover 0.18, plantain 0.12, Yorkshire fog 0.\n\nEmpty bins: grass 152 to 74, clover 215 to 75, plantain 305 to 80, and what is\nleft is the road. Grass placed 112,594 to 129,039. All eight top-down tiles\nshow continuous cover.\n\n2.6 is wired in. shadowProxy() decimates any caster over 200k triangles — the\ntop 3% by area plus a hashed 30% of the rest — on a shadow-only layer mask.\nCasters went 4.93M to 2.75M triangles, the big tree 1,072,213 to 344,691 across\nall three instances. It returns null rather than a proxy when the instance\ncount does not match: the first version copied one matrix instead of three and\nonly one tree cast a shadow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"168dcb999dbf22919c4a767fe16e14cf8a419e18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/168dcb999dbf22919c4a767fe16e14cf8a419e18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/80c31344c7a71683e6e862de5ba438da716daf60","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/80c31344c7a71683e6e862de5ba438da716daf60","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDgwYzMxMzQ0YzdhNzE2ODNlNmU4NjJkZTViYTQzOGRhNzE2ZGFmNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/618b80418d7b7fd37278ad696dad4cb02709d69b","sha":"618b80418d7b7fd37278ad696dad4cb02709d69b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/618b80418d7b7fd37278ad696dad4cb02709d69b"}],"sha":"80c31344c7a71683e6e862de5ba438da716daf60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/80c31344c7a71683e6e862de5ba438da716daf60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/618b80418d7b7fd37278ad696dad4cb02709d69b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T17:26:08Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T17:26:08Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Fix the bald patch, and cross off what was already settled\n\nThe bald patch is 1.4''s place field, far too strong, and reported from the\nboard rather than found by me. Three things compounded: placeA ran at a 77\nhalf-foot wavelength on a 440 x 300 board, so one low noise cell is an enormous\nregion; unmown floored at 0.56 of height while alive separately took 0.80 in\nthe same places, and grow multiplies by alive, so effective height was 0.45 at\n20% fewer plants; and those short plants still carry 1.1e''s lean of 0.90, so\nthey read as a flat mat.\n\nNow three octaves weighted 0.42/0.34/0.24 so the structure is patchy rather\nthan one swell, unmown floors at 0.82, trodden takes 30% instead of 48%, and\nalive follows place only between 0.94 and 1.06. Verified on the whole board\nfrom above with bab.shot().\n\nThe plan page was still asking for decisions the user had already made. 1.1d is\nsettled at 50% and 1.1f at 300%, both ticked; the queue is now \"Next up\" and\nsays nothing is waiting on them. The headline numbers were also stale — 21.5 ms\nand 230,937 plants against the board''s actual 31.25 and 481,740 — and the frame\nbar now carries the GPU passes the HUD reports.\n\nThree standing rules added, one per thing that went wrong today:\n\n  - Kill every background task before the turn ends.\n  - A decision is crossed off in the same turn it is made.\n  - Photograph the whole board after any change to the compute pass; a\n    field-scale bug is invisible at the play camera and at close range, which\n    is where every shot of 1.4 was.\n\npage-check matched text case-sensitively and missed a line the CSS uppercases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fb57b51155d0f9718134db3316460cef4680a629","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/fb57b51155d0f9718134db3316460cef4680a629"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/618b80418d7b7fd37278ad696dad4cb02709d69b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/618b80418d7b7fd37278ad696dad4cb02709d69b","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDYxOGI4MDQxOGQ3YjdmZDM3Mjc4YWQ2OTZkYWQ0Y2IwMjcwOWQ2OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/5aa71ea87603422550f3692d78c4378cbc1500f3","sha":"5aa71ea87603422550f3692d78c4378cbc1500f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/5aa71ea87603422550f3692d78c4378cbc1500f3"}],"sha":"618b80418d7b7fd37278ad696dad4cb02709d69b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/618b80418d7b7fd37278ad696dad4cb02709d69b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/5aa71ea87603422550f3692d78c4378cbc1500f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T16:55:24Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T16:55:24Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Every screenshot of this board had a 0.5/255 noise floor under it\n\nThe board runs TAA at 16 samples with a 0.16 blend, which jitters the\nprojection matrix a fraction of a pixel every frame. On grass — nothing but\nhigh-frequency edges — that moves a great many pixels. With the camera\nbyte-for-byte static, the wind stopped and nothing in the scene changing:\n\n  single frames, TAA on      0.514 mean / 57 max\n  mean of 24 frames, TAA on  0.136 / 10\n  single frames, TAA off     0.000 / 0\n\nThat floor was never subtracted from any image comparison in PLAN.md. The\ncasualty: \"card and twist are 0.78 mean apart\" was measuring the jitter. The\nconclusion still stands, because the 45% blend reading (5.35) and the blend-off\nreading (6.31) are an order of magnitude clear of the floor — but the 0.78\nmeant nothing. The shadow-proxy readings are two to three times the floor and\nwant re-running.\n\nbab.shot(width) is the fix: it switches the jitter off, stops the wind, waits\nfour frames, grabs, and restores both in a finally. Three consecutive calls\nreturn byte-identical PNGs. Stage gained jitter(on)/jittering().\n\nThe camera was never drifting. alpha, beta, radius and the view matrix are\nidentical across grabs; only the projection matrix changes, in elements 8 and 9,\nwhich is where the jitter offset lives. The diagnostic that appeared to show the\nboard resetting the camera was itself wrong — it set alpha before setTarget, and\nArcRotateCamera.setTarget recomputes the angles from position.\n\nboard-measure carries all of it now, plus the rule that every A/B must report a\nliveness signal for both arms: three times this session an arm that drew nothing\nread as a large saving.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"34be3691f9e6dbb310e507a03a19cf66a3f3c3ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/34be3691f9e6dbb310e507a03a19cf66a3f3c3ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/5aa71ea87603422550f3692d78c4378cbc1500f3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/5aa71ea87603422550f3692d78c4378cbc1500f3","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDVhYTcxZWE4NzYwMzQyMjU1MGYzNjkyZDc4YzQzNzhjYmMxNTAwZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/dadfb3c1740e584a1670dc69ed6b4bb337844580","sha":"dadfb3c1740e584a1670dc69ed6b4bb337844580","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/dadfb3c1740e584a1670dc69ed6b4bb337844580"}],"sha":"5aa71ea87603422550f3692d78c4378cbc1500f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/5aa71ea87603422550f3692d78c4378cbc1500f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/dadfb3c1740e584a1670dc69ed6b4bb337844580/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T16:04:45Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T16:04:45Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Grass, not sward; leaf normal at 50% and wind at 300%\n\nResting values chosen on the board: leaf normal 50%, which lets a little\nper-blade colour and texture through instead of shading every blade by the\nground it stands on, and wind 300%, because below that it does not read as\nwind at all.\n\nBoth were also broken: setLeafNormal and setWind were only called from\nsetShape, which went away with the card and blade switch, so neither default\nreached the meadow at startup. They are applied after grow() now.\n\n\"Sward\" is gone from the code — it is grass everywhere, including\nswardLattice, SWARD_FADE_*, swardColor, swardProxy, the mesh names and the\npart toggle. lab/sward-patch.ts is lab/grass-patch.ts. The HUD says grass\nrather than twist.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"68a71da18bd84d67ff3f734426774f7e3fdbacaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/68a71da18bd84d67ff3f734426774f7e3fdbacaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/dadfb3c1740e584a1670dc69ed6b4bb337844580","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/dadfb3c1740e584a1670dc69ed6b4bb337844580","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGRhZGZiM2MxNzQwZTU4NGExNjcwZGM2OWVkNmI0YmIzMzc4NDQ1ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/54941e2e8bee7071209f8c763053927a579a6325","sha":"54941e2e8bee7071209f8c763053927a579a6325","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/54941e2e8bee7071209f8c763053927a579a6325"}],"sha":"dadfb3c1740e584a1670dc69ed6b4bb337844580","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/dadfb3c1740e584a1670dc69ed6b4bb337844580"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/54941e2e8bee7071209f8c763053927a579a6325/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:00:54Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:00:54Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Cross the twist decision into the plan page, and drop the blade''s lab row\n\npage-check caught that the markdown had the decision and the HTML did not,\nwhich is the first thing it has been useful for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6120afc8aa1faccfd232c37b247a99da879ae25a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/6120afc8aa1faccfd232c37b247a99da879ae25a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/54941e2e8bee7071209f8c763053927a579a6325","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/54941e2e8bee7071209f8c763053927a579a6325","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDU0OTQxZTJlOGJlZTcwNzEyMDlmOGM3NjMwNTM5MjdhNTc5YTYzMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/a395d5818e281fe7ef547241042c5bc1a3372627","sha":"a395d5818e281fe7ef547241042c5bc1a3372627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a395d5818e281fe7ef547241042c5bc1a3372627"}],"sha":"54941e2e8bee7071209f8c763053927a579a6325","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/54941e2e8bee7071209f8c763053927a579a6325"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a395d5818e281fe7ef547241042c5bc1a3372627/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:00:10Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T15:00:10Z","email":"grifftatarsky@gmail.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The sward is the twist, and the other two are gone\n\nDecided on the board: the twist runs about five frames ahead of cards and far\nahead of blades, and the blade no longer carried the extra fidelity to justify\nitself once the cards were leaned over and given nine a plant.\n\nRemoved rather than left switchable:\n\n  - blade-geometry.ts and lab/blade.ts deleted, with the lab''s entry.\n  - EDGE_FAN in foliage-cards.ts is tan(0.3pi) now, not 0.3 — so cardGeometry\n    *is* the twist and there is no second path. LeafShape, CARD_SHAPE,\n    cardShape(fan) and the `leaf` override existed only so blades could be\n    swapped in, and are gone with the helper exports that only\n    blade-geometry imported.\n  - The board''s Shape type, sward switch, grown map, setShape and resowing\n    signal are gone; grow() takes no argument.\n\nAlso fixes the plan page, which I published blank. An unescaped class=\"mono\"\ninside a double-quoted string ended the string early and killed the whole\n<script>, so nothing rendered at all.\n\nTwo checks had been reporting green while checking nothing:\n\n  - wgsl-lint with no arguments linted no files and printed \"wgsl clean\".\n  - The plan page''s \"js parses\" check sliced from indexOf(\"const PLAN\"), and\n    there is no const PLAN in that file — indexOf returned -1, the slice came\n    back empty, and an empty string always parses.\n\ntools/page-check.mjs replaces the second: it loads the page in the browser,\ncounts rendered items, and fails on console errors or missing text. The plan\npage now opens with a \"Waiting on you\" block carrying each open decision, its\noptions and its measured cost, instead of burying them in prose.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"08525d1909d73002099ee8c5646dfc6f0e10d4f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/08525d1909d73002099ee8c5646dfc6f0e10d4f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/a395d5818e281fe7ef547241042c5bc1a3372627","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52219673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky","id":52219673,"login":"grifftatarsky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMjE5Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grifftatarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/a395d5818e281fe7ef547241042c5bc1a3372627","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGEzOTVkNTgxOGUyODFmZTdlZjU0NzI0MTA0MmM1YmMxYTMzNzI2Mjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/cd4d1fb44c5cc541b12855ac3b0fabe1d98e8dd9","sha":"cd4d1fb44c5cc541b12855ac3b0fabe1d98e8dd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/cd4d1fb44c5cc541b12855ac3b0fabe1d98e8dd9"}],"sha":"a395d5818e281fe7ef547241042c5bc1a3372627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a395d5818e281fe7ef547241042c5bc1a3372627"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/cd4d1fb44c5cc541b12855ac3b0fabe1d98e8dd9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T07:59:53Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T07:59:53Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Baking loses to instancing, and two thirds of the shadow cost is one tree\n\n2.4, refused with the opposite of the forum''s claim. 112,543 grass plants, the\nsame plants both ways, coverage matched to 0.1% of the view, the empty-scene\nframe subtracted: thin instances 6.5 ms, baked into one buffer 7.65 — 18%\nslower, not four times faster. Baking also costs 9.45M vertices and 86 MB of\nindex buffer against an 84-vertex mesh, and gives up the wind, the\nground-normal shading, the per-plant tint and the compute placement, all of\nwhich read the instance matrix columns.\n\nTwo false results came first and both would have been published.\n`src.geometry.constructor` is a Geometry, not a VertexData: assigning\npositions to it and calling applyToMesh is silent and does nothing, so the\nbaked arm drew nothing and read exactly the empty baseline, which looked like\na 45% win. Every A/B of a draw path reports its own coverage now.\n\n2.6, examined. The 4.1 ms splits 1.8 receiving and 2.3 casting: shadows off\n26.4 ms, on with an empty caster list 28.2, all casters 30.5. The caster list\nis 4.93M triangles and scan-island_tree_02-0 is 3.22M of them — 403k\ntriangles, eight instances, into both cascades every frame, for a shadow a few\ndozen texels across. Dropping it saves 1.2 ms and its shadow is visibly\nmissed, so the answer is a decimated proxy. The seven stones are 0.1 ms.\n\nDo not change numCascades at runtime on WebGPU: Babylon emits a fragment\nshader with an empty argument slot and it fails to parse as a warning, leaving\nthe board silently unshadowed.\n\nstanding.ts is stripped of comments; what they knew is in PLAN.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4be3e8a0c64c5fc9efc0d0bdf2e9dbe855f81a6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/4be3e8a0c64c5fc9efc0d0bdf2e9dbe855f81a6f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/cd4d1fb44c5cc541b12855ac3b0fabe1d98e8dd9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/cd4d1fb44c5cc541b12855ac3b0fabe1d98e8dd9","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGNkNGQxZmI0NGM1Y2M1NDFiMTI4NTVhYzNiMGZhYmUxZDk4ZThkZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/d494146d6b22928b2e312fcf1c408cb42f163052","sha":"d494146d6b22928b2e312fcf1c408cb42f163052","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/d494146d6b22928b2e312fcf1c408cb42f163052"}],"sha":"cd4d1fb44c5cc541b12855ac3b0fabe1d98e8dd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/cd4d1fb44c5cc541b12855ac3b0fabe1d98e8dd9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/d494146d6b22928b2e312fcf1c408cb42f163052/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T07:03:12Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T07:03:12Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Flora that beds into the sward, and the pale leaves are the scan\n\nColour dilation under the mask was already done (0748ad4), so 1.5''s remaining\nparts were the drift and the bedding. Flora drift is three octaves instead of\none; each plant sinks 22% of its height into the sward rather than 6%, and\ntakes a small lean and roll so it is not stamped upright on the ground.\n\nTranslucency is off on both the sward material and the scanned-leaf material —\n2.3 measured it at 0.4 ms and visibly darker, and this is the board change\nthat finding was waiting on.\n\nThe paleness is refused to the asset, with numbers. The rosette cut-outs are\npale yellow-green in the atlas; pulled out and looked at, all five. An albedo\nwash on the species takes the pale-leaf area from 5.91% of the view to 4.65%\nand no further, because the leaf is blown out by direct sun rather than by its\nalbedo — and raising its ground blend makes it worse, since the ground normal\npoints at the sun too. Wash 0.70 is taken. A darker source cut belongs in\nfoliage-pack.mjs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"01345385895c761c67808bddcf458ed9608fe16b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/01345385895c761c67808bddcf458ed9608fe16b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/d494146d6b22928b2e312fcf1c408cb42f163052","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/d494146d6b22928b2e312fcf1c408cb42f163052","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGQ0OTQxNDZkNmIyMjkyOGIyZTMxMmZjZjFjNDA4Y2I0MmYxNjMwNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/8bc978dd69eeddfd7b9d7505a372a1d9029059e7","sha":"8bc978dd69eeddfd7b9d7505a372a1d9029059e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/8bc978dd69eeddfd7b9d7505a372a1d9029059e7"}],"sha":"d494146d6b22928b2e312fcf1c408cb42f163052","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/d494146d6b22928b2e312fcf1c408cb42f163052"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/8bc978dd69eeddfd7b9d7505a372a1d9029059e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T06:39:38Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T06:39:38Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Plants that are not one scale of one mesh, and a field with places\n\n1.3 was mostly already built: hue, curve, azimuth, root ambient occlusion and\nthe base-to-tip ramp were all in the compute pass or the wind plugin. The one\nthing missing was that `tall` and `wide` were the same scalar, so every one of\nthe 230,000 plants was a *uniform* scale of the same 114 triangles. A stretch\nterm splits them and takes the width back by its square root, so the mass\nstays put. Height over width now runs 0.72 to 1.34 across the field, read off\nthe matrix buffer; it was exactly 1.000 everywhere before.\n\n1.4 gives the sward a stature field from two octaves of value noise: drifts at\n1.42 of normal height, mown places at 0.56. The grass also shortens by up to\nhalf as wear climbs toward the track, so the verge is trodden down rather than\nsimply absent, and density follows stature between 0.80 and 1.10.\n\nFree, and in fact slightly cheaper — 29.8 ms at the play camera against 31.9,\nbecause the mown places are shorter and cover fewer pixels.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"255da2190374c0937ff282202e381e1dc8ac5a66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/255da2190374c0937ff282202e381e1dc8ac5a66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/8bc978dd69eeddfd7b9d7505a372a1d9029059e7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/8bc978dd69eeddfd7b9d7505a372a1d9029059e7","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDhiYzk3OGRkNjllZWRkZmQ3YjlkNzUwNWEzNzJhMWQ5MDI5MDU5ZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/e005f849dd55663e29104c1127e99454abb25106","sha":"e005f849dd55663e29104c1127e99454abb25106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/e005f849dd55663e29104c1127e99454abb25106"}],"sha":"8bc978dd69eeddfd7b9d7505a372a1d9029059e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/8bc978dd69eeddfd7b9d7505a372a1d9029059e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/e005f849dd55663e29104c1127e99454abb25106/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T06:18:51Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T06:18:51Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Wind that moves in patches, and a linter that was checking nothing\n\nThe gust was four sines summed with the time subtracted from each phase, which\nis four plane waves each running along its own axis. It is a travelling\npattern now: the field is sampled at root.xz - downwind * t, so every gust\nmoves downwind together and reads as flow over the field rather than as bars\ncrossing it. Lulls come from a smoothstep that actually reaches zero, and a\nper-plant flutter rides on the local gust so neighbouring blades are not one\nsheet.\n\nFree: 31.0 ms with the wind stopped, 30.8 blowing. It also moves 2.2x as much\nas the old wind at the same slider setting, which is most of why the wind\ncould not be seen.\n\npatchSize and gustBias are live on the plugin, so the gust can be tuned from\nthe console without a rebuild.\n\nTwo instrument faults found on the way, both of which had been reporting\ngreen:\n\n  - `patch` is a WGSL reserved word. The pipeline refuses the shader as a\n    *warning*, isReady() still answers true, and the field simply has no grass\n    in it. wgsl-lint now carries the reserved list.\n  - wgsl-lint with no arguments linted no files and printed \"wgsl clean\". It\n    walks projects/ when given nothing — 157 files.\n\nblade-wind.ts is stripped of comments; what they knew is in PLAN.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b469ac132d54189669addbfee6470d5855dea3cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/b469ac132d54189669addbfee6470d5855dea3cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/e005f849dd55663e29104c1127e99454abb25106","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/e005f849dd55663e29104c1127e99454abb25106","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGUwMDVmODQ5ZGQ1NTY2M2UyOTEwNGMxMTI3ZTk5NDU0YWJiMjUxMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/d974e55a5bbc66d8db06a3072c00e1505387bf6e","sha":"d974e55a5bbc66d8db06a3072c00e1505387bf6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/d974e55a5bbc66d8db06a3072c00e1505387bf6e"}],"sha":"e005f849dd55663e29104c1127e99454abb25106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/e005f849dd55663e29104c1127e99454abb25106"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/d974e55a5bbc66d8db06a3072c00e1505387bf6e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T05:14:01Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T05:14:01Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Lean the cards over, and give the wind a slider\n\nYou see ground through cards and not through blades, and the cause is not\nwidth: an upright quad seen from above is a line. Five near-vertical cards a\nplant leave gaps between them; a blade is a solid tapered tube that presents\narea from every direction.\n\nLeaning is the free half of the fix — same triangles, same plants. Grass goes\nto lean 0.90 and 9 cards. Fresh browser, four sowings back to back, holes as\nthe share of a steep view that is hole or dirt:\n\n  5 at lean 0.34   5.6%   27.7 ms   (as it was)\n  5 at lean 0.90   4.3%   28.3 ms\n  7 at lean 0.90   2.5%   30.2 ms\n  9 at lean 0.90   1.8%   31.9 ms   (this)\n  blades           1.2%   ~50 ms\n\nRaising the plant count half again reached 1.0% at 39.9, untaken. Tinting the\nterrain green to hide the gaps was refused before it was proposed.\n\nThe wind was running the whole time and cannot be seen: strength is\n0.62 * stiff against the plugin''s own 1.35 default, and the sward sweeps about\n7 of 255 over three seconds. There is a Wind slider now; 250% is plainly\nvisible. Its resting value is open, and the shape of the gust is still 1.2.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f4006d93824b6aa1dd1095b5e8a5e1a6586685e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/f4006d93824b6aa1dd1095b5e8a5e1a6586685e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/d974e55a5bbc66d8db06a3072c00e1505387bf6e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/d974e55a5bbc66d8db06a3072c00e1505387bf6e","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGQ5NzRlNTVhNWJiYzY2ZDhkYjA2YTMwNzJjMDBlMTUwNTM4N2JmNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/370bb4018178333a5eb0952a867ab67f9aee9917","sha":"370bb4018178333a5eb0952a867ab67f9aee9917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/370bb4018178333a5eb0952a867ab67f9aee9917"}],"sha":"d974e55a5bbc66d8db06a3072c00e1505387bf6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/d974e55a5bbc66d8db06a3072c00e1505387bf6e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/370bb4018178333a5eb0952a867ab67f9aee9917/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T04:00:13Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T04:00:13Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Card and twist are one mesh, and the blend is what hides the difference\n\nThe sward stays on cards — the blade''s fidelity is not worth ten frames.\n1.1 is closed on that call; the blade''s lab and its code stay.\n\n1.1b is not done and is not ticked. It fails the criterion written before it\nwas built: \"any measurable cost, or the user cannot see it.\" Card against\ntwist over the whole field is 0.78 mean out of 255. The two are the same\nmesh — same vertices, triangles, texture and cost — differing only in the\n`fan` that tilts each edge vertex''s normal: 0.3 for the card (16.7° out),\ntan(0.3pi) for the twist (54°).\n\nThe blend is the real item, so it has its own row now (1.1d). At 45% the\ncard/twist switch goes from 0.78 to 5.35 mean, which is the whole reason the\ntwist has nothing to show at 100%.\n\nCard thickness is 1.1e: card width is `spec.tall * cut.aspect`, locked to the\ncut''s photographed aspect, so widening one needs a new `widen` on CardSpec.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"914705d796aa8e9d23a76c91fc9f804df958cc51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/914705d796aa8e9d23a76c91fc9f804df958cc51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/370bb4018178333a5eb0952a867ab67f9aee9917","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/370bb4018178333a5eb0952a867ab67f9aee9917","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDM3MGJiNDAxODE3ODMzM2E1ZWIwOTUyYTg2N2FiNjdmOWFlZTk5MTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/900a9e55c8bbf0393011519698a872deeb43ff46","sha":"900a9e55c8bbf0393011519698a872deeb43ff46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/900a9e55c8bbf0393011519698a872deeb43ff46"}],"sha":"370bb4018178333a5eb0952a867ab67f9aee9917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/370bb4018178333a5eb0952a867ab67f9aee9917"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/900a9e55c8bbf0393011519698a872deeb43ff46/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T23:56:31Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T23:56:31Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Publish a, b and c to the plan page\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cbeafe885a0f0e6d5434151f741f5f4568810c5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/cbeafe885a0f0e6d5434151f741f5f4568810c5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/900a9e55c8bbf0393011519698a872deeb43ff46","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/900a9e55c8bbf0393011519698a872deeb43ff46","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDkwMGE5ZTU1YzhiYmYwMzkzMDExNTE5Njk4YTg3MmRlZWI0M2ZmNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/0edde464fba5bc965edced22e209f096aaea6c93","sha":"0edde464fba5bc965edced22e209f096aaea6c93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/0edde464fba5bc965edced22e209f096aaea6c93"}],"sha":"900a9e55c8bbf0393011519698a872deeb43ff46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/900a9e55c8bbf0393011519698a872deeb43ff46"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/0edde464fba5bc965edced22e209f096aaea6c93/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T23:55:28Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T23:55:28Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"(c) Give the blade a texture, and find where its cost actually is\n\nAt matched cost the card won the first comparison easily, and the reason\nwas that the blade had no texture — a flat albedo off the species table.\nIt could not take one from the cut-out atlas: a spray''s interior is the\ntransparent gap between blades, which the alpha test turns into holes,\nand making the material opaque sampled the atlas''s black background\ninstead and came out near-black.\n\nThe `blade` group cuts are single opaque strands. A photographed blade\nmaps straight onto the generated geometry — the geometry''s two edges to\nthe cut''s own silhouette edges at each height, holding off the top 12%\nwhere the scan thins to a hair and left dotted streaks. Sprays fall\nthrough to `addCard`, because a sparse multi-blade photo is a good card\nand a bad blade. The tuft has midribs, yellowing and real colour\nvariation now.\n\n**The blade is not geometry-bound.** Five blades a card to two — 638\ntriangles to 162 — moved the frame 52.4 ms to 49.4. Resolution says\nwhere it really goes:\n\n  card    1.68 ms per megapixel, 14.6 ms fixed\n  blade   3.38 ms per megapixel, 25.4 ms fixed\n\nTwice the fill, because the blade draws twice the grass: solid geometry\nwith nothing discarded, against a card that is mostly empty quad and\nthrows four fifths of its fragments away at the alpha test. That is the\ntrade, and it is not waste on either side.\n\nCard at 100% is 26.8 ms; the textured blade at 38% is 33.0. Both sit on\nthe board''s sward switch. Neither is refused.\n\nAlso checked the density slider end to end: 100% is 230,937 plants, 50%\nis 115,347, 25% is 57,912 — exact, and it repeats.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a883c2bc4e85e8e562afb3b86eda2c39dcfe6409","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/a883c2bc4e85e8e562afb3b86eda2c39dcfe6409"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/0edde464fba5bc965edced22e209f096aaea6c93","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/0edde464fba5bc965edced22e209f096aaea6c93","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDBlZGRlNDY0ZmJhNWJjOTY1ZWRjZWQyMmUyMDlmMDk2YWFlYTZjOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/4e4d691d5847771fd6d051b61956daf467755f67","sha":"4e4d691d5847771fd6d051b61956daf467755f67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/4e4d691d5847771fd6d051b61956daf467755f67"}],"sha":"0edde464fba5bc965edced22e209f096aaea6c93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/0edde464fba5bc965edced22e209f096aaea6c93"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/4e4d691d5847771fd6d051b61956daf467755f67/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T23:32:59Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T23:32:59Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"(b) The twist is inert, and the reason is worth more than the twist\n\nMeasured it on a rig that now repeats. Card against twist, one grass\ntuft, eight angles, pixel diff per channel out of 255:\n\n  ground blend 0.9 (ships)   0.06 - 0.10     nothing\n  ground blend 0.4           0.42 - 0.52     nearly nothing\n\nAcross midday, 9am, 7am and 6am, the same. The normals are not the\nproblem — card and twist differ by 37 degrees mean, 38.6 worst,\nmeasured off the VertexData.\n\n**`blade-wind.ts` throws them away.** It sets the shading normal to\n`mix(leafNormal, groundNormal, bladeGround.x)` and `bladeGround.x` is\n`plant.lit`, which is 0.9 for grass. Ninety per cent of the sward''s\nshading is the terrain''s normal, so a 37-degree change to a leaf becomes\nunder four degrees on screen. Any per-blade normal work is invisible\nwhile that stands — which is also why the twist measured 1.46 on the old\nwide cards and nothing on the new narrow ones: less leaf area, same 10%.\n\nThe lever that does work is that blend. Scaling every species'' `lit` by\n0.45 at an 8am sun takes the sward''s shading contrast from 37.2 to 46.4,\na quarter more, and the field gains a per-blade shimmer it does not have\nat 1.0. At midday it is a wash — 47.9 to 44.6 — because a high sun reads\nmostly the normal''s Y and `lift()` pins that.\n\nSo it is a control, not a decision: **Leaf normal** in the tools panel,\n100% as it ships. The twist is on the sward switch beside cards and\nblades.\n\nAlso fixed the measuring rig, which had been lying quietly. Instance 0\nof the sow is whichever compute thread won the atomicAdd, so it was a\ndifferent plant every page load and every coverage number carried its\nscale. The probe overwrites instance 0 with a canonical unit matrix and\na white tint now; three separate page loads agree to 0.01 per mille.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d7a8f380c3797916dc0fb07afeb18c010775d6ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/d7a8f380c3797916dc0fb07afeb18c010775d6ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/4e4d691d5847771fd6d051b61956daf467755f67","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/4e4d691d5847771fd6d051b61956daf467755f67","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDRlNGQ2OTFkNTg0Nzc3MWZkNmQwNTFiNjE5NTZkYWY0Njc3NTVmNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/a980bf3095c57c2b299bfd9281d61fdbc4fcdac2","sha":"a980bf3095c57c2b299bfd9281d61fdbc4fcdac2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a980bf3095c57c2b299bfd9281d61fdbc4fcdac2"}],"sha":"4e4d691d5847771fd6d051b61956daf467755f67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/4e4d691d5847771fd6d051b61956daf467755f67"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a980bf3095c57c2b299bfd9281d61fdbc4fcdac2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T23:11:03Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T23:11:03Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"(a) Kill the bar: grass is built from the single-blade cuts now\n\nPulled the two spray cut-outs out of the atlas and looked at them. The\nbar is a real strand in spray cut 0 — a short, fat, dark diagonal leaf\nin its lower left — and with two cuts over three cards it was landing\ntwice on every plant.\n\nThe sheet already had better material. The `blade` group is seven\ndistinct, clean, full-height single blades with midribs, fine tips and\nreal colour variation, at 35-60% fill against the sprays'' ~4%. Grass is\nfive of those plus one spray for the arch.\n\n  cuts per card   all three were cut 0 — `cuts[(n + placed*3) % 2]`\n                  is 0 for n = 0,1,2. Cycles on the leaf index now.\n  lean            every card took `spec.lean` verbatim, so nothing\n                  splayed and five blades stood in a bundle like a leek.\n                  Each card gets its own lean from the golden ratio now.\n\nPer-angle green coverage of the frame, camera fixed so the framing\ncannot move the metric:\n\n  as it was    2.7  4.2  6.5  4.2  2.1  4.9  6.6  5.7   swing 3.2x  mean 4.6\n  now         11.8 10.4 10.6 13.0 13.2 10.0  8.5 11.3   swing 1.6x  mean 11.1\n\n20 triangles to 40. Play camera 27.3 ms against about 21 for the\noriginal, and the field is a lush meadow with fine-tipped blades instead\nof a scatter of letterforms.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"75ac78e3fd8947bdd9d09548779f9bdb6e935368","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/75ac78e3fd8947bdd9d09548779f9bdb6e935368"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/a980bf3095c57c2b299bfd9281d61fdbc4fcdac2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/a980bf3095c57c2b299bfd9281d61fdbc4fcdac2","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGE5ODBiZjMwOTVjNTdjMmIyOTliZmQ5MjgxZDYxZmRiYzRmY2RhYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/a81ad4477bb39ed41ddc583e27a94c8c6019ff36","sha":"a81ad4477bb39ed41ddc583e27a94c8c6019ff36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a81ad4477bb39ed41ddc583e27a94c8c6019ff36"}],"sha":"a980bf3095c57c2b299bfd9281d61fdbc4fcdac2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a980bf3095c57c2b299bfd9281d61fdbc4fcdac2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a81ad4477bb39ed41ddc583e27a94c8c6019ff36/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:55:44Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:55:44Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Fix the card, which had never been looked at on its own\n\nFour faults, each measured by isolating one plant and orbiting it\nthrough eight angles. Green coverage of the frame, per angle:\n\n  as it was   2.7  4.2  6.5  4.2  2.1  4.9  6.6  5.7   swing 3.2x  mean 4.6\n  fixed       7.8  6.3  6.7  8.2  7.5  6.7  7.2  9.1   swing 1.4x  mean 7.4\n  (blade)    25.2 25.4 23.1 24.5 24.5 22.5 23.5 20.9   swing 1.2x  mean 23.7\n\n**The cards were not spaced.** A spec with `count: 1` took its azimuth\nfrom `Math.sin(placed * 7.3) * 0.9`, which for grass''s two cards is 0 and\n44 degrees — two nearly parallel planes that go edge-on together. Leaf\ncards now divide pi evenly across the plant, which is the right period\nfor a double-sided quad. On its own: 3.2x swing to 1.8x, no cost.\n\n**Every card drew the same photograph.** `cuts[(n + placed * 3) % 2]`\nevaluates to 0 for all three of grass''s cards. It cycles on the leaf\nindex now, so the two spray cuts alternate.\n\n**One of the two cards was a bar.** The second was a single-strand\n`blade` cut leaned at 0.34, which draws as a dark diagonal stroke across\nthe plant and is most of why it read as a letterform — F, X, A, K. Grass\nis three `spray` cards now.\n\n**The cards were leaned into their own arch.** The spray scan is already\nof arching grass and `lean: 0.17` tilted each card outward on top of it,\nso three of them splayed into a spider instead of standing. At 0.05 they\nstand and the arch comes from the photograph, where it belongs.\n\n20 triangles to 30, and the field is visibly fuller. It costs about\n8 ms at the play camera because there is 61% more grass on screen per\nplant, which is the point.\n\nWhat is left is in the asset, not the geometry: spray cut 0 carries a\nthick near-horizontal dark strand, and it is still one per plant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"24172ee2a98bab38f7fb3e1907f74b665072e448","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/24172ee2a98bab38f7fb3e1907f74b665072e448"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/a81ad4477bb39ed41ddc583e27a94c8c6019ff36","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/a81ad4477bb39ed41ddc583e27a94c8c6019ff36","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGE4MWFkNDQ3N2JiMzllZDQxZGRjNTgzZTI3YTk0YzhjNjAxOWZmMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/bdddb284b1fc858474929cbc65fac9c3d006aba6","sha":"bdddb284b1fc858474929cbc65fac9c3d006aba6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/bdddb284b1fc858474929cbc65fac9c3d006aba6"}],"sha":"a81ad4477bb39ed41ddc583e27a94c8c6019ff36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a81ad4477bb39ed41ddc583e27a94c8c6019ff36"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/bdddb284b1fc858474929cbc65fac9c3d006aba6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:37:56Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:37:56Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Photograph the card the way I photographed the blade\n\nIt had never been isolated. A hundred and twelve thousand of them had\nbeen looked at; not one of them.\n\n**A grass card is two crossed flat strips carrying two or three\nphotographed strands.** From most of eight angles it reads as a\nletterform — F, X, A, K — and at two of them it is a pair of hairlines.\nGreen coverage of the frame, per angle:\n\n  card    2.7  4.2  6.5  4.2  2.1  4.9  6.6  5.7   swing 3.2x  mean 4.6\n  blade  25.2 25.4 23.1 24.5 24.5 22.5 23.5 20.9   swing 1.2x  mean 23.7\n\nThe card loses two thirds of its silhouette depending on where you\nstand; the blade tuft is stable to within twenty per cent. The field\nhides it because the facings are random and the aggregate is smooth, but\nno single plant is a plant.\n\nAnd the part that undoes something I published: **a card draws a fifth\nof the plant a blade tuft does** at the same instance count. Every cost\ncomparison here has been at equal instances, not equal coverage — the\nblade was putting five times more grass on screen for its 2.2x. Matched\non coverage, the cost question is open and untested.\n\nI also wrote last message that a card carries \"a photo of five-to-ten\nreal blades\". It carries two or three.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2880166703df037d291d368fe453352ec07bb826","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/2880166703df037d291d368fe453352ec07bb826"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/bdddb284b1fc858474929cbc65fac9c3d006aba6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/bdddb284b1fc858474929cbc65fac9c3d006aba6","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGJkZGRiMjg0YjFmYzg1ODQ3NDkyOWNiYzY1ZmFjOWMzZDAwNmFiYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/bc803ebc5c8d51ff7d712f387ae519a8a9228248","sha":"bc803ebc5c8d51ff7d712f387ae519a8a9228248","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/bc803ebc5c8d51ff7d712f387ae519a8a9228248"}],"sha":"bdddb284b1fc858474929cbc65fac9c3d006aba6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/bdddb284b1fc858474929cbc65fac9c3d006aba6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/bc803ebc5c8d51ff7d712f387ae519a8a9228248/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:31:41Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:31:41Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Stop refusing; the call is the user''s\n\n\"Refused\" is not mine to write. Measure it, show it, say what it costs\nand what it looks like, and put the question. One subpoint at a time,\nand wait for the answer before starting the next.\n\nThe blade is why. It was written off twice — once on cost and once on\n\"it looks like a mown lawn\" — and the look objection was four bugs in my\nown geometry that a distant screenshot could not show. Rebuilt correctly\nit looks better than what ships. A refusal from me closed a door that\nwas not mine to close.\n\nAlso correcting a number I quoted in the last message: the blade is\n**458 triangles against the card''s 70 across the four species, 6.5x**,\nnot the 90-vs-70 I wrote — that compared grass alone against an\nall-species total. Per species: grass 20 → 90, fog 22 → 94, clover\n8 → 49, and plantain 20 → 225, because plantain is a rosette of five\nbroad ribbed leaves and every one is being turned into five grass\nblades. That is botanically wrong and about half the added cost, and\nrestricting blades to the grasses is untried.\n\nCost rises 2.2x on 6.5x the triangles, so it is not purely geometry —\nthe card''s alpha-test overdraw is real and the blade does not pay it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"764ce53c950e4edc398ceb56472a2ce2f0c0c9de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/764ce53c950e4edc398ceb56472a2ce2f0c0c9de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/bc803ebc5c8d51ff7d712f387ae519a8a9228248","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/bc803ebc5c8d51ff7d712f387ae519a8a9228248","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGJjODAzZWJjNWM4ZDUxZmY3ZDcxMmYzODdhZTUxOWE4YTkyMjgyNDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/25c7ad7525f1266621b86ebd25ce1f5894332060","sha":"25c7ad7525f1266621b86ebd25ce1f5894332060","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/25c7ad7525f1266621b86ebd25ce1f5894332060"}],"sha":"bc803ebc5c8d51ff7d712f387ae519a8a9228248","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/bc803ebc5c8d51ff7d712f387ae519a8a9228248"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/25c7ad7525f1266621b86ebd25ce1f5894332060/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:27:38Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T22:27:38Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The blade, implemented properly this time\n\nThe refusal stands but its reasoning was half wrong, and the half that\nwas wrong was my geometry.\n\nAsked to look at one tuft from eight angles, which I should have done\nbefore judging a field of them from three hundred half-feet away. Four\nfaults, all invisible at that distance:\n\n- **Width came from `cut.aspect`** — 0.65 for a spray cut and 0.04 for a\n  blade cut, through the same divisor, so one group was ten times the\n  other. Slabs and wires in the same field. It is absolute now, from\n  `plant.wide`.\n- **No taper.** `pow(1 - t, 0.5)` over three stacks is a parallel-sided\n  ribbon with a blunt end. Shoulder-then-point over five stacks now.\n- **The tuft splayed into a five-foot starfish** from a three-foot plant,\n  fan and tilt and root spread compounding. The blades turn on the\n  golden angle now, so a tuft is round instead of a paper fan.\n- **The holes were the alpha test.** I UV''d solid geometry into the\n  interior of a cut-out''s bounding span, which is the transparent gap\n  between the scanned blades.\n\nAnd the deeper one: **a generated blade cannot be textured from a cut-out\natlas.** Making the material opaque to stop the holes sampled the atlas''s\nblack background instead and the tuft came out near-black. It takes its\ncolour from the species table now, with the root-to-tip gradient\n`blade-wind` already had and the scans had made unnecessary.\n\nRebuilt it reads as grass from every angle and **looks better than the\ncards close up**. It costs 21.0 ms against 47.1 at the play camera on the\nwhole board, so the refusal stands on cost alone — but the \"it looks like\na mown lawn\" in the first result was a bug, not the technique, and that\nis corrected in the lab entry.\n\nIt is on the board behind a cards/blades switch, lazily built, so the\ncomparison can be made on the real field.\n\nAlso: `grow()` sowed twice because it always re-applied density, which\nraced the tally reset and reported 225k grass where there were 112k.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"313e1967234ad3d241bcd3305b87045ab4fb1a80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/313e1967234ad3d241bcd3305b87045ab4fb1a80"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/25c7ad7525f1266621b86ebd25ce1f5894332060","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/25c7ad7525f1266621b86ebd25ce1f5894332060","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDI1YzdhZDc1MjVmMTI2NjYyMWI4NmViZDI1Y2UxZjU4OTQzMzIwNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/7fb1775115f68eb7c4f55ad510704e6b0e3c38b6","sha":"7fb1775115f68eb7c4f55ad510704e6b0e3c38b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/7fb1775115f68eb7c4f55ad510704e6b0e3c38b6"}],"sha":"25c7ad7525f1266621b86ebd25ce1f5894332060","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/25c7ad7525f1266621b86ebd25ce1f5894332060"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/7fb1775115f68eb7c4f55ad510704e6b0e3c38b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T21:30:23Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T21:30:23Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"1.1: the blade is refused, the twist is free\n\nThree sowings on one field with the same seeds, so every plant stands in\nthe same place in all three and only its geometry differs: the card as\nit ships, the same card with the reference twist on its edge normals,\nand Bezier blades standing in for each scanned spray. The middle option\nis the point — without it a result cannot be attributed to the shape or\nto the shading.\n\nScene GPU pass on the lab patch:\n\n  card          70 tris   4.80 ms   —        control 0.41\n  card + twist  70 tris   4.82 ms   +0.02    change 1.46\n  blade        358 tris   8.97 ms   +4.17    change 18.68\n\n**Wall clock said nothing.** All three sat at 16.7 ms because the lab\npatch finishes inside the refresh, which is the trap the audit just\ndocumented — so the lab reads the `scene` pass counter as well, and says\nso on screen when every option''s wall clock matches.\n\n**The blade is refused on cost**: +4.17 ms against a 1.0 ms threshold at\n5.1x the triangles. A triangle-neutral version is about 1.4 blades per\nspray, which is not a tuft, so it cannot be made cheap and still look\nlike grass here. That is forum 46756''s regime exactly — geometry is the\nscarce thing on this board.\n\n**It was diffed against the reference before refusing**, per the lab''s\nown rule. The first attempt read as a leafy mat because the blades were\nabout seventeen times too wide: a real blade is a hundredth of its height\nacross and mine was a fifth of a spray. Narrowed to a fourteenth and\nmultiplied from three to seven it reads as fine dense turf — better, and\nstill a mown lawn rather than a meadow. It loses the long blade\nsilhouettes the scans carry, which is what the sward is currently best\nat.\n\n**The twist is the half worth keeping.** Jahrmann rotates the edge\nnormals 0.3 pi about the blade''s axis so a flat strip shades like a\ncylinder; the cards already fan theirs, but by atan(0.3) — a third of\nthat. The reference angle on the geometry that already ships costs\n+0.02 ms and moves the image 1.46 against a control of 0.51. It is 1.1b,\nand it wants a look on the board before it lands.\n\nThe lab harness now takes N options rather than two, and `sowMeadow`\ntakes a geometry factory so variants share one placement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7a4f2c3b64cc7c21fa24aac41e064eeb945d18c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/7a4f2c3b64cc7c21fa24aac41e064eeb945d18c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/7fb1775115f68eb7c4f55ad510704e6b0e3c38b6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/7fb1775115f68eb7c4f55ad510704e6b0e3c38b6","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDdmYjE3NzUxMTVmNjhlYjdjNGY1NWFkNTEwNzA0ZTZiMGUzYzM4YjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/7da41441e05c147f4e11f53862e38c3f7fdc9d2e","sha":"7da41441e05c147f4e11f53862e38c3f7fdc9d2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/7da41441e05c147f4e11f53862e38c3f7fdc9d2e"}],"sha":"7fb1775115f68eb7c4f55ad510704e6b0e3c38b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/7fb1775115f68eb7c4f55ad510704e6b0e3c38b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/7da41441e05c147f4e11f53862e38c3f7fdc9d2e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T20:39:49Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T20:39:49Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The audit found the measurement, not the renderer\n\nTwo things outside the code were moving the numbers more than anything\nin it, and neither was being checked.\n\n**The browser''s age.** A Chrome that has been reloading the board all\nsession leaks WebGPU adapters and the board gets slower with no error\nanywhere. The same frame at the same resolution reads 23.9 ms on a worn\nbrowser and **21.5 ms on a fresh one** — and the sward alone reads 8.57\nagainst 4.88, so the *shape* of the breakdown moves, not only its scale.\nOn the worn browser the sward looked like the whole problem. It is not:\ntrees and scrub is the largest piece at 4.93 ms, a hair above it. The\nother symptom of the same leak is `requestAdapter` hanging silently,\nwhich is how this was found — the probe simply stopped seeing a board.\n\n**The window''s display.** `adaptToDeviceRatio` takes the pixel count from\nwhichever screen the window landed on, so a probe window on a non-Retina\ndisplay renders a quarter of the pixels and says nothing. One audit run\ncame back at exactly 16.67 ms with every component at 0.00, which is the\n60 Hz refresh rather than a fast board — wall clock cannot see below\nvsync. `board-check.sh` and `board-angles.mjs` take `SCALING` (default\n0.5) and report the render size; `FrameCost` carries `pixels` and\n`megapixels`, and the HUD shows them. A frame number without its pixel\ncount is not a measurement.\n\nThe board, measured properly — play camera, 3600 x 2026, 7.29 MP, fresh\nbrowser, three bracketed runs, drift 0.37 ms: **21.5 ms, 47 fps.** Trees\n4.93, sward 4.88, shadows 4.03, terrain 2.13, flora 1.87, temporal aa\n1.42, everything else 0.67, unattributed 1.22.\n\nAlso: reading a StorageBuffer before timing stalls the pipeline — a\n`cost()` taken after one reported 32.5 ms of CPU frame time on a board\nrunning at 43 fps. And `chrome-probe.mjs` now drives the tab matching the\nURL it was given, so the three standing tabs do not fight over it.\n\nBOARD-HANDOFF.md §0 and the board-measure skill lead with both rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cba3df13ed39babdff48e967ddd9c182086b925a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/cba3df13ed39babdff48e967ddd9c182086b925a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/7da41441e05c147f4e11f53862e38c3f7fdc9d2e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/7da41441e05c147f4e11f53862e38c3f7fdc9d2e","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDdkYTQxNDQxZTA1YzE0N2Y0ZTExZjUzODYyZTM4YzNmN2ZkYzlkMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/5d11b812f529b6faa0cfafca5d91e2db75282260","sha":"5d11b812f529b6faa0cfafca5d91e2db75282260","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/5d11b812f529b6faa0cfafca5d91e2db75282260"}],"sha":"7da41441e05c147f4e11f53862e38c3f7fdc9d2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/7da41441e05c147f4e11f53862e38c3f7fdc9d2e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/5d11b812f529b6faa0cfafca5d91e2db75282260/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T20:16:35Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T20:16:35Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Audit Phase 0, and three of its claims did not survive\n\n**The frame was overstated.** 22.9 ms / 45 fps was one reading at the fast\nend of the distribution. Five repeats put the median between 23.6 and\n24.4 with a p95 near 26, so the board is 23.9 ms / 42 fps. The render\nsize was identical across all of them, so this is drift and thermal\nstate, not resolution.\n\n**The density slider did not thin uniformly**, which is the thing 0.3\nclaimed to fix. Grass, clover and plantain scaled exactly, but Yorkshire\nfog came back at 61% of itself at half density instead of 50%: slots a\ncell were *rounded*, so its `keep x crowd` came to 1.44, and its lottery\nsaturated at full density rather than at half. Slots round up now, with\na float tolerance because the grass''s `wanted x crowd` is exactly 5.0\nand `ceil` was handing it 6. Measured after: every species 0.498-0.502\nat half and 0.249-0.252 at a quarter. Fog gains 2,685 plants.\n\n**\"Adding or removing a species changes only that species'' count\" was\nnever true of the count.** The allocation is decoupled exactly — remove\nclover and every other species'' slots, cap, keep and the lattice are\nidentical, measured — but the drift lottery is deliberately coupled,\nbecause a species'' share of a spot depends on what else wants it, and\nthat is worth up to 21% (grass +0.7%, fog +2.2%, plantain +20.6%). The\ncriterion is now about allocation, which is what was fixed.\n\nTwo instruments repaired:\n\n`splitFrame` took one baseline and compared thirteen readings to it over\nthirteen seconds. On a machine whose load moved, every component\ninflated — one audit run had the parts summing to 73.6 ms of a 28.7 ms\nframe, with `stone` at 5.2. Each slice is bracketed between the\non-readings either side of it now, and the run reports its own drift, so\na reading taken on a busy machine says so.\n\nThe sky dome was drawn every frame and had no switch, so it sat in\n`unattributed` — `setSkyLight` toggles the image-based light, not the\nmesh. It has its own toggle, and `unattributed` is 0.00.\n\nAlso: `Meadow.dispose()` was disposing the foliage sheet it does not\nown, which would have blanked the board the first time a lab shared one;\nownership moved to the callers. `FrameCost.frameMs` is `cpuMs`, because\na field meaning CPU time inside `scene.render` and a function meaning\nwall clock between presents should not share a name.\n\nstage.ts and ooze.routes.ts stripped of comments, with twenty\ntried-and-failed facts moved to PLAN.md first — the SSAO2 and god-ray\nattempts, the `antialias: true` provenance of the 24 ms MSAA figure, the\n`imageProcessingEnabled` master-switch trap, and the bloom threshold\nsweep among them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cff6fac123e07cc2129464fe13cc5eff34637a5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/cff6fac123e07cc2129464fe13cc5eff34637a5b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/5d11b812f529b6faa0cfafca5d91e2db75282260","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/5d11b812f529b6faa0cfafca5d91e2db75282260","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDVkMTFiODEyZjUyOWI2ZmFhMGNmYWZjYTVkOTFlMmRiNzUyODIyNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/2ef30c4a0b98dd07e991135280ed6277e0940a05","sha":"2ef30c4a0b98dd07e991135280ed6277e0940a05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/2ef30c4a0b98dd07e991135280ed6277e0940a05"}],"sha":"5d11b812f529b6faa0cfafca5d91e2db75282260","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/5d11b812f529b6faa0cfafca5d91e2db75282260"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/2ef30c4a0b98dd07e991135280ed6277e0940a05/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:44:01Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:44:01Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The lab, and its first verdict\n\n`/board/lab` is the place a technique gets accepted or refused. One\nscreen each, on the smallest scene that exercises it — for grass that is\na flat 60 x 60 foot patch of the real sward under the board''s own sun,\nsky and post chain, not the whole board. Each screen carries an A/B\nswitch that moves one thing, its own wall clock, and a criterion written\nbefore the demo was built.\n\nThe pixel diff also takes a **control** — the same state grabbed twice —\nbecause a toggle diff has twice come back all zeros here and been\nbelieved the first time. A switch that does nothing now says so on\nscreen instead of reading as a result. The scene freezes for the grab,\nor the wind is the whole diff; the first reading after load is a cold\noutlier, so a warm-up is discarded.\n\nThe measurement is `frameMs()` out of `split-frame.ts` rather than a\nsecond copy of it.\n\nFirst verdict, 2.3: **subsurface translucency on the sward is refused.**\nIt costs 0.4 ms (10.2 on / 9.7 off) and it is flatly darker and less\nsaturated across the whole patch — the Broken criterion, not the\nWorking one. Change 8.4 against a control of 0.5, so the switch is\nreal. Babylon''s pbrBlockFinalLitComponents multiplies diffuse irradiance\nby (1 - translucencyIntensity) before adding the transmitted term, and\nat 0.55 the sward is not getting it back. Turning it off on the board is\nits own change, with the board-level measurement repeated.\n\nBOARD-PLAN.md is the worklist now, and it is published as an Artifact so\nit can be crossed off from the GUI. Ticks live in the page''s own store,\nso a republish from here does not undo them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a1a219396c9e6cee2f43f28fa6916aaef6085d1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/a1a219396c9e6cee2f43f28fa6916aaef6085d1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/2ef30c4a0b98dd07e991135280ed6277e0940a05","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/2ef30c4a0b98dd07e991135280ed6277e0940a05","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDJlZjMwYzRhMGI5OGRkMDdlOTkxMTM1MjgwZWQ2Mjc3ZTA5NDBhMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/7787a1873481e3355b13d80ec417e10e910f76ef","sha":"7787a1873481e3355b13d80ec417e10e910f76ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/7787a1873481e3355b13d80ec417e10e910f76ef"}],"sha":"2ef30c4a0b98dd07e991135280ed6277e0940a05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/2ef30c4a0b98dd07e991135280ed6277e0940a05"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/7787a1873481e3355b13d80ec417e10e910f76ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:27:29Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:27:29Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Attribute the whole frame, and the 8 ms was the instrument\n\nThe unattributed baseline does not exist. `split-frame.ts` was reading\n`gpuTimeInFrameForMainPass`, which with a post chain installed times one\nfull-screen blit — the same counter PLAN.md has warned about for weeks.\nIt measures wall clock now and drives the board''s own `show` toggles\ninstead of owning a second list of meshes, so the parts sum to within a\nmillisecond of the whole. Play camera, 23.2 ms: sward 8.1, trees 4.8,\nshadows 3.8, terrain 1.9, flora 1.7, temporal aa 1.2.\n\n`gpu-passes.ts` reads the per-pass counters nobody had walked — every\nrender target carries `gpuTimeInFrame` and so does every ComputeShader.\nTwo traps in them, both measured: a counter that stops being written\nkeeps reporting its last average forever, and the post-chain counters\noverlap so badly they sum to 48 ms of a 22 ms frame. `FrameCost` carries\nno summed `gpuMs` for that reason.\n\nThe bald ring was three systems disagreeing about where the sward stops\n— sowing faded out at wear 0.62, the ground bake painted to 0.82, the\nshadow proxy stood to 0.82. `SWARD_FADE_FROM`/`TO` is the one definition\nnow. A matrix readback binned on a 44x30 grid has no thin cell off the\ntrack.\n\nAnd `MAX_PLANTS` was a budget, not a ceiling: split by share, so the mix,\nthe density slider and the lattice pitch were one number and deleting a\nspecies inflated the survivors. Species declare plants per square\nhalf-foot, the pitch comes from the densest rather than the rarest, and\nthe integer rounding is paid for by the sowing lottery so a three per\ncent species no longer gets a whole slot a cell. `swardLattice()` is pure\nand tested: adding or removing a species leaves every other species''\nnumbers exactly equal.\n\nThe board opened at `density = 0.5` while the slider read 100%. It opens\nat maximum now — 228,355 plants against 94,503, grass 112,597 against a\nprevious ceiling of 108,258.\n\nNo comments in any file touched, per the new rule. What could not be\nrecovered from the code — what was tried and failed — is in PLAN.md\nunder \"Traps that used to live in comments\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"39956232e6df57f70d397522914ae8422388d744","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/39956232e6df57f70d397522914ae8422388d744"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/7787a1873481e3355b13d80ec417e10e910f76ef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/7787a1873481e3355b13d80ec417e10e910f76ef","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDc3ODdhMTg3MzQ4MWUzMzU1YjEzZDgwZWM0MTdlMTBlOTEwZjc2ZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/cf7f72f30e0ec5d97c9574fcef1cf5c167e6e72a","sha":"cf7f72f30e0ec5d97c9574fcef1cf5c167e6e72a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/cf7f72f30e0ec5d97c9574fcef1cf5c167e6e72a"}],"sha":"7787a1873481e3355b13d80ec417e10e910f76ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/7787a1873481e3355b13d80ec417e10e910f76ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/cf7f72f30e0ec5d97c9574fcef1cf5c167e6e72a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T18:33:58Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T18:33:58Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"A handoff, and no more subagents\n\nThe fan-out was the mistake. Five research agents consumed the user''s entire\nfive-hour token window in about thirty minutes and every one of them died\nmid-run on a 429 having written no report. That is now a permanent rule in\nCLAUDE.md and in memory: no Agent, no Workflow, no fan-out on this repo, ever,\nincluding when a system-reminder says ultracode is on. Research inline and\nverify each claim against the installed Babylon source.\n\nWhat was salvageable was their downloads. Before dying they had pulled ninety\nBabylon doc pages, forty-four forum threads, five papers and a dozen grass\nimplementations into the scratchpad, and mining those locally produced the whole\nresearch section in a handful of greps. Worth knowing for the next time a\nbackground task dies.\n\nBOARD-HANDOFF.md is the deliverable: measured state, open regressions with\nfile:line, cited research, an ordered plan with pass/fail criteria per item, and\na repo map. CLAUDE.md and PLAN.md now point at it.\n\nThe two regressions, both diagnosed rather than guessed:\n\nThe bald ring is two systems disagreeing about one threshold. The compute pass\nfades grass out over wear 0.42 to 0.62 (meadow.ts:305, wearMax 0.62 minus 0.2),\nwhile the ground paints grass until 0.82 (splat-bake.ts:175) and the sward\nshadow proxy stands until 0.82 (terrain.ts:214). The band between is painted\ngreen, casts a grass shadow and has no grass in it — a ring around every stretch\nof track, mid-field where the track forks. Confirmed by reading the compute\npass''s instance matrices onto a grid and overlaying the wear field on the same\ngrid.\n\nAnd \"100% grass\" never meant maximum grass. MAX_PLANTS is a total split by each\nspecies'' share normalised over the sum of shares, with the lattice pitch derived\nfrom the rarest share — so the mix and the density are coupled. Reproduced\narithmetically: two species gives grass a cap of 299,250 and 92,098 placed; four\ngives 160,125 and 46,419. Deleting clover and plantain handed their slots to the\ngrass and restoring them halved it. Both behaviours are consistent and both are\nwrong for what was asked.\n\nAlso corrected two of my own claims. Frame numbers in this repo were all read\nfrom gpuTimeInFrameForMainPass, which the Babylon d.ts says times only the main\npass — one blit with a post chain installed. The board is 18.3 ms at the\nwhole-board camera, not the ~9 quoted for weeks. And the 93 per cent black\nfigure for the scrub was texture-space, not screen-space; the mask fix was right\nbut its visible effect on the trees was smaller than I said.\n\nThe research says the board''s architecture is already correct. Ghost of\nTsushima''s published grass pipeline is compute shader to blade list with an\natomic count to a finalize pass to an indirect draw, which is what meadow.ts\ndoes. What is missing is in the blade and the shading: a Bezier blade with\nrotated normals so a flat blade shades round, per-instance variety, and the\nricher wind this project used to have in three.js and still has in the old file.\nA Babylon forum thread plants a million blades with a ShaderMaterial and culls\nin the vertex shader, which is the existence proof that the target is reachable.\n\nThree skills so the next instance does not relearn this: board-measure,\nfoliage-scan, graphics-lab — the last being the protocol the user asked for, one\nprovable demo screen per technique with its pass and fail criteria written\nbefore it is built.\n\n126 tests, all builds green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a0a127a1cb3cc23fab3f4975afd13e7a2500e0c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/a0a127a1cb3cc23fab3f4975afd13e7a2500e0c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/cf7f72f30e0ec5d97c9574fcef1cf5c167e6e72a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/cf7f72f30e0ec5d97c9574fcef1cf5c167e6e72a","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGNmN2Y3MmYzMGUwZWM1ZDk3Yzk1NzRmY2VmMWNmNWMxNjdlNmU3MmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/b447c1d30a9df12a30dd78f35a4baab03030d728","sha":"b447c1d30a9df12a30dd78f35a4baab03030d728","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/b447c1d30a9df12a30dd78f35a4baab03030d728"}],"sha":"cf7f72f30e0ec5d97c9574fcef1cf5c167e6e72a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/cf7f72f30e0ec5d97c9574fcef1cf5c167e6e72a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/b447c1d30a9df12a30dd78f35a4baab03030d728/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:40:33Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:40:33Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Restore the sward''s understorey, and measure what the bald patch actually is\n\nThe clover and plantain cards were deleted when the flowers became scans, on the\ntheory that scans would replace all the broadleaf. They were the sward''s dense\nlow cover, and taking them out of the drift competition dropped it from about\n105,000 plants to 92,000 grass plus 13,000 fog. Restored. The scanned flowers\nstand in the understorey; they do not replace it.\n\nThat was not the bald patch, though. Reading the compute pass''s instance\nmatrices back onto a 44 x 30 grid of the board, before and after the restore,\nthe empty band is in the same place both times — and laid over the wear field\nsampled on the same grid it coincides exactly with the cart track. Grass is\nfaded out by the compute pass between wear 0.42 and 0.62, while the terrain\npaints that zone with its green thin-turf layer and keeps its sward shadow\nproxy up to wear 0.82. So around every stretch of road there is a ring ten to\ntwenty feet wide that the ground says is grassy and the sward says is bare, and\nwhere the track branches that ring sits in the middle of the field. One\nthreshold, two systems disagreeing about it; fixed in the plan with the\nmeasurement, not poked at here.\n\nRestoring the species also exposed a flaw in the sowing: the lattice pitch is\nderived from the rarest species'' share, so changing the mix changes the total —\n94,503 placed now against 105,000 with two species, with grass halved. Density\nand mix should be independent. Also in the plan.\n\nTwo skills written from what this cost: board-measure (the instruments that lied\nand the ones that do not) and foliage-scan (every trap in bringing a scan onto\nthe board). 126 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"098bc3aa9d75e51de2914b3b79fa69a43d628be2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/098bc3aa9d75e51de2914b3b79fa69a43d628be2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/b447c1d30a9df12a30dd78f35a4baab03030d728","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/b447c1d30a9df12a30dd78f35a4baab03030d728","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGI0NDdjMWQzMGE5ZGYxMmEzMGRkNzhmMzVhNGJhYWIwMzAzMGQ3Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/0748ad4fb6ff1cf4977e01ecc8aa248ef34311dc","sha":"0748ad4fb6ff1cf4977e01ecc8aa248ef34311dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/0748ad4fb6ff1cf4977e01ecc8aa248ef34311dc"}],"sha":"b447c1d30a9df12a30dd78f35a4baab03030d728","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/b447c1d30a9df12a30dd78f35a4baab03030d728"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/0748ad4fb6ff1cf4977e01ecc8aa248ef34311dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:03:42Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:03:42Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The scans were painting their own background\n\nA four-way research dive said the same thing from two independent directions and\nit is not a rendering bug at all. Poly Haven''s plant and tree scans are flat\ncut-out cards whose base colour is an atlas of foliage on solid black. The JPEG\ndownload carries the atlas and not the mask, JPEG cannot hold an alpha channel,\nand glTF says a base-colour texture without alpha is opaque — so `alphaCutOff`\nwas comparing 1.0 against 0.4 on every fragment and discarding nothing, ever.\nEvery plant was painting its own black background.\n\nMeasured over the UV area each primitive actually covers: 54 to 66 per cent of a\ncelandine is black, 41 per cent of a dandelion, 49 per cent of island_tree_02''s\nleaves, and 93 per cent of searsia_lucida''s. That last one is the uncomfortable\npart — the trees had this the whole time and this board has been holding them up\nas proof the scans were fine. A canopy reads as a canopy at a distance whatever\nis between its leaves, which is exactly why nobody noticed.\n\nBefore the research I changed the alpha blend mode, then the shadow caster list,\nthen the receive-shadows flag. Two of those were worth keeping on their own\nmerits. None of them was the bug. The one-line falsification that would have\nsaved all three is `alphaCutOff = 0.99` — if nothing disappears, alpha is 1.0\neverywhere and no transparency setting can help. It is written down now.\n\nThe fix binds Poly Haven''s separate `Alpha` download as an opacity texture read\nfrom luminance, which works because Babylon''s `_hasAlphaChannel()` is satisfied\nby a non-null `opacityTexture` alone, so the glTF never has to be re-authored.\nWhich materials need it is derived rather than tabulated: the loader has already\nset a transparency mode on exactly the cut-out ones, and the mask''s filename is\nthe atlas''s with `_diff_` swapped for `_alpha_`. Two traps in that, both hit:\n`invertY` is the fourth `Texture` argument with no setter and defaults the\nopposite way to the glTF loader, and glTF `OPAQUE` is 0 rather than null — so a\nnull guard let the bark through and handed it masks that 404.\n\nAnd the frame numbers in this project have been wrong. `board-check.sh` read\n`gpuTimeInFrameForMainPass`, which PLAN.md has documented as the wrong\ninstrument since the day it was found — with a post pipeline that pass is one\nfull-screen blit. It reads wall clock now and the numbers roughly doubled:\nwhole board 18.3 ms, not 9.2. Component costs at the play camera, by switching\neach off: sward 4.3, trees 3.2, flora 1.9, shadows 1.9, and about 8.1 ms of\nterrain, sky, temporal resolve, grade and present that nothing has ever been\nmeasured against.\n\nTwo more ways the tooling lied, on top of the two already recorded: the dev\nserver serves the last good bundle when a build fails, and can serve a stale\nchunk even when it succeeds. `tools/build-ok.sh` catches the first. The only\nguard against the second is to verify on a clean production build.\n\nNew instruments: `board-angles.mjs` sweeps nine fixed cameras and times each,\nbecause one screenshot is not a review; `foliage-trim.mjs` measures stalk\njunctions off the sheet''s alpha. Both probes now disable the browser cache.\n\nFOLIAGE-REPORT.md carries the reasoning, the citations, the disagreements\nbetween the research lines and how each was resolved, and the verified dead\nends — including alpha-to-coverage, which is a silent no-op here because it is\ngated on a sample count of more than one and this engine is built with\n`antialias: false`. That closes an open question in PLAN.md.\n\n118 tests, all builds green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c151a950a263543e47ddd6661ff5729c20ed8402","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/c151a950a263543e47ddd6661ff5729c20ed8402"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/0748ad4fb6ff1cf4977e01ecc8aa248ef34311dc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/0748ad4fb6ff1cf4977e01ecc8aa248ef34311dc","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDA3NDhhZDRmYjZmZjFjZjQ5NzdlMDFlY2M4YWEyNDhlZjM0MzExZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/c65e2f65ee1f019fc08e1b51e94406b395e061ff","sha":"c65e2f65ee1f019fc08e1b51e94406b395e061ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/c65e2f65ee1f019fc08e1b51e94406b395e061ff"}],"sha":"0748ad4fb6ff1cf4977e01ecc8aa248ef34311dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/0748ad4fb6ff1cf4977e01ecc8aa248ef34311dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/c65e2f65ee1f019fc08e1b51e94406b395e061ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T05:36:35Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T05:36:35Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Geometry tests, and the first run found a real one\n\nEvery foliage bug this renderer has had was a geometry bug that looked like a\ntexture bug. The daisy rendered as a white cigarette and the cut-out on the\nsheet is a perfect photographed flower; the clover had two stems and the scan\nhas one. Both times the picture was right and the mesh carrying it was wrong,\nand both times it took several rounds of squinting at screenshots to work out\nwhich. Nineteen tests now assert the mesh directly, on no GPU — `cardGeometry`\nis a pure function from a plant and a cut-out table to vertex data, which is the\nwhole reason it is worth keeping pure.\n\nWhat they cover: that a card is never narrower than the silhouette it carries at\nany row count (the cigarette, as a regression test); that trimming starts the\ncard at the junction the sheet recorded and leaves it alone when nothing was\nrecorded; that a flower head''s centre is on the stem axis at the height asked\nfor, that its rim is a circle of the right radius, that the ring closes, that it\nis dished rather than flat, that it draws one triangle a segment and samples\nonly inside its own cut-out; and for every plant the board actually sows, that\nthe mesh is finite, that indices point at vertices that exist, that nothing\nhangs below the ground, and that every normal is unit length and above the\nhorizon.\n\nThe last of those failed on the first run, and it was real: `lift` normalises\nthe leaf normal and *then* clamps its y to a floor, which un-normalises it. The\nnormals this function has been shipping measure between 0.9994 and 1.0002. The\nshader renormalises so nothing was visibly wrong, but it was arithmetic that\ndid not mean what it said. Solving for the horizontal part that keeps the vector\nunit while the floor holds is the same two lines.\n\nOne test was wrong rather than the code: it picked a row band by height, and the\ncard''s own size jitter meant the window could miss every row and take the\nmaximum of an empty list. Picked by index now.\n\n118 tests, all builds green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"24b887a082c3ff3a5a38678f04baeb47373b96bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/24b887a082c3ff3a5a38678f04baeb47373b96bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/c65e2f65ee1f019fc08e1b51e94406b395e061ff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/c65e2f65ee1f019fc08e1b51e94406b395e061ff","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGM2NWUyZjY1ZWUxZjAxOWZjMDhlMWI1MWU5NDQwNmIzOTVlMDYxZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/e250c1d16e87a8ee4c0779b7eaa039c5ad8b6dd8","sha":"e250c1d16e87a8ee4c0779b7eaa039c5ad8b6dd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/e250c1d16e87a8ee4c0779b7eaa039c5ad8b6dd8"}],"sha":"c65e2f65ee1f019fc08e1b51e94406b395e061ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/c65e2f65ee1f019fc08e1b51e94406b395e061ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/e250c1d16e87a8ee4c0779b7eaa039c5ad8b6dd8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T05:33:14Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T05:33:14Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The flowers and broadleaf are scans now, and the dev server was lying\n\nThe trees are photogrammetry and the sward was flat photographs, which is the\nwhole reason one looked better than the other. Poly Haven has scanned plants as\nwell as scanned trees, so the flowers and the broadleaf plants come from the\nsame place the trees do: `celandine_01` and `dandelion_01`, real geometry, real\npetals, 442 to 3180 triangles each. The oxeye daisy, white clover and ribwort\nplantain cards are deleted.\n\nThe grass stays cards and that is not a compromise. A scanned tuft is 700 to\n2500 triangles and there are eighty-eight thousand of them; three thousand\nscanned flowers is 3 M triangles and eighty-eight thousand scanned tufts is 60.\nGrass also already works.\n\nPlacement is deliberately sparse — about three thousand plants over thirty-three\nthousand square feet, two to a five-foot square — on a jittered lattice with a\nslow noise field per species so they gather into drifts rather than spreading\nevenly. Grass defaults to 100% now.\n\nTwo bugs found on the way, and the second is the bad one.\n\nThe flora rendered near-black. I had appended it to the same array the board\nhands to `addShadowCaster`, so three thousand one-foot plants became shadow\ncasters and receivers at a cascade resolution where each is well under one\ntexel: every leaf shadowed itself against its own depth. Acne on something that\nsmall is not a stripe, it is the whole plant. The sward beside it neither casts\nnor receives, for the same reason, and never has.\n\nAnd I spent an hour debugging that against a bundle that was not running. The\ndev server keeps serving the last good build when a compile fails — no error on\nthe page, no error in the probe, the board simply is not the board in the\nworking tree. Two of my fixes were already correct and I could not see it,\nbecause the page still had the old code and reported the old values. That is\nthe same class as `board-shot.mjs` not navigating. `tools/build-ok.sh` reads the\nserve log and refuses to let a measurement be taken against a stale bundle.\n\nWhole board 9.2 ms. 99 tests, all builds green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bafd25413121290ccbc9c1968fd4d60a645a5d0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/bafd25413121290ccbc9c1968fd4d60a645a5d0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/e250c1d16e87a8ee4c0779b7eaa039c5ad8b6dd8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/e250c1d16e87a8ee4c0779b7eaa039c5ad8b6dd8","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGUyNTBjMWQxNmU4N2E4ZWU0YzA3NzliN2VhYTAzOWM1YWQ4YjZkZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/674e8a462d643f6ec008dbc5231fe3eab734bb28","sha":"674e8a462d643f6ec008dbc5231fe3eab734bb28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/674e8a462d643f6ec008dbc5231fe3eab734bb28"}],"sha":"e250c1d16e87a8ee4c0779b7eaa039c5ad8b6dd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/e250c1d16e87a8ee4c0779b7eaa039c5ad8b6dd8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/674e8a462d643f6ec008dbc5231fe3eab734bb28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T04:55:32Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T04:55:32Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Measure the stalk instead of guessing it, and make the head a disc\n\nThird time on the clover, and the first two were the same mistake with\ndifferent numbers: reading the trim point off the silhouette. It cannot be read\noff the silhouette. A clover''s petiole runs up the middle *between* the two\nlower leaflets, so the moment the leaflets appear the cut is at full width\nwhile the stalk still has half its length to go. Any rule on extent trims to\nwhere the leaf gets wide, which is well below where the stalk stops — so a stub\nstayed on the card, the drawn stem ran into it, and the leaf had two stems.\n\nWhat separates them is coverage, not extent: a row of stalk is two per cent\nalpha and a row of leaf is eighty. `tools/foliage-trim.mjs` measures it off the\nsheet once and writes it into the table, so nothing at runtime decodes a PNG.\nThe first row reaching four fifths of a cut''s own peak coverage is its\njunction; on the three clover scans that is 0.425, 0.275 and 0.575, against\n0.167, 0.000 and 0.417 from the rule it replaces. Checked by cropping the\nsheet to the window each card would actually sample and looking at it, which is\nwhat should have settled this the first time.\n\nNode has no PNG decoder, so the tool borrows the headless Chrome the packer\nalready drives.\n\nThe daisy head is a dished disc now. A card is a strip growing from a root,\nwhich is what a leaf does; a head is a disc centred on the top of a stalk. Built\nas a card it hung off the stem by its bottom edge and vanished edge-on, which is\nwhat the crossed pair was covering for. It is a fan: one vertex on the stem, a\nring around it, the photograph mapped onto the circle inscribed in its cut-out,\nand the rim raised a little the way ray florets sit — so it has a silhouette\nfrom the side where a flat one had none, and it is attached to the stem rather\nthan beside it. Nine triangles against two, on five per cent of the sward.\n\nWhole board 8.5 ms. 99 tests, all builds green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4599fe57dd2dc1cda1b43661f95ecec6d8349bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/e4599fe57dd2dc1cda1b43661f95ecec6d8349bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/674e8a462d643f6ec008dbc5231fe3eab734bb28","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/674e8a462d643f6ec008dbc5231fe3eab734bb28","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDY3NGU4YTQ2MmQ2NDNmNmVjMDA4ZGJjNTIzMWZlM2VhYjczNGJiMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/be01d8b0746fb74910fc51e40f24cd3a6b842e0c","sha":"be01d8b0746fb74910fc51e40f24cd3a6b842e0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/be01d8b0746fb74910fc51e40f24cd3a6b842e0c"}],"sha":"674e8a462d643f6ec008dbc5231fe3eab734bb28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/674e8a462d643f6ec008dbc5231fe3eab734bb28"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/be01d8b0746fb74910fc51e40f24cd3a6b842e0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T04:43:56Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T04:43:56Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Trim the whole stalk, and one daisy head\n\nTwo easy outs, both called out, both replaced.\n\nThe stalk trim was under-cutting. It looked for the first row wider than a\nthird of the cut and then *backed off a sample* \"so the join survives\" — which\nis keeping exactly the thing being removed. Worse, a third is a constant, and\none of the three clover scans is a wide leaf whose second row is already past\nit: that cut trimmed nothing at all, so the drawn stem ran straight up into a\nphotographed petiole. Measured per cut, the old rule trimmed to t=0.167, 0.000\nand 0.417; against half of each cut''s own widest, with no backing off, it is\n0.250, 0.167 and 0.500.\n\nThe daisy''s crossed pair was the other one. It was there to guarantee a face at\nevery angle, and a crossed pair is two flat quads in an X, which is what it\nlooked like. A daisy head is a disc and the honest mesh for a disc carried on a\nphotograph is one card.\n\nWhat rescues the low angle is not a second quad, it is the field: ten thousand\nheads with a jittered azimuth each, so some are always turned toward the eye. A\nreal oxeye holds its face to the sky and is a white sliver from the side —\nerring that way errs the way the flower does. Sixty-six degrees over, nodding\nrather than perfectly flat, because flat is right for exactly one camera.\n\nTurning the head toward the eye per frame would be the third option and it is\nthe view-space thickening this renderer already removed once: it reads the eye\nposition, so the field rotates slightly on every zoom — visible immediately in\nuse and in no screenshot. The `cross` field is deleted rather than left unused.\n\nWhole board 7.0 ms. 99 tests, all builds green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"466b7f494695e17bade06930b033144c19f42240","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/466b7f494695e17bade06930b033144c19f42240"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/be01d8b0746fb74910fc51e40f24cd3a6b842e0c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/be01d8b0746fb74910fc51e40f24cd3a6b842e0c","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGJlMDFkOGIwNzQ2ZmI3NDkxMGZjNTFlNDBmMjRjZDNhNmI4NDJlMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/aede5d29fa94ca99aa8fdf39dfcd541624e07646","sha":"aede5d29fa94ca99aa8fdf39dfcd541624e07646","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/aede5d29fa94ca99aa8fdf39dfcd541624e07646"}],"sha":"be01d8b0746fb74910fc51e40f24cd3a6b842e0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/be01d8b0746fb74910fc51e40f24cd3a6b842e0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/aede5d29fa94ca99aa8fdf39dfcd541624e07646/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T04:30:03Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T04:30:03Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The clover is a mesh fix now, not a rotation\n\nLeaning the card was a rotation standing in for a mesh, and it deserved to be\ncalled out. The shape was diagnosed correctly — a trefoil flat on a petiole —\nand then implemented as fifty-four degrees, which is not flat, still reads\nwrong from above, and is edge-on from somewhere no matter what number goes in.\n\nThe reason the card could not simply be laid flat is that the scan has the\npetiole photographed into it. One quad carries leaf *and* stalk, so the leaf\ncannot lie down without its stalk lying down with it, and the only knob left is\nthe angle of the pair. Trimming the stalk off the bottom of the cut-out fixes\nthe actual problem: the card is then just the leaf, it lies flat, and the mesh\ndraws a real petiole under it out of the stem geometry that was already there.\n\nWhere the stalk ends is read from the silhouette rather than authored, because\nit differs per cut — of the three clover scans one has a long petiole, one a\nshort one and one almost none.\n\nThe daisy''s second flower was mine and it was a bug, not depth. A card roots at\nits position and grows upward, which is right for a leaf and wrong for a head:\ntwo crossed cards at different leans put their middles in different places, so\nthe pair read as two flowers side by side. Cards can be shifted back along\ntheir own axis now, and a head straddles its stem.\n\nThe panel is all the assets, not just the plants: the sward, the four scanned\nstanding plants and the seven fieldstones, each loaded into the panel''s own\nscene from the same glTF the board instances. The catalogues moved out of the\nfunctions that plant them so the panel shows what the board is actually made of\nrather than a second list that drifts.\n\nWhole board 7.5 ms. 99 tests, all builds green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cca0b99bc43b1cdd6395c32edfd3ff1e8084ee99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/cca0b99bc43b1cdd6395c32edfd3ff1e8084ee99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/aede5d29fa94ca99aa8fdf39dfcd541624e07646","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/aede5d29fa94ca99aa8fdf39dfcd541624e07646","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGFlZGU1ZDI5ZmE5NGNhOTlhYThmZGYzOWRmY2Q1NDE2MjRlMDc2NDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/86ca81481849d73b1d14d53bedf29752b4b633b7","sha":"86ca81481849d73b1d14d53bedf29752b4b633b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/86ca81481849d73b1d14d53bedf29752b4b633b7"}],"sha":"aede5d29fa94ca99aa8fdf39dfcd541624e07646","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/aede5d29fa94ca99aa8fdf39dfcd541624e07646"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/86ca81481849d73b1d14d53bedf29752b4b633b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T03:36:03Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T03:36:03Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The cards were clipping the pictures they carry\n\nThe oxeye daisy rendered as a white cigarette with a yellow stripe, and the\ncut-out on the sheet is a perfect photographed daisy — so the fault was never\nthe texture. A card is a quad strip fitted to the silhouette sampled once per\nrow, and with one row that is the outline at t=0 joined to the outline at t=1\nby a straight line. A daisy head is a disc: narrow at the bottom, widest in the\nmiddle, narrow again at the top. The quad came out forty-five per cent of the\nflower''s width and the mesh cut the petals off before the alpha test could see\nthem.\n\nThe shape of a cut-out comes from its alpha. All the geometry has to do is\ncontain it. So a row now takes the widest the silhouette gets anywhere in the\nband it covers, rather than its width at one point — the quad always covers the\npicture whatever the row count, and `rows` goes back to meaning how much the\ncard can bend rather than what shape it is. No extra triangles, and it fixes\nevery card at once rather than five hand-tuned numbers. The clover escaped the\nbug only because its own outline happens to reach the edges at both ends.\n\nWhite clover was held fifteen degrees off vertical, which is the one thing a\nclover leaf never does — it sits out flat on its petiole where the light is.\nIt also meant the board''s own camera, which looks down, was seeing the thinnest\npart of nearly a quarter of the sward. Fifty-four degrees now.\n\nA flower head is built as a crossed pair, and neither half is laid flat.\nPerfectly horizontal is right for exactly one camera and draws a hard black\nline from every other, because a card seen along its own plane is a sliver lit\nby a normal pointing away. Seventy-two degrees over and thirty-one over, a\nright angle apart, with a different cut for each so the pair reads as one head\nwith depth. Two triangles.\n\nThe panel is the Assets panel now and it is the instrument this should have\nbeen judged with all along: bigger preview, a fixed top / three-quarter / low /\nside rig instead of only a turntable, the turntable on a switch, and a table of\nevery card the plant is made of with any row count under three flagged. Top and\nlow are there because they are the two angles a card renderer fails at, and a\nturntable passes through both too fast to notice.\n\nBloom is off by default and still wired. Measured as a threshold sweep with the\npipeline left alone so nothing else moved between captures: noise floor 2.3,\nthreshold 0 moves 117, threshold 0.2 moves 36, and every threshold from 0.4 up\nsits at the noise floor. Nothing on a midday meadow exceeds about 0.4 luminance\nand everything else is just underneath it, so there is no highlight to separate\n— low enough to catch anything catches the whole frame. It stays for torches\nand fire.\n\nAnd the linter now reads Angular templates as well as shaders. The backtick\nthat closes a template literal has cost this project eight incidents; the\neighth was prose inside an HTML comment inside a component''s template, which\nfails identically and was not being looked at.\n\nWhole board 7.2 ms. 99 tests, all builds green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"64a60d397b21df415b86275d6b32b0788e218e69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/64a60d397b21df415b86275d6b32b0788e218e69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/86ca81481849d73b1d14d53bedf29752b4b633b7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/86ca81481849d73b1d14d53bedf29752b4b633b7","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDg2Y2E4MTQ4MTg0OWQ3M2IxZDE0ZDUzYmVkZjI5NzUyYjRiNjMzYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/ebdac9be18f149531018f3cd4aa6081dd9107955","sha":"ebdac9be18f149531018f3cd4aa6081dd9107955","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/ebdac9be18f149531018f3cd4aa6081dd9107955"}],"sha":"86ca81481849d73b1d14d53bedf29752b4b633b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/86ca81481849d73b1d14d53bedf29752b4b633b7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/ebdac9be18f149531018f3cd4aa6081dd9107955/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T03:09:32Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T03:09:32Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The board takes the whole window\n\nFour rows of controls used to stack above the canvas and push it down, so a\nthird of the screen was diagnostics about a picture you could not see. They are\none collapsible panel over the map now, remembered per browser, with the frame\ntime on its collapsed bar because that is the one number worth watching while\nyou drag a slider.\n\nThe dice rail goes with them. It is always-visible chrome on every ooze page,\nand a board is the one kind of page where always-visible chrome is wrong — it\ntakes a strip off the right of the thing the page exists to show. Declared on\nthe route as `full` rather than matched by path, so a page saying \"I am a map\"\nis a fact about that page and not a list of URLs kept in the shell.\n\nDark, and dark here rather than everywhere: the app''s tokens are redefined by a\n`.dark` class, so the board asks for it by wearing one. White chrome around a\nlit field is a lamp pointed at the viewer, and every judgement about the\npicture''s exposure was being made against it.\n\nSized to the visible viewport with `dvh`, minus `--ooze-shell-header` — 3.5rem\nunder the host''s bar, and zero standalone, which ooze''s own shell now says. The\nglobe does the same thing for the same reason. It has to be a `:host` rule and\nnot a class: Angular scopes a component''s styles with a content attribute and\nthe host carries a host attribute, so the class version matched nothing and the\nboard collapsed to zero height with the canvas still in it.\n\nFraming fits the window now instead of a constant tuned against the old short\ncanvas. Babylon''s fov is vertical, so a wide window is limited by height and a\ntall one by width, and the board''s on-screen footprint is its width by its\ndepth laid down — at a low angle the depth is foreshortened to nothing.\n\nPanning: shift-drag and the middle button join right-drag and ctrl-left, and an\norbit/pan pair in the corner for a trackpad with one button. This took two\ngoes. Babylon 9.26 replaced `panningMouseButton` and `useCtrlForPanning` with a\ndeclarative table on `camera.movement.input`, and writing the old properties is\na silent no-op — the first attempt appeared to work only because right-drag\npanning is in the default table and always was. Verified by dispatching each\ngesture and reading the camera a frame later: left orbits, shift-left, middle\nand right pan, pan mode swaps the left drag, and the target stops at 483 units\nfrom the board against a limit of 484.\n\n99 tests, all builds green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0990d6415e72d89232efe8cbd2478e2dbbf5cf9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/0990d6415e72d89232efe8cbd2478e2dbbf5cf9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/ebdac9be18f149531018f3cd4aa6081dd9107955","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/ebdac9be18f149531018f3cd4aa6081dd9107955","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGViZGFjOWJlMThmMTQ5NTMxMDE4ZjNjZDRhYTYwODFkZDkxMDc5NTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/c3a9b6531a33c8f5e976ef76527a20807ab758f5","sha":"c3a9b6531a33c8f5e976ef76527a20807ab758f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/c3a9b6531a33c8f5e976ef76527a20807ab758f5"}],"sha":"ebdac9be18f149531018f3cd4aa6081dd9107955","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/ebdac9be18f149531018f3cd4aa6081dd9107955"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/c3a9b6531a33c8f5e976ef76527a20807ab758f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T02:47:48Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T02:47:48Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Seven stones, seven different rocks\n\nEleven copies of the same boulder reads as eleven copies of the same boulder\nhowever they are rotated and scaled, so the count was never the whole problem.\n`scatterStone` is a short table of one-offs now rather than a count and a\nscatter: two in the open grass, five turned out along the verge, each one a\ndifferent rock.\n\nVariety turned out to be nearly free. `rock_moss_set_01` is six separate mossy\nrocks in one three-megabyte file at six thousand vertices each, which is what\nthis needed and what the two Karoo boulders could never be — they are desert\nscans and read orange under a Virginia sun. One stays for the colour break;\n`boulder_01` joins it with lichen on it. Seven stones now cost 125k vertices\nagainst the 500k eleven of two shapes were costing.\n\nSized by height, not width, which is the mistake that ate the first attempt.\nThe moss rocks are slabs about twice as wide as they are tall, so asking for a\nfour-foot stone got one under two feet high — and the sward stands over two\nfeet. Seven boulders went in and two could be seen. Measured proud of the\nground they are 4 to 4.5 feet for the pair in the grass and 2.5 for the rest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0be6a926241f15299ab5d720f332569327c55f6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/0be6a926241f15299ab5d720f332569327c55f6b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/c3a9b6531a33c8f5e976ef76527a20807ab758f5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/c3a9b6531a33c8f5e976ef76527a20807ab758f5","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGMzYTliNjUzMWEzM2M4ZjVlOTc2ZWY3NjUyN2EyMDgwN2FiNzU4ZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/c5286c58dc9ce4d9b241d7883631490614882323","sha":"c5286c58dc9ce4d9b241d7883631490614882323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/c5286c58dc9ce4d9b241d7883631490614882323"}],"sha":"c3a9b6531a33c8f5e976ef76527a20807ab758f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/c3a9b6531a33c8f5e976ef76527a20807ab758f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/c5286c58dc9ce4d9b241d7883631490614882323/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T02:32:52Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T02:32:52Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Four toggles that were lying, and the scale underneath them\n\nThe grade toggle did nothing because the grade was off board-wide.\n`DefaultRenderingPipeline.imageProcessingEnabled` is not a local flag — its\nsetter writes `scene.imageProcessingConfiguration.isEnabled`, which every PBR\nmaterial reads. Set false the day bloom shipped, it disabled tone mapping,\ncontrast, exposure and vignette everywhere, and the toggle has been flipping\nsettings on a configuration nothing applied ever since.\n\nBloom''s white wedge was the same bug seen from the other side. `SkyMaterial`\ndoes no image processing, so with the grade living inside each material the\natmosphere was the one surface in the frame nothing compressed — several times\nwhite, blurred, added back, clipped. Making the grade a post pass covers the\nsky and the wedge is gone with no change to bloom''s own settings.\n\nSky light was real and set to 0.14, from when the meadow read it too. The\nmeadow opts out now, so all it reaches is the ground, the stone and the trees —\nthe three things that were reading as flat cutouts. 0.45.\n\nVerified by pixel diff, on a capture taken inside `requestAnimationFrame`\nbecause a WebGPU canvas reads blank anywhere else: grade 11062 of 11200 pixels,\nsky light 8821, bloom 2340, shadows 8039, ground relief 8009, temporal aa 2181.\n\nThen the trees, which were three separate mistakes:\n\n`part` indexed primitives where it meant plants. A multi-primitive glTF node\nbecomes children named `<node>_primitiveN`, so the flat list runs bark, leaves,\ntwigs of the first plant and then of the second — indexing it picks a material.\nThe board has been showing five copies of one bush''s twigs and ten of another''s\nbark. That is the disconnected sticks.\n\n`MergeMeshes` builds its result in the scene already, so the `addMesh` after it\nput the tree in `scene.meshes` twice and every tree was drawn two times. 2.6 ms.\n\nAnd the scans are small plants. `island_tree_02` is 3.4 m, the biggest\n`searsia_lucida` is 2.3 m, and both were being asked for at eight and twelve\ntimes that — leaf density falls with the cube of it, which is the whole reason\nthe scrub was pale and see-through. They are used near their captured size now,\nand the shrub scan makes shrubs.\n\nTrees floated for two reasons and both are fixed: the rebase anchored on the\nbounding box, which stands a plant on its lowest drooping branch, and the\nplacement read `heightAt`, which is not the surface anybody sees — the terrain\nmesh has a vertex per half-foot and interpolates above the height field over\nruts. Anchored on the bark primitive''s base, placed on the lowest lattice\nsample under the footprint. Measured: every instance now sits 0.1 to 0.5 feet\nunder the highest ground beside it.\n\nStone: eleven, not twenty-six, both kinds placed in one pass so they cannot\nland on each other, and off the track rather than preferring it. The two\nidentical boulders in the middle of the road were two kinds placed separately\nwith nothing to stop them.\n\nWhole board 12.5 ms, trees 1.9 of it. 99 tests, all builds green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"20dcced5f8d63028424d482351e559c55b43a281","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/20dcced5f8d63028424d482351e559c55b43a281"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/c5286c58dc9ce4d9b241d7883631490614882323","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/c5286c58dc9ce4d9b241d7883631490614882323","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGM1Mjg2YzU4ZGM5Y2U0ZDliMjQxZDc4ODM2MzE0OTA2MTQ4ODIzMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/ad324bacd54eb6fc46cde1bd5027750446ba8365","sha":"ad324bacd54eb6fc46cde1bd5027750446ba8365","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/ad324bacd54eb6fc46cde1bd5027750446ba8365"}],"sha":"c5286c58dc9ce4d9b241d7883631490614882323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/c5286c58dc9ce4d9b241d7883631490614882323"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/ad324bacd54eb6fc46cde1bd5027750446ba8365/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T21:02:32Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T21:02:32Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"The board gets the rest of the year\n\nThe species table was one July mixture and the sun was the only thing that knew\na date. A map builder that can only make midsummer can only make one map, so\nthere is a season slider beside the clock now and it drives three things that\nare really one thing: where the sun rises and how high it gets, how green the\nsward is, and whether anything is in flower.\n\n**Two curves, not one.** Green peaks in late spring and decays through a dry\nAugust before the frosts take it; bloom is a narrow window around midsummer and\nnothing outside it. A single seasonal scalar gives a field that is greenest\nexactly when it is most in flower, which is a month wrong in both directions.\n\nThe season sits on top of the drift rather than replacing it — the drift decides\nwhich stand is ahead of which, and the season decides where they all are. And\nonly what carries a bloom keeps a flowering calendar: an oxeye daisy is out for\nsix weeks and absent the rest of the year, but grass goes brown without going\naway, and a clover mat is a mat in October.\n\nThe ground and the scanned trees are tinted along with it. They are photographs\nand cannot be re-shot, and a board where only the grass knows what month it is\nlooks worse than one where nothing does.\n\n**And it shipped a silently empty meadow for two builds.** `green` was read by\nthe sward''s height before it was declared for the sward''s colour, which WGSL\nrefuses — and the refusal is a shader that fails to compile, a compute pass that\nwrites nothing and a field with no grass in it, reported nowhere except the\nconsole. The linter does not catch declaration order. The console probe does,\nand is the reason this is the paragraph rather than the bug.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"afd46bb8d5b4167e30c6a4b6d2d8cddbcdce6fee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/afd46bb8d5b4167e30c6a4b6d2d8cddbcdce6fee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/ad324bacd54eb6fc46cde1bd5027750446ba8365","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/ad324bacd54eb6fc46cde1bd5027750446ba8365","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGFkMzI0YmFjZDU0ZWI2ZmM0NmNkZTFiZDUwMjc3NTA0NDZiYTgzNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/022c0163fe8817c3f864abee845a0cc55d2af60d","sha":"022c0163fe8817c3f864abee845a0cc55d2af60d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/022c0163fe8817c3f864abee845a0cc55d2af60d"}],"sha":"ad324bacd54eb6fc46cde1bd5027750446ba8365","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/ad324bacd54eb6fc46cde1bd5027750446ba8365"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/022c0163fe8817c3f864abee845a0cc55d2af60d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:52:27Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:52:27Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Volumetric scattering, and a cheaper meadow material, both measured and both refused\n\nEvery screen-space effect refused on this board was refused for needing the\nscene rendered a second time, and god rays looked like the exception: the\npipeline renders *occluders* into a fifth-resolution buffer with a black\nmaterial, not the whole scene. It is not the exception. Installed and drawing\nnothing — noon, sun off screen — the frame went from 15.7 ms to 22.9. The pass\nruns whatever the sun is doing.\n\nIt did not look right either. With the sky box as the light''s stand-in the whole\nframe floods white rather than throwing shafts, because the occluder is the\nthing the rays are meant to come from and the sky is not an object.\n\nAnd the cheaper meadow material is off the plan, on its own arithmetic. The\nthree milliseconds it promised came from unlit costing 2.78 against 7.26 — and\nthat gap was image-based lighting and fog, both since removed. Measured again\nwith them gone: the meadow costs 4.7 ms and unlit is 2.0 below it, so 2.0 is the\nceiling and a material that still lights anything sees less. None of PBR''s own\ncheaper switches move it either — energy conservation, the correlated visibility\nterm, physical light falloff, translucency and the specular highlight together\nmeasured inside the noise.\n\nWhich leaves the refused table as the most useful thing in the plan, and the\nboard where it is.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef742a17544b02a34ff9fa89168e0061df91934f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/ef742a17544b02a34ff9fa89168e0061df91934f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/022c0163fe8817c3f864abee845a0cc55d2af60d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/022c0163fe8817c3f864abee845a0cc55d2af60d","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKDAyMmMwMTYzZmU4ODE3YzNmODY0YWJlZTg0NWEwY2M1NWQyYWY2MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/a35e2c975acb48e4bca81817bcece23b476c6f7a","sha":"a35e2c975acb48e4bca81817bcece23b476c6f7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a35e2c975acb48e4bca81817bcece23b476c6f7a"}],"sha":"022c0163fe8817c3f864abee845a0cc55d2af60d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/022c0163fe8817c3f864abee845a0cc55d2af60d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a35e2c975acb48e4bca81817bcece23b476c6f7a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:47:29Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:47:29Z","email":"griff.tatarsky@unacast.com","name":"Griff"},"message":"Bloom, measured, at a quarter resolution\n\nThe one thing a low sun over a field actually does is spill light around the\nbright edges of things, and nothing else in the default pipeline is wanted here:\nits anti-aliasing is already done better by the temporal resolve, and depth of\nfield, grain and chromatic aberration are filters on a board that wants to be\nread rather than photographed.\n\nAt half resolution it measured 1.8 ms, which is more than the sun costs, for an\neffect that only appears at dusk. A blur of a blur is the same blur, so it runs\nat a quarter now: 1.2 ms. High threshold as well — almost nothing on a meadow is\nbright enough to bloom, and a low threshold blooms the whole field into soup.\n\nIt has its own switch, like everything else now.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f57132a2ecb7f2903bddcf5b118076e63ccab202","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/trees/f57132a2ecb7f2903bddcf5b118076e63ccab202"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/git/commits/a35e2c975acb48e4bca81817bcece23b476c6f7a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/297998085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gt-una","id":297998085,"login":"gt-una","node_id":"U_kgDOEcMXBQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gt-una","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/a35e2c975acb48e4bca81817bcece23b476c6f7a","node_id":"C_kwDONOaLmdoAKGEzNWUyYzk3NWFjYjQ4ZTRiY2E4MTgxN2JjZWNlMjNiNDc2YzZmN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commit/83a1c8388725a99658c0b26cc1ff8dccafb6dde6","sha":"83a1c8388725a99658c0b26cc1ff8dccafb6dde6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/83a1c8388725a99658c0b26cc1ff8dccafb6dde6"}],"sha":"a35e2c975acb48e4bca81817bcece23b476c6f7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits/a35e2c975acb48e4bca81817bcece23b476c6f7a"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/grifftatarsky/akira-platform/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=5acde531e22ff2f25b35ff3a4739d001500da1aa&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T15%3A53%3A33.