-publish-all/commits/d03eadd6cc668d15b125a2fe3619c7f774cf73ff"}],"sha":"4bf4c7cd062b7dbde72879d391851ae424218371","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/force-publish-all/commits/4bf4c7cd062b7dbde72879d391851ae424218371"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/force-publish-all/commits/d03eadd6cc668d15b125a2fe3619c7f774cf73ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T17:31:35Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T17:31:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Harden force-publish-all: security, error handling, AAA accessibility, tests (#10)\n\n* fix: harden ForcePublication — security, error handling, null-safety, tests\n\nCRITICAL-1: Selective RepositoryException handling in live-delete\n- Only ItemNotFoundException/PathNotFoundException are silently ignored\n  (node not yet in LIVE is expected); any other RepositoryException is\n  logged with UUID+path context and aborts — the publication job is NOT\n  scheduled when live-delete fails.\n\nCRITICAL-2: Correct error log in catch block\n- Replaced logger.error(PERMISSION_PUBLISH) (logged the literal string\n  \"publish\", dropped the exception) with\n  logger.error(\"Force publication failed for path {}\", path, e) so\n  the full stack trace is captured.\n\nCRITICAL-3: Null-check OSGi services\n- BundleUtils.getOsgiService() for ComplexPublicationService and\n  SchedulerService can return null. Both are now null-checked; a\n  descriptive JahiaRuntimeException is thrown if either is absent.\n\nSECURITY (HIGH): Dual-permission gate\n- Mutation now requires both ''publish'' AND ''site-admin'' node-level\n  permissions (matching requiredPermission: [''publish'',''site-admin'']\n  declared in ForcePublishAllComponent.jsx). AccessDeniedException is\n  thrown with the permission name and node path for each missing right.\n\nHIGH: nodeMutation field made private final.\n\nMEDIUM:\n- validateNodeWorkspace changed from protected to private (class is final)\n- Javadoc on forcePublish() rewritten to describe delete-then-republish\n  semantics, required permissions, DESTRUCTIVE note, and thrown exceptions\n- \"Publication\" job label extracted to named constant JOB_LABEL_PUBLICATION\n- getCurrentUserSession now uses explicit Constants.EDIT_WORKSPACE arg\n- PERMISSION_PUBLISH constant no longer reused as error/exception message\n- getAllUuids changed from private to package-private (with comment) to\n  enable direct unit testing without reflection\n\nTESTS (HIGH): new src/test tree with 11 JUnit 5 unit tests\n- Covers: empty input, DELETED exclusion, mixed statuses, node identifier\n  null handling, translation node identifier null handling, deleted\n  translation identifiers, all identifiers combined, multi-node order\n- Mockito 5.12.0 + junit-jupiter 5.10.5 added as test-scoped deps\n- maven-surefire-plugin 3.2.5 configured for JUnit Platform\n- java-only Maven profile added to skip frontend build during test runs\n\nREADME.md: documented required permissions, DESTRUCTIVE behavior,\npublication-workflow bypass, and failure/rollback behavior.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: harden force-publish-all UI, a11y, i18n and lint/test setup\n\n- split Cancel/Confirm so cancelling no longer fires the publish mutation\n- add mutation error handling + loading guard against double-submit\n- WCAG 2.2 AAA: alertdialog role, live region, focus return, button types, i18n (en/fr)\n- finalize ForcePublication catch (rethrow with context, no log+rethrow; S2139)\n- remove console.log, dead SCSS, unused deps; fix data-cm-role and description typo\n- add eslint config + jest setup with 6 component tests\n- keep Yarn classic lockfile; gitignore Yarn Berry/coverage byproducts\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review — drive isLoading via setProperties, a11y + lint toolchain\n\n- isLoading now pushed through componentRenderer.setProperties during the\n  mutation so the Confirm button actually disables (prevents double-submit)\n- aria-describedby now references both the consequence and the path paragraph\n- update jest assertions for the new isLoading patch in error paths\n- pin internal-slot ^1.1.0 to fix react/boolean-prop-naming rule crash under\n  the @jahia/eslint-config tree (es-iterator-helpers GeneratorState)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"da901a55df9f3c24bb1e850d45d71994b295428d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/force-publish-all/git/trees/da901a55df9f3c24bb1e850d45d71994b295428d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/force-publish-all/git/commits/d03eadd6cc668d15b125a2fe3619c7f774cf73ff","verification":{"payload":"tree da901a55df9f3c24bb1e850d45d71994b295428d\nparent 4b474afc87bd4066c555f8e6a2a758131dd1693e\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781976695 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781976695 +0200\n\nHarden force-publish-all: security, error handling, AAA accessibility, tests (#10)\n\n* fix: harden ForcePublication — security, error handling, null-safety, tests\n\nCRITICAL-1: Selective RepositoryException handling in live-delete\n- Only ItemNotFoundException/PathNotFoundException are silently ignored\n  (node not yet in LIVE is expected); any other RepositoryException is\n  logged with UUID+path context and aborts — the publication job is NOT\n  scheduled when live-delete fails.\n\nCRITICAL-2: Correct error log in catch block\n- Replaced logger.error(PERMISSION_PUBLISH) (logged the literal string\n  \"publish\", dropped the exception) with\n  logger.error(\"Force publication failed for path {}\", path, e) so\n  the full stack trace is captured.\n\nCRITICAL-3: Null-check OSGi services\n- BundleUtils.getOsgiService() for ComplexPublicationService and\n  SchedulerService can return null. Both are now null-checked; a\n  descriptive JahiaRuntimeException is thrown if either is absent.\n\nSECURITY (HIGH): Dual-permission gate\n- Mutation now requires both ''publish'' AND ''site-admin'' node-level\n  permissions (matching requiredPermission: [''publish'',''site-admin'']\n  declared in ForcePublishAllComponent.jsx). AccessDeniedException is\n  thrown with the permission name and node path for each missing right.\n\nHIGH: nodeMutation field made private final.\n\nMEDIUM:\n- validateNodeWorkspace changed from protected to private (class is final)\n- Javadoc on forcePublish() rewritten to describe delete-then-republish\n  semantics, required permissions, DESTRUCTIVE note, and thrown exceptions\n- \"Publication\" job label extracted to named constant JOB_LABEL_PUBLICATION\n- getCurrentUserSession now uses explicit Constants.EDIT_WORKSPACE arg\n- PERMISSION_PUBLISH constant no longer reused as error/exception message\n- getAllUuids changed from private to package-private (with comment) to\n  enable direct unit testing without reflection\n\nTESTS (HIGH): new src/test tree with 11 JUnit 5 unit tests\n- Covers: empty input, DELETED exclusion, mixed statuses, node identifier\n  null handling, translation node identifier null handling, deleted\n  translation identifiers, all identifiers combined, multi-node order\n- Mockito 5.12.0 + junit-jupiter 5.10.5 added as test-scoped deps\n- maven-surefire-plugin 3.2.5 configured for JUnit Platform\n- java-only Maven profile added to skip frontend build during test runs\n\nREADME.md: documented required permissions, DESTRUCTIVE behavior,\npublication-workflow bypass, and failure/rollback behavior.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: harden force-publish-all UI, a11y, i18n and lint/test setup\n\n- split Cancel/Confirm so cancelling no longer fires the publish mutation\n- add mutation error handling + loading guard against double-submit\n- WCAG 2.2 AAA: alertdialog role, live region, focus return, button types, i18n (en/fr)\n- finalize ForcePublication catch (rethrow with context, no log+rethrow; S2139)\n- remove console.log, dead SCSS, unused deps; fix data-cm-role and description typo\n- add eslint config + jest setup with 6 component tests\n- keep Yarn classic lockfile; gitignore Yarn Berry/coverage byproducts\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR review — drive isLoading via setProperties, a11y + lint toolchain\n\n- isLoading now pushed through componentRenderer.setProperties during the\n  mutation so the Confirm button actually disables (prevents double-submit)\n- aria-describedby now references both the consequence and the path paragraph\n- update jest assertions for the new isLoading patch in error paths\n- pin internal-slot ^1.1.0 to fix react/boolean-prop-naming rule crash under\n  the @jahia/eslint-config tree (es-iterator-helpers GeneratorState)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGI