ams/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevwilliams","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/compute/commits/d432ce0ed1c7c6272e88b69bf844062c5a15a693/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T18:55:08Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T18:55:08Z","email":"kwilliams@datum.net","name":"Kevin"},"message":"feat(ui): Two-column workload overview and instance pages for staff\n\nThe provider plugin''s workload Overview repeated replica counts across a\nstat strip and two cards, showed metric tiles with no history, and gave\ninstances only a flat table with no page of their own.\n\nOverview now leads with a Needs attention card (non-True conditions,\nfailed or long-pending instances, scheduling gates) shown only when\nsomething is wrong. Below it, a main column holds CPU, memory, request\nrate and p99 latency cards with last-hour sparklines, an instance table\nwith per-instance CPU and memory, and conditions with healthy ones\nhidden. A side column merges General and Configuration into one Details\ncard with copy buttons, plus an Endpoint card.\n\nInstance names link to a new InstanceDetail page at\n:workloadName/instances/:instanceName with the instance''s own metrics,\nstatus message, conditions, details, network addresses, and logs.\n\nMetric cards say No data when a query returns no series, because the\nstaff-portal metrics route turns an empty result into 0. The sparkline\ncomponents are ported from ui/consumer. The page root uses inline-size\ncontainment so long rows scroll inside their card instead of widening\nthe host page.","tree":{"sha":"8047b08a9c0683040af5b466ac1663badf671fc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/compute/git/trees/8047b08a9c0683040af5b466ac1663badf671fc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/compute/git/commits/d432ce0ed1c7c6272e88b69bf844062c5a15a693","verification":{"payload":"tree 8047b08a9c0683040af5b466ac1663badf671fc3\nparent 1f8a5df07185952736eb49a3c71ba2cc0bf44e4e\nauthor Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1791399308 -0700\ncommitter Kevin <kwilliams@datum.net> 1791399308 -0700\n\nfeat(ui): Two-column workload overview and instance pages for staff\n\nThe provider plugin''s workload Overview repeated replica counts across a\nstat strip and two cards, showed metric tiles with no history, and gave\ninstances only a flat table with no page of their own.\n\nOverview now leads with a Needs attention card (non-True conditions,\nfailed or long-pending instances, scheduling gates) shown only when\nsomething is wrong. Below it, a main column holds CPU, memory, request\nrate and p99 latency cards with last-hour sparklines, an instance table\nwith per-instance CPU and memory, and conditions with healthy ones\nhidden. A side column merges General and Configuration into one Details\ncard with copy buttons, plus an Endpoint card.\n\nInstance names link to a new InstanceDetail page at\n:workloadName/instances/:instanceName with the instance''s own metrics,\nstatus message, conditions, details, network addresses, and logs.\n\nMetric cards say No data when a query returns no series, because the\nstaff-portal metrics route turns an empty result into 0. The sparkline\ncomponents are ported from ui/consumer. The page root uses inline-size\ncontainment so long rows scroll inside their card instead of widening\nthe host page.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEEb8FNfGdgytwOrlKr53J8QGQJ2j0FAmrGlYwACgkQ53J8QGQJ\n2j0vKBAAncKhDJx3/FOKnhtMaRkQojlvUdGuCV2fYnixvzJ712fDqBE5vIsBS0DO\ndmPJC/h931Npb0L0xrQcXevlJTUtoCek9Sqq2xBY6