},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6007097?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/scotwells","id":6007097,"login":"scotwells","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDcwOTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scotwells","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/compute/commits/70e5917dd023903560c2b43c03e754b76ad42c7b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T21:49:07Z","email":"wells.scot@gmail.com","name":"Scot Wells"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T21:49:07Z","email":"wells.scot@gmail.com","name":"Scot Wells"},"message":"fix: Require a click before a shell window runs a command\n\nThe shell window connected as soon as it opened with a container and a\ncommand in its URL, so anyone who could get a signed-in user to open a\ncrafted link could run a command in that user''s instance.\n\nA link''s container and command now only fill in the start panel, and the\nuser has to click Connect. The window connects at once only for a hand-off\nfrom the user''s own tab: Open in new window records a random nonce, the\ncontainer, the command and a 30-second expiry in this browser''s storage,\nand opens the window with the nonce alone. The window reads the record\nonce, deletes it, and takes the container and command from it.\n\nKey changes:\n- Carry only a one-time nonce in the window URL\n- Ignore a nonce that is unknown, replayed, expired or for another\n  instance, and fall back to prefilling the panel\n- Prune expired hand-offs, and discard one whose popup was blocked\n- Test crafted links, valid hand-offs, replays, expiry and the instance\n  check","tree":{"sha":"46ed506e055eea962e22fa31adc8552de6f66d66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/compute/git/trees/46ed506e055eea962e22fa31adc8552de6f66d66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/datum-cloud/compute/git/commits/70e5917dd023903560c2b43c03e754b76ad42c7b","verification":{"payload":"tree 46ed506e055eea962e22fa31adc8552de6f66d66\nparent c8d03592d03e0e2e6390f36ba88bca48b7d21fee\nauthor Scot Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1790804947 -0500\ncommitter Scot Wells <wells.scot@gmail.com> 1790804947 -0500\n\nfix: Require a click before a shell window runs a command\n\nThe shell window connected as soon as it opened with a container and a\ncommand in its URL, so anyone who could get a signed-in user to open a\ncrafted link could run a command in that user''s instance.\n\nA link''s container and command now only fill in the start panel, and the\nuser has to click Connect. The window connects at once only for a hand-off\nfrom the user''s own tab: Open in new window records a random nonce, the\ncontainer, the command and a 30-second expiry in this browser''s storage,\nand opens the window with the nonce alone. The window reads the record\nonce, deletes it, and takes the container and command from it.\n\nKey changes:\n- Carry only a one-time nonce in the window URL\n- Ignore a nonce that is unknown, replayed, expired or for another\n  instance, and fall back to prefilling the panel\n- Prune expired hand-offs, and discard one whose popup was blocked\n- Test crafted links, valid hand-offs, replays, expiry and the instance\n  check\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQR/ozPp/oJ2P+NplhUmO