e_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/26e48d5d5e0b5a9d467384ad2b894ec5a8c8fd76","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDI2ZTQ4ZDVkNWUwYjVhOWQ0NjczODRhZDJiODk0ZWM1YThjOGZkNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/e8c6206e59aa53e3747b830ce8eac7ed947c2d22","sha":"e8c6206e59aa53e3747b830ce8eac7ed947c2d22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/e8c6206e59aa53e3747b830ce8eac7ed947c2d22"}],"sha":"26e48d5d5e0b5a9d467384ad2b894ec5a8c8fd76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/26e48d5d5e0b5a9d467384ad2b894ec5a8c8fd76"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/e8c6206e59aa53e3747b830ce8eac7ed947c2d22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:20:17Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:20:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Assessment: Allow coaches and lecturers to assess students independently (#2269)\n\n* Add opt-in independent assessment flag and table to the assessment service\n\nAdds independent_assessment (one score per student, competency and\nassessor) and the per-phase independent_assessment_enabled flag, off by\ndefault. An omitted flag in a config PUT keeps the stored value, the copy\nendpoint carries it over, and RequireIndependentAssessmentEnabled guards\nwrites that need it.\n\n* Let coaches and lecturers score students independently\n\nAdds POST /student-assessment/independent for Editors and Lecturers on\nphases that opted in. Each assessor keeps one score per competency, the\nauthor and phase come from the token and URL, and the scores freeze once\nthe final assessment is marked final.\n\nGET /student-assessment/:id now returns every assessor''s independent\nscores plus the caller''s own, which the client needs because it has no\nKeycloak user id. Privacy export and deletion cover the new table.\nIndependent scores count as assessment data for shared schemas, so a\nschema edit copies the schema for the phase and remaps the scores\ninstead of cascading them away.\n\n* Add the independent assessments switch to the assessment settings\n\nLecturers opt a phase in from the \"Assessment workflow\" section. The\n\"Show evaluation results before submission\" description now mentions\nthat it also reveals other assessors'' independent scores.\n\n* Add \"My assessment\" and \"Final assessment\" tabs to the participant page\n\nOn phases with independent assessments, the participant page opens on\n\"My assessment\", where the assessor scores the student without seeing\nanyone else''s input. \"Final assessment\" is the existing page plus one\nicon per score level listing the assessors who picked it, gated by the\nsame visibility rule as the self and peer icons. Without the opt-in the\npage is unchanged.\n\nAlso types the save hook''s error instead of using any.\n\n* Document independent assessments in the assessment guide\n\n* Reject scores for competencies outside the phase''s assessment schema\n\nMap completed and not-yet-started assessments to 409 instead of 500 on\nboth score routes.\n\n* Hide score indicators while switching participants\n\nThe disabled state during a participant switch showed the previous\nparticipant''s self, peer and independent scores before finalization.","tree":{"sha":"a8107c8e35f93d26e0edfd8aa379fa2f991ca6db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/a8107c8e35f93d26e0edfd8aa379fa2f991ca6db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/e8c6206e59aa53e3747b830ce8eac7ed947c2d22","verification":{"payload":"tree a8107c8e35f93d26e0edfd8aa379fa2f991ca6db\nparent f0df7cd8b7e0114904b618512b6bb05add66d013\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791184817 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791184817 +0000\n\nAssessment: Allow coaches and lecturers to assess students independently (#2269)\n\n* Add opt-in independent assessment flag and table to the assessment service\n\nAdds independent_assessment (one score per student, competency and\nassessor) and the per-phase independent_assessment_enabled flag, off by\ndefault. An omitted flag in a config PUT keeps the stored value, the copy\nendpoint carries it over, and RequireIndependentAssessmentEnabled guards\nwrites that need it.\n\n* Let coaches and lecturers score students independently\n\nAdds POST /student-assessment/independent for Editors and Lecturers on\nphases that opted in. Each assessor keeps one score per competency, the\nauthor and phase come from the token and URL, and the scores freeze once\nthe final assessment is marked final.\n\nGET /student-assessment/:id now returns every assessor''s independent\nscores plus the caller''s own, which the client needs because it has no\nKeycloak user id. Privacy export and deletion cover the new table.\nIndependent scores count as assessment data for shared schemas, so a\nschema edit copies the schema for the phase and remaps the scores\ninstead of cascading them away.\n\n* Add the independent assessments switch to the assessment settings\n\nLecturers opt a phase in from the \"Assessment workflow\" section. The\n\"Show evaluation results before submission\" description now mentions\nthat it also reveals other assessors'' independent scores.\n\n* Add \"My assessment\" and \"Final assessment\" tabs to the participant page\n\nOn phases with independent assessments, the participant page opens on\n\"My assessment\", where the assessor scores the student without seeing\nanyone else''s input. \"Final assessment\" is the existing page plus one\nicon per score level listing the assessors who picked it, gated by the\nsame visibility rule as the self and peer icons. Without the opt-in the\npage is unchanged.\n\nAlso types the save hook''s error instead of using any.\n\n* Document independent assessments in the assessment guide\n\n* Reject scores for competencies outside the phase''s assessment schema\n\nMap completed and not-yet-started assessments to 409 instead of 500 on\nboth score routes.\n\n* Hide score indicators while switching participants\n\nThe disabled state during a participant switch showed the previous\nparticipant''s self, peer and independent scores before finalization.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw0+xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5vwQACqW6UF/6e7J1/BgWPJjaZeI\nTkWplYjksF9XMxPMhlT5hlbLFdPovaeTPhXHkZ2Ib2lF7HcS5Ta5ATyhdLliC2qS\nuXzN/SsI62kBYe8P8+Bwt4XwusM/1mD+cvv1u1ShG/f6x/4slI7CRT9yfta2KBtc\neG0y7geoFb149rmBct8kYUgKxVba7tx7IJwbw1FEEnYaTwteFh+jh2H7kFc6kOU8\nexNk7Za7fOwF3ifJKrATfMSsHUz3RAZFOoLqgog6DAsQ7nQbpQhPFA3Cd13eG0p1\nBV/hBVvAmQiUE8F7ffYVb6I274nURdakRtYFNocQkhgPBhY6ZfoMLlhF4G/dkQMp\ntLxqjud6UfclVOsKcMZsIhZjFMjVExrG3ciC/x3uZL+3SLo9yvIUeSwy9uweS4eA\nOAH7NCZwsfseLeMl74R2IOqVNRGPqatOP+uida9j4njN6k3aFl2fbGh61NHYO756\nMlV0QQIBkZ61klxnpLfUMCO2YV9CYBYGNjYlm6GZn13tSU5z9mYm3bssMqtEcz4N\nshlrbwQDOFrdHkTy1mQRMuk4TlevOyL2b7qeWOPoyC2VRsWmVHfwPW04HLTkLCu+\npzJgwV8Sx6szhXD78sOe13BxxUrnjpXuQhk1uvf8s6xOLGhSvK0E5v5Z/z6/VuZC\nwtjxwjr2vq3W7hwZ9Fdg\n=kCNg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T07:20:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/e8c6206e59aa53e3747b830ce8eac7ed947c2d22","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKGU4YzYyMDZlNTlhYTUzZTM3NDdiODMwY2U4ZWFjN2VkOTQ3YzJkMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/f0df7cd8b7e0114904b618512b6bb05add66d013","sha":"f0df7cd8b7e0114904b618512b6bb05add66d013","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/f0df7cd8b7e0114904b618512b6bb05add66d013"}],"sha":"e8c6206e59aa53e3747b830ce8eac7ed947c2d22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/e8c6206e59aa53e3747b830ce8eac7ed947c2d22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/f0df7cd8b7e0114904b618512b6bb05add66d013/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:02:04Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:02:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Application: Fix file upload answers accepting files from other course phases (#2257)\n\n* Core: Trim trailing whitespace in the application queries and test dump\n\nWhitespace only, so the next commit''s query change stays readable.\n\n* Application: Only accept file answers for files uploaded to the course phase in the URL\n\nThe answer stored the fileID from the body unchecked, so it could reference any file and return its download URL. The upsert now selects the file and question joined on the URL phase, skips soft-deleted files and, for applicants, matches the uploader: the token user on the authenticated route and the external uploader on the public one. A file that does not match is rejected with 400, and resubmitting an unchanged answer is a no-op. The unscoped CreateApplicationAnswerFileUpload query had no callers and is removed.\n\n* Application: Accept phase files on the public route and make the uploader scope explicit\n\nThe public apply route has no user identity, and a logged-in user filling\nthe public form uploads through the authenticated route, so the file is\nstored with their user id instead of the shared external uploader. Scope\npublic file answers to the course phase in the URL only.\n\nReplace the pgtype.Text uploader parameter with a fileUploader value built\nby uploadedBy or anyUploaderInPhase. Its zero value matches no file, so a\nnew caller cannot turn the uploader check off by accident.\n\nAdd tests for soft-deleted files, for the public route accepting a file of\na logged-in uploader, and for the zero-value uploader.\n\n* Application: Reject an empty uploader instead of matching anonymized files\n\nPrivacy deletion sets uploaded_by_user_id to an empty string, so uploadedBy(\"\") and the zero value still matched a deleted user''s leftover files in the phase.\n\n* Application: Keep a replaced file while another answer still references it\n\nThe answer foreign key cascades on file deletion, so hard-deleting a replaced file also deleted every other answer that pointed at it.","tree":{"sha":"2797f53ed290996e59f2cda40e4441e27fb1cd79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/2797f53ed290996e59f2cda40e4441e27fb1cd79"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/f0df7cd8b7e0114904b618512b6bb05add66d013","verification":{"payload":"tree 2797f53ed290996e59f2cda40e4441e27fb1cd79\nparent 541da8a67dea5d3c384422fcdeac32567de71663\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791183724 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791183724 +0200\n\nApplication: Fix file upload answers accepting files from other course phases (#2257)\n\n* Core: Trim trailing whitespace in the application queries and test dump\n\nWhitespace only, so the next commit''s query change stays readable.\n\n* Application: Only accept file answers for files uploaded to the course phase in the URL\n\nThe answer stored the fileID from the body unchecked, so it could reference any file and return its download URL. The upsert now selects the file and question joined on the URL phase, skips soft-deleted files and, for applicants, matches the uploader: the token user on the authenticated route and the external uploader on the public one. A file that does not match is rejected with 400, and resubmitting an unchanged answer is a no-op. The unscoped CreateApplicationAnswerFileUpload query had no callers and is removed.\n\n* Application: Accept phase files on the public route and make the uploader scope explicit\n\nThe public apply route has no user identity, and a logged-in user filling\nthe public form uploads through the authenticated route, so the file is\nstored with their user id instead of the shared external uploader. Scope\npublic file answers to the course phase in the URL only.\n\nReplace the pgtype.Text uploader parameter with a fileUploader value built\nby uploadedBy or anyUploaderInPhase. Its zero value matches no file, so a\nnew caller cannot turn the uploader check off by accident.\n\nAdd tests for soft-deleted files, for the public route accepting a file of\na logged-in uploader, and for the zero-value uploader.\n\n* Application: Reject an empty uploader instead of matching anonymized files\n\nPrivacy deletion sets uploaded_by_user_id to an empty string, so uploadedBy(\"\") and the zero value still matched a deleted user''s leftover files in the phase.\n\n* Application: Keep a replaced file while another answer still references it\n\nThe answer foreign key cascades on file deletion, so hard-deleting a replaced file also deleted every other answer that pointed at it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw0tsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjDwQAEeQfBPA+UZKreaWvmr4UdJe\nCY+NQacuWooOGgLAayQzRdbvUnwI/DsfBWHbLALdE5TvPgRUPhTadq