","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/541da8a67dea5d3c384422fcdeac32567de71663","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDU0MWRhOGE2N2RlYTVkM2MzODQ0MjJmY2RlYWMzMjU2N2RlNzE2NjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/e9ce54d7747242258079a8fb80d116355fd864f0","sha":"e9ce54d7747242258079a8fb80d116355fd864f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/e9ce54d7747242258079a8fb80d116355fd864f0"}],"sha":"541da8a67dea5d3c384422fcdeac32567de71663","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/541da8a67dea5d3c384422fcdeac32567de71663"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169448471?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mathildeshagl","id":169448471,"login":"mathildeshagl","node_id":"U_kgDOChmUFw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/e9ce54d7747242258079a8fb80d116355fd864f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T23:52:09Z","email":"mathilde.s.hagl@tum.de","name":"Mathilde Hagl"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T23:52:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Interview: Merge Manage Interviews into a clickable Participants table (#2260)\n\n* Interview: Merge Manage Interviews into a clickable Participants table\n\nThe Participants table now shows each interviewee''s slot, location,\napplication score, interview score and a link to the application, with\nsorting and filters for the slot day and both scores. Clicking a row opens\nthe interview profile, which moves to /participants/:studentId.\n\nManage Interviews is removed from the sidebar together with its card grid\nand sort dropdown, and the old /manage URLs redirect to the new pages.\n\n* Interview: Build the profile link from the route params\n\nOpening a participant from the table appended the student id to the current\npathname, so on a URL with a trailing slash Cmd/Ctrl-click opened\n/participants//<id>, which matches no route. Build the target from the\ncourse and phase ids instead, the same way the /manage redirects do.\n\n* Core: Show the participant''s name in profile breadcrumbs\n\nThe last crumb of a participant page fell back to \"Participant\" unless the\nApplication phase had loaded its participations, and it only matched\ncourse participation ids. Interview profiles are keyed by student id, so\nthey never showed a name.\n\nBreadcrumbs now also read the phase''s participations from the shared query\ncache, without fetching them, and match the segment against both the\ncourse participation id and the student id.","tree":{"sha":"acac607bc0114ffcebbfd169e939de727e5ee00c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/acac607bc0114ffcebbfd169e939de727e5ee00c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/e9ce54d7747242258079a8fb80d116355fd864f0","verification":{"payload":"tree acac607bc0114ffcebbfd169e939de727e5ee00c\nparent 61b3f512671969ade257b68164eed01113f7ceef\nauthor Mathilde Hagl <mathilde.s.hagl@tum.de> 1791157929 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791157929 +0000\n\nInterview: Merge Manage Interviews into a clickable Participants table (#2260)\n\n* Interview: Merge Manage Interviews into a clickable Participants table\n\nThe Participants table now shows each interviewee''s slot, location,\napplication score, interview score and a link to the application, with\nsorting and filters for the slot day and both scores. Clicking a row opens\nthe interview profile, which moves to /participants/:studentId.\n\nManage Interviews is removed from the sidebar together with its card grid\nand sort dropdown, and the old /manage URLs redirect to the new pages.\n\n* Interview: Build the profile link from the route params\n\nOpening a participant from the table appended the student id to the current\npathname, so on a URL with a trailing slash Cmd/Ctrl-click opened\n/participants//<id>, which matches no route. Build the target from the\ncourse and phase ids instead, the same way the /manage redirects do.\n\n* Core: Show the participant''s name in profile breadcrumbs\n\nThe last crumb of a participant page fell back to \"Participant\" unless the\nApplication phase had loaded its participations, and it only matched\ncourse participation ids. Interview profiles are keyed by student id, so\nthey never showed a name.\n\nBreadcrumbs now also read the phase''s participations from the shared query\ncache, without fetching them, and match the segment against both the\ncourse participation id and the student id.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwuapCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIRYQAK1hYccnMt4RzHdAWMKxPK5H\n6OLGmZGa5UZg9w2s+rLojBt+sFnH50gkBxOtfP5jEY8Aa6cON9GZ9wpo2exIMoo8\n41yptle8W45hSkku3i05e/SfDb74faF9siaTzvK5HZrRLtkD0nLa/I8I4eJw1N5I\nlWQbDqrqxkgOzKxZX4zndICPrPid3XHcqUpvzVdxEjLEVxRW6yxzsZ/bixIf54nm\nIAlGGk2HEw+HRIPSWgLmpVG37iXkXGn2vy8/E2kGbjLRPhPurmeJLDSyopScCIvc\ntBfjSg8vHjcQer1m5fugA7wDc8+22GIlk5uTY2lhOoGf+robtGcipf9R7ZbVht9Y\nssKyxqAZ49788cy2bLWczri+JBnNo0qXhg8+rGHMYnHW41hbHAYboT/mPYUs2zhU\n22PGV66OhM88gpHvx/G4NhlSIJIKlJapmHnp9MrLb50R/7ElQmThB33bCyCc865V\nht4aR2mYqrONX7E4Rppq5dBDqHx6tA1nscLQqHU3LVbTnAT+SA9Zpk4YGD6ocPG4\n/eEmcNB9KBC/1SZrlddKrf2nf95ZkqH/1sIIzAjlosuneOEW539Us4nIdGqVHDnx\nhMw0M2IH+1/w9BIn0LtgGA4rMs5yZ1UHJoL0IVn6pcNzx4cmi2AxKqMxsUyjK6xF\ntSqFQc6sSiFI+y0wj0tJ\n=toLL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T23:52:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/e9ce54d7747242258079a8fb80d116355fd864f0","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKGU5Y2U1NGQ3NzQ3MjQyMjU4MDc5YThmYjgwZDExNjM1NWZkODY0ZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/61b3f512671969ade257b68164eed01113f7ceef","sha":"61b3f512671969ade257b68164eed01113f7ceef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/61b3f512671969ade257b68164eed01113f7ceef"}],"sha":"e9ce54d7747242258079a8fb80d116355fd864f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/e9ce54d7747242258079a8fb80d116355fd864f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169448471?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mathildeshagl","id":169448471,"login":"mathildeshagl","node_id":"U_kgDOChmUFw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/61b3f512671969ade257b68164eed01113f7ceef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:48:08Z","email":"mathilde.s.hagl@tum.de","name":"Mathilde Hagl"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:48:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Core: Add a central study program list managed by admins (#2275)\n\n* Core: Manage the study program list centrally\n\nPROMPT admins now maintain the study programs applicants can pick in core\ninstead of the hardcoded list in prompt-shared-state. Core stores the list\nin a new study_program table, seeded with the four existing programs and\ntheir short names, and serves it on a public GET /api/study-programs. Adding,\nrenaming, deleting and the per-program student counts are PromptAdmin-only.\nA rename updates every student with the previous name in the same\ntransaction, and a deletion leaves stored student values untouched.\n\nThe application form, its public pages and the study background diagram\nread the list from core. The diagram now counts programs that are not on the\nlist as Other instead of dropping them, and empty values as Unknown. A new\nadmin page under Admin > Study Programs manages the list.\n\n* Core: Lock the study program row during a rename\n\nTwo concurrent renames of the same program both read the old name, so the\nsecond one renamed the program but moved no students, leaving them on the\nfirst new name. Reading the row with FOR UPDATE makes the second rename wait\nand see the committed name.\n\nThe study program chart also showed its loading placeholder forever when the\nlist failed to load; it now shows an error message instead.","tree":{"sha":"a0733d9c2e16b67f8ad58e5bad5a993a6facf916","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/a0733d9c2e16b67f8ad58e5bad5a993a6facf916"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/61b3f512671969ade257b68164eed01113f7ceef","verification":{"payload":"tree a0733d9c2e16b67f8ad58e5bad5a993a6facf916\nparent 08ed26015137790b6ead8b0ce7d6ac0636ec7ff3\nauthor Mathilde Hagl <mathilde.s.hagl@tum.de> 1791154088 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791154088 +0000\n\nCore: Add a central study program list managed by admins (#2275)\n\n* Core: Manage the study program list centrally\n\nPROMPT admins now maintain the study programs applicants can pick in core\ninstead of the hardcoded list in prompt-shared-state. Core stores the list\nin a new study_program table, seeded with the four existing programs and\ntheir short names, and serves it on a public GET /api/study-programs. Adding,\nrenaming, deleting and the per-program student counts are PromptAdmin-only.\nA rename updates every student with the previous name in the same\ntransaction, and a deletion leaves stored student values untouched.\n\nThe application form, its public pages and the study background diagram\nread the list from core. The diagram now counts programs that are not on the\nlist as Other instead of dropping them, and empty values as Unknown. A new\nadmin page under Admin > Study Programs manages the list.\n\n* Core: Lock the study program row during a rename\n\nTwo concurrent renames of the same program both read the old name, so the\nsecond one renamed the program but moved no students, leaving them on the\nfirst new name. Reading the row with FOR UPDATE makes the second rename wait\nand see the committed name.\n\nThe study program chart also showed its loading placeholder forever when the\nlist failed to load; it now shows an error message instead.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwteoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPKEQAJBW0HmZpzMvGmE3Kd7w+GR7\n6mohHhZAJqMfpIjyp0nnf2UUbUZ5df+wHH7fcgU9LwxKT3lTlx+iEp/RA09Y6eit\ntBJc2NF2dvKS/vBPElMQOgfPyeLl1ZQYYLnLwNJE1+WxlS1knRXyrhbU2g9M6S9R\n9+dgfzK/bHBSGVnum5SRZw+Sn2Os47CrujjZBS6RBH3Z1h2oEeRuW3CRpojR3vX0\nvxTxkDU94mHui4hPr4mQT46JDslTN0wOO0mlUQEeL3N+XimLtlGSTt39pwqjOpzR\nllecdUd7Yrvs70s84apHQsOvwj8cytZkwW9dt+zrao7bJzdSUg91Kd11FBfWXPLq\nXcO1AqlMt+R5ugqv+tGNkhsKGb7K/3YgddRiq53fmxezjYE1VSJCl9cmhS5vOcpM\nEUj3333YrBfhH4wfFTQdFVNJbngCZhBfoUPDVvFxP53fBQI1Ue6bhZjngluji8kA\nGJ+9rwp5vF7E3jFjUphkZEqA5nc4cEoTNZXUnJQ3X8feZwpXUscfTgEmdMvX/t79\nvm0lADSVMu/gAApfv4tIQnw8t9YIE0bvJkR8g2QnA0Y89L+1+jln0eDNjBrwrNvd\nmvu4Hp9jKzMDq2Ca6r0UmR8I14tck/CB1GK4nCbY9K3ZbFTNNzKeh10qZHDs+R2v\nT7OLMb8FvcKXGdojbtke\n=YQlg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T22:48:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/61b3f512671969ade257b68164eed01113f7ceef","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDYxYjNmNTEyNjcxOTY5YWRlMjU3YjY4MTY0ZWVkMDExMTNmN2NlZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/08ed26015137790b6ead8b0ce7d6ac0636ec7ff3","sha":"08ed26015137790b6ead8b0ce7d6ac0636ec7ff3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/08ed26015137790b6ead8b0ce7d6ac0636ec7ff3"}],"sha":"61b3f512671969ade257b68164eed01113f7ceef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/61b3f512671969ade257b68164eed01113f7ceef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169448471?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mathildeshagl","id":169448471,"login":"mathildeshagl","node_id":"U_kgDOChmUFw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/orgs","received_events_url":"