rview profile\n\nCore exposes the application assessment''s notes and history panel over\nModule Federation, and the interview profile loads it when the new\nphase setting is enabled.\n\n* Testing: Drop the stray FASTLANE mention from the verify skill\n\n* Interview: Load the core remote only when the student history panel needs it\n\n* Core: Stop loading the core remote entry on every page\n\n* Interview: Span the student history panel across the row on medium screens","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwtc8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs7QQAGZ6Aa8iODvyKufX78NWyTNR\nuD0N6YGa5+JsIz2Ovu0dEC8HrZWA/jyXBP053Pxev8dAezRlo7c+OIzdFUxScvdI\n+7yIOvVvS3ER5XGIIU6l//Dnxq29vxfcrL/eH71PQbOdfG+ZJQ1MnnYKl9N88/x+\nfef1lF4owPfKlYPiM5aUH+rpH+GpqmMfc5XBBRuMZomf5R0s8POPxlLsjPs46uPB\no13mFUPARk82Z9erpSx/zZI86RBYn6mjeAbXH+iZvoks9hLVYhYR6VFbbRVGoXq8\nHk1/KF9Q+nF0KGjb6SvUlf1Xw+vhMOx5hc6bzqnd3eWYMbztdcQyu3+GubbgFqBg\ncHn6Xt+qEJaP2ZaHyFtJkPsE3M1l94MfmUwHu6bkgliD1XFIU6A9v1WdbobZyU7k\nYJdxapu0IXe/tKLh6zL3q42E0m+13aIGO9v4hbWwHemcIWNAvgYUbqOafbwPKr/W\nXzP3Nx/6KeUArIL/ZGNNzRiovr0qHJx5fFdCaPpkBOTYqDeRW43Lt5L5XvdjSimt\nz1A4UNlqrM45K99lU7j6ULeomcvDF4ZVpT/cx9+Rwfg1LOwqJ6grE5arUSX3sFT5\ny7sZ7IPKqDVBuCaeLxM5HobQHZzKQgSAdH33abQvI3fJ0Z1M4Hk3gWbGM7d1NdXH\nzxWZcE5CN3ebZSMQVBdo\n=PDVq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T22:46:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/08ed26015137790b6ead8b0ce7d6ac0636ec7ff3","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDA4ZWQyNjAxNTEzNzc5MGI2ZWFkOGIwY2U3ZDZhYzA2MzZlYzdmZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/34a4f9ea67ad2d2a37b8959d8c6189ab5ce847e2","sha":"34a4f9ea67ad2d2a37b8959d8c6189ab5ce847e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/34a4f9ea67ad2d2a37b8959d8c6189ab5ce847e2"}],"sha":"08ed26015137790b6ead8b0ce7d6ac0636ec7ff3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/08ed26015137790b6ead8b0ce7d6ac0636ec7ff3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/34a4f9ea67ad2d2a37b8959d8c6189ab5ce847e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:33:21Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T22:33:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Team Allocation: Allow tutors to edit allocations for their assigned team (#2132)\n\n* Team Allocation: Add team-scoped allocation write queries and a participant lookup\n\nThe two new queries carry an optional expected_team_id guard so a scoped write\ncan only touch a row that is still in that team, keeping authorization and\nmutation in one statement. The core lookup proves phase membership and supplies\nthe names cached on an allocation, without following resolution endpoints.\n\n* Team Allocation: Add allocation upsert and delete to the allocation service\n\nBoth take an expected source team that scopes the write, verify the participant\nbelongs to the course phase before touching the database, and report a refused\nscoped write distinctly from a missing allocation.\n\n* Team Allocation: Allow tutors to edit the allocations of their assigned team\n\nPUT and DELETE on an allocation are now open to CourseEditor. Reads deliberately\nfail open for an editor the scoping middleware cannot resolve; writes fail\nclosed, so an editor who is not a recorded tutor is refused. A tutor may only\nname their own team as the target and only move a participant who is unallocated\nor already in that team, which the query guard enforces against the row itself.\n\n* Team Allocation: Cover the tutor-scoped allocation writes with tests\n\nThe write fixtures live in their own course phase so the existing read\nassertions cannot be disturbed by test order. Covers a tutor writing their own\nteam, a tutor refused on a foreign team as target and as source, an editor with\nno tutor record refused, lecturers and admins unrestricted, and a failed\nparticipant lookup leaving the database untouched.\n\n* Team Allocation: Register the allocation write routes in the API catalog\n\nAlso records on the TEASE save that its whole-phase draft overwrites allocations\nwritten directly since the draft was loaded.\n\n* Team Allocation: Keep a tutor''s writes scoped when they also hold PROMPT_Lecturer\n\nThe write routes do not admit PROMPT_Lecturer directly, so such a user arrives as\na course editor and their reads are tutor-scoped; treating the raw role as\nprivileged would have unscoped only their writes. A missing token user now\nanswers 401 instead of a misleading team-scoping 403, and a participant with no\nallocation no longer logs at error level on the way to its 404.\n\n* Team Allocation: Take the tutor write policy from the SDK tutorscope package\n\nWrites now authorize through tutorscope.AuthorizeWrite, check the target team\nwith Access.AllowsTeam and pass Access.Guard() as the atomic source-team guard.\nBoth routers resolve tutors with tutorscope.NewPgxResolver, so the local\ntutorscope package, its GetTutorTeamByUniversityLogin query and\nteamDTO.NormalizeUniversityLogin are removed.\n\n* Team Allocation: Document 403 on the scoped team and allocation lists\n\n* Team Allocation: Deny tutor-scoped reads to editors who are not tutors of the phase\n\nPins prompt-sdk to the head of prompt-edu/prompt-sdk#132, which makes the scoping middleware answer 403 for an editor who is not a tutor of a phase that has tutors, also when the token carries no university login. Phases without tutors keep unscoped editor reads. Bump to the release tag before merging.\n\n* Team Allocation: Bump prompt-sdk to v1.4.1\n\nReplaces the pseudo-version of prompt-edu/prompt-sdk#132 with the release\nthat ships the fail-closed tutor read rule.","tree":{"sha":"3e873d369f2042421fa69066c078f46e974c0213","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/3e873d369f2042421fa69066c078f46e974c0213"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/34a4f9ea67ad2d2a37b8959d8c6189ab5ce847e2","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e873d369f2042421fa69066c078f46e974c0213\nparent 869b52e5f11ffc82b6bc088d2283c57bfbb4c642\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791153201 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791153201 +0000\n\nTeam Allocation: Allow tutors to edit allocations for their assigned team (#2132)\n\n* Team Allocation: Add team-scoped allocation write queries and a participant lookup\n\nThe two new queries carry an optional expected_team_id guard so a scoped write\ncan only touch a row that is still in that team, keeping authorization and\nmutation in one statement. The core lookup proves phase membership and supplies\nthe names cached on an allocation, without following resolution endpoints.\n\n* Team Allocation: Add allocation upsert and delete to the allocation service\n\nBoth take an expected source team that scopes the write, verify the participant\nbelongs to the course phase before touching the database, and report a refused\nscoped write distinctly from a missing allocation.\n\n* Team Allocation: Allow tutors to edit the allocations of their assigned team\n\nPUT and DELETE on an allocation are now open to CourseEditor. Reads deliberately\nfail open for an editor the scoping middleware cannot resolve; writes fail\nclosed, so an editor who is not a recorded tutor is refused. A tutor may only\nname their own team as the target and only move a participant who is unallocated\nor already in that team, which the query guard enforces against the row itself.\n\n* Team Allocation: Cover the tutor-scoped allocation writes with tests\n\nThe write fixtures live in their own course phase so the existing read\nassertions cannot be disturbed by test order. Covers a tutor writing their own\nteam, a tutor refused on a foreign team as target and as source, an editor with\nno tutor record refused, lecturers and admins unrestricted, and a failed\nparticipant lookup leaving the database untouched.\n\n* Team Allocation: Register the allocation write routes in the API catalog\n\nAlso records on the TEASE save that its whole-phase draft overwrites allocations\nwritten directly since the draft was loaded.\n\n* Team Allocation: Keep a tutor''s writes scoped when they also hold PROMPT_Lecturer\n\nThe write routes do not admit PROMPT_Lecturer directly, so such a user arrives as\na course editor and their reads are tutor-scoped; treating the raw role as\nprivileged would have unscoped only their writes. A missing token user now\nanswers 401 instead of a misleading team-scoping 403, and a participant with no\nallocation no longer logs at error level on the way to its 404.\n\n* Team Allocation: Take the tutor write policy from the SDK tutorscope package\n\nWrites now authorize through tutorscope.AuthorizeWrite, check the target team\nwith Access.AllowsTeam and pass Access.Guard() as the atomic source-team guard.\nBoth routers resolve tutors with tutorscope.NewPgxResolver, so the local\ntutorscope package, its GetTutorTeamByUniversityLogin query and\nteamDTO.NormalizeUniversityLogin are removed.\n\n* Team Allocation: Document 403 on the scoped team and allocation lists\n\n* Team Allocation: Deny tutor-scoped reads to editors who are not tutors of the phase\n\nPins prompt-sdk to the head of prompt-edu/prompt-sdk#132, which makes the scoping middleware answer 403 for an editor who is not a tutor of a phase that has tutors, also when the token carries no university login. Phases without tutors keep unscoped editor reads. Bump to the release tag before merging.\n\n* Team Allocation: Bump prompt-sdk to v1.4.1\n\nReplaces the pseudo-version of prompt-edu/prompt-sdk#132 with the release\nthat ships the fail-closed tutor read rule.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwtQxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt0gQAC3FHPPU5lH7ZJQFb+fmpX84\niD7Qr0sRTARb2V1LucC4poccGXzbk3DQDfkMUIfh1jxoh7uae368eCD/naW5kpn2\nYh0tQ7qcWCx8exN1p8IZrj9Lb5jE3uZ7tUYOIl0XLvcddMFu5lKQ9QYDsoZFYQ08\niOF1daR+ldOQrUYrOkDyJPjc7cZg3VareZni2p4LzT4ElpjFNGdZgHCgYNpVoxeV\nbz7o54N5USvhqd96XxgZAfedOPlU5GOYoAPMnRj7cGM1C6zoZ7M2VVwfnS7ZXVjt\ndPnplffd8VbbSmF7cQ/Nhlx+VhHXrIhkakNyGFIoXhxnDT/T3bujCFi0F4OUD/Um\nYCcyA1xzrQwnBKJDxk+8Z8PScBvXbMSqcrj/4vDaxtQYpfKb2vEQB1xAG+NY4jQr\nFT3WCcqTSJxcW52g6Gg78fgpHZlpu9VqQtt1E0esCjowOUplX6BD4TR+8Rc27Qir\nYFGSDUue8m2dsQVl6reMr4r4szqo3fi5aAspHDrv987dkKM6TxjdMHQ1CcBG07ZB\nZiInleooR44G3g3TLQgWG12KzsqzjEduDNRxf5GV+z5CZS7e39bwuCI6HqCkozRI\n+O97JuDN1+KS8zTC/hFwhzSjR0OreSQx+4hhPwRO4CwAjcSEgzGJejSH+fixTUbP\no5hmGucpdsui/rUTltew\n=DW60\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T22:33:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/34a4f9ea67ad2d2a37b8959d8c6189ab5ce847e2","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDM0YTRmOWVhNjdhZDJkMmEzN2I4OTU5ZDhjNjE4OWFiNWNlODQ3ZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/869b52e5f11ffc82b6bc088d2283c57bfbb4c642","sha":"869b52e5f11ffc82b6bc088d2283c57bfbb4c642","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/869b52e5f11ffc82b6bc088d2283c57bfbb4c642"}],"sha":"34a4f9ea67ad2d2a37b8959d8c6189ab5ce847e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/34a4f9ea67ad2d2a37b8959d8c6189ab5ce847e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/869b52e5f11ffc82b6bc088d2283c57bfbb4c642/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T21:46:01Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T21:46:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"General: Replace inlined query loading and error gates with the shared QueryGate (#2189)\n\n* Gate the phase data shells with the shared QueryGate\n\nThe three bespoke shells each combined their queries by hand into isPending,\nisError and refetch before rendering the same ErrorPage/LoadingPage ternary.\ncombineQueryStates already drops disabled queries, so the enablement guards\ncollapse into passing the query objects.\n\n* Gate the assessment pages and panels with the shared QueryGate\n\nThe enablement flags each page carried into its isPending, isError and\nrefetch expressions are already on the queries themselves, so passing the\nquery objects to QueryGate drops the guards along with the ternary.\nPages with curated error copy or a local spinner keep it through\nerrorFallback and loadingFallback.\n\n* Gate the team allocation pages with the shared QueryGate\n\nThe self team allocation page kept its lecturer path ungated, so a failed\nteams or timeframe fetch left the disabled-UI notice with an empty body.\nGating both queries for lecturers surfaces the error instead. The tease\ndata check no longer forwards its loading and error flags to the summary\ncard: the card only renders once the gate has passed, so both were\nconstant.\n\n* Gate the remaining phase pages with the shared QueryGate\n\nPages whose query is enabled on the phase ID now reject a missing ID up\nfront instead of leaving the query disabled, which also removes the\nnon-null assertions they passed to the participation table.\n\n* Keep the self team allocation 404 fallback on the student path\n\nA disabled query keeps its cached error, so a lecturer whose teams or\ntimeframe fetch failed could be sent to the unauthorized page by a stale\nparticipation 404 from an earlier student session.\n\n* General: Keep the QueryGate fallbacks in their owning container\n\nGuard the interview participants page against a missing phaseId with the\nErrorPage the other participants pages use, instead of asserting it non-null.\n\nMove the student detail dialog''s gate into the dialog body so the loading and\nerror fallbacks render inside the modal instead of inline next to the student\ntable, and so nothing renders once the dialog is closed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Team Allocation: Show the student detail load error inside the dialog\n\n* Interview: Keep the participants header when the phase ID is missing\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"da33b0cb461de8e23dd84baa139c7fd18f56da0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/da33b0cb461de8e23dd84baa139c7fd18f56da0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/869b52e5f11ffc82b6bc088d2283c57bfbb4c642","verification":{"payload":"tree da33b0cb461de8e23dd84baa139c7fd18f56da0a\nparent 7e0f0f8b2e6dafe45c2f9af13d32bc9f19daa1a8\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791150361 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791150361 +0000\n\nGeneral: Replace inlined query loading and error gates with the shared QueryGate (#2189)\n\n* Gate the phase data shells with the shared QueryGate\n\nThe three bespoke shells each combined their queries by hand into isPending,\nisError and refetch before rendering the same ErrorPage/LoadingPage ternary.\ncombineQueryStates already drops disabled queries, so the enablement guards\ncollapse into passing the query objects.\n\n* Gate the assessment pages and panels with the shared QueryGate\n\nThe enablement flags each page carried into its isPending, isError and\nrefetch expressions are already on the queries themselves, so passing the\nquery objects to QueryGate drops the guards along with the ternary.\nPages with curated error copy or a local spinner keep it through\nerrorFallback and loadingFallback.\n\n* Gate the team allocation pages with the shared QueryGate\n\nThe self team allocation page kept its lecturer path ungated, so a failed\nteams or timeframe fetch left the disabled-UI notice with an empty body.\nGating both queries for lecturers surfaces the error instead. The tease\ndata check no longer forwards its loading and error flags to the summary\ncard: the card only renders once the gate has passed, so both were\nconstant.\n\n* Gate the remaining phase pages with the shared QueryGate\n\nPages whose query is enabled on the phase ID now reject a missing ID up\nfront instead of leaving the query disabled, which also removes the\nnon-null assertions they passed to the participation table.\n\n* Keep the self team allocation 404 fallback on the student path\n\nA disabled query keeps its cached error, so a lecturer whose teams or\ntimeframe fetch failed could be sent to the unauthorized page by a stale\nparticipation 404 from an earlier student session.\n\n* General: Keep the QueryGate fallbacks in their owning container\n\nGuard the interview participants page against a missing phaseId with the\nErrorPage the other participants pages use, instead of asserting it non-null.\n\nMove the student detail dialog''s gate into the dialog body so the loading and\nerror fallbacks render inside the modal instead of inline next to the student\ntable, and so nothing renders once the dialog is closed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Team Allocation: Show the student detail load error inside the dialog\n\n* Interview: Keep the participants header when the phase ID is missing\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwskZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/VsQABnD3Bl1dx38mEBoEVh1DMk4\nrk2hYs2uM0hWYV2HseAcqPy6X0Wx8F9ypltqoMvpm+sQ/jFBQCTyPKpHB14P1EFG\nBJDaEj0BEhCl51a5K1ROZ5K60NKBOBTF6nIcIL4pmVIYA9UTG5m+QB0vMrKDleGq\nvGgPiMNgtsTQ/DIdWQ+uasFHyeFuI+z2+Kl+xjT/rYaGp3tr8j+VAblfOZy5B06s\n3XP92fDPs9uO0wFjbSHGNVSJ+U8zbebfUA7Mb6o+kQglzk1MJ6ha/tFOo9Q+VBUj\nVgd0bTau74tTBRHd8q0NNQC9mt6MUS/GN3lMOJbKtUIGGavFkLfrUOrKLm+Zdeog\nx1mIhtkyGT9xu72G+cxfwcpi94KqepUHjyxBWoWUs2y7JYp42QWK2NW3RM8+RzHA\nhESRFGJznX3qQ/3SqAUrwBV48cZHwW08vDT4N+sDByvH4tfPVXKhjxVjOjzbN1Ze\nRFnrS5vjdPqjeYhd2BbkDj9tNHfgVgJ6QcFRUDokj3Ii428vKnd25w+bnYyGFSOW\ndG8fgzp0+OajysqZui9O9Q4/QD0Pi3ipFYDaQ5gU3wp37DQn14cwVldYzGjE8Tbg\nEuubah7POmPmApkDpQ5WxVjG2CqtUQOoHZKB7R/eN6gZKRdPkM/CaU4EFJJs9k2Y\nCFnx0gm2v+jbSNDgX0Hl\n=I/Yw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T21:46:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events