ntation`: Read the query caches through the key module\n\n* `Presentation`: Invalidate the query caches through named events","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwrIkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8UwQAJu2nCyVuOrg0QpvN1mmQxpa\niQME/dfiLtOw0XWeAxUEbGB4m/pK5NBKbbJRqUiLBTctR3ZQxRjxuE6mVzfABJ4Q\ndvKUI6EVD/ZDTva8UT35bNvsHCZm+d/vCXMdz0mf3gdeVe6VlyctJqlEBtTwzFzj\nfIrck0/TaHHfKQEsS4Auieakiqpf05ilHRgZqANEVDIRIcP8U3gUyfDA2O/1KouA\nWIDiZlSOg2dlbUgt8JLOtXow1xn5Fb7W8aaVqgaKft2m2hxYjt0XJDGl8F/MTwAX\nVs7HjQJ9x84LzDW996dkXIxHCMJ6Ax/qJIgr64sM/NLjNGUyCMLf1JZQmnjMKD82\nQ9S4MKax7MERJ7zqCQuEG/eazmbAHOP4dcT/srvdqR/iNKEr21m/+XD5dhggNmPj\nsXU5tg1Z9Eo508tHr6xNDeoBZmrBsVxUcbanGxSK+KJYMOKk7jC4wiCwp89qxJ+W\nv84dm7U3xTHoxPAP7fm4xQ7LllDul76pi+hDpYCvL/TnQtLI/NJ6KApl+zgxAp0d\n/E1aSBusJky2y1GE++89qFBMzBZt3dBDE68yJ/02X9Q5IZ1jYHacUNvjLIvOAHKp\nQBdi/EJ9RajcxLd0exx6jfhVe6A5s10i4kEyCNVkk7nOZUHWZ47SSK7FPZnRbm8K\nze9xJBw1fElqZjH93zmJ\n=7pno\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T20:08:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/d0ecbc46dde5f6e6cab075ea24ae4196224d5032","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKGQwZWNiYzQ2ZGRlNWY2ZTZjYWIwNzVlYTI0YWU0MTk2MjI0ZDUwMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/46b386091647ec5c30a29f4b347794bbafda5ef6","sha":"46b386091647ec5c30a29f4b347794bbafda5ef6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/46b386091647ec5c30a29f4b347794bbafda5ef6"}],"sha":"d0ecbc46dde5f6e6cab075ea24ae4196224d5032","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/d0ecbc46dde5f6e6cab075ea24ae4196224d5032"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/46b386091647ec5c30a29f4b347794bbafda5ef6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T20:05:11Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T20:05:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Course Phases: Add participants, provisioning and a student page to the infrastructure setup phase (#2206)\n\n* Module Federation: Share the UI library so remote toasts render\n\nEvery remote bundled its own copy of @tumaet/prompt-ui-components. The toast\nstore lives at module level in that library and core mounts the only\n<Toaster />, so each toast a remote raised landed in a store nothing renders:\nsaving, validating, deleting and triggering in a phase gave no feedback at\nall, whether it succeeded or failed.\n\nAdd the library to the singleton share scope, and move the infrastructure\nsetup and presentation remotes onto the shared rspack factory. Both had\nforked configs that would not have picked up the new share scope.\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Record who each resource was provisioned for\n\nAn instance only names its target, a team or one student, so nothing could\ntell a student which of their team''s resources they can reach, or a\nlecturer which members a partial run left out.\n\nRecord the people of every run in a resource_instance_member table, with\nwhether each was granted access. Providers now report warnings with the\nmembers they concern instead of bare strings, so \"not added\" no longer\ndepends on parsing an error message. The table is covered by the privacy\nexport and deletion and by the phase deletion.\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Add student resources and a provisioning preview\n\nGET /my-resources lets a student of the phase see what was provisioned for\nthem and their team, and whether they were let in. It carries no error\ntext, since a partial run''s message names the other members who were left\nout, and no Keycloak link, which only points into the admin console.\n\nGET /execute/preview runs a trigger''s checks and target resolution without\nwriting, so the provisioning page can say what a click will do and what\nblocks it before anyone clicks. The trigger and the preview share one plan.\n\nGET /instances now carries each instance''s members, and a phase no teams\nreach answers 400 with where to fix it instead of a 500.\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Restructure the phase around participants and provisioning\n\nThe phase root was an overview that only linked to four lecturer pages, so a\nstudent opening the phase got Access Denied and a lecturer got the same page\nfrom the phase and from its Overview entry. The four pages split one setup\ninto steps with nothing tying them to the run, and none of them let a\nlecturer see a student''s resources or move students on.\n\nThe phase root is now the student page: the resources provisioned for the\nstudent and their team, whether they were let in, and what to do if not.\nLecturers see it with the usual notice and a preview built from the\nconfiguration. Behind it are three pages:\n\n- Participants: the shared participants table with a column per resource,\n  filterable by state, so ready students can be set passed in bulk.\n- Configuration: semester tag, providers and resources as the three steps\n  of one page.\n- Provisioning: a readiness checklist backed by the server''s dry run, what\n  the next run does, the button that starts it, and the status list.\n\nThe resource dialog now scrolls inside the viewport; its Save button was\nout of reach on a laptop screen.\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Cover the phase end to end through its pages\n\nThe existing journey drives the phase through its API only, which is how a\npage whose every save gave no feedback, and a dialog whose Save button was\nout of reach, went unnoticed.\n\nThe new journey configures the phase on its pages, checks that each save\nreports back, provisions it against the stack''s own Keycloak, and reads the\noutcome on the participants table and on the student''s own page. Stan has\na Keycloak account and Niclas does not, so one run ends with a participant\nwho was let in and one who was not. The runner receives the realm''s\ntest-only prompt-server secret for it.\n\nThe contributor guide describes the new pages, the member tracking, the\npreview and the student endpoint.\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Show a queued team resource to its members\n\nA team instance only reached its members once its run had recorded them, so\na team waiting for a free worker read as never provisioned, while a student\nwith a personal resource in the same state already saw it being set up.\nThe trigger now records the people of every instance it queues, with\nnobody let in yet, and the run replaces them with what it did.\n\nStudent links are now allowed per provider rather than hidden for Keycloak\nonly, so a provider added later shows no link until someone checks that a\nstudent can open it.\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Refresh the provisioning preview after every change\n\nEvery configuration change alters what the next run does, so each one now\nrefreshes the preview, as retrying and deleting an instance already did.\nThe dry run is only requested once the phase''s own checks pass: before\nthat the server refuses it for the reasons the checklist already shows.\n\n* Module Federation: Export StudentDetail from the infrastructure setup and presentation remotes\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Keep error details out of the student resources response","tree":{"sha":"53b07b86a63491ff86f97d87500d4a3258651685","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/53b07b86a63491ff86f97d87500d4a3258651685"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/46b386091647ec5c30a29f4b347794bbafda5ef6","verification":{"payload":"tree 53b07b86a63491ff86f97d87500d4a3258651685\nparent 8fc3ba99a3bd5330e815a888fbec37606665b064\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791144311 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791144311 +0000\n\nCourse Phases: Add participants, provisioning and a student page to the infrastructure setup phase (#2206)\n\n* Module Federation: Share the UI library so remote toasts render\n\nEvery remote bundled its own copy of @tumaet/prompt-ui-components. The toast\nstore lives at module level in that library and core mounts the only\n<Toaster />, so each toast a remote raised landed in a store nothing renders:\nsaving, validating, deleting and triggering in a phase gave no feedback at\nall, whether it succeeded or failed.\n\nAdd the library to the singleton share scope, and move the infrastructure\nsetup and presentation remotes onto the shared rspack factory. Both had\nforked configs that would not have picked up the new share scope.\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Record who each resource was provisioned for\n\nAn instance only names its target, a team or one student, so nothing could\ntell a student which of their team''s resources they can reach, or a\nlecturer which members a partial run left out.\n\nRecord the people of every run in a resource_instance_member table, with\nwhether each was granted access. Providers now report warnings with the\nmembers they concern instead of bare strings, so \"not added\" no longer\ndepends on parsing an error message. The table is covered by the privacy\nexport and deletion and by the phase deletion.\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Add student resources and a provisioning preview\n\nGET /my-resources lets a student of the phase see what was provisioned for\nthem and their team, and whether they were let in. It carries no error\ntext, since a partial run''s message names the other members who were left\nout, and no Keycloak link, which only points into the admin console.\n\nGET /execute/preview runs a trigger''s checks and target resolution without\nwriting, so the provisioning page can say what a click will do and what\nblocks it before anyone clicks. The trigger and the preview share one plan.\n\nGET /instances now carries each instance''s members, and a phase no teams\nreach answers 400 with where to fix it instead of a 500.\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Restructure the phase around participants and provisioning\n\nThe phase root was an overview that only linked to four lecturer pages, so a\nstudent opening the phase got Access Denied and a lecturer got the same page\nfrom the phase and from its Overview entry. The four pages split one setup\ninto steps with nothing tying them to the run, and none of them let a\nlecturer see a student''s resources or move students on.\n\nThe phase root is now the student page: the resources provisioned for the\nstudent and their team, whether they were let in, and what to do if not.\nLecturers see it with the usual notice and a preview built from the\nconfiguration. Behind it are three pages:\n\n- Participants: the shared participants table with a column per resource,\n  filterable by state, so ready students can be set passed in bulk.\n- Configuration: semester tag, providers and resources as the three steps\n  of one page.\n- Provisioning: a readiness checklist backed by the server''s dry run, what\n  the next run does, the button that starts it, and the status list.\n\nThe resource dialog now scrolls inside the viewport; its Save button was\nout of reach on a laptop screen.\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Cover the phase end to end through its pages\n\nThe existing journey drives the phase through its API only, which is how a\npage whose every save gave no feedback, and a dialog whose Save button was\nout of reach, went unnoticed.\n\nThe new journey configures the phase on its pages, checks that each save\nreports back, provisions it against the stack''s own Keycloak, and reads the\noutcome on the participants table and on the student''s own page. Stan has\na Keycloak account and Niclas does not, so one run ends with a participant\nwho was let in and one who was not. The runner receives the realm''s\ntest-only prompt-server secret for it.\n\nThe contributor guide describes the new pages, the member tracking, the\npreview and the student endpoint.\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Show a queued team resource to its members\n\nA team instance only reached its members once its run had recorded them, so\na team waiting for a free worker read as never provisioned, while a student\nwith a personal resource in the same state already saw it being set up.\nThe trigger now records the people of every instance it queues, with\nnobody let in yet, and the run replaces them with what it did.\n\nStudent links are now allowed per provider rather than hidden for Keycloak\nonly, so a provider added later shows no link until someone checks that a\nstudent can open it.\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Refresh the provisioning preview after every change\n\nEvery configuration change alters what the next run does, so each one now\nrefreshes the preview, as retrying and deleting an instance already did.\nThe dry run is only requested once the phase''s own checks pass: before\nthat the server refuses it for the reasons the checklist already shows.\n\n* Module Federation: Export StudentDetail from the infrastructure setup and presentation remotes\n\n* Infrastructure Setup: Keep error details out of the student resources response","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwrF3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6/oQACbIR5WS4u/ZL3ivl3CT+NXj\noWmEvU/UcR47JJ9eseNqVt1YXXa8q//VuzBv+/9FRxWmwHufoZphZM8vZqEZWkAt\nOT6t2EggqxIa6eLgvjVBfesQbY9/I5DhX/8mNVIE7wOXUY4gDVqe5VhKsFBkaVrz\nZ2rrm75CL6hDVkhdGAVY0T2QAR2mvMBXV1s8gOtYeXs1D+E0qAhHrR7DuEPNE535\nw1t35H4A9mI04TwLWnh8ZVbKw+Ag2ungPNgnPu0lEy80AiGIxn6016Oa96WomLZe\nBn3gnWRKyJsRARlp6f0UJm/uVOQ0OdIOw2p2JCSiyu64V6mdMGn+dk53xb8tCxi+\no756PRs5fuf0SYwLs8WiGPIt4lJvlUMDIB2Fsqk2JSD6+jqK6ohg0vc6zWgqgRGy\nzgCV89xcxvYSxSqj1GZIWHMaUqrCgbgThw5qpwaHPQV41NAUuWHU0XlEWR9Tbs71\nlwWllA3OZmlMpx5jzGQbYTU3lkUO6X8S/TiRD3WdM9j3ywTa34R4cMpZb3pruMWZ\nlRZq79Hs2bbVNslsLMlxFf4FxkhySUAAwePy3CAN69GUKU/xH46FDhfUFFpgEAwF\nxqrEO4sY1TfM7qxyRGEi1lEPr7nR/yhgK5/tc7/EF8t9MtCkPkwSPI0Ad5pTlwjz\nXbb29nOKn8xcQ7nWJu1I\n=uySI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T20:05:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","followi