"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/4fc49f18f889c26522c62d537c0fd3d44ca401fe","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDRmYzQ5ZjE4Zjg4OWMyNjUyMmM2MmQ1MzdjMGZkM2Q0NGNhNDAxZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/1f68717ea7b939c6c4e2bcb616bbec415f4e9cf8","sha":"1f68717ea7b939c6c4e2bcb616bbec415f4e9cf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/1f68717ea7b939c6c4e2bcb616bbec415f4e9cf8"}],"sha":"4fc49f18f889c26522c62d537c0fd3d44ca401fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/4fc49f18f889c26522c62d537c0fd3d44ca401fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169448471?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mathildeshagl","id":169448471,"login":"mathildeshagl","node_id":"U_kgDOChmUFw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathildeshagl","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/1f68717ea7b939c6c4e2bcb616bbec415f4e9cf8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T11:04:03Z","email":"mathilde.s.hagl@tum.de","name":"Mathilde Hagl"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T11:04:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Documentation: Update the initial setup guide (#2144)\n\n* Documentation: Update the initial setup guide\n\nBring the contributor setup guide in line with the current codebase:\n\n- Embed copies of `.env.template` and `.env.dev.template`, and explain\n  which file is used by Docker and which by the Makefile-started servers.\n- Drop the `go mod download` step; the toolchain fetches on demand.\n- Correct the tool versions (Go 1.27, Node 24.19.0, Yarn 4) and replace\n  the Webpack reference with rspack.\n- Replace the manual Keycloak realm/user creation steps: the realm is\n  imported automatically and ships seeded users for every role.\n- Point `KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET` at `.env.dev` / `.env` instead of\n  `servers/core/main.go`, and warn that an empty value in `.env.dev`\n  overrides `.env`.\n- Use the Makefile targets (`make db`, `make server`, `make clients`) and\n  document Docker, the per-service databases, SeaweedFS, the current\n  micro-frontend ports, and the `make lint` / `make test` check.\n\nAlso fix the broken `#adjust-environment-variables` anchor in the\nproduction setup guide so the docs build reports no warnings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* General: Use the container port for the example and interview databases\n\nThe base template is consumed by docker compose, where the servers reach\nthese databases over the compose network. 5437 and 5438 are host port\nmappings onto the PostgreSQL container port, which stays 5432 like every\nother service in the file. .env.dev keeps the host ports for servers run\noutside Docker.\n\n* Documentation: Correct the setup guide from review feedback\n\nSeaweedFS is required, not optional: the core and presentation servers\nabort during startup when the bucket check fails, so it now precedes the\nserver step and names the actual errors.\n\nWarn that the client secret has to replace the FIXME comment in\n.env.template, since the Makefile include keeps the space before the # in\nthe value and Keycloak then returns invalid_client.\n\nList the six per-client make targets that exist instead of implying one\nper microfrontend.\n\nPoint the production guide''s standalone Keycloak link at the Keycloak\nlocal development guide, which still documents the realm import the\nsetup guide no longer covers.\n\n* Documentation: Bring the setup guide in line with main\n\nmake db now starts every service database, so the guide drops the manual\ndocker compose step and lists all host ports, including the new\ninfrastructure setup database on 5441.\n\nAdd the infrastructure setup server target and client port, a demo data\nstep for make seed, and Node 24.21.0. Refresh the copies of .env.template\nand .env.dev.template from the current files.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"095bd257c3c083cda9faa0fd30565f986b79d7e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/095bd257c3c083cda9faa0fd30565f986b79d7e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/1f68717ea7b939c6c4e2bcb616bbec415f4e9cf8","verification":{"payload":"tree 095bd257c3c083cda9faa0fd30565f986b79d7e2\nparent 88c5060568d72736967319b18453604c5ef501c4\nauthor Mathilde Hagl <mathilde.s.hagl@tum.de> 1791111843 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791111843 +0200\n\nDocumentation: Update the initial setup guide (#2144)\n\n* Documentation: Update the initial setup guide\n\nBring the contributor setup guide in line with the current codebase:\n\n- Embed copies of `.env.template` and `.env.dev.template`, and explain\n  which file is used by Docker and which by the Makefile-started servers.\n- Drop the `go mod download` step; the toolchain fetches on demand.\n- Correct the tool versions (Go 1.27, Node 24.19.0, Yarn 4) and replace\n  the Webpack reference with rspack.\n- Replace the manual Keycloak realm/user creation steps: the realm is\n  imported automatically and ships seeded users for every role.\n- Point `KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET` at `.env.dev` / `.env` instead of\n  `servers/core/main.go`, and warn that an empty value in `.env.dev`\n  overrides `.env`.\n- Use the Makefile targets (`make db`, `make server`, `make clients`) and\n  document Docker, the per-service databases, SeaweedFS, the current\n  micro-frontend ports, and the `make lint` / `make test` check.\n\nAlso fix the broken `#adjust-environment-variables` anchor in the\nproduction setup guide so the docs build reports no warnings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* General: Use the container port for the example and interview databases\n\nThe base template is consumed by docker compose, where the servers reach\nthese databases over the compose network. 5437 and 5438 are host port\nmappings onto the PostgreSQL container port, which stays 5432 like every\nother service in the file. .env.dev keeps the host ports for servers run\noutside Docker.\n\n* Documentation: Correct the setup guide from review feedback\n\nSeaweedFS is required, not optional: the core and presentation servers\nabort during startup when the bucket check fails, so it now precedes the\nserver step and names the actual errors.\n\nWarn that the client secret has to replace the FIXME comment in\n.env.template, since the Makefile include keeps the space before the # in\nthe value and Keycloak then returns invalid_client.\n\nList the six per-client make targets that exist instead of implying one\nper microfrontend.\n\nPoint the production guide''s standalone Keycloak link at the Keycloak\nlocal development guide, which still documents the realm import the\nsetup guide no longer covers.\n\n* Documentation: Bring the setup guide in line with main\n\nmake db now starts every service database, so the guide drops the manual\ndocker compose step and lists all host ports, including the new\ninfrastructure setup database on 5441.\n\nAdd the infrastructure setup server target and client port, a demo data\nstep for make seed, and Node 24.21.0. Refresh the copies of .env.template\nand .env.dev.template from the current files.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwjKjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8LAQAC/NW5iIDdOsQjqXIJpESSyQ\n0N/lriqtl9kWM7TrEinFapeIKP2mh37R2HbOPJiJWntrIHTmzG9Ovf3p/yxnbRs+\ndVOSVIRHyL4QXB+BMeXn+9gxdaGspBEnm11UlWo3+mNU+Sm0D/ZQIK/MYZIf6kaM\nKs1w5ya2GWFNmprQwNxEGwmBealY5KWS8xLSyTgw9+tCM4ipsACmd8Ao8JWY8J6r\nOuF7KbLTaQxwaj4BDd7NAxdQKqgiQcQAyISgzhIa1xAkQgalAlsgnPIGIjZd0++b\nwu4oi0J0gLtUfpu6RPLme7duQpWoEQM3sLLzYpXbt/Wz2HNp556GkaKndR9OMeTs\nUYZpH3fsant5CM3VnuemmuMWBsP/6MqaireOiT9imWkwC0+3nPvsknTpEDLmpgSB\nVVP3b+OrR8hdHac2tUyU8tFV3A+ISpD9v0lK4N7ylHYkrPI6bcQuRGeXWsL8fPI7\nJvoaKtTbjpYd84CSrrM7MYidPBUeP2Y+U5h6lsK+HfCUWTwHNx/UbQVQNJO9OUKy\nOpO8zzGpEFrS9+BsO7as9jS6nmUNJ7TUbypyW+POA1RPqyRs6+CDIe5Fuae4lUjb\nkvnrmOuGj2QtqM+xQ2xe+3/zn01+IfIR0Su8jZaleriXu6BsSVzK1y2sSi9P2R9e\nBDVszrFf/AeGlmiLnT6I\n=6/E0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T11:04:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/1f68717ea7b939c6c4e2bcb616bbec415f4e9cf8","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDFmNjg3MTdlYTdiOTM5YzZjNGUyYmNiNjE2YmJlYzQxNWY0ZTljZjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/88c5060568d72736967319b18453604c5ef501c4","sha":"88c5060568d72736967319b18453604c5ef501c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/88c5060568d72736967319b18453604c5ef501c4"}],"sha":"1f68717ea7b939c6c4e2bcb616bbec415f4e9cf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/1f68717ea7b939c6c4e2bcb616bbec415f4e9cf8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/88c5060568d72736967319b18453604c5ef501c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:23:34Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T10:23:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Core: Fix course phase update and create ignoring the ids in the URL (#2235)\n\n* Core: Update the course phase named in the URL\n\nThe update handler ignored the :uuid the permission middleware checked and wrote to the phase named by the body''s id. The id field is removed from the request.\n\n* Core: Stop sending the course phase id in the update body\n\nThe id only goes into the URL now. The shared-state hook still sends it in the body, which the server ignores.\n\n* Core: Return 404 when updating a course phase that does not exist\n\nWith the URL as the only target, a wrong id used to succeed silently. The id is now a GetDBModel argument so no caller can forget to set it.\n\n* Core: Create course phases in the course from the URL\n\nThe handler compared the body''s courseID with the URL and, on a mismatch, passed a nil error to handleError, which panicked into a 500. The course now comes only from the URL the permission middleware checked, and the client stops sending it in the body.\n\n* Assessment: Stop sending the course phase id in the reminder''s core update body\n\nCore takes the phase from the URL. The id is now a parameter of the core update call instead of a request field.","tree":{"sha":"c0c211be5873cf44e69fc7e36a0caf7ba8864ded","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/c0c211be5873cf44e69fc7e36a0caf7ba8864ded"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/88c5060568d72736967319b18453604c5ef501c4","verification":{"payload":"tree c0c211be5873cf44e69fc7e36a0caf7ba8864ded\nparent d51b4ebbe5a43e1cafe067b5cf9b1ea61e0eb267\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1791109414 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791109414 +0000\n\nCore: Fix course phase update and create ignoring the ids in the URL (#2235)\n\n* Core: Update the course phase named in the URL\n\nThe update handler ignored the :uuid the permission middleware checked and wrote to the phase named by the body''s id. The id field is removed from the request.\n\n* Core: Stop sending the course phase id in the update body\n\nThe id only goes into the URL now. The shared-state hook still sends it in the body, which the server ignores.\n\n* Core: Return 404 when updating a course phase that does not exist\n\nWith the URL as the only target, a wrong id used to succeed silently. The id is now a GetDBModel argument so no caller can forget to set it.\n\n* Core: Create course phases in the course from the URL\n\nThe handler compared the body''s courseID with the URL and, on a mismatch, passed a nil error to handleError, which panicked into a 500. The course now comes only from the URL the permission middleware checked, and the client stops sending it in the body.\n\n* Assessment: Stop sending the course phase id in the reminder''s core update body\n\nCore takes the phase from the URL. The id is now a parameter of the core update call instead of a request field.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwikmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAb6UQABGN5SVkc3y3SjPH8gLcqO9q\nJd/l2BrI2w3iqrqcTbA1McrER4tYIfyN+hvYdNuV4IB/xoieV43ZqdlLxQSUi43L\nlGK9l94HjOMBhI8npxKvkuL5AEeuYymzz353F52fuhWZ3Dc8si4kKJt7rEUiwKan\nLpa2tHU0c55QSM6CtReJI+hgcZNSopPy+t+nWAFf12YEh1BINATKQf0+TRBnhZfQ\nWDOP3+6oF6aqYXHJviI7R69UVteyiNjxav5hD5SdGXPJFDSh/eJ7Na/NOfCCiSij\nv+y+TnEOQ0+rJf02yMI7BjspSvsy4UsyUL+rpH8DARCQ7e+arA0voLTV8g376FxW\nGVRFLLry+cfqS+CP1Z/jKVW9YkOegpcSIhhxAb0LkkVm84a2iVucpGcIEJposSst\nny8bdphm5at+BlsF4SmJjFyy63srctXXdCaoK7eLEQBkfIqZquCJR/LSmuSyfvnT\n8xTinqkcw9kgYlqlgldj3VvwL3YcNHnVg/Nb/Jh2w6VnzPVVzdUg+5tJvVBJN7x5\nUOibnIAsfhjJz66wAvtNzCQhkAF/ydv8iAWs0O6PO++8ctb7fb/DU78/ylMbC8RD\nV9R6OX+RAY4+BFqCwzmr5sGUR6ZVvkiXvncfyup8sBCvfWJqrFDRXnYcmGKwjs9B\na3HtLxzBC3jCmJGInMno\n=jfqc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T10:23:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web