w_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/3f1dff10502a4fa3be74addced5998a2f4b3b8a1","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDNmMWRmZjEwNTAyYTRmYTNiZTc0YWRkY2VkNTk5OGEyZjRiM2I4YTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/3f0cfc920cca8c8beba56c1a4cc2f3b86b3788a1","sha":"3f0cfc920cca8c8beba56c1a4cc2f3b86b3788a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/3f0cfc920cca8c8beba56c1a4cc2f3b86b3788a1"}],"sha":"3f1dff10502a4fa3be74addced5998a2f4b3b8a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/3f1dff10502a4fa3be74addced5998a2f4b3b8a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73171182?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/magkue","id":73171182,"login":"magkue","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMTcxMTgy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/magkue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/3f0cfc920cca8c8beba56c1a4cc2f3b86b3788a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:31:29Z","email":"73171182+magkue@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Magnus Kühne"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T09:31:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Core: Fix the header breadcrumb overflowing on long trails (#2218)\n\n* Core: Collapse the breadcrumb instead of wrapping it in the header\n\nThe header has a fixed height, so a trail that wrapped (long participant names,\nnarrow windows) overflowed it. Once the full trail no longer fits, the crumbs\nbetween the first and the last move into a menu, and the last one truncates.\n\n* Core: Measure the visible breadcrumb instead of a hidden copy\n\nThe hidden full-length copy used to measure the trail duplicated every crumb in\nthe DOM, so text queries such as the course overview e2e check matched the\ninvisible copy. The trail now measures itself while shown in full and keeps that\nwidth to decide when to collapse. Adds an e2e check for collapsing and expanding,\nand the course overview page object only matches visible text.\n\n* Core: Remeasure new breadcrumb trails and cap crumbs only when collapsed\n\nA trail that changed while collapsed kept the previous trail''s width, so\nit could stay collapsed although it fit. Forget the stored width instead,\nso the new trail is measured before paint.\n\nEarlier crumbs are now capped in width only in the collapsed form, so long\ncourse or phase names are no longer cut off when the full trail fits.\ncollapseBreadcrumbs returns a single shape for every trail length.\n\n* E2E: Revert the visible-only course name locator\n\nIt was needed for the hidden measuring copy of the breadcrumb, which is\ngone, and the course overview trail never collapses.","tree":{"sha":"a41f60801790b55e752f13a025f725f2e1436730","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/a41f60801790b55e752f13a025f725f2e1436730"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/3f0cfc920cca8c8beba56c1a4cc2f3b86b3788a1","verification":{"payload":"tree a41f60801790b55e752f13a025f725f2e1436730\nparent 4117e0d86dee4a22f25d9e66176b328aeb795dff\nauthor Magnus Kühne <73171182+magkue@users.noreply.github.com> 1791106289 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791106289 +0200\n\nCore: Fix the header breadcrumb overflowing on long trails (#2218)\n\n* Core: Collapse the breadcrumb instead of wrapping it in the header\n\nThe header has a fixed height, so a trail that wrapped (long participant names,\nnarrow windows) overflowed it. Once the full trail no longer fits, the crumbs\nbetween the first and the last move into a menu, and the last one truncates.\n\n* Core: Measure the visible breadcrumb instead of a hidden copy\n\nThe hidden full-length copy used to measure the trail duplicated every crumb in\nthe DOM, so text queries such as the course overview e2e check matched the\ninvisible copy. The trail now measures itself while shown in full and keeps that\nwidth to decide when to collapse. Adds an e2e check for collapsing and expanding,\nand the course overview page object only matches visible text.\n\n* Core: Remeasure new breadcrumb trails and cap crumbs only when collapsed\n\nA trail that changed while collapsed kept the previous trail''s width, so\nit could stay collapsed although it fit. Forget the stored width instead,\nso the new trail is measured before paint.\n\nEarlier crumbs are now capped in width only in the collapsed form, so long\ncourse or phase names are no longer cut off when the full trail fits.\ncollapseBreadcrumbs returns a single shape for every trail length.\n\n* E2E: Revert the visible-only course name locator\n\nIt was needed for the hidden measuring copy of the breadcrumb, which is\ngone, and the course overview trail never collapses.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwhzxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAx84QAC+n/Yw1T6I38bMUHGOBz1oa\nDj8A8dN1kjsUkKSD4+z/BZMgouVseK6L6Nxm8tB+Voc9bonE1Y86j+Op3l3UtBpU\n426dGtBkUeq1NYIAYUFGLtj/EjxjeFcPsYFa5hYTsrZ2CgQNF85rJp/dksoxcq2w\nqERsz4GMwsKVroXOVipJL1dJPRkM4LSjIDcsUs9Tfqcuo5Hqa0S18jszFkMxeByV\nF+XMffdt3At4i3PBRWCaGQvGLfNU0kKwDq8uOAQEmNodb4XUAqdQJNB9y3+rhdDd\nMlxKptvdw8qFD3gIo84QyrxKuLLMMdK2C+Ec5ZkCax1D6uk7KKE1BRoY6cZZg7vM\nOHdJRLE+r4uMzX/mhWvF8P6aM6s/0gLtsAFvXVspLst5Jzsoork08m+wABYkJSur\nv0Ewa77B1vGhvTDYDb/bu5