at /manage/:studentId;\nold links redirect there.\n\n* Interview: Navigate to and from profiles with relative paths\n\n* Interview: Assert the exact profile URL using the seeded student id\n\n* Interview: Skip profile navigation for students without an id","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwUKECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAaUQACldPbwBK0vS37xT2oJxCiRw\nVcSgCBErI3Klvi0VTVUWn+erxYQRAQpAskVTSr3FukORaNxhNM3F41WUJjtH8rto\nT3gNaFpDHxD6j5zcyTbm8rAxqJd5pLtm61Wti30T7gBnel2oCNxtlDtglzlc1hyX\nO71O8wXBcaMmY0dqe+XQLS3QoBHL9p6HlOUS3mSL/xzlY1Pa7uNJQ15rT5hwwdZI\nSUN591jesUm+1m3/peTO/SyUs2V6In5zsrcH8KhswllsmAXksv1EqAXgC21UEaK+\ndUB0pua6dS+D8oXJcCR3/UTy0UJryNoXDi3wcWNoLl7ReoW+3NEBJg4DXFOqTvsC\nd8gmhBCHImIY6r+5URe4XUr8xMut3IPGZb+9urQpcVWU1tgRKH6Yn1hVn4Z3WZcP\nfeN/V9p2hWJ5V85K5pLvUG1hIzjUsoRfrsnkO9b+OgEKUgvaYYI4blUixQ2Pg5EU\n4TICUeIRfS0UyXirDoHlWRCe54QxhMA4MXdggFYhU8JEXNWQGGxz+YsLG3PD5e08\ngs27QN24egYkQn6q9/VlQvskJgpJGdgMGReFgB42218G97BXNjJCEq0Gca0uV5hx\nhHBoeDByKKkCBdaS5PIrbcGRyJ1/KbWb49zD21EtC/g7Cm4PdR2v/mxP37qZTwCa\nqvok0r8ycjnIt/hJTs0Y\n=OEH9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T17:59:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/bba9fb7ff4dd6226c97808f3c919c7168a2027b7","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKGJiYTlmYjdmZjRkZDYyMjZjOTc4MDhmM2M5MTljNzE2OGEyMDI3Yjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/daf219939e62e2bc0907ba46b0691371b3764b2a","sha":"daf219939e62e2bc0907ba46b0691371b3764b2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/daf219939e62e2bc0907ba46b0691371b3764b2a"}],"sha":"bba9fb7ff4dd6226c97808f3c919c7168a2027b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/bba9fb7ff4dd6226c97808f3c919c7168a2027b7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/daf219939e62e2bc0907ba46b0691371b3764b2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T16:39:50Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T16:39:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Core: Delete the phase modules'' data when a phase or course is deleted (#2195)\n\n* Core: Add a query for the phase modules holding a course phase''s data\n\nResolves each course phase to its type''s base URL in one round trip, which is\nwhat the deletion fan-out needs to address the modules.\n\n* Core: Delete the phase modules'' data when a course phase is deleted\n\nThe modules implement the SDK''s phase deletion endpoint, but nothing reached\nit, so every module kept its data for a phase that no longer existed.\n\nCore now asks each module that advertises the phase.deletion capability in its\n/info before it drops the phase row. Discovery goes through /info rather than\ninferring support from the deletion endpoint''s status: a reverse proxy without\na route for the module answers a DELETE with 405 and a GET with the client''s\nSPA document under status 200, neither of which may be read as ''this module\nhas nothing to delete''. Anything but a clean answer therefore fails the\ndeletion and keeps the phase, so the whole operation can be retried.\n\n* Core: Delete the phase modules'' data when a course is deleted\n\nA course row cascades into its phases, so the modules never got a chance to be\nasked once the course was gone. The fan-out now runs before anything else in\nDeleteCourse: the module''s own authorization resolves the course lecturer role\nthrough core, which needs both the phase row and the Keycloak roles to still\nexist, and a module that fails leaves the course fully intact for a retry.\n\n* Core: Refuse a course deletion when a phase was added during the module cleanup\n\nThe modules are asked about the course''s phases before the course row\ncascades into them, so a phase created in between was removed without its\nmodule ever being asked. DeleteCourse now locks the course row in the\ntransaction that deletes it. Inserting a phase takes a key share lock on its\ncourse, so no phase can appear from there on, and a phase that was added\nwhile the modules were asked fails the deletion with 409 before Keycloak or\nthe course are touched. A retry covers the new phase.\n\n* Core: Ask a module about every phase even after one of them fails\n\nThe first failed phase stopped the loop, so a phase that kept failing on\nevery retry meant the module was never asked about the phases after it.\nEvery failure is now collected and reported together.\n\n* Core: Only send the caller''s credentials to modules over HTTPS or internal hosts\n\nThe phase deletion forwards the caller''s Authorization header to the module.\nA base URL that uses plain HTTP to a public host would carry that token\nunencrypted, so the deletion is refused for it. Plain HTTP stays allowed for\nloopback and private addresses and for single-label hosts, which covers the\nlocal and Docker stacks.\n\n* Core: Answer a failed module deletion with a generic 502 and log it\n\nA failed phase deletion sent the module error to the client as it was,\nincluding the module URL and up to 1 KB of its response body, and nothing\nwas logged. Module failures are now marked with ErrModuleDeletionFailed.\nThe phase and course deletion handlers log them and answer 502 Bad Gateway\nwith a generic message. Any other phase deletion failure is logged and\nanswered with a generic 500.\n\n* Core: Bound the course deletion transaction with a timeout\n\nThe transaction that locks and deletes the course ran on the request\ncontext, which has no deadline. The course row lock and the pool connection\nwere therefore held for as long as the Keycloak deletion inside it took. The\ntransaction now runs under a 30 second timeout. That is longer than the\ndefault query timeout because it also covers the Keycloak network calls.\n\n* Core: Answer the deletion of a missing course with 404\n\nLocking the course row expects exactly one row, so deleting a course that\ndoes not exist failed with pgx.ErrNoRows and was answered with 500. The\nmissing row is now passed on and the handler answers 404.","tree":{"sha":"01cbb6eb1961691f37e142ef3034badc4ee119db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/01cbb6eb1961691f37e142ef3034badc4ee119db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/daf219939e62e2bc0907ba46b0691371b3764b2a","verification":{"payload":"tree 01cbb6eb1961691f37e142ef3034badc4ee119db\nparent c51a7380fdd41023b033063379cfaeb0ab26d2de\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1790959190 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790959190 +0200\n\nCore: Delete the phase modules'' data when a phase or course is deleted (#2195)\n\n* Core: Add a query for the phase modules holding a course phase''s data\n\nResolves each course phase to its type''s base URL in one round trip, which is\nwhat the deletion fan-out needs to address the modules.\n\n* Core: Delete the phase modules'' data when a course phase is deleted\n\nThe modules implement the SDK''s phase deletion endpoint, but nothing reached\nit, so every module kept its data for a phase that no longer existed.\n\nCore now asks each module that advertises the phase.deletion capability in its\n/info before it drops the phase row. Discovery goes through /info rather than\ninferring support from the deletion endpoint''s status: a reverse proxy without\na route for the module answers a DELETE with 405 and a GET with the client''s\nSPA document under status 200, neither of which may be read as ''this module\nhas nothing to delete''. Anything but a clean answer therefore fails the\ndeletion and keeps the phase, so the whole operation can be retried.\n\n* Core: Delete the phase modules'' data when a course is deleted\n\nA course row cascades into its phases, so the modules never got a chance to be\nasked once the course was gone. The fan-out now runs before anything else in\nDeleteCourse: the module''s own authorization resolves the course lecturer role\nthrough core, which needs both the phase row and the Keycloak roles to still\nexist, and a module that fails leaves the course fully intact for a retry.\n\n* Core: Refuse a course deletion when a phase was added during the module cleanup\n\nThe modules are asked about the course''s phases before the course row\ncascades into them, so a phase created in between was removed without its\nmodule ever being asked. DeleteCourse now locks the course row in the\ntransaction that deletes it. Inserting a phase takes a key share lock on its\ncourse, so no phase can appear from there on, and a phase that was added\nwhile the modules were asked fails the deletion with 409 before Keycloak or\nthe course are touched. A retry covers the new phase.\n\n* Core: Ask a module about every phase even after one of them fails\n\nThe first failed phase stopped the loop, so a phase that kept failing on\nevery retry meant the module was never asked about the phases after it.\nEvery failure is now collected and reported together.\n\n* Core: Only send the caller''s credentials to modules over HTTPS or internal hosts\n\nThe phase deletion forwards the caller''s Authorization header to the module.\nA base URL that uses plain HTTP to a public host would carry that token\nunencrypted, so the deletion is refused for it. Plain HTTP stays allowed for\nloopback and private addresses and for single-label hosts, which covers the\nlocal and Docker stacks.\n\n* Core: Answer a failed module deletion with a generic 502 and log it\n\nA failed phase deletion sent the module error to the client as it was,\nincluding the module URL and up to 1 KB of its response body, and nothing\nwas logged. Module failures are now marked with ErrModuleDeletionFailed.\nThe phase and course deletion handlers log them and answer 502 Bad Gateway\nwith a generic message. Any other phase deletion failure is logged and\nanswered with a generic 500.\n\n* Core: Bound the course deletion transaction with a timeout\n\nThe transaction that locks and deletes the course ran on the request\ncontext, which has no deadline. The course row lock and the pool connection\nwere therefore held for as long as the Keycloak deletion inside it took. The\ntransaction now runs under a 30 second timeout. That is longer than the\ndefault query timeout because it also covers the Keycloak network calls.\n\n* Core: Answer the deletion of a missing course with 404\n\nLocking the course row expects exactly one row, so deleting a course that\ndoes not exist failed with pgx.ErrNoRows and was answered with 500. The\nmissing row is now passed on and the handler answers 404.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv95WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs9MQAGWFoCNOmj1r2By49hVUUPc4\nhpVCf/g/M43sp+UCOlqunEwF6GLHLl9qcWu8zEobNzhjcqWGutArRWu99c5sbQtJ\nhN9YNuB+/wqys7jtcvbO/ml/m/bxuJy8yv5i9FG/Sq30bS/GEy2Wcipn5woijN0d\nPAlG3AC/dAu73Sa6cZx87uEF2bV0Ccc1EyiCM5lobgUT6PkPF0swOuYNAI+9NMsU\nJ+NbpfSJNfU3OMFefweMpY9dTIsCfzASvoakDi4VNqRQLx1JKsT2l4xGsiG4r1t0\nz92viJ04KB1euPms46Zr1UALy7QDSWurUFBl+B4kP5344pKCjBs4cG0KEKFoxZ80\nWgWeHjgZf7+/PfLZ2z6d8yAc4aReLY1isikeibya2ixa4Gr5mIdkvUDCtzQKHXdB\nNgfe/+uFNHy07N2j3k1AxemLqCRxz6N87Pd1z5wXegyJWpaXntfKvIQsI/CdtRNJ\nW9vk2Ue+eH/HxHi0UvTbdJKkcpA9Q0xG23iLRJN462FS4L4ihNb8dt/p75s6bHIV\n2hfHZ55vdcXgawIiLnJUAi19n7A7fBtgGWWK4RkBCl9CsTpWUAsTl+pSwlHgLuPv\nZxOQf3RXJIbF0r43jd9Aeq0PA9kD+BhX/wdlZbz/tl3qSaKWMeOyzw8pcWq08anq\nJWQtqhEJxrrAhkhSw0rl\n=I3c8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T16:39:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.gi