om/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/2cf9b1622a734bf4a48b827c4d6b4df7a2ca8e0d","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDJjZjliMTYyMmE3MzRiZjRhNDhiODI3YzRkNmI0ZGY3YTJjYThlMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/69018ca896a4fd5ac5300005185982e72490b28b","sha":"69018ca896a4fd5ac5300005185982e72490b28b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/69018ca896a4fd5ac5300005185982e72490b28b"}],"sha":"2cf9b1622a734bf4a48b827c4d6b4df7a2ca8e0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/2cf9b1622a734bf4a48b827c4d6b4df7a2ca8e0d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/69018ca896a4fd5ac5300005185982e72490b28b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:05:09Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:05:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Assessment: Allow lecturers to rename tutors in the assessment phase (#2199)\n\n* Assessment: Add a tutor display name column to the phase config\n\n* Assessment: Let lecturers set the tutor display name via the config API\n\n* Assessment: Add a tutor display name field to the tutor-evaluation settings\n\n* Assessment: Show the configured tutor display name across the phase\n\n* Docs: Explain how to rename tutors in the assessment phase\n\n* Assessment: Show the tutor display name in the sidebar\n\n* Assessment: Keep the lowercase tutor wording in running text\n\nThe tutor label now has a title form for headers and labels and a text form\nfor sentences. Without a custom display name, sentences read \"tutor\" again\ninstead of \"Tutor\"; a configured name is used exactly as entered. Sentences\nthat needed a plural are rephrased so they also work with names like \"PL\".\n\n* Assessment: Stop lowercasing the configured tutor name\n\nThe schema detail description and the reminder confirmation dialog lowercased\nthe whole title, so \"PL-Evaluation\" read \"pl-evaluation\". Both now use an\ninline form that only lowercases the built-in words.\n\n* Assessment: Load the tutor display name for every sidebar viewer\n\nThe sidebar skipped the config request for anyone enrolled in the course, so\nan enrolled lecturer saw \"Tutor Overview\" instead of the configured name.\nThe config endpoint already allows students, so the request is no longer\ngated.\n\n* Assessment: Trim the tutor display name before saving\n\nThe server trims the name, but the settings card compared and submitted the\nraw input. Saving \" Coach\" stored \"Coach\" and left the card dirty with Save\nstill enabled.\n\n* Docs: Describe the renamed sidebar entry for custom tutor names","tree":{"sha":"7b5b1042a372ce7cb77ccc7cf0c8afa4d429fe4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/7b5b1042a372ce7cb77ccc7cf0c8afa4d429fe4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/69018ca896a4fd5ac5300005185982e72490b28b","verification":{"payload":"tree 7b5b1042a372ce7cb77ccc7cf0c8afa4d429fe4e\nparent 7614fced7d5e5891f984d1a0479aae1f590005f4\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1790683509 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790683509 +0200\n\nAssessment: Allow lecturers to rename tutors in the assessment phase (#2199)\n\n* Assessment: Add a tutor display name column to the phase config\n\n* Assessment: Let lecturers set the tutor display name via the config API\n\n* Assessment: Add a tutor display name field to the tutor-evaluation settings\n\n* Assessment: Show the configured tutor display name across the phase\n\n* Docs: Explain how to rename tutors in the assessment phase\n\n* Assessment: Show the tutor display name in the sidebar\n\n* Assessment: Keep the lowercase tutor wording in running text\n\nThe tutor label now has a title form for headers and labels and a text form\nfor sentences. Without a custom display name, sentences read \"tutor\" again\ninstead of \"Tutor\"; a configured name is used exactly as entered. Sentences\nthat needed a plural are rephrased so they also work with names like \"PL\".\n\n* Assessment: Stop lowercasing the configured tutor name\n\nThe schema detail description and the reminder confirmation dialog lowercased\nthe whole title, so \"PL-Evaluation\" read \"pl-evaluation\". Both now use an\ninline form that only lowercases the built-in words.\n\n* Assessment: Load the tutor display name for every sidebar viewer\n\nThe sidebar skipped the config request for anyone enrolled in the course, so\nan enrolled lecturer saw \"Tutor Overview\" instead of the configured name.\nThe config endpoint already allows students, so the request is no longer\ngated.\n\n* Assessment: Trim the tutor display name before saving\n\nThe server trims the name, but the settings card compared and submitted the\nraw input. Saving \" Coach\" stored \"Coach\" and left the card dirty with Save\nstill enabled.\n\n* Docs: Describe the renamed sidebar entry for custom tutor names","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu6l1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApzUQAEjehUGmTj5JY3hLqA6+JA2g\nXTnociwqYmuIjixdAvG6gHLrWiyv0E4j/K+C/k5prz5yucyXqkSSJTKsXzUT+SXA\nAOBqabrv6QyMP4v9lNxCGOCL85/hKgJ4QGeR+zEfmsNRliPwX65CCQIhMLv3E60k\nPWjKaCs00Wb0RZ8o/dnQ0b5zYfwc9cdW27SFwTlG7xC2IVnZfQn74PfLv974CQBN\nLzSQ5KPv+2B+098r0NWcFZVpl+WTQ43NQGSrnI4dDXWTN6WS0BRD3UUKrI0ishog\njszj2pSYb9b9W02Nkg4z3Z5n/HAlnLjz+BL9MUuK9eSaW1+ZB5XQA1bq6vpwrVZK\nqbIlZgSJp0qFydsGgTFDTOYfid5IX3f86Ej6Cqb3xt1uAzS84l/+cxHi0yNpAPfg\nl951uOwihRM/tKAaoUzd6cL3y55IjUhBGcv0OS6+ZcC4K4kgyZy0v/MERyuhXbKx\nlgQIiSkRM2COXkGQCfxGxtYm57aUoRutiWj78BWqxPleE3QbJv+wQwwaE3G8RaSu\nug2UHKMuwP0JX20SbIRAuDCtx11wN4NbHhMLemcJ624rvV3CXcqhNw6zMFlDD4YK\nJj00wtPLnvrPm+lcWZNypj0y+dw3LUaDiHYpum074ZNXFIJ/N3S2cKUr0LLC1kUk\nN77T74C9Oo8RaoohFqSW\n=gT5P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T12:05:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/69018ca896a4fd5ac5300005185982e72490b28b","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDY5MDE4Y2E4OTZhNGZkNWFjNTMwMDAwNTE4NTk4MmU3MjQ5MGIyOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/7614fced7d5e5891f984d1a0479aae1f590005f4","sha":"7614fced7d5e5891f984d1a0479aae1f590005f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/7614fced7d5e5891f984d1a0479aae1f590005f4"}],"sha":"69018ca896a4fd5ac5300005185982e72490b28b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/69018ca896a4fd5ac5300005185982e72490b28b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/7614fced7d5e5891f984d1a0479aae1f590005f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:04:16Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:04:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Certificate: Support phase copy, the standardized config endpoint, and phase deletion (#2210)\n\n* Certificate: Move the settings routes off the standardized /config path\n\nThe SDK reserves `GET .../course_phase/:coursePhaseID/config` for the phase\nconfig contract, a map of configuration keys to their configured state. The\ncertificate service served its bespoke settings payload there instead, so the\nstandard endpoint could not be added next to it.\n\nThe settings routes now live under `/settings` (`GET`/`PUT /settings`,\n`/settings/release-date`, `/settings/student-page-text`, `/settings/template`)\nwith unchanged roles, handlers, and audit descriptions. The certificate client,\nthe router and audit wiring tests, and the e2e helpers and page object follow\nthe new paths.\n\n* Certificate: Serve the standardized phase config endpoint\n\nThe service advertised `phase.config` without serving the SDK contract. With\nthe settings moved to `/settings`, `GET .../config` is now registered through\n`promptTypes.RegisterConfigModule` for PromptAdmin and CourseLecturer, like the\nother phase modules.\n\nIt reports a single key, `template`: a template is the only setting a phase\nneeds before students can download, since a missing release date means the\ncertificate is available immediately. Unlike the settings read, the status\ncheck never creates the default config row.\n\n* Certificate: Treat a phase without a release date as unreleased\n\nA certificate phase without a release date was released: the student download\nand the status endpoint only withheld the certificate while a set date was\nstill in the future. The user documentation already describes the opposite,\nwith **Clear** making certificates unavailable until a new date is set, and a\npermissive default would release every copied phase from day one.\n\nStudents can now download only once a release date is set and has passed.\nWithout one, the status endpoint reports that the instructor has not released\nthe certificates yet. Staff access is unchanged.\n\nMigration 0004 keeps today''s released phases released: every config row with a\ntemplate and no release date gets the migration time as its release date, so\nthose certificates print that date from now on. The settings page copy, the\nstudent documentation, and the e2e journey that relied on the implicit release\nfollow the new rule.\n\n* Certificate: Copy the template and student page text with a course phase\n\nThe service had no copy endpoint, so core''s copyability check listed every\ncertificate phase as not copyable and a course copy left the new phase without\nits template.\n\nA new `copy` package implements `promptTypes.PhaseCopyHandler`, registered\nthrough `promptTypes.RegisterCopyModule` on the api group where core calls it,\nand `/info` now advertises `phase.copy`. It follows the team allocation module:\ncore''s self-copy probe is suppressed in the audit log, and a real copy records\nan event scoped to the target phase.\n\nThe copy is a single upsert that carries the Typst template and the student\npage text. The release date stays behind, so the copied phase is unreleased\nuntil a lecturer sets one, and download records belong to the source phase''s\nstudents. The user documentation describes what a course copy carries over.\n\n* Certificate: Delete course phase data when a phase is removed\n\nImplements the SDK''s course phase deletion handler, following the team\nallocation module. A new `coursePhaseDeletion` package registers\n`promptTypes.RegisterPhaseDeletionModule` on the `:coursePhaseID` group, where\nthe SDK protects the endpoint itself (PromptAdmin and CourseLecturer), and\n`/info` now advertises `phase.deletion`.\n\nThe handler deletes the phase''s certificate downloads and its config row with\nthe template, release date, and student page text inside one transaction. The\ntwo tables carry no foreign keys, so nothing cascades. Deleting a phase without\nstored data, or deleting it twice, succeeds.\n\nAs with the other modules, core does not call the endpoint yet (#2146).\n\n* Certificate: Fix doc comments and a test name from review\n\nThe phase config doc now says the release date is deliberately not a setup key, isReleased sits above ensureTemplateConfigured''s doc comment, and the copy probe test is named after the CopyPhase call it makes.","tree":{"sha":"e63610c5db0feb0b6701034c9947badd6fa66d7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/e63610c5db0feb0b6701034c9947badd6fa66d7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/7614fced7d5e5891f984d1a0479aae1f590005f4","verification":{"payload":"tree e63610c5db0feb0b6701034c9947badd6fa66d7b\nparent 5c41d866a0d1747e967eefab5f51a752c6ed504b\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1790683456 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790683456 +0200\n\nCertificate: Support phase copy, the standardized config endpoint, and phase deletion (#2210)\n\n* Certificate: Move the settings routes off the standardized /config path\n\nThe SDK reserves `GET .../course_phase/:coursePhaseID/config` for the phase\nconfig contract, a map of configuration keys to their configured state. The\ncertificate service served its bespoke settings payload there instead, so the\nstandard endpoint could not be added next to it.\n\nThe settings routes now live under `/settings` (`GET`/`PUT /settings`,\n`/settings/release-date`, `/settings/student-page-text`, `/settings/template`)\nwith unchanged roles, handlers, and audit descriptions. The certificate client,\nthe router and audit wiring tests, and the e2e helpers and page object follow\nthe new paths.\n\n* Certificate: Serve the standardized phase config endpoint\n\nThe service advertised `phase.config` without serving the SDK contract. With\nthe settings moved to `/settings`, `GET .../config` is now registered through\n`promptTypes.RegisterConfigModule` for PromptAdmin and CourseLecturer, like the\nother phase modules.\n\nIt reports a single key, `template`: a template is the only setting a phase\nneeds before students can download, since a missing release date means the\ncertificate is available immediately. Unlike the settings read, the status\ncheck never creates the default config row.\n\n* Certificate: Treat a phase without a release date as unreleased\n\nA certificate phase without a release date was released: the student download\nand the status endpoint only withheld the certificate while a set date was\nstill in the future. The user documentation already describes the opposite,\nwith **Clear** making certificates unavailable until a new date is set, and a\npermissive default would release every copied phase from day one.\n\nStudents can now download only once a release date is set and has passed.\nWithout one, the status endpoint reports that the instructor has not released\nthe certificates yet. Staff access is unchanged.\n\nMigration 0004 keeps today''s released phases released: every config row with a\ntemplate and no release date gets the migration time as its release date, so\nthose certificates print that date from now on. The settings page copy, the\nstudent documentation, and the e2e journey that relied on the implicit release\nfollow the new rule.\n\n* Certificate: Copy the template and student page text with a course phase\n\nThe service had no copy endpoint, so core''s copyability check listed every\ncertificate phase as not copyable and a course copy left the new phase without\nits template.\n\nA new `copy` package implements `promptTypes.PhaseCopyHandler`, registered\nthrough `promptTypes.RegisterCopyModule` on the api group where core calls it,\nand `/info` now advertises `phase.copy`. It follows the team allocation module:\ncore''s self-copy probe is suppressed in the audit log, and a real copy records\nan event scoped to the target phase.\n\nThe copy is a single upsert that carries the Typst template and the student\npage text. The release date stays behind, so the copied phase is unreleased\nuntil a lecturer sets one, and download records belong to the source phase''s\nstudents. The user documentation describes what a course copy carries over.\n\n* Certificate: Delete course phase data when a phase is removed\n\nImplements the SDK''s course phase deletion handler, following the team\nallocation module. A new `coursePhaseDeletion` package registers\n`promptTypes.RegisterPhaseDeletionModule` on the `:coursePhaseID` group, where\nthe SDK protects the endpoint itself (PromptAdmin and CourseLecturer), and\n`/info` now advertises `phase.deletion`.\n\nThe handler deletes the phase''s certificate downloads and its config row with\nthe template, release date, and student page text inside one transaction. The\ntwo tables carry no foreign keys, so nothing cascades. Deleting a phase without\nstored data, or deleting it twice, succeeds.\n\nAs with the other modules, core does not call the endpoint yet (#2146).\n\n* Certificate: Fix doc comments and a test name from review\n\nThe phase config doc now says the release date is deliberately not a setup key, isReleased sits above ensureTemplateConfigured''s doc comment, and the copy probe test is named after the CopyPhase call it makes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu6lACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR4oQAHvuhhzxX9mEg7v29aNcZWJD\nj5cksSkUfBjW2nBrXZH+TglLLzD+Xpai+3eoWX3HWSCHTeBkHrxQ+Flx5ysatxd4\nMeOREwiz+6uZyggDjAb7E3DtbIKPSjYcp1pRKr3ZgbWkH/YzY8bVjmmLDcG1NqYA\n9ZpG9rnEIjtJqYLONq8HWZ/w2B1CeMUOoUjpGwP2cbO3BUIHSltS88pEFZTvsdtm\nPbBF/A2GCYwyQNonCv0eE93Yroz02Y7fwsPjWGJdcStU6W5Ejo3MhcowCgs2/svN\nF3OXufp4U8bQn+5OkKBJiydW+2UJ7OiZc28PfkuXv2XS/4EV2CewrmyfSVDsT0Hu\nJl2s0iaJtMkz+KgOl+MxEVxlhIQKjDsHsD0F9tae2Ep0/A3tZvLmtlE7CpEddKCv\ntjTeibetjYrNNB/xqsWiu6CIcuBVxFcN4fVRsQQMXvZfEDfLculI2P08ully5/jD\ndCMcOSqsTYtKdo6fGbAa/U1jEv4lSrf+Dvmv6hA+Ct6cSEnwyGvke5ZpZUrjZWJ8\nd9WaWzqcZDHMrEw8WEjY2GSudRk4M3RuJkSCXIbF2lBe8jf+Uc4AFeB1DYoSPPTm\nhOmT7B+DTxL6qCzNHDLTYPjDpeJfWerEc8cTHuTT5Ol0+4ZYaCOnC9i4BbKgDsYb\nkh5A+mNsLJG5gIXEeDH9\n=EJdR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T12:04:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/7614fced7d5e5891f984d1a0479aae1f590005f4","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDc2MTRmY2VkN2Q1ZTU4OTFmOTg0ZDFhMDQ3OWFhZTFmNTkwMDA1ZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/5c41d866a0d1747e967eefab5f51a752c6ed504b","sha":"5c41d866a0d1747e967eefab5f51a752c6ed504b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/5c41d866a0d1747e967eefab5f51a752c6ed504b"}],"sha":"7614fced7d5e5891f984d1a0479aae1f590005f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/7614fced7d5e5891f984d1a0479aae1f590005f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/5c41d866a0d1747e967eefab5f51a752c6ed504b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T11:39:49Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T11:39:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Presentation: Delete course phase data when a phase is removed (#2208)\n\n* Presentation: Delete every stored material under a course phase prefix\n\nPhase deletion has to remove the uploaded materials of a phase even when their\nrows are already gone, so a retry after a failed storage call can finish the\njob. The storage adapter gains `DeletePrefix`, and the key prefix every\nmaterial of a phase is stored under moves into `storage.CoursePhasePrefix` so\nthe upload path and the cleanup cannot drift apart.\n\nThe S3 adapter lists the objects and deletes them one by one with the\nsingle-object call the service already uses against SeaweedFS, rather than\nthrough the batched `DeleteObjects`, and refuses an empty prefix, which would\nmatch the whole bucket.\n\n* Presentation: Delete a course phase''s data when the phase is removed\n\nImplements the SDK''s course phase deletion handler in a new\n`coursePhaseDeletion` package, laid out like team allocation''s.\n\nOne transaction deletes the phase''s presentations, which cascade to their\nmaterials, feedback forms, answers and contributors, then its slots, then its\nconfig, which cascades to the feedback categories. The order follows the\nschema: a presentation holds its slot with ON DELETE RESTRICT, and a feedback\nanswer restricts deleting its category.\n\nAfter the commit, every stored object under the phase''s key prefix is deleted,\nand a failure there fails the request so core keeps its rows and retries.\nWorking from the prefix rather than the deleted rows keeps that retry\neffective, and also removes uploads that were presigned but never completed.\n\n* Presentation: Serve and advertise the course phase deletion endpoint\n\nMount the deletion handler on the course phase group, so it answers\n`DELETE /presentation/api/course_phase/:coursePhaseID`, and report the\n`phase.deletion` capability on `/info`. Core''s deletion fan-out only calls\nmodules that advertise it.\n\nThe audit wiring test gains the new route, so its label stays the\nmodule-specific one rather than the derived \"Deleted course phase\".\n\n* Presentation: Refuse a delete prefix broader than one nested directory\n\n`DeletePrefix` only refused an empty prefix. A prefix without the trailing\nslash also matches sibling keys that merely start the same way, and a\ntop-level one such as `presentations/` would wipe every course phase.\n\nThe new `storage.ValidateDeletePrefix` accepts only a nested directory that\nends in a slash, like `CoursePhasePrefix` returns. The S3 adapter and the\nfake storage both call it, so tests cannot pass with a prefix production\nwould refuse.\n\n* Presentation: Delete a course phase''s stored materials in batches\n\n`DeletePrefix` deleted objects one request at a time, and core''s deletion\nfan-out gives each module request 10 s. A phase with a few hundred materials\ncould run past that and need several retries.\n\nEach listed page now goes out as one `DeleteObjects` call. Pages are capped at\n1000 keys, the batch limit, so a phase takes one request per thousand objects.\nA successful response can still report keys it failed to delete, and those\nfail the request so core retries.\n\nChecked against SeaweedFS 4.47, the version production runs, with S3 auth\nenabled: 2100 objects under one phase prefix went in about a second, while\nobjects of a neighboring phase and a key sharing the phase ID''s characters\nsurvived.","tree":{"sha":"916636042630cd578456858917376aa0c658628b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/916636042630cd578456858917376aa0c658628b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/5c41d866a0d1747e967eefab5f51a752c6ed504b","verification":{"payload":"tree 916636042630cd578456858917376aa0c658628b\nparent 727a68086df022b26e6f7087519172f744a49bf0\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1790681989 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790681989 +0200\n\nPresentation: Delete course phase data when a phase is removed (#2208)\n\n* Presentation: Delete every stored material under a course phase prefix\n\nPhase deletion has to remove the uploaded materials of a phase even when their\nrows are already gone, so a retry after a failed storage call can finish the\njob. The storage adapter gains `DeletePrefix`, and the key prefix every\nmaterial of a phase is stored under moves into `storage.CoursePhasePrefix` so\nthe upload path and the cleanup cannot drift apart.\n\nThe S3 adapter lists the objects and deletes them one by one with the\nsingle-object call the service already uses against SeaweedFS, rather than\nthrough the batched `DeleteObjects`, and refuses an empty prefix, which would\nmatch the whole bucket.\n\n* Presentation: Delete a course phase''s data when the phase is removed\n\nImplements the SDK''s course phase deletion handler in a new\n`coursePhaseDeletion` package, laid out like team allocation''s.\n\nOne transaction deletes the phase''s presentations, which cascade to their\nmaterials, feedback forms, answers and contributors, then its slots, then its\nconfig, which cascades to the feedback categories. The order follows the\nschema: a presentation holds its slot with ON DELETE RESTRICT, and a feedback\nanswer restricts deleting its category.\n\nAfter the commit, every stored object under the phase''s key prefix is deleted,\nand a failure there fails the request so core keeps its rows and retries.\nWorking from the prefix rather than the deleted rows keeps that retry\neffective, and also removes uploads that were presigned but never completed.\n\n* Presentation: Serve and advertise the course phase deletion endpoint\n\nMount the deletion handler on the course phase group, so it answers\n`DELETE /presentation/api/course_phase/:coursePhaseID`, and report the\n`phase.deletion` capability on `/info`. Core''s deletion fan-out only calls\nmodules that advertise it.\n\nThe audit wiring test gains the new route, so its label stays the\nmodule-specific one rather than the derived \"Deleted course phase\".\n\n* Presentation: Refuse a delete prefix broader than one nested directory\n\n`DeletePrefix` only refused an empty prefix. A prefix without the trailing\nslash also matches sibling keys that merely start the same way, and a\ntop-level one such as `presentations/` would wipe every course phase.\n\nThe new `storage.ValidateDeletePrefix` accepts only a nested directory that\nends in a slash, like `CoursePhasePrefix` returns. The S3 adapter and the\nfake storage both call it, so tests cannot pass with a prefix production\nwould refuse.\n\n* Presentation: Delete a course phase''s stored materials in batches\n\n`DeletePrefix` deleted objects one request at a time, and core''s deletion\nfan-out gives each module request 10 s. A phase with a few hundred materials\ncould run past that and need several retries.\n\nEach listed page now goes out as one `DeleteObjects` call. Pages are capped at\n1000 keys, the batch limit, so a phase takes one request per thousand objects.\nA successful response can still report keys it failed to delete, and those\nfail the request so core retries.\n\nChecked against SeaweedFS 4.47, the version production runs, with S3 auth\nenabled: 2100 objects under one phase prefix went in about a second, while\nobjects of a neighboring phase and a key sharing the phase ID''s characters\nsurvived.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu6OFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdEYQAERWqFW/YAggM4sJ37cQ2rCH\nl3W2LXTk5IM3wtfy8sAIyTcPpioZiZm4MZmaXAmZ3yftPGQ2eSc2m/+sSZ+5+UOZ\nh9dE9f5UlCybFN34nhN9RvM6TGiCEp+F9YwIESNTDSTOK4bOsesAOLC3Roc8huAj\nQWoasqqCVZB7jBvN3VeFSHi0gH/XWHa1epb6k+D1ieBLTV9AjYAHstpGtgu73998\nmvVT2Mhj/2iPFvUDnUtPYKpAs1Neql2xRtSwnQyviIoEKwtG21tG2wOhkezRcI/C\nlQcSfv/CWRagCtm8ToAGsQZsy8nGmMHoIB8wSfUFPhQ9ymwegNLlPx0t+eZ9aKsG\nJs7lHgOcH5d5FFtCoNMh4VqokhcTovo+QXI4SEIsYeUaVDjQqm+CWhBwU4tevgd2\nm6mtDrvJ5ddgh0OipK4P6bAn3DPyxC1k3Tb3Qp6tzKGlCGRt+N/4nnYrEK7td7s0\n1djD9f47k4dgSBt/eHpBHVEGkkLO5nf28X5EqezIvixAVdHkJmbxdIDRgaEJdS8E\nJ1wTcDnjKZDSoH4aUq/rCZu3IakLvXH3paRX0B+5Eqf9TPvT4xdwHPMyCwA0vRxT\nN6K/7MC6SwTsLqq3k5Jxuhjo1m8+V/qRleG/o+mfC6/mSViLUGyyszxC9EQYfw6+\nrC5i5m0p8JzXO2KP79zg\n=7JxW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T11:39:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/5c41d866a0d1747e967eefab5f51a752c6ed504b","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDVjNDFkODY2YTBkMTc0N2U5NjdlZWZhYjVmNTFhNzUyYzZlZDUwNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/727a68086df022b26e6f7087519172f744a49bf0","sha":"727a68086df022b26e6f7087519172f744a49bf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/727a68086df022b26e6f7087519172f744a49bf0"}],"sha":"5c41d866a0d1747e967eefab5f51a752c6ed504b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/5c41d866a0d1747e967eefab5f51a752c6ed504b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/renovate","id":29139614,"login":"renovate[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjkxMzk2MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/727a68086df022b26e6f7087519172f744a49bf0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T11:37:12Z","email":"29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"renovate[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T11:37:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Dependencies: Update all non-major dependencies (#2212)\n\n* Dependencies: Update all non-major dependencies\n\n* Core: Use the SDK''s ErrorResponse instead of a local copy\n\nprompt-sdk v1.4.0 ships utils.ErrorResponse, identical to core''s. With both\nparsed, swag no longer finds a unique utils.ErrorResponse and the API spec\ncheck fails. Core now builds its error bodies from the SDK type, so the\ngenerated swagger docs stay unchanged.\n\n* E2E: Expect 403 for role denials from phase servers\n\nprompt-sdk v1.4.0 answers an authenticated caller without the required role\nwith 403 instead of 401. Unauthenticated requests still get 401.\n\n* E2E: Open the date range picker through its calendar button\n\nprompt-ui-components 1.5.0 replaced the #date trigger of DatePickerWithRange\nwith typed start/end inputs and an \"Open calendar\" button, so the course\ncreate and copy specs timed out waiting for #date.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maximilian Rapp <maximilian.rapp@tum.de>","tree":{"sha":"81212089deda1b11d16606bebe5946411c57ec00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/81212089deda1b11d16606bebe5946411c57ec00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/727a68086df022b26e6f7087519172f744a49bf0","verification":{"payload":"tree 81212089deda1b11d16606bebe5946411c57ec00\nparent cae3c39557398d84330a7961cef74b35d8727324\nauthor renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790681832 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790681832 +0200\n\nDependencies: Update all non-major dependencies (#2212)\n\n* Dependencies: Update all non-major dependencies\n\n* Core: Use the SDK''s ErrorResponse instead of a local copy\n\nprompt-sdk v1.4.0 ships utils.ErrorResponse, identical to core''s. With both\nparsed, swag no longer finds a unique utils.ErrorResponse and the API spec\ncheck fails. Core now builds its error bodies from the SDK type, so the\ngenerated swagger docs stay unchanged.\n\n* E2E: Expect 403 for role denials from phase servers\n\nprompt-sdk v1.4.0 answers an authenticated caller without the required role\nwith 403 instead of 401. Unauthenticated requests still get 401.\n\n* E2E: Open the date range picker through its calendar button\n\nprompt-ui-components 1.5.0 replaced the #date trigger of DatePickerWithRange\nwith typed start/end inputs and an \"Open calendar\" button, so the course\ncreate and copy specs timed out waiting for #date.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maximilian Rapp <maximilian.rapp@tum.de>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu6LoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5yIQAEQbkyWEKZyDiqZhImwF6q97\n/R39g+dGzNGr/RCiUbiaVMWxnAbMhTgEJYMK/yxkMDqbcBIwxanwa7aMsXcmZzz9\n7p7VWidgNe9rLwlTqqVXqSz8VM0iPxDea6o/hxYl+XFZVa4zYALvHJMe7vXDlvym\n3ZpYWMJxXgD4DzauG6cbufHeJALDOEhD0Mv5WVqs0Bx8MnsX8C9sUvDvYZo3S3jc\n+YzqoF3L93DJbmrc1UranTZR2SaxUCPH9P7DQOtBdX0bodikCalufS1Nx58tfZvH\nWivuOGZ0cTiW3BhZISfE+ReujdaZMVksVJVHG8oFj1iL4gzaGFkntRkIwFnQrA6h\nUuW+rcJH5ImUbB0a8GyFidm7ZE2TDMaZ2B4SHq/oZUAdQtA4IrDX7qYc65AHwB+6\nmJVSHSgqCI0lkuzTDgmVdul7dm7hBL9TKoIC90GHJUI361ILIVh2KUo4pdHagyJx\nVvTRehU+Xq1bqhMtgrsmrfLv+5zhp8Zk8oHi3YjqCGM8aMOWSjn59VJxXQ9lwNtX\nywFAVgIZ8kL4FR0C5RfGkLBGaeFmMWbWYz/0MXSFHal34AT86LxayFsqOwiYuX7G\nAUwgjapmqbjhAVJYOyEXgS7Zn0/96jgVodh1C1aRy+vKFiD54txYziIUlPR3sGLx\n1Iywetbn0nxP0sL0u055\n=YO+3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T11:37:12Z"}},"commit