lowing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/4e62757d3570522cae20e8581482907690cf624d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T21:59:52Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T21:59:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Core: Fix the cache invalidations that reached less than their name suggested (#2159)\n\n* `Core`: Delete the configurator graph invalidation that reaches nothing\n\n* `Core`: Scope the application assessment invalidation to the assessed phase\n\n* `Core`: Invalidate the caches a student university data write makes stale\n\n* `Core`: Stop a missing id turning a scoped invalidation into a no-op\n\nScoping `applicationAssessmentSaved` to the assessed phase reaches less\nthan the unscoped key it replaced when the phase id is missing:\n`invalidateQueries` compares every segment of the prefix it matches on,\nso a key holding `undefined` matches nothing cached at all, where the\nold `participations.all()` always matched.\n\nThe ids come from `useParams`, so every id-scoped event in this module\ncan be handed an `undefined`. Truncate the key at the missing segment\ninside `invalidate`, which over-invalidates for the price of a refetch\ninstead of leaving stale rows on screen, and closes the class rather\nthan this one event. Every key in `coreKeys` opens with a literal, so a\ntruncated key is never the whole cache.","tree":{"sha":"b2383c905e7ea3d4174c725d2b707081ec9da9f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/b2383c905e7ea3d4174c725d2b707081ec9da9f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/4e62757d3570522cae20e8581482907690cf624d","verification":{"payload":"tree b2383c905e7ea3d4174c725d2b707081ec9da9f7\nparent c1cb0f3910513743e4d49e292fc36610c3274a07\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788904792 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788904792 +0100\n\nCore: Fix the cache invalidations that reached less than their name suggested (#2159)\n\n* `Core`: Delete the configurator graph invalidation that reaches nothing\n\n* `Core`: Scope the application assessment invalidation to the assessed phase\n\n* `Core`: Invalidate the caches a student university data write makes stale\n\n* `Core`: Stop a missing id turning a scoped invalidation into a no-op\n\nScoping `applicationAssessmentSaved` to the assessed phase reaches less\nthan the unscoped key it replaced when the phase id is missing:\n`invalidateQueries` compares every segment of the prefix it matches on,\nso a key holding `undefined` matches nothing cached at all, where the\nold `participations.all()` always matched.\n\nThe ids come from `useParams`, so every id-scoped event in this module\ncan be handed an `undefined`. Truncate the key at the missing segment\ninside `invalidate`, which over-invalidates for the price of a refetch\ninstead of leaving stale rows on screen, and closes the class rather\nthan this one event. Every key in `coreKeys` opens with a literal, so a\ntruncated key is never the whole cache.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoIVYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApmUQAKq8/sz0SmjmIeWOLHTP7Ror\nxdHBsTkF2xcWBTBBu/jScGVU2K2KCbN6BA1FKXLXRUIG9x22S86+QwAzZcHuwJpZ\nyziwr4kCh5twDdLNXDsi2Uyu/a7fd5P6RBIH+G3wtGthwqY2Fk9sv3A/BeFKc2SH\nT60MFYGnLdWlA5TygRJeMi/DZwXRM67Q5RsVX5TPeniXWHtw/DW4aB3VytWdxIk5\nuVC9U8RthkOQL2/HaAcXnz0aqWcZ1QpQ8yjqIa9yoK0zgeW2dLZpfhtLu9KvCvok\nqdo8kKJGMURnqDpRl3BZ0KrKPDJEfvCUMdMTanqTjp/zuMGqZJ0R0mX98MkvsLaP\nkO098J2P2YPv/BUEoPcOmNy6iDg5sZ4M0NL49dpXKH/KK5jFHiorm+GM9R7xzdJU\nU7griQwa4ZUkXE3gZB0TMSh3dTgzCqemlM6blumpavfLC78clCV5OvhNIdJhf0YR\nwKcrfOCDjHfvhK4ZRxwa/EvdjeqLkaI1GEHy/qmFxp2TD50s8y3u2nk8nTmEdW4t\nNMmgl8Lp35zBIsDkt1HJhiXkL+qXF9Ez/WNqeTqOklgFJKogZ+v2dJgYbVlcU5J7\nD6b68IPRA9GiQAYHZB4PtO2m12bKJTUslDoXcnTzTv5ta4f6nwwV9TBuYrzCTEuH\nJm6JBP9qK1mYab1yz6jm\n=SZnF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T21:59:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/4e62757d3570522cae20e8581482907690cf624d","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDRlNjI3NTdkMzU3MDUyMmNhZTIwZTg1ODE0ODI5MDc2OTBjZjYyNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/c1cb0f3910513743e4d49e292fc36610c3274a07","sha":"c1cb0f3910513743e4d49e292fc36610c3274a07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/c1cb0f3910513743e4d49e292fc36610c3274a07"}],"sha":"4e62757d3570522cae20e8581482907690cf624d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/4e62757d3570522cae20e8581482907690cf624d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/c1cb0f3910513743e4d49e292fc36610c3274a07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T21:58:49Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T21:58:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Core: Adopt the shared PromptTable column types (#2155)\n\n* Core: Use the shared PromptTable column types in the management console tables\n\nThe management console tables declared their columns with ColumnDef and Row\nimported straight from @tanstack/react-table, while the tables that render them\ncome from @tumaet/prompt-ui-components and are built on the lib''s own table\nfeature set. Switch them to the PromptTableColumnDef and PromptTableRow aliases\nthe lib exports, so the column definitions are tied to the table that consumes\nthem instead of to a directly imported table version.\n\nAlso replace the two remaining getValue<string>() calls with the\ngetValue() as string cast already used by the surrounding columns.\n\n* Assessment: Use the shared PromptTable column types in the overview tables\n\nSame change as for the core tables: the tutor overview and evaluation\nparticipants overview declared their columns with ColumnDef imported from\n@tanstack/react-table even though PromptTable renders them, so point them at\nthe PromptTableColumnDef alias exported by @tumaet/prompt-ui-components.","tree":{"sha":"d746cbb06ba1874317b47bb574ba1a7471dce32e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/d746cbb06ba1874317b47bb574ba1a7471dce32e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/c1cb0f3910513743e4d49e292fc36610c3274a07","verification":{"payload":"tree d746cbb06ba1874317b47bb574ba1a7471dce32e\nparent 6a0245e5e306680c2c607932db8c992fc8c461b7\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788904729 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788904729 +0100\n\nCore: Adopt the shared PromptTable column types (#2155)\n\n* Core: Use the shared PromptTable column types in the management console tables\n\nThe management console tables declared their columns with ColumnDef and Row\nimported straight from @tanstack/react-table, while the tables that render them\ncome from @tumaet/prompt-ui-components and are built on the lib''s own table\nfeature set. Switch them to the PromptTableColumnDef and PromptTableRow aliases\nthe lib exports, so the column definitions are tied to the table that consumes\nthem instead of to a directly imported table version.\n\nAlso replace the two remaining getValue<string>() calls with the\ngetValue() as string cast already used by the surrounding columns.\n\n* Assessment: Use the shared PromptTable column types in the overview tables\n\nSame change as for the core tables: the tutor overview and evaluation\nparticipants overview declared their columns with ColumnDef imported from\n@tanstack/react-table even though PromptTable renders them, so point them at\nthe PromptTableColumnDef alias exported by @tumaet/prompt-ui-components.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoIUZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVtQQAAI+wKBwUj6Tm53s27Wetzsu\n84aIgFyRVaOG6qPxJlO68giL7qV9D9DJeaEDnP63dQQzGiHl1rbWJq2wc2DI7W9W\nSKCJny/APJrVTOEeyHqKdCNteIWwuuBaRKcpdNVfuvVyAp+fZClxXI+1Sr/xdWjo\nYTKaez90Wj1YDcW4bnNclshrQ18qgDrvS5FbIBBN91j/NR8HDEEYx8bh8qkkXF42\ncAgFT31XVJKS+Cu0yBFlCFZFJzOzXjsNZ8FaILenHF3he5hbtTjrOrmIwf4Yhl5F\ngPGzH5dGoeG8ehhwv3pTu/NEXD00sWk4Ik2/iFkRs0cvpYuhi0B9C8CulmXnt1Bw\ng3tUXI/YEYEqAMzlgJs9JFpEMZ9Iv9qkrsY64dv/VqN6wdgTdmuEb6v8Vc6ROmPK\nrrYUoSpBPvinm3hFVl81oDXD9J/90uctHI0AqtVKno9QI9cwqaWvRUh1fIMtgbdL\n8c0LbmqHcQQijZNUlMY3GCb/ToNfN/CWvQ7/aUAem3qhbzhie+wK+S3pAGZwEhKE\nYwDXldIRwJjYZrYSPpVRXg7fiBtMKsV0Oy64SFbx9ndyhHw+/e/m44wWvHg2HoYE\ns/gUXvcwgdmZxDNyaOwZzRoflAMIAj8O4kvZ81Aqb/PLIJeWk1bHbX8rWK+A2TdS\nMc5L6TeLXFuS0BXfonfI\n=l5Ij\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T21:58:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/c1cb0f3910513743e4d49e292fc36610c3274a07","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKGMxY2IwZjM5MTA1MTM3NDNlNGQ0OWUyOTJmYzM2NjEwYzMyNzRhMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/6a0245e5e306680c2c607932db8c992fc8c461b7","sha":"6a0245e5e306680c2c607932db8c992fc8c461b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/6a0245e5e306680c2c607932db8c992fc8c461b7"}],"sha":"c1cb0f3910513743e4d49e292fc36610c3274a07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/c1cb0f3910513743e4d49e292fc36610c3274a07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/6a0245e5e306680c2c607932db8c992fc8c461b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T21:36:41Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T21:36:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Core: Sort about page contributors by commit count (#2151)\n\n* Core: Sort about page contributors by commit count\n\nThe about page ordered contributor cards by a hand-maintained `position`\nfield that had drifted from reality. Replace it with the commit count the\nGitHub contributors API already returns, keeping a single `pinnedPosition`\noverride so the project manager stays first.\n\nAlso refresh the roles to match what people actually worked on, and add\nMagnus Kühne (developer tooling and testing infrastructure) and Felix T.J.\nDietrich (intro course phase), who were missing entirely.\n\n* Core: Pin the PROMPT creator on the about page\n\nValeryia Andraichuk is not returned by the contributors endpoint, so her\n`contributions` count is 0 by construction and commit-count sorting could\nonly ever place her last. A `pinnedPosition` keeps her second, as she was\nbefore, independent of commit count.\n\nDedupe the contributor list by login so the special-case fetch cannot\nrender a second card with a duplicate React key if she ever does appear\nin the contributors response.\n\n* `Core`: Assert the pinned position the contributor test only claimed to check\n\nWith a single pinned entry at position 2, the contributor landed first\nwhatever its position was, so the assertion held for position 1 as well\nand the test name was the only thing pinning it. A second pinned entry\nahead of it makes the position part of what fails.","tree":{"sha":"529aa994bed1e1e29edc2f5729de9a9e8b3849a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/529aa994bed1e1e29edc2f5729de9a9e8b3849a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/6a0245e5e306680c2c607932db8c992fc8c461b7","verification":{"payload":"tree 529aa994bed1e1e29edc2f5729de9a9e8b3849a3\nparent 512ce641133fbf2388f95f77c123da69df0caae8\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788903401 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788903401 +0100\n\nCore: Sort about page contributors by commit count (#2151)\n\n* Core: Sort about page contributors by commit count\n\nThe about page ordered contributor cards by a hand-maintained `position`\nfield that had drifted from reality. Replace it with the commit count the\nGitHub contributors API already returns, keeping a single `pinnedPosition`\noverride so the project manager stays first.\n\nAlso refresh the roles to match what people actually worked on, and add\nMagnus Kühne (developer tooling and testing infrastructure) and Felix T.J.\nDietrich (intro course phase), who were missing entirely.\n\n* Core: Pin the PROMPT creator on the about page\n\nValeryia Andraichuk is not returned by the contributors endpoint, so her\n`contributions` count is 0 by construction and commit-count sorting could\nonly ever place her last. A `pinnedPosition` keeps her second, as she was\nbefore, independent of commit count.\n\nDedupe the contributor list by login so the special-case fetch cannot\nrender a second card with a duplicate React key if she ever does appear\nin the contributors response.\n\n* `Core`: Assert the pinned position the contributor test only claimed to check\n\nWith a single pinned entry at position 2, the contributor landed first\nwhatever its position was, so the assertion held for position 1 as well\nand the test name was the only thing pinning it. A second pinned entry\nahead of it makes the position part of what fails.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoH/pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZDsQAKQrmNmzl2psRn0Hf5VjQxnm\nIQq1/h7Sv5YeTiMo1lE7wwsQazyP64j4v4ng561trTeaMcHXjEdVd+RgRJ+zXqzs\nrlTLMYBILgVnfMetQ0yavdEmkhXe6BJD9HdyflDngky/g/b45QQh8idMs1Sbnrvt\ndfIjAMEa4WevcPk4gad5oO61KgZEPPnQaCXgIPWdnGWxhV2xZkJcUaW12ocP5hBw\nyYJUBqACtoew2KMSRYaq5+nQYFKjBPoMA46pn2+1g0NH2kiR+xRkptHcnh+5HLSc\n6zwp6kGGvNQYGaNELjAAwWvbs4a/eVRTlXS/CnLR5pPvydv0tm9N+GAuv2By9Mcu\n+XKgD/4d+FMdjZzETefEfu+LsJ/V88UxlcdayK2tRpF2O1JxHyLjLvp88pMpCaBI\nmh8CI2AdFM7YKv/VTqxZxlXj8dAEKeq9egC+NGsiW1D