062ac1e7ae60043dfa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/417879406f741de25fd15a6069627cacfff2087b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:35:52Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:35:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"New Phase: Replace the example server service singletons with constructors (#2137)\n\n* Example: Replace the example service singleton with a constructor\n\n`InitExampleModule` built the service, assigned it to a package variable and\nregistered the routes in one call that returned nothing. It is now\n`NewExampleService(queries, conn)` plus `RegisterRoutes(group, service,\nauthMiddleware)`, and the handler and the business function became methods on\nthe service.\n\nThis service is the template `make new-phase` copies, so the shape here is the\nshape every new phase starts from. The comments say which part is the pattern\nand which part is the placeholder, so a phase author fills in the body rather\nthan reintroducing a global.\n\n`GetExampleInfo` now takes the request context explicitly rather than the gin\ncontext, which is the split the other services use: gin stops at `router.go`.\n\n* Example: Replace the config and copy singletons with constructors\n\nBoth modules now expose `NewXService(queries, conn)` and `RegisterRoutes(group,\nservice, authMiddleware)`, and the SDK handler methods moved onto the services.\n\n`promptTypes.PhaseConfigHandler` and `promptTypes.PhaseCopyHandler` are\nstructural interfaces, so `ConfigService` and `CopyService` implement them\ndirectly and the registration passes the service itself. The\n`ExampleServerConfigHandler` and `ExampleServerCopyHandler` structs are gone:\nthey held no state, and a zero-value handler is exactly the shape a scaffolded\nphase should not start from, because it compiles and then dereferences nil at\nrequest time once someone fills in the body.\n\nUnlike the interview service, which had the same two unused services and lost\nthem, these stay: this is the template `make new-phase` copies, and their whole\njob is to show a phase author where the queries and the pool belong.\n\nEvery service is constructed in one block in `main.go` before any route group\nis registered. Registration order itself is unchanged.\n\n* Example: Update the scaffolding scripts and README for the new module shape\n\n`make new-phase` and the external-phase `init.sh` renamed `InitExampleModule`,\n`setupExampleRouter`, `ExampleServerConfigHandler` and `ExampleServerCopyHandler`\ninto the new phase''s names. None of those identifiers exist any more, so the\nsubstitutions are dropped. `ExampleService` still needs renaming and now also\ncovers `NewExampleService`; `RegisterRoutes` is package-scoped and needs none.\n\nThe README''s file map still described `example/main.go` and \"creates the service\nsingleton\". It now describes the constructor and route registration split, and\nsays to reach the database through the receiver.\n\n* General: Document the service construction pattern in the Go rules\n\nThe rules pointed at `example_server`''s `config/` and `copy/` packages as the\npattern to copy while those packages still held singletons and zero-value\nhandler structs, so the guidance and the reference disagreed.\n\nThree rules are now written down: construction is separate from route\nregistration, handlers are methods on the service they use, and the SDK config\nand copy interfaces are implemented on the service rather than on a wrapper.\nEach records when the exception applies, so a handler struct that composes two\nservices or stands in for a service defined in another package still reads as\ncorrect.\n\n* Example: Rename the camelCase service variable when scaffolding a phase\n\nThe generator smoke test failed because `exampleService`, the local variable\nintroduced in the example server''s main.go, survived `rename_tokens`. The\n`\\bexample\\b` fallback does not fire inside a compound identifier, and the\nexisting `ExampleService` rule is case-sensitive, so the scaffolded phase kept\nthe literal token.\n\nAdd the camelCase counterpart to both scaffolders, next to the PascalCase rule\nand alongside the other camelCase entries (`exampleInfo`, `exampleRouter`,\n`exampleServer`).","tree":{"sha":"ca02391e1d9e692ab067e767ee22f83ad1eec8e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/ca02391e1d9e692ab067e767ee22f83ad1eec8e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/417879406f741de25fd15a6069627cacfff2087b","verification":{"payload":"tree ca02391e1d9e692ab067e767ee22f83ad1eec8e4\nparent 2b3f0d103d9a7f71af1820cb461106585289f5fd\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788356152 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788356152 +0200\n\nNew Phase: Replace the example server service singletons with constructors (#2137)\n\n* Example: Replace the example service singleton with a constructor\n\n`InitExampleModule` built the service, assigned it to a package variable and\nregistered the routes in one call that returned nothing. It is now\n`NewExampleService(queries, conn)` plus `RegisterRoutes(group, service,\nauthMiddleware)`, and the handler and the business function became methods on\nthe service.\n\nThis service is the template `make new-phase` copies, so the shape here is the\nshape every new phase starts from. The comments say which part is the pattern\nand which part is the placeholder, so a phase author fills in the body rather\nthan reintroducing a global.\n\n`GetExampleInfo` now takes the request context explicitly rather than the gin\ncontext, which is the split the other services use: gin stops at `router.go`.\n\n* Example: Replace the config and copy singletons with constructors\n\nBoth modules now expose `NewXService(queries, conn)` and `RegisterRoutes(group,\nservice, authMiddleware)`, and the SDK handler methods moved onto the services.\n\n`promptTypes.PhaseConfigHandler` and `promptTypes.PhaseCopyHandler` are\nstructural interfaces, so `ConfigService` and `CopyService` implement them\ndirectly and the registration passes the service itself. The\n`ExampleServerConfigHandler` and `ExampleServerCopyHandler` structs are gone:\nthey held no state, and a zero-value handler is exactly the shape a scaffolded\nphase should not start from, because it compiles and then dereferences nil at\nrequest time once someone fills in the body.\n\nUnlike the interview service, which had the same two unused services and lost\nthem, these stay: this is the template `make new-phase` copies, and their whole\njob is to show a phase author where the queries and the pool belong.\n\nEvery service is constructed in one block in `main.go` before any route group\nis registered. Registration order itself is unchanged.\n\n* Example: Update the scaffolding scripts and README for the new module shape\n\n`make new-phase` and the external-phase `init.sh` renamed `InitExampleModule`,\n`setupExampleRouter`, `ExampleServerConfigHandler` and `ExampleServerCopyHandler`\ninto the new phase''s names. None of those identifiers exist any more, so the\nsubstitutions are dropped. `ExampleService` still needs renaming and now also\ncovers `NewExampleService`; `RegisterRoutes` is package-scoped and needs none.\n\nThe README''s file map still described `example/main.go` and \"creates the service\nsingleton\". It now describes the constructor and route registration split, and\nsays to reach the database through the receiver.\n\n* General: Document the service construction pattern in the Go rules\n\nThe rules pointed at `example_server`''s `config/` and `copy/` packages as the\npattern to copy while those packages still held singletons and zero-value\nhandler structs, so the guidance and the reference disagreed.\n\nThree rules are now written down: construction is separate from route\nregistration, handlers are methods on the service they use, and the SDK config\nand copy interfaces are implemented on the service rather than on a wrapper.\nEach records when the exception applies, so a handler struct that composes two\nservices or stands in for a service defined in another package still reads as\ncorrect.\n\n* Example: Rename the camelCase service variable when scaffolding a phase\n\nThe generator smoke test failed because `exampleService`, the local variable\nintroduced in the example server''s main.go, survived `rename_tokens`. The\n`\\bexample\\b` fallback does not fire inside a compound identifier, and the\nexisting `ExampleService` rule is case-sensitive, so the scaffolded phase kept\nthe literal token.\n\nAdd the camelCase counterpart to both scaffolders, next to the PascalCase rule\nand alongside the other camelCase entries (`exampleInfo`, `exampleRouter`,\n`exampleServer`).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmCY4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdiwQAGCtI3yPcsCkeSokKMdDeHy9\n7wv2QZ+zojSf1poggwJCmCw7grmaL3Y8t3gs8RDizCR9N/TElFl9uBjklsYSogXN\ntPNqCEo1xIdNJzVVxB2dHHi1pjdvwHhNjUKsH/asMExVB7+LUyB0ZGYSNA8pLBQE\naHEBk3ypf9vMhkJkSVODV0GrfJWKC3/Klt2k8RSU6ovdYOYurDNnOzfqyxst7jEV\nybX/4nixDVQ9hKHA/3+BSuQCymFEd04XDqmfsMA4g0yjUYpo6U/yllo70vsyHU60\nxkN29dYLR0FM0PwiQtBZC4/APuWZHr1hQqMrA59adySdCME8yaVsBFpW0I2RdPdG\nXAOTlBhxLoda1xUySnMhLiakE6xkgWkPE4c/nOGDkesgGQKLbJWBgmU3Q36BKxkF\n+rLRvWXAxSd0kCW1YUkuGD79TzKv9OyJrysxgmbo8XQUZvsMcp71Jv05xpA+SNP0\nNUogWDaqXoWXK7ADEsq171dcQIUGItrZM4FlOWF3jcE3ZEVynEps2KR+VBUukMI6\nRX+azMHSNz6kmbYukGGOoz03YfSydBcKbrMTT7c1BwcvwBi3eGvEb94QTxNiJAp7\nXGeWzLNO8faEnCqWRZ4dvpTksfYgdyovJPEHni81aitXZ/6t5dz6/VMEGcm8cHVo\nqeFHzgEaVsEwnbyzaCVJ\n=Ldks\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T13:35:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/417879406f741de25fd15a6069627cacfff2087b","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDQxNzg3OTQwNmY3NDFkZTI1ZmQxNWE2MDY5NjI3Y2FjZmZmMjA4N2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/2b3f0d103d9a7f71af1820cb461106585289f5fd","sha":"2b3f0d103d9a7f71af1820cb461106585289f5fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/2b3f0d103d9a7f71af1820cb461106585289f5fd"}],"sha":"417879406f741de25fd15a6069627cacfff2087b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/417879406f741de25fd15a6069627cacfff2087b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/2b3f0d103d9a7f71af1820cb461106585289f5fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:35:11Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T13:35:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Core: Consolidate the client cache keys and request modules (#2149)\n\n* `Core`: Add a cache module for the client query keys\n\nWhich caches a write invalidates was knowledge held in 30 files and nowhere\nelse, as 102 bare key literals and 47 invalidation calls. A typo in one of them\nis a silent stale read rather than a build error.\n\n`keys.ts` owns every key as a factory, with the prefix hierarchy made explicit so\nthe relationship between an unscoped, a course-scoped and a phase-scoped key is\nvisible. `events.ts` names the twenty write events the hooks actually have and\nholds each fan-out once.\n\nThe tests pin what the rest of this change must not alter: every key literal, the\n`undefined` id slot that the current keys deliberately keep, and the prefix\nsemantics that make an unscoped invalidation reach its descendants.\n\nThree collisions the key module now states rather than hides. `course_phase` and\n`coursePhase` cache the same phase under two literals, so the archive dialog\nneither shares the shell entry nor is reached by its invalidation.\n`application_form` and `applicationForm` read different endpoints despite the\nnear-identical name. And the two-element `application` key holds a phase id on\nthe student page and a participation id in the staff dialog.\n\n`coursePhaseGraphSaved` keeps the configurator''s single composite key. Because\n`invalidateQueries` matches by prefix and nothing caches under that key, it\nreaches none of the four graphs it names; the test says so.\n\n* `Core`: Read the query caches through the key module\n\nEvery `useQuery`, `useQueries` and `fetchQuery` in core now names its cache\nthrough a factory instead of a literal.\n\nThree private key helpers disappear into the module that should have owned them:\n`courseStaffQueryKey` in `useCourseStaff`, and the `campaignsKey` /\n`campaignKey` / `recipientPreviewKey` trio in `useCourseMailingCampaigns`, whose\nrecipient preview query was the one call site that restated its literal rather\nthan calling the local helper.\n\nTwo keys keep a `?? ''''` at the call site rather than passing the id straight\nthrough: the staff and campaign hooks cache under an empty string while their\nid is still undefined, and the factories take `string | undefined`, so dropping\nthe fallback would silently move those entries.\n\n* `Core`: Invalidate the query caches through named events\n\nThe 47 invalidation calls across 30 files become 30 event calls, and the fan-out\neach one performs now lives in `events.ts`.\n\nThree writes carried a fan-out that was copy-pasted rather than shared. The two\nstaff hooks each invalidated the course staff and every cached user search; the\nimport and score upload dialogs each invalidated both application participation\ncaches; and five of the six mail campaign hooks each restated which of the three\ncampaign caches their write makes stale.\n\nThe events preserve today''s behaviour exactly, including the three\ninconsistencies worth naming. An application assessment invalidates the\nparticipations of every phase rather than the one it was written to, because the\nkey it uses is unscoped. The same is true of a student gaining university data,\nwhich is at least what that write means. And the configurator''s graph save sends\none composite key that matches nothing, so it invalidates none of the four\ngraphs it names.\n\n`courseCreated` keeps the invalidate-then-refetch pair the three course creation\npaths share: each navigates into the new course as soon as it resolves, so the\nlist has to be back rather than merely marked stale.\n\n* `Core`: Add a request module for the client endpoints\n\n`client.ts` owns what the 63 endpoint modules each restated: the `/api` prefix,\nwhich of the two shared axios instances a route belongs on, the content type on\nwrites, and one place that logs a failure once, sanitized, and rethrows the\noriginal error so the `onError` handlers keep reading `error.response.data.error`.\n\nIt wraps each call rather than installing an interceptor. `axiosInstance` is a\nModule Federation singleton shared with every remote, and core has no business\nlogging their requests.\n\n`api/` groups the endpoints by the domain noun their route already uses, so a\ncall reads `coreApi.applications.form(phaseId)` and the resource id comes first.\nThe two application namespaces are split the way the routes are: `applications`\nis the staff-facing `/api/applications`, `apply` is the student-facing\n`/api/apply`, whose three unauthenticated endpoints are the only reason the\nsecond axios instance exists.\n\nWrites now all announce `application/json`. The modules this replaces were split\nbetween `application/json-path+json`, `application/json` and nothing at all, and\nthree reads sent a content type on a request with no body. Every core handler\nbinds with `BindJSON`, which never reads the header, so the split was noise.\n\n`routes.test.ts` is the route manifest: for all 88 endpoints it asserts the\nmethod, the resolved URL, the body, the query parameters and the content type,\nplus the behaviour that is not a route. The 401 that means \"member of no course\"\nand answers with an empty list, the two 204s that map to a ready status, and the\ntwo endpoints where the server sends null instead of an empty list. Its table\ndiffs against the old modules per method and URL with only `GET /api/students/`\nmissing, the one endpoint nothing imports.\n\nInterfaces that lived inside the query modules move to `interfaces/`, so the api\nmodules hold routes and nothing else.\n\nThe vitest config gains core''s two tsconfig path aliases: rspack resolves them\nfor the build, and without them a test cannot load a module that imports one by\nvalue.\n\n* `Core`: Call the endpoints through the request module\n\nThe 63 one-endpoint modules are gone, along with the 57 copies of\n`try / console.error / throw`, the 63 restatements of the `/api` prefix, and the\nchoice each one made about which axios instance and which content type to use.\n\n`getStudents` is deleted rather than ported: nothing imported it, and the route\nmanifest diff shows `GET /api/students/` as the only method and URL pair that\ndisappears.\n\n`archiveCourses` is the one write that mirrors its result into the course store\nrather than invalidating a cache, so it moves to `shared/hooks/courseArchive`\nand the request module keeps only the endpoint it calls.\n\nTwo declared return types were wrong and are now what they always were.\n`deleteCoursePhase` said `Promise<string | undefined>` while returning the whole\naxios response, which `handleSave` awaited and discarded; the nine other writes\nthat did the same were already typed `Promise<void>`. And `getStudentsWithCourses`\nloses the `console.log` of every student it fetched.\n\nThe interfaces the privacy and student modules declared alongside their requests\nmove to `interfaces/`, and the audit log query builder keeps its test next to the\nnamespace that now owns it.\n\n* `Core`: Point the docs at the modules that replaced the endpoint files\n\nThe templating guide named three of the deleted one-endpoint modules, and the\ndata-fetching rule described the one-file-per-endpoint pattern as the only one.\nIt still is, for the seven workspaces with too few endpoints to earn a module.\n\n* `Core`: Name the application participation cache keys after what they hold\n\n`participations.inPhase` held the phase''s additional score names and `participations.students`\nheld the participation list. Rename them to `additionalScores` and `participations.inPhase`,\nkeeping both literals so the invalidation prefixes are unchanged.\n\n* `Core`: Keep the DELETE body off the request options that carry no body\n\n`WriteOptions.data` existed for `del`, but `post` and `put` accepted it too and spread it after\ntheir positional body, so passing it silently dropped the body. Only `del` takes it now.\n\nAlso record why the audit log builds its query string by hand rather than through `params`.","tree":{"sha":"a05386a19c54130d4ccce307a366a168da78f155","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/a05386a19c54130d4ccce307a366a168da78f155"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/2b3f0d103d9a7f71af1820cb461106585289f5fd","verification":{"payload":"tree a05386a19c54130d4ccce307a366a168da78f155\nparent b61e620d122c797568acaa12533698f084c586ae\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788356111 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788356111 +0200\n\nCore: Consolidate the client cache keys and request modules (#2149)\n\n* `Core`: Add a cache module for the client query keys\n\nWhich caches a write invalidates was knowledge held in 30 files and nowhere\nelse, as 102 bare key literals and 47 invalidation calls. A typo in one of them\nis a silent stale read rather than a build error.\n\n`keys.ts` owns every key as a factory, with the prefix hierarchy made explicit so\nthe relationship between an unscoped, a course-scoped and a phase-scoped key is\nvisible. `events.ts` names the twenty write events the hooks actually have and\nholds each fan-out once.\n\nThe tests pin what the rest of this change must not alter: every key literal, the\n`undefined` id slot that the current keys deliberately keep, and the prefix\nsemantics that make an unscoped invalidation reach its descendants.\n\nThree collisions the key module now states rather than hides. `course_phase` and\n`coursePhase` cache the same phase under two literals, so the archive dialog\nneither shares the shell entry nor is reached by its invalidation.\n`application_form` and `applicationForm` read different endpoints despite the\nnear-identical name. And the two-element `application` key holds a phase id on\nthe student page and a participation id in the staff dialog.\n\n`coursePhaseGraphSaved` keeps the configurator''s single composite key. Because\n`invalidateQueries` matches by prefix and nothing caches under that key, it\nreaches none of the four graphs it names; the test says so.\n\n* `Core`: Read the query caches through the key module\n\nEvery `useQuery`, `useQueries` and `fetchQuery` in core now names its cache\nthrough a factory instead of a literal.\n\nThree private key helpers disappear into the module that should have owned them:\n`courseStaffQueryKey` in `useCourseStaff`, and the `campaignsKey` /\n`campaignKey` / `recipientPreviewKey` trio in `useCourseMailingCampaigns`, whose\nrecipient preview query was the one call site that restated its literal rather\nthan calling the local helper.\n\nTwo keys keep a `?? ''''` at the call site rather than passing the id straight\nthrough: the staff and campaign hooks cache under an empty string while their\nid is still undefined, and the factories take `string | undefined`, so dropping\nthe fallback would silently move those entries.\n\n* `Core`: Invalidate the query caches through named events\n\nThe 47 invalidation calls across 30 files become 30 event calls, and the fan-out\neach one performs now lives in `events.ts`.\n\nThree writes carried a fan-out that was copy-pasted rather than shared. The two\nstaff hooks each invalidated the course staff and every cached user search; the\nimport and score upload dialogs each invalidated both application participation\ncaches; and five of the six mail campaign hooks each restated which of the three\ncampaign caches their write makes stale.\n\nThe events preserve today''s behaviour exactly, including the three\ninconsistencies worth naming. An application assessment invalidates the\nparticipations of every phase rather than the one it was written to, because the\nkey it uses is unscoped. The same is true of a student gaining university data,\nwhich is at least what that write means. And the configurator''s graph save sends\none composite key that matches nothing, so it invalidates none of the four\ngraphs it names.\n\n`courseCreated` keeps the invalidate-then-refetch pair the three course creation\npaths share: each navigates into the new course as soon as it resolves, so the\nlist has to be back rather than merely marked stale.\n\n* `Core`: Add a request module for the client endpoints\n\n`client.ts` owns what the 63 endpoint modules each restated: the `/api` prefix,\nwhich of the two shared axios instances a route belongs on, the content type on\nwrites, and one place that logs a failure once, sanitized, and rethrows the\noriginal error so the `onError` handlers keep reading `error.response.data.error`.\n\nIt wraps each call rather than installing an interceptor. `axiosInstance` is a\nModule Federation singleton shared with every remote, and core has no business\nlogging their requests.\n\n`api/` groups the endpoints by the domain noun their route already uses, so a\ncall reads `coreApi.applications.form(phaseId)` and the resource id comes first.\nThe two application namespaces are split the way the routes are: `applications`\nis the staff-facing `/api/applications`, `apply` is the student-facing\n`/api/apply`, whose three unauthenticated endpoints are the only reason the\nsecond axios instance exists.\n\nWrites now all announce `application/json`. The modules this replaces were split\nbetween `application/json-path+json`, `application/json` and nothing at all, and\nthree reads sent a content type on a request with no body. Every core handler\nbinds with `BindJSON`, which never reads the header, so the split was noise.\n\n`routes.test.ts` is the route manifest: for all 88 endpoints it asserts the\nmethod, the resolved URL, the body, the query parameters and the content type,\nplus the behaviour that is not a route. The 401 that means \"member of no course\"\nand answers with an empty list, the two 204s that map to a ready status, and the\ntwo endpoints where the server sends null instead of an empty list. Its table\ndiffs against the old modules per method and URL with only `GET /api/students/`\nmissing, the one endpoint nothing imports.\n\nInterfaces that lived inside the query modules move to `interfaces/`, so the api\nmodules hold routes and nothing else.\n\nThe vitest config gains core''s two tsconfig path aliases: rspack resolves them\nfor the build, and without them a test cannot load a module that imports one by\nvalue.\n\n* `Core`: Call the endpoints through the request module\n\nThe 63 one-endpoint modules are gone, along with the 57 copies of\n`try / console.error / throw`, the 63 restatements of the `/api` prefix, and the\nchoice each one made about which axios instance and which content type to use.\n\n`getStudents` is deleted rather than ported: nothing imported it, and the route\nmanifest diff shows `GET /api/students/` as the only method and URL pair that\ndisappears.\n\n`archiveCourses` is the one write that mirrors its result into the course store\nrather than invalidating a cache, so it moves to `shared/hooks/courseArchive`\nand the request module keeps only the endpoint it calls.\n\nTwo declared return types were wrong and are now what they always were.\n`deleteCoursePhase` said `Promise<string | undefined>` while returning the whole\naxios response, which `handleSave` awaited and discarded; the nine other writes\nthat did the same were already typed `Promise<void>`. And `getStudentsWithCourses`\nloses the `console.log` of every student it fetched.\n\nThe interfaces the privacy and student modules declared alongside their requests\nmove to `interfaces/`, and the audit log query builder keeps its test next to the\nnamespace that now owns it.\n\n* `Core`: Point the docs at the modules that replaced the endpoint files\n\nThe templating guide named three of the deleted one-endpoint modules, and the\ndata-fetching rule described the one-file-per-endpoint pattern as the only one.\nIt still is, for the seven workspaces with too few endpoints to earn a module.\n\n* `Core`: Name the application participation cache keys after what they hold\n\n`participations.inPhase` held the phase''s additional score names and `participations.students`\nheld the participation list. Rename them to `additionalScores` and `participations.inPhase`,\nkeeping both literals so the invalidation prefixes are unchanged.\n\n* `Core`: Keep the DELETE body off the request options that carry no body\n\n`WriteOptions.data` existed for `del`, but `post` and `put` accepted it too and spread it after\ntheir positional body, so passing it silently dropped the body. Only `del` takes it now.\n\nAlso record why the audit log builds its query string by hand rather than through `params`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmCYQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGzcQAD6jilISFsMRzdw4tMuE4Djw\nUD74YSka76AFNpafZuivxTJDRrRTw6sdTF3puYdPc7oAZBQoz/Mvg4sh5D5OadId\nFW/mKyjKVVibaYm9ojLXkmOfcuCmiJAyjfamtiA0wstJfPF6g7w6M7ae0PZJiejk\n7HInIu2aDb8/txosTBGxhnJVdz952Z7YgNApq+y4AexbWahz7uNG+gSBfwWMGW4X\n6OUqmCZmePOMAfJXNOTjjdoA7HHVH7DenyQ8ilq/4/6FIMzYpED/vgdSBjLw11lU\nTCysLMXawexOD7FR6EEgIRdRiAazJNG6GqaExq0ZLBJ+6kVQQVt5v0WE2e38FSKg\nRrkkb+CdZmI3jHuAzsDKwSlqxs6Sy9Bpdjv8t0uR7dYD8ZJkTkPnYC3olpKJMglO\nfprL+2dCQlp8IljZ2X0vn06aeTiRp37seCZQpKzERpZKCxdhk8ydC2c1ldzMw0ZD\nwmXrrkfWtmVf2ReT98LCv6Dga3MHm+9ditLIlovMKnkMyUr4eoX4lIVy1rdyfATr\n5j7i7byxmxhStBmES034PM6MtuYYhEvprbqzAuVlopTE3Sqkyqtagii3cvGwY6Qa\nu+gRTQnXkMhZIlD1r5qDAdXMExU3tMkp7Sd/Ks0sZlbMR12SYFHHrMg2UEmfMRL1\ndfVSJwFvEXJmHw5i1/7G\n=9Qej\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T13:35:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/2b3f0d103d9a7f71af1820cb