us nothing for @tumaet/prompt-shared-state, @tumaet/prompt-ui-components and github.com/prompt-edu/prompt-sdk, which we publish and review ourselves, and it delays our own fixes by a week. Every other dependency keeps the 7-day cooldown.","tree":{"sha":"247a2c45af0ad231941f0f67ee2525f916cbec01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/247a2c45af0ad231941f0f67ee2525f916cbec01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/b61e620d122c797568acaa12533698f084c586ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 247a2c45af0ad231941f0f67ee2525f916cbec01\nparent d77234b5e3b2ea496c5629a9c6fbc8494cb68ec5\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788352718 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788352718 +0200\n\nInfrastructure: Exempt the packages we maintain from the Renovate minimum release age (#2153)\n\nThe blanket minimumReleaseAge of 7 days guards us against compromised or broken third-party releases. It buys us nothing for @tumaet/prompt-shared-state, @tumaet/prompt-ui-components and github.com/prompt-edu/prompt-sdk, which we publish and review ourselves, and it delays our own fixes by a week. Every other dependency keeps the 7-day cooldown.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmBjOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa2YQAEoheTYGlui4wxlusndWLC30\n6XljGxv7646aG17bpDnjdtBcSVkd1s60RhdT+9xL+QhVUirfY/40Yfy8UDSuVeRX\ntTJjDSSDZ90cL8x0mMshODHCgWdCoZn0c5gK+vOPwzFtyu2IM97otB1NsGLjokSD\nAh8/W/dVORbDprMEHVdbewDnLbKb4hUsmcPj50zOWy6hPh7jfYsT0eN9oBy4AYgd\nB6mjOpfTuilGkSwhczJy5lanak1aCSTy2DQKwK3awe4VsuHhgkcf7Ie6LE0Mtnuv\nhazg/+0+FnjpEOvcVGPc66txDOikT1aRm3siT/KBvK4rxZyo29Tf3hoovLPkUUSE\nmrT6jEOXiWQI14g9s545T1EBLCIflU8z4uo/Ca/BqBM2qJDTnfBqJtI/84d/8dXd\nGYRwQv/oZeTOu1lkIFfUDeAdn2M3RRb096cIfv8ip28R0so2gN/841Ddu7eKDlPh\nTVrXowLu4KstWEQWl3JWEG+PTuw2wHBt6/9WFI6LtLbusNYWDQzy/E0WDR/lCB5D\njrZLK3BGhcDqKvpxXzQICXMcwt5SeYuvhN362BlYtEE/CZ07f5atCd7SboGnGrvT\ndDoLAvYVzojI6aKgul3Il5hX6LRmQyRqYXftUFcE7bE/LTI2rCZ2+mwkqLYaq9U+\nrIYKaiALoYHxJlhNkrCB\n=qcfw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T12:38:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/b61e620d122c797568acaa12533698f084c586ae","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKGI2MWU2MjBkMTIyYzc5NzU2OGFjYWExMjUzMzY5OGYwODRjNTg2YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/d77234b5e3b2ea496c5629a9c6fbc8494cb68ec5","sha":"d77234b5e3b2ea496c5629a9c6fbc8494cb68ec5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/d77234b5e3b2ea496c5629a9c6fbc8494cb68ec5"}],"sha":"b61e620d122c797568acaa12533698f084c586ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/b61e620d122c797568acaa12533698f084c586ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/d77234b5e3b2ea496c5629a9c6fbc8494cb68ec5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:37:01Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T12:37:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Seeding: Add a full-course seed for every service database (#2108)\n\n* `Seeding`: Add the seed runner and cross-database check\n\nAdds scripts/seed.sh, which loads the SQL files under seed/ into every service\ndatabase, and scripts/seed-check.sh, which verifies statically that the UUIDs\nlinking those databases resolve.\n\nThe schemas belong to the servers (core shells out to migrate, the phase\nservices call sdkUtils.RunMigrations), so the runner is data-only and waits per\ndatabase until schema_migrations reaches the version its migration directory\ndeclares. Core additionally waits for the eight phase type names the seed\nresolves by name: those are created at startup with random UUIDs, Application\nseparately from the other seven, so seeding before both bootstrap modules have\nfinished would insert a null course_phase_type_id.\n\nThe script is POSIX sh rather than bash because it also runs inside a\npostgres:15.19-alpine container, where the only shell is busybox ash. `make\nseed` runs it there too, so no host psql is needed and local and CI take the\nsame code path.\n\n`make db` and `db-down` now cover all eight service databases: they previously\nhandled only the core one while `make servers` started eight services.\n\n* `Seeding`: Add the core database seed\n\nseed/core.sql carries two things.\n\nThe first is every fixture the Playwright suite asserts against, ported out of\ne2e/seed/e2e_seed.sql with its pinned UUIDs and its explanatory comments intact.\nThe port drops the schema (the server owns it), the schema_migrations pin, and\nthe course_phase_type and DTO rows: core creates those itself and skips the DTO\ndescriptors whenever the type row already exists, which is why the old dump had\nto hand-mirror initializeTypes.go and why Interview, Matching and Team\nAllocation ended up with no DTO metadata at all. Phases now resolve their type\nby name instead, so the descriptors are the server''s own and base_url is\ncorrect per environment rather than hardcoded to the Docker form.\n\nThe second is iPraktikumDemo, the full course example: nine phases covering\nevery phase type, eight applicants narrowing to six participants, a configured\napplication form with answers and scores, interview scores, a mail campaign,\nand the participation and phase data dependency edges that let a downstream\nphase resolve an upstream one''s data. It is a separate course rather than an\nextension of iPraktikumFull because the e2e journeys own that course''s phases.\n\nThe seed is authoritative for the rows it owns: it deletes them and reinserts\nthem, so re-running reconciles drift. Deleting a seeded student is the one\ndestructive step, since course_participation.student_id cascades and would take\nan unrelated enrollment with it, so a guard refuses to run when a seeded student\nis referenced outside the seeded courses.\n\n* `Seeding`: Add the phase module database seeds\n\nOne data-only file per phase service, all scoped to the iPraktikumDemo phases:\ninterview slots and assignments, team allocation skills/teams/survey\nresponses/published allocation, self team allocation teams and assignments, an\nassessment rubric with graded participants and a completed self evaluation\nround, a released certificate template, a team presentation schedule with\nfeedback categories, and the example phase row.\n\nNotes on the three that are not mechanical:\n\n- Assessment brings its own assessment_schema rows instead of reusing the four\n  the migrations create with gen_random_uuid(): those carry no categories and\n  are the fallback every other phase relies on. The peer and tutor schema\n  columns are left out of the config insert so their column DEFAULTs still\n  apply, and course_phase_config is deleted before the schemas it references\n  with ON DELETE RESTRICT.\n- Certificate leaves certificate_download.id to its SERIAL; inserting explicit\n  ids would desync the sequence.\n- Presentation deletes presentations before categories, because\n  feedback_answer.category_id is ON DELETE RESTRICT.\n\nThe links between these databases and core are bare UUID values with nothing\nenforcing them, hence scripts/seed-check.sh.\n\n* `Testing`: Point the e2e stack at the shared seed\n\nThe stack loaded its own `pg_dump` through `/docker-entrypoint-initdb.d`, which\nmeant the seed carried a frozen copy of the core schema pinned at\n`schema_migrations = 24` while core had moved to 28, and the seven phase\ndatabases were never seeded at all.\n\nIt now uses `seed/`, the same data-only files `make seed` applies. A one-shot\n`seed` service runs `scripts/seed.sh` after the servers start, and `e2e-runner`\nwaits for it with `service_completed_successfully`. Both `make test-e2e-shard`\nand the CI workflow go through `docker compose run --rm e2e-runner` without\n`--no-deps`, so both pick the dependency up.\n\nEvery fixture keeps its pinned UUID, so the specs are untouched apart from two\nconsequences of the seed no longer owning course phase types: the configurator\npage object resolves the palette''s test ids from `GET /api/course_phase_types`\ninstead of hardcoding them, and `SEEDED_COURSE_COUNT` accounts for the demo\ncourse the seed adds.\n\n* `Core`: Add the demo course roles to the Keycloak realm\n\nCreateCourseGroupsAndRoles only runs on the course-create API path, so a course\ninserted by the seed gets no Keycloak roles and only PromptAdmin can see it.\nStudents are unaffected: their course access is derived in the database from\nmatriculation_number and university_login.\n\nMirrors what the API path would have built for iPraktikumDemo: the\nios2526-iPraktikumDemo-Lecturer and -Editor client roles on prompt-server, the\n/Prompt/ios2526-iPraktikumDemo/{Lecturer,Editor} groups carrying them, and the\nseeded staff users placed in those groups.\n\nThe realm is imported only into an empty Keycloak, so an existing local install\nneeds its Keycloak volume dropped to pick this up - documented in the seeding\nguide.\n\ne2e/keycloak/realm.json deliberately stays as it is: no spec touches the demo\ncourse, and granting the e2e users a role on it would change what the\npermission matrix sees.\n\n* `Docs`: Document the seeding workflow\n\nAdds docs/contributor/guide/seeding.md (what `make seed` produces, which user\nsees what, why the seed is data only and runs after the servers, and how to\nextend it), links it from the contributor index, adds the optional seeding step\nto the quick start, and records the make targets and the phase type rule in\nAGENTS.md.\n\nseed/README.md carries the rules that are easy to get wrong while editing the\nSQL - never insert a course_phase_type row, scope every delete, the graph is a\nchain - plus the pinned id ranges the cross-database references use.\n\n* `Seeding`: Fix the self-evaluation author and the mail body newlines\n\nBoth seeded `feedback_items` rows carried `type = ''self''` with an author\ndifferent from the reviewed participant, the exact combination migration\n0016 classifies as `peer`, so the self-evaluation view attributed Selma''s\nfeedback to Stan.\n\n`standard_conforming_strings` is on, so the mail campaign body stored a\nliteral backslash-n instead of a newline.\n\n* `Seeding`: Require a seeded core before any phase database\n\n`scripts/seed.sh example_server` against an empty stack wrote a\ncore-owned `course_phase_id` that core had never created. Nothing across\nservice databases enforces that link, so the result was silently\nunreachable data rather than an error.\n\nThe script now applies `core` first whatever order the targets arrive in,\nand aborts with a pointer to `make seed` when a phase target runs without\ncore holding the demo course.\n\n* `Seeding`: Stop pinning the example_component phase type id\n\nNo service owns this type: core creates the other eight at startup and\nthe example server never registers itself, so the seed has to insert it\nfor the rest of `core.sql` to resolve it by name.\n\nNothing references the row''s id, so it is now generated the way core\ngenerates every other type''s, leaving `base_url` as the only seed-owned\npart. `seed/README.md` and the seeding guide now name that gap instead of\npresenting the insert as a pattern worth copying.\n\n* `Docs`: Seed the databases in the documented verify boot path\n\nThe boot command started `client-core` and `server-core`, neither of\nwhich depends on `seed`, and the driver command''s `--no-deps` skipped it\ntoo, so the documented workflow ran against empty databases. Name `seed`\nin the boot command and check it in the readiness block.\n\nAlso hyphenates `self-evaluation` in the seed prose.\n\n* `Seeding`: Follow the interview reviews into their own service\n\nThe interview phase stopped keeping its score, interviewer and answers on core''s\nparticipation restricted_data, so the demo course''s interview data no longer\nreached the phase or the Matching phase that resolves it over REST.\n\nMove the six reviews into the interview database''s interview_review table and\nconfigure the two questions their answers reference on the phase itself.\n\n* `Seeding`: Address the review on credentials, CI and the demo dates\n\nGive every database its own connection settings in scripts/seed.sh, falling\nback to the core values, and pass each service''s DB_<SERVICE>_* through both\ncompose files, so a changed password fails against that database instead of\nbeing silently replaced by core''s.\n\nRun scripts/seed-check.sh from quality-servers.yml, since a cross-database id\ntypo otherwise only shows up as an empty screen.\n\nRefresh the e2e phase database comments, which still claimed no seed is loaded,\nand document the demo timeline: the dates stay pinned to the ios2526 semester so\na reseed reproduces the same course, and seed/README.md now says so.\n\n* `Seeding`: Restore universityLoginAvailable on the fullCourse application phase\n\nThe port of the e2e dump into the shared seed flipped universityLoginAvailable\nto false on the open Application phase of fullCourse. Without it, a logged-in\nstudent stays on /apply/:phaseId instead of being redirected to the\n/authenticated form, which failed the auth session-persistence spec and the\ncore e2e shard with it.\n\n* Seeding: Pin the allocation timeframes to an explicit UTC offset\n\nThe team_allocation and self_team_allocation seeds were the only ones\nwriting bare timestamp literals. The columns are zone-less today, so the\nvalue lands as written, but once they become TIMESTAMPTZ PostgreSQL\nresolves a bare literal against the session zone, and the db containers\nrun TZ=Europe/Berlin. Spelling out +00 keeps the window at the same\ninstant under either schema.\n\n* `Seeding`: Fail the seed when a data dependency edge does not resolve\n\nThe dependency graph inserts resolve phase types and DTO descriptors by name\nthrough inner joins, so a renamed or missing descriptor dropped an edge instead\nof failing. The seed then completed and the downstream phase showed no resolved\ncolumns. Each insert now asserts its row count and aborts the transaction\notherwise.\n\n* `Seeding`: Correct the phase type and migration notes in the docs\n\nThe e2e README claimed core creates every phase type, but example_component is\nthe exception that core.sql inserts itself. The seeding guide implied psql always\nfails loudly on a schema change, which only holds for renamed or dropped columns.","tree":{"sha":"c901d793f17b37d531199baa375c1d3acbfe63ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/c901d793f17b37d531199baa375c1d3acbfe63ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/d77234b5e3b2ea496c5629a9c6fbc8494cb68ec5","verification":{"payload":"tree c901d793f17b37d531199baa375c1d3acbfe63ec\nparent 370331078d67b3cea667609a3d2eb5cc704e497c\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788352621 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788352621 +0200\n\nSeeding: Add a full-course seed for every service database (#2108)\n\n* `Seeding`: Add the seed runner and cross-database check\n\nAdds scripts/seed.sh, which loads the SQL files under seed/ into every service\ndatabase, and scripts/seed-check.sh, which verifies statically that the UUIDs\nlinking those databases resolve.\n\nThe schemas belong to the servers (core shells out to migrate, the phase\nservices call sdkUtils.RunMigrations), so the runner is data-only and waits per\ndatabase until schema_migrations reaches the version its migration directory\ndeclares. Core additionally waits for the eight phase type names the seed\nresolves by name: those are created at startup with random UUIDs, Application\nseparately from the other seven, so seeding before both bootstrap modules have\nfinished would insert a null course_phase_type_id.\n\nThe script is POSIX sh rather than bash because it also runs inside a\npostgres:15.19-alpine container, where the only shell is busybox ash. `make\nseed` runs it there too, so no host psql is needed and local and CI take the\nsame code path.\n\n`make db` and `db-down` now cover all eight service databases: they previously\nhandled only the core one while `make servers` started eight services.\n\n* `Seeding`: Add the core database seed\n\nseed/core.sql carries two things.\n\nThe first is every fixture the Playwright suite asserts against, ported out of\ne2e/seed/e2e_seed.sql with its pinned UUIDs and its explanatory comments intact.\nThe port drops the schema (the server owns it), the schema_migrations pin, and\nthe course_phase_type and DTO rows: core creates those itself and skips the DTO\ndescriptors whenever the type row already exists, which is why the old dump had\nto hand-mirror initializeTypes.go and why Interview, Matching and Team\nAllocation ended up with no DTO metadata at all. Phases now resolve their type\nby name instead, so the descriptors are the server''s own and base_url is\ncorrect per environment rather than hardcoded to the Docker form.\n\nThe second is iPraktikumDemo, the full course example: nine phases covering\nevery phase type, eight applicants narrowing to six participants, a configured\napplication form with answers and scores, interview scores, a mail campaign,\nand the participation and phase data dependency edges that let a downstream\nphase resolve an upstream one''s data. It is a separate course rather than an\nextension of iPraktikumFull because the e2e journeys own that course''s phases.\n\nThe seed is authoritative for the rows it owns: it deletes them and reinserts\nthem, so re-running reconciles drift. Deleting a seeded student is the one\ndestructive step, since course_participation.student_id cascades and would take\nan unrelated enrollment with it, so a guard refuses to run when a seeded student\nis referenced outside the seeded courses.\n\n* `Seeding`: Add the phase module database seeds\n\nOne data-only file per phase service, all scoped to the iPraktikumDemo phases:\ninterview slots and assignments, team allocation skills/teams/survey\nresponses/published allocation, self team allocation teams and assignments, an\nassessment rubric with graded participants and a completed self evaluation\nround, a released certificate template, a team presentation schedule with\nfeedback categories, and the example phase row.\n\nNotes on the three that are not mechanical:\n\n- Assessment brings its own assessment_schema rows instead of reusing the four\n  the migrations create with gen_random_uuid(): those carry no categories and\n  are the fallback every other phase relies on. The peer and tutor schema\n  columns are left out of the config insert so their column DEFAULTs still\n  apply, and course_phase_config is deleted before the schemas it references\n  with ON DELETE RESTRICT.\n- Certificate leaves certificate_download.id to its SERIAL; inserting explicit\n  ids would desync the sequence.\n- Presentation deletes presentations before categories, because\n  feedback_answer.category_id is ON DELETE RESTRICT.\n\nThe links between these databases and core are bare UUID values with nothing\nenforcing them, hence scripts/seed-check.sh.\n\n* `Testing`: Point the e2e stack at the shared seed\n\nThe stack loaded its own `pg_dump` through `/docker-entrypoint-initdb.d`, which\nmeant the seed carried a frozen copy of the core schema pinned at\n`schema_migrations = 24` while core had moved to 28, and the seven phase\ndatabases were never seeded at all.\n\nIt now uses `seed/`, the same data-only files `make seed` applies. A one-shot\n`seed` service runs `scripts/seed.sh` after the servers start, and `e2e-runner`\nwaits for it with `service_completed_successfully`. Both `make test-e2e-shard`\nand the CI workflow go through `docker compose run --rm e2e-runner` without\n`--no-deps`, so both pick the dependency up.\n\nEvery fixture keeps its pinned UUID, so the specs are untouched apart from two\nconsequences of the seed no longer owning course phase types: the configurator\npage object resolves the palette''s test ids from `GET /api/course_phase_types`\ninstead of hardcoding them, and `SEEDED_COURSE_COUNT` accounts for the demo\ncourse the seed adds.\n\n* `Core`: Add the demo course roles to the Keycloak realm\n\nCreateCourseGroupsAndRoles only runs on the course-create API path, so a course\ninserted by the seed gets no Keycloak roles and only PromptAdmin can see it.\nStudents are unaffected: their course access is derived in the database from\nmatriculation_number and university_login.\n\nMirrors what the API path would have built for iPraktikumDemo: the\nios2526-iPraktikumDemo-Lecturer and -Editor client roles on prompt-server, the\n/Prompt/ios2526-iPraktikumDemo/{Lecturer,Editor} groups carrying them, and the\nseeded staff users placed in those groups.\n\nThe realm is imported only into an empty Keycloak, so an existing local install\nneeds its Keycloak volume dropped to pick this up - documented in the seeding\nguide.\n\ne2e/keycloak/realm.json deliberately stays as it is: no spec touches the demo\ncourse, and granting the e2e users a role on it would change what the\npermission matrix sees.\n\n* `Docs`: Document the seeding workflow\n\nAdds docs/contributor/guide/seeding.md (what `make seed` produces, which user\nsees what, why the seed is data only and runs after the servers, and how to\nextend it), links it from the contributor index, adds the optional seeding step\nto the quick start, and records the make targets and the phase type rule in\nAGENTS.md.\n\nseed/README.md carries the rules that are easy to get wrong while editing the\nSQL - never insert a course_phase_type row, scope every delete, the graph is a\nchain - plus the pinned id ranges the cross-database references use.\n\n* `Seeding`: Fix the self-evaluation author and the mail body newlines\n\nBoth seeded `feedback_items` rows carried `type = ''self''` with an author\ndifferent from the reviewed participant, the exact combination migration\n0016 classifies as `peer`, so the self-evaluation view attributed Selma''s\nfeedback to Stan.\n\n`standard_conforming_strings` is on, so the mail campaign body stored a\nliteral backslash-n instead of a newline.\n\n* `Seeding`: Require a seeded core before any phase database\n\n`scripts/seed.sh example_server` against an empty stack wrote a\ncore-owned `course_phase_id` that core had never created. Nothing across\nservice databases enforces that link, so the result was silently\nunreachable data rather than an error.\n\nThe script now applies `core` first whatever order the targets arrive in,\nand aborts with a pointer to `make seed` when a phase target runs without\ncore holding the demo course.\n\n* `Seeding`: Stop pinning the example_component phase type id\n\nNo service owns this type: core creates the other eight at startup and\nthe example server never registers itself, so the seed has to insert it\nfor the rest of `core.sql` to resolve it by name.\n\nNothing references the row''s id, so it is now generated the way core\ngenerates every other type''s, leaving `base_url` as the only seed-owned\npart. `seed/README.md` and the seeding guide now name that gap instead of\npresenting the insert as a pattern worth copying.\n\n* `Docs`: Seed the databases in the documented verify boot path\n\nThe boot command started `client-core` and `server-core`, neither of\nwhich depends on `seed`, and the driver command''s `--no-deps` skipped it\ntoo, so the documented workflow ran against empty databases. Name `seed`\nin the boot command and check it in the readiness block.\n\nAlso hyphenates `self-evaluation` in the seed prose.\n\n* `Seeding`: Follow the interview reviews into their own service\n\nThe interview phase stopped keeping its score, interviewer and answers on core''s\nparticipation restricted_data, so the demo course''s interview data no longer\nreached the phase or the Matching phase that resolves it over REST.\n\nMove the six reviews into the interview database''s interview_review table and\nconfigure the two questions their answers reference on the phase itself.\n\n* `Seeding`: Address the review on credentials, CI and the demo dates\n\nGive every database its own connection settings in scripts/seed.sh, falling\nback to the core values, and pass each service''s DB_<SERVICE>_* through both\ncompose files, so a changed password fails against that database instead of\nbeing silently replaced by core''s.\n\nRun scripts/seed-check.sh from quality-servers.yml, since a cross-database id\ntypo otherwise only shows up as an empty screen.\n\nRefresh the e2e phase database comments, which still claimed no seed is loaded,\nand document the demo timeline: the dates stay pinned to the ios2526 semester so\na reseed reproduces the same course, and seed/README.md now says so.\n\n* `Seeding`: Restore universityLoginAvailable on the fullCourse application phase\n\nThe port of the e2e dump into the shared seed flipped universityLoginAvailable\nto false on the open Application phase of fullCourse. Without it, a logged-in\nstudent stays on /apply/:phaseId instead of being redirected to the\n/authenticated form, which failed the auth session-persistence spec and the\ncore e2e shard with it.\n\n* Seeding: Pin the allocation timeframes to an explicit UTC offset\n\nThe team_allocation and self_team_allocation seeds were the only ones\nwriting bare timestamp literals. The columns are zone-less today, so the\nvalue lands as written, but once they become TIMESTAMPTZ PostgreSQL\nresolves a bare literal against the session zone, and the db containers\nrun TZ=Europe/Berlin. Spelling out +00 keeps the window at the same\ninstant under either schema.\n\n* `Seeding`: Fail the seed when a data dependency edge does not resolve\n\nThe dependency graph inserts resolve phase types and DTO descriptors by name\nthrough inner joins, so a renamed or missing descriptor dropped an edge instead\nof failing. The seed then completed and the downstream phase showed no resolved\ncolumns. Each insert now asserts its row count and aborts the transaction\notherwise.\n\n* `Seeding`: Correct the phase type and migration notes in the docs\n\nThe e2e README claimed core creates every phase type, but example_component is\nthe exception that core.sql inserts itself. The seeding guide implied psql always\nfails loudly on a schema change, which only holds for renamed or dropped columns.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmBhtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0SAQAK8Hst2NEkXhz4+WnePPUOpc\n1CQ/DmImhQkzKdf5tz9N5RJUTIYfRWkzONzdUyXAK5rA68tCEhW5TRsZF5SyKDHo\nppZeDvO5kwdGdxTGQNgu0leni6sd9w68JaDaSvMwJHY6q8auEcwJdjFkGRnkhGQp\ns0qHTC75Uu1lO7A/x4C6wqjRU/JwYRpa3K3zjQJo6KN8Z0VeC1ARFryxLt3r08LQ\nJMOv/HCiQ/kV8c0fzMJXOba+IjsZRLW1oM7fFKtd6JE/dvLf59/AuFkASbbi6aHS\nh/DBsXeWYOMr5lQR4bRZFzN5IiLEUBIYvdA1i80AKMnutBZX/EyuCx5m0URA2DZW\nX10PwXy/U7P3FlA8VeEMuRQ2MKRv3jMus0B0eltlBr+D6gUqXVeK4QbAjWAVJL4j\nVN7bCKyH16pL4RQmGOnFkZVu4QZJwh20vMC3PhLpUfOLh5hs5dtN1VNAbLmngOFV\n86v3Cwj1eCIxxV66n8HR6LWtTNVO67vdDm7XXtPzIJkLUmW+Fj1ejbsYUzG9tRbS\nf4PVfBcaixrwYOkbciCRlaroElWUh4Df3SCO60D2ZjmZ0ZGpzN5pHqSO+pA0om84\nvRJTs51bfUqYYFxjNOnNe1RGD9o6SQ/99uArP47MUeuKdbPwHuu+MFMKp8l4JM2A\n1YQssC77wgmP60AUCZ7j\n=Rk2c\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T12:37:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.gith