/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/61f08660d9bb35d07d560a790d3480e63ea08843","sha":"61f08660d9bb35d07d560a790d3480e63ea08843","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/61f08660d9bb35d07d560a790d3480e63ea08843"}],"sha":"18e41f971e13bcd6c917e2470ae9c4b8d277ae59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/18e41f971e13bcd6c917e2470ae9c4b8d277ae59"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/61f08660d9bb35d07d560a790d3480e63ea08843/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:24:49Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:24:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Team Allocation: Delete course phase data when a phase is removed (#2141)\n\n* Bump prompt-sdk to v1.3.1 in team allocation\n\nv1.3.1 adds CoursePhaseDeletionHandler, RegisterPhaseDeletionModule and the\nphase.deletion capability constant.\n\n* Add queries deleting the team allocation data of a course phase\n\nOnly the four phase-scoped root tables are deleted. The ON DELETE CASCADE\nconstraints on team and skill remove the student responses, allocations and\ntutors, which the queries document.\n\n* Handle course phase deletion in team allocation\n\nImplements the SDK''s CoursePhaseDeletionHandler so the service drops\neverything it stores for a phase once the phase is permanently deleted. The\ndeletes run in one transaction and the handler is idempotent, as the SDK\nrequires.\n\nThe endpoint stays inert until the core server dispatches to phase modules on\ndeletion (prompt-edu/prompt#984).\n\n* Harden the course phase deletion tests and bound the transaction\n\nThe generated child-table queries join their parent, so asserting on them\ncould not tell a cascaded delete apart from an orphaned row. Count the raw\ntables instead, which fails if a migration ever weakens a cascade.\n\nBound the transaction with the service''s timeout context: the deletes take row\nlocks and would otherwise hold a pool connection for as long as a concurrent\ntransaction runs.","tree":{"sha":"5a4f53fd33b8c5c722f86a16d247e118d0e747a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/5a4f53fd33b8c5c722f86a16d247e118d0e747a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/61f08660d9bb35d07d560a790d3480e63ea08843","verification":{"payload":"tree 5a4f53fd33b8c5c722f86a16d247e118d0e747a1\nparent 85b76262b032c37110faa840bd8cdaba36de2a0e\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788251089 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788251089 +0200\n\nTeam Allocation: Delete course phase data when a phase is removed (#2141)\n\n* Bump prompt-sdk to v1.3.1 in team allocation\n\nv1.3.1 adds CoursePhaseDeletionHandler, RegisterPhaseDeletionModule and the\nphase.deletion capability constant.\n\n* Add queries deleting the team allocation data of a course phase\n\nOnly the four phase-scoped root tables are deleted. The ON DELETE CASCADE\nconstraints on team and skill remove the student responses, allocations and\ntutors, which the queries document.\n\n* Handle course phase deletion in team allocation\n\nImplements the SDK''s CoursePhaseDeletionHandler so the service drops\neverything it stores for a phase once the phase is permanently deleted. The\ndeletes run in one transaction and the handler is idempotent, as the SDK\nrequires.\n\nThe endpoint stays inert until the core server dispatches to phase modules on\ndeletion (prompt-edu/prompt#984).\n\n* Harden the course phase deletion tests and bound the transaction\n\nThe generated child-table queries join their parent, so asserting on them\ncould not tell a cascaded delete apart from an orphaned row. Count the raw\ntables instead, which fails if a migration ever weakens a cascade.\n\nBound the transaction with the service''s timeout context: the deletes take row\nlocks and would otherwise hold a pool connection for as long as a concurrent\ntransaction runs.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlovRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiacQAJ3CxUmXBdpDvojCIigndpVP\nhUibeqpn9ufvm+THzc+qzD8O1wgmLqSCnkcEy5N0cOVi4TUF4mBhcTjF5JsknNZR\nxlxHULuESmE8tTY3wEUKQv9lJVvdaijaofUezp8xFJAF1FW1ZGAXHqNO/YYNAr5O\nH+sYbsLJPYSyMCbq2La+KK/VMujwJfP8kNfayIVGJHsnJ/iqk28b/Cahc13cX65m\nei/E0GiD5Kw5tyGKMfF9bviiYla8searkoGJjB2dC8s9W/IumDiwZwZQtC7J1b8+\nqEgDJ+ZEatTn1kUNGorKmOWJuQGQYdydh5CiEFQZduZoqWgFUWKVtQu90Hg3xMJm\na63XAOFzIqqnsvoR8cqc3zq9TCilmcmgouZ59kid9n1hHcXRZp8adrNjzXEnH1HL\nJ7WkDZyfnSE3EALnlUcFbvKPWM31Co55/kpBhUxf7aKYa3qvd5sne+p/zRlLmaJr\n3Zrcb1BC8K6tcl3E2nJD3mtIAI18yyhlfe4ZnrP8iyr9kLQiw6Rm/pVuCoBDjGtl\njKGYJcBYknnZ69iXwNXt4ip42m/l1fsJUKmkYn3h2WEPaGsz/UhnCh2WQHq8lMDq\n1g2vkqvqDan7MOrkDFoju/sBvMcJrCpTK+M7c8r+r4PklC2ftaxohON/WC8uHZy/\nkm04ZDZ/Z89P2IZpGL8E\n=aGZH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T08:24:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/61f08660d9bb35d07d560a790d3480e63ea08843","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDYxZjA4NjYwZDliYjM1ZDA3ZDU2MGE3OTBkMzQ4MGU2M2VhMDg4NDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/85b76262b032c37110faa840bd8cdaba36de2a0e","sha":"85b76262b032c37110faa840bd8cdaba36de2a0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/85b76262b032c37110faa840bd8cdaba36de2a0e"}],"sha":"61f08660d9bb35d07d560a790d3480e63ea08843","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/61f08660d9bb35d07d560a790d3480e63ea08843"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/85b76262b032c37110faa840bd8cdaba36de2a0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:23:12Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:23:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Core: Tighten the sidebar navigation spacing (#2143)\n\n* Tighten the sidebar spacing\n\nAdjacent SidebarGroups each contribute the primitive''s p-2, so the gap above\nthe Course Phases label stacked to 28px against 8px below it. Collapsing the\nfacing paddings evens the rhythm out to 12px above and 8px below.\n\nIn the general sidebar the group headings offset their text with\ntranslate-y-1 while keeping symmetric margins, which pushed the label away\nfrom the group above and against the items below. Dropping the transform and\ntightening the group gap reclaims the vertical space a single item group was\nspending.\n\n* Keep the Course Phases label closer to the list it heads\n\nZeroing both facing paddings left the label 12px below the previous group and\n8px above its own items, which reads as equidistant. A 4px top padding\nrestores the 16px/8px grouping while still cutting the original 28px gap.","tree":{"sha":"e36a576cc4e0a7952fda1d8a3b2a0aba98fc42e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/e36a576cc4e0a7952fda1d8a3b2a0aba98fc42e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/85b76262b032c37110faa840bd8cdaba36de2a0e","verification":{"payload":"tree e36a576cc4e0a7952fda1d8a3b2a0aba98fc42e4\nparent ffbaa101d36c1c083c46e76c32f50494bcaf9675\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788250992 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788250992 +0200\n\nCore: Tighten the sidebar navigation spacing (#2143)\n\n* Tighten the sidebar spacing\n\nAdjacent SidebarGroups each contribute the primitive''s p-2, so the gap above\nthe Course Phases label stacked to 28px against 8px below it. Collapsing the\nfacing paddings evens the rhythm out to 12px above and 8px below.\n\nIn the general sidebar the group headings offset their text with\ntranslate-y-1 while keeping symmetric margins, which pushed the label away\nfrom the group above and against the items below. Dropping the transform and\ntightening the group gap reclaims the vertical space a single item group was\nspending.\n\n* Keep the Course Phases label closer to the list it heads\n\nZeroing both facing paddings left the label 12px below the previous group and\n8px above its own items, which reads as equidistant. A 4px top padding\nrestores the 16px/8px grouping while still cutting the original 28px gap.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlotwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj6QQAJXsguov5Lxp/6rJDPdwZGFd\nBxIe4bPFuocgYqy57FeDiprIBmcPwuJUW9X/95aZksPkmQFDpnN33PcOdOfR4RK3\noflOkJAe2dfx1oWtcyaH7ABGUsiH15yRQA33LL9XDZNrfMaiZhTjbmu9rW8VLaZK\n1hvicUz3tDEHKgzcJnVyOOD3CJ1uAvUQFFdmxCbDThNY4Wephz+5AuukRxA/S0ip\ns1+fjPv5NWL55f1eKE0vEab0CiVwHu+SWSiAro7yhYT1gcVK0Cib7Yqv81aZoMhS\nawN0YRdFdui8aOcRFWm0dAD4PnULXnIqw/v3QSkhtJpjJTMDUetzdgnRO1RSbv4g\njV3eYVZLlKBpm7mvlKNifPweWvzKUeoV1zuD/n9UMosR4K/7SFAaGezN2Oy7w6uL\nclfZSnzuw6ZT1zGHK10WsvmK40zhkhuOUvvY8n6nwH8GFVm9KNoWcynZYg4JQWMP\nZ3kLyCBjeCebN9vqN3v1sK/L5rmHQMOaG4JyK4IXpEVh4LdSpjM2xf/BH4BlZbgl\nOc49x6Kh8YkWAponzOHmgwpnlWeKhrE4J/O2yQuUSnKumjmVjGZhdui2ZT7Qpp6Y\nVaRY+Ia+8FNwH+P3/4hgE0+JCS4xQk5S275SMjisEXdVkx/F/n6IvM2M7gwUcj/H\ntm0FngEKBhb4GH9oN1Ag\n=6Dxc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T08:23:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198