rgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/ffbaa101d36c1c083c46e76c32f50494bcaf9675/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:20:39Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:20:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Self Team Allocation: Fix the oversized create team button and the empty state padding (#2142)\n\nThe create button carried w-full max-w-lg mx-auto, stretching it to 512px\nnext to the auto-width Refresh Teams button. Dropping those classes sizes it\nto its content like its siblings.\n\nThe empty state combined p-12 with mt-4 on the icon, so the top inset was 16px\nlarger than the bottom one.\n\nThe icons also carried mr-2 on top of the button''s own gap-2, doubling the gap\nbetween icon and label.","tree":{"sha":"65c846b7bb736ce398007a45ed44ec831506ab6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/65c846b7bb736ce398007a45ed44ec831506ab6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/ffbaa101d36c1c083c46e76c32f50494bcaf9675","verification":{"payload":"tree 65c846b7bb736ce398007a45ed44ec831506ab6d\nparent 1bbc76df3509b331dcdd4b67db4f52115487a567\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788250839 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788250839 +0200\n\nSelf Team Allocation: Fix the oversized create team button and the empty state padding (#2142)\n\nThe create button carried w-full max-w-lg mx-auto, stretching it to 512px\nnext to the auto-width Refresh Teams button. Dropping those classes sizes it\nto its content like its siblings.\n\nThe empty state combined p-12 with mt-4 on the icon, so the top inset was 16px\nlarger than the bottom one.\n\nThe icons also carried mr-2 on top of the button''s own gap-2, doubling the gap\nbetween icon and label.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlorXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp0UQAG3GcFliiLbFCykXkBRLntgU\nSglaQfgcTfbOZuDCz4UnE+YVIHLpnZZ2IE/sTYDmItVCT0kic4Lpp8PATSzpaQ9l\nfJqojLtv8Hp8XPg4LPyPy5f4uj8zr6NXmCRJX3Qv27FLM4NQLkE/Dd7m5pk2x9Xb\nznrrw+4HL6O1X5wngq6PdlyZa/SopPJfClUzbnp5aG0L+TZe1AMBypCuuBw6iP2w\nvr50MvqOrtvx3Y+073Nzwh4euG96czf7JWmuFJGEaNoN5FAmRgXFziYgyew6tDjp\n7B0Ho95fFlW3qEcPk4cM3tbYDeOtISDnDeDomWCdDf8oKNS2k0wftC/8xfqBfBEl\n3hx94y8YDaZNah+iD9bNDY1XRYJaFN/Pss1P0XIZ+INVjP0P/sc6EjPki0jOGMw/\nX9vxkDujP/UGMSihA9CmnZOsBG1rwbU8hysYFpjbN1eoxmj6N6+RKe/TxZRAql2y\nMWje9blQP0+zwo2MSdwCUs0Pwo9v2LJjkxfM7YFt9YO1k2hyUHIiCSOKJoSghwn5\nCpieB8vXYhKrfMrXzPpHVrJVjpBw8zEq1qxzYc4nHdxGzwSG6ifVpmJVeH+tERm1\nda5rVKpMKKrLxXXcNH2jmb3dX8OmhdZlxRACXtUTnz3fdZIVL8UNZSXzdGn3IND8\nxTmVJOFnVHpKVUk8bRI/\n=4lHc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T08:20:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/ffbaa101d36c1c083c46e76c32f50494bcaf9675","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKGZmYmFhMTAxZDM2YzFjMDgzYzQ2ZTc2YzMyZjUwNDk0YmNhZjk2NzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/1bbc76df3509b331dcdd4b67db4f52115487a567","sha":"1bbc76df3509b331dcdd4b67db4f52115487a567","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/1bbc76df3509b331dcdd4b67db4f52115487a567"}],"sha":"ffbaa101d36c1c083c46e76c32f50494bcaf9675","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/ffbaa101d36c1c083c46e76c32f50494bcaf9675"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/1bbc76df3509b331dcdd4b67db4f52115487a567/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:20:15Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:20:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"General: Use the SDK student-ownership helper instead of per-service copies (#2140)\n\n* Bump prompt-sdk to v1.3.1 in assessment and interview\n\nv1.3.1 adds the shared student-ownership helper in keycloakTokenVerifier.\nThe indirect upgrades (testcontainers-go v0.44.0 and the otel stack) come\nfrom the SDK''s own requirements via MVS.\n\n* Use the SDK student-ownership helper instead of local copies\n\nservers/assessment/utils/ownership.go and servers/interview/utils/ownership.go\nwere identical apart from one error string. Both are deleted in favour of\nkeycloakTokenVerifier, whose ValidateStudentOwnership takes the owned entity\nname so the forbidden message stays unchanged.\n\nThe interview copy''s ErrOwnershipValidation had no call sites, which empties\nservers/interview/utils entirely.\n\n* Name evaluations correctly in the evaluation ownership error\n\ncreateOrUpdateEvaluation acts on evaluations, not evaluation completions.\nThe shared sentinel could not tell the two apart; the SDK helper''s entity\nname parameter can.","tree":{"sha":"b6b0f576fd8200e59203401bad2212ac28ce4cb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/b6b0f576fd8200e59203401bad2212ac28ce4cb3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/1bbc76df3509b331dcdd4b67db4f52115487a567","verification":{"payload":"tree b6b0f576fd8200e59203401bad2212ac28ce4cb3\nparent c602cabe7a02f578331453a494898e17d6af6165\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788250815 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788250815 +0200\n\nGeneral: Use the SDK student-ownership helper instead of per-service copies (#2140)\n\n* Bump prompt-sdk to v1.3.1 in assessment and interview\n\nv1.3.1 adds the shared student-ownership helper in keycloakTokenVerifier.\nThe indirect upgrades (testcontainers-go v0.44.0 and the otel stack) come\nfrom the SDK''s own requirements via MVS.\n\n* Use the SDK student-ownership helper instead of local copies\n\nservers/assessment/utils/ownership.go and servers/interview/utils/ownership.go\nwere identical apart from one error string. Both are deleted in favour of\nkeycloakTokenVerifier, whose ValidateStudentOwnership takes the owned entity\nname so the forbidden message stays unchanged.\n\nThe interview copy''s ErrOwnershipValidation had no call sites, which empties\nservers/interview/utils entirely.\n\n* Name evaluations correctly in the evaluation ownership error\n\ncreateOrUpdateEvaluation acts on evaluations, not evaluation completions.\nThe shared sentinel could not tell the two apart; the SDK helper''s entity\nname parameter can.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqloq/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJoEQAAm/oynwhBKEjOEgCLNMtcpA\n/gCjwzQzc7KfgUasnYyE9EJtSqlrOKIcwH3vWRyq6ReF0M1f9+uy14H9XbmNdDZ/\n0+m4M+MlSOvySiizWasTiYgpM99VNOt3K3lMduo4qmmnbSbiBkbBSGylsbiEdg5N\nipRX7y0Y3xXw91Zk17C0GdFsHbb9Cc/cAD4hlrI5M4SQYR2fDxZCZLnI95iy+bsQ\nVPuhQ96ZAjmbUFGGN1g0Wz0bS5KU5QWme1D2F35YtshQBuI4OfDKmZxfH/R9geLG\nF2X3Uei4+9KG/eSIibH11aMwyy4jO8ezfj5rOzUy2YvklFpbdCL05vnaOeSqWFh3\nOU4A1OWgF8yrPiX9WY5Uli4ZhKA9gjmWlDsjAhzRMdkDEbaDuK0xNeGkTCU/0Y3p\nXHcADuZN9Vt9kMSXjJmLrDqJLFCn4ESZLw/rMKGsT3C+kLAmqFnAHcmw7W0KWl8b\n7BKf3IMvkWI3k7QGKHeQVG0bVHe04qD6jIcAiqnq4+l3HkdARRl7pVeEB3xI9XoS\nd7yfdZuUYQYihqHXoPxxSGTt+VdPwxcLCd8F/oMvUxBdoFm1klpZgNRbul4bP27N\nFFwriHyUjVjydHWmGJB6lEolMe5CAsJYOqKvlVcKKkBNd+Pos0qE30t2ekvSGdRF\neDPPnj4e6jD748RKYTjS\n=NO1u\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T08:20:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/1bbc76df3509b331dcdd4b67db4f52115487a567","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDFiYmM3NmRmMzUwOWIzMzFkY2RkNGI2N2RiNGY1MjExNTQ4N2E1Njc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/c602cabe7a02f578331453a494898e17d6af6165","sha":"c602cabe7a02f578331453a494898e17d6af6165","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/c602cabe7a02f578331453a494898e17d6af6165"}],"sha":"1bbc76df3509b331dcdd4b67db4f52115487a567","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/1bbc76df3509b331dcdd4b67db4f52115487a567"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/c602cabe7a02f578331453a494898e17d6af6165/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:19:55Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:19:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Core: Add an optional welcome text to the application form (#2133)\n\n* Core: Serve an optional application welcome text to applicants\n\nThe apply endpoint is unauthenticated and projects named restricted_data keys\nrather than the whole bucket, so welcomeText needs its own projection to reach an\napplicant. The projection is coalesced because a phase that never set the key\nwould otherwise fail the scan and take the whole endpoint down.\n\nThe value is capped and type-checked on write, since it is served publicly.\n\n* Core: Let instructors write a welcome text for the application form\n\nThe text is edited with the shared description editor in the application settings\nand rendered above the form on both apply pages through the existing sanitized\nHTML renderer, which gains an optional class so the welcome text is not smaller\nthan the course description beside it. Clearing the editor sends null, so the key\ndisappears rather than lingering as an empty string.\n\n* Testing: Cover the application welcome text end to end\n\nThe spec owns a dedicated course and Application phase, because it edits the\nphase''s welcomeText and only one initial phase is allowed per course. The seeded\nvalue carries a script tag and an inline event handler so the sanitizer is\nactually exercised: both must be stripped and neither may ever run.\n\n* Core: Show the stored welcome text when the settings editor loads\n\nThe phase metadata is parsed asynchronously, so the card can render before the\ntext is known, and the rich text editor reads its content only once when it is\ncreated. Re-seeding from the metadata and remounting the editor on the stored\nvalue makes the editor show what is actually saved.\n\n* Core: Address review findings on the application welcome text\n\nContent that renders without any text of its own (a horizontal rule, a pasted\nimage) no longer counts as an empty editor, which would have blocked saving it or\nsilently deleted it. The size cap now also guards phase creation, which the copy\nflow goes through. The e2e save helper waits for the write to land rather than\nfor a button that is disabled while it is still in flight, and the welcome-text\nAPI assertions moved into the spec that owns the phase, since they read a phase\nthat spec mutates and spec files run in parallel workers.\n\n* Core: Treat a lone line break as an empty welcome text\n\nAn editor holding only `<p><br></p>` looks empty but was persisted, so the apply\npage rendered an empty block.\n\n* Core: Decide the welcome text is empty by parsing, not by stripping tags\n\nA regex tag-strip reads like a sanitizer and is flagged as an incomplete one,\neven though this only decides whether the editor holds anything; the HTML is\nsanitized where it is rendered.","tree":{"sha":"4c229b83d6a1de9f5eb445aa3e0ec2dcb3aa4306","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/4c229b83d6a1de9f5eb445aa3e0ec2dcb3aa4306"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/c602cabe7a02f578331453a494898e17d6af6165","verification":{"payload":"tree 4c229b83d6a1de9f5eb445aa3e0ec2dcb3aa4306\nparent 1cf3aeadedd11317fa28bf832a38cb83fbaedbbf\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788250795 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788250795 +0200\n\nCore: Add an optional welcome text to the application form (#2133)\n\n* Core: Serve an optional application welcome text to applicants\n\nThe apply endpoint is unauthenticated and projects named restricted_data keys\nrather than the whole bucket, so welcomeText needs its own projection to reach an\napplicant. The projection is coalesced because a phase that never set the key\nwould otherwise fail the scan and take the whole endpoint down.\n\nThe value is capped and type-checked on write, since it is served publicly.\n\n* Core: Let instructors write a welcome text for the application form\n\nThe text is edited with the shared description editor in the application settings\nand rendered above the form on both apply pages through the existing sanitized\nHTML renderer, which gains an optional class so the welcome text is not smaller\nthan the course description beside it. Clearing the editor sends null, so the key\ndisappears rather than lingering as an empty string.\n\n* Testing: Cover the application welcome text end to end\n\nThe spec owns a dedicated course and Application phase, because it edits the\nphase''s welcomeText and only one initial phase is allowed per course. The seeded\nvalue carries a script tag and an inline event handler so the sanitizer is\nactually exercised: both must be stripped and neither may ever run.\n\n* Core: Show the stored welcome text when the settings editor loads\n\nThe phase metadata is parsed asynchronously, so the card can render before the\ntext is known, and the rich text editor reads its content only once when it is\ncreated. Re-seeding from the metadata and remounting the editor on the stored\nvalue makes the editor show what is actually saved.\n\n* Core: Address review findings on the application welcome text\n\nContent that renders without any text of its own (a horizontal rule, a pasted\nimage) no longer counts as an empty editor, which would have blocked saving it or\nsilently deleted it. The size cap now also guards phase creation, which the copy\nflow goes through. The e2e save helper waits for the write to land rather than\nfor a button that is disabled while it is still in flight, and the welcome-text\nAPI assertions moved into the spec that owns the phase, since they read a phase\nthat spec mutates and spec files run in parallel workers.\n\n* Core: Treat a lone line break as an empty welcome text\n\nAn editor holding only `<p><br></p>` looks empty but was persisted, so the apply\npage rendered an empty block.\n\n* Core: Decide the welcome text is empty by parsing, not by stripping tags\n\nA regex tag-strip reads like a sanitizer and is flagged as an incomplete one,\neven though this only decides whether the editor holds anything; the HTML is\nsanitized where it is rendered.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqloqrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARdsQAHuAu4pr/C75IkMIcNb2Hbwv\nnfo0xeiZq+ih4tO0eVFIXulPNvW0sBngQqdujUjXi3XDWH53y3OyEdJIoQ6gerBu\nmw6XhcA47V3ICI9SUWMF9RSgc40g3+Fjn+bImO1dKUFa+1HCZj5hf0GWs7P0jNn/\nubHiX4GIz7tfx6fw2Y69df6Ng6V/OJqGG+QE4tsSfCVO3S3pOFgBaNMOTWnfLnQk\nwr7CXvs0dp7sFuw6KNYDNI/zqF07Uomiqpm8zLf2Vr73Ri0Kf4uFdP5mlFcn575a\n/BTicw4Jm3cRncuiGMhoYO1sYvDCcnrrzr588SU+l+1mR4NEg/+2D58tsoeT3MGc\nGjD566+wvxEdujcBLgk7XUXXe7PLsqcRKfJnkv1rKCVBkIePPWHQUOjbjNjUUWew\nUpu2PEdjH+8pqwNzoUl85JiSMsR1LyAG4Gl78aGqqHSn2wK1XmB1J9Rrr0DjE+02\n/4GKaIX6vR+JzBI7apUp0mxchG9yK9Uqoxb4D9N1aa/CDDkYBTmGBKDRqZw8FrBB\nZWB29icTN76HBSkAC2CjhMn66yYdYhwKjE+L8DbpGwAL3AqYeQqPFA20Y6xVS2IY\nL2SzwIthdif4lHqdzfqwy/zNq9MjdHVbnO7QG2sKxUM0wluw1dLYO/Za85POAL4W\nj68OqT9olOI9E0wvAKvE\n=ellv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T08:20:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/c602cabe7a02f578331453a494898e17d6af6165","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKGM2MDJjYWJlN2EwMmY1NzgzMzE0NTNhNDk0ODk4ZTE3ZDZhZjYxNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/1cf3aeadedd11317fa28bf832a38cb83fbaedbbf","sha":"1cf3aeadedd11317fa28bf832a38cb83fbaedbbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/1cf3aeadedd11317fa28bf832a38cb83fbaedbbf"}],"sha":"c602cabe7a02f578331453a494898e17d6af6165","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/c602cabe7a02f578331453a494898e17d6af6165"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/1cf3aeadedd11317fa28bf832a38cb83fbaedbbf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:19:07Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T08:19:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Certificate: Add a customizable instructor text to the student download page (#2134)\n\n* Certificate: Store an instructor text for the student download page\n\nAdds a student_page_text column and a dedicated PUT endpoint rather than widening\nthe existing config PUT, whose templateContent is required and would let a\ntext-only write erase the template. The upsert also creates the config row, which\nthe release-date update does not.\n\nThe text reaches students through the certificate status endpoint they already\ncall, in every status including \"not configured\" and \"not yet released\", which is\nexactly where an instructor would explain the wait.\n\n* Certificate: Let instructors write the text on the student download page\n\nThe settings page gains a rich text card, and the student page renders the saved\ntext above the certificate status through a local sanitizing renderer. A Module\nFederation remote cannot import core''s FormDescriptionHTML, so this is a local\nequivalent; it registers its DOMPurify hook once instead of per render, scopes it\nto anchors and forces rel=noopener noreferrer. Its long-term home is\n@tumaet/prompt-ui-components.\n\n* Certificate: Cover the instructor download-page text end to end\n\nThe spec owns its own fixture phase, since it writes the text and spec files run\nin parallel workers. The seeded value carries a script tag, an inline event\nhandler and a javascript: URL, so the sanitizer is exercised with markup an\nattacker would use rather than only with a benign paragraph, and the lecturer\njourney checks the student''s real view from a second browser context.\n\nAlso asserts that a student can no longer read the config payload.\n\n* Certificate: Address review findings on the student download-page text\n\nThe settings card moves into its own component, mounted only once the config has\nloaded, so the editor starts from the stored text without an effect that could\noverwrite an unsaved draft when the config refetches. The editor re-serializes on\ncreate, so its first emission is taken as the comparison baseline rather than as\nan edit, and a lone line break no longer counts as content.\n\nThe text write no longer stamps updated_at/updated_by: the settings page presents\nthose as the template''s provenance, so editing the text claimed the template had\njust been reconfigured, and an unattributed write nulled the previous editor.\n\nThe sanitizer registers its DOMPurify hook lazily rather than at import, which\nwould throw where there is no DOM, and save failures now surface the server''s\nreason instead of a fixed message.\n\n* Certificate: Decide the editor is empty by parsing, not by stripping tags\n\nA regex tag-strip reads like a sanitizer and is flagged as an incomplete one,\neven though this only decides whether the editor holds anything; the HTML is\nsanitized where it is rendered.","tree":{"sha":"6bef4eba9c81fd428f578f376ceba8667703a1c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/6bef4eba9c81fd428f578f376ceba8667703a1c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/1cf3aeadedd11317fa28bf832a38cb83fbaedbbf","verification":{"payload":"tree 6bef4eba9c81fd428f578f376ceba8667703a1c5\nparent 60e66ec065d8006eb73db5a4128c296bd5d3e812\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788250747 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788250747 +0200\n\nCertificate: Add a customizable instructor text to the student download page (#2134)\n\n* Certificate: Store an instructor text for the student download page\n\nAdds a student_page_text column and a dedicated PUT endpoint rather than widening\nthe existing config PUT, whose templateContent is required and would let a\ntext-only write erase the template. The upsert also creates the config row, which\nthe release-date update does not.\n\nThe text reaches students through the certificate status endpoint they already\ncall, in every status including \"not configured\" and \"not yet released\", which is\nexactly where an instructor would explain the wait.\n\n* Certificate: Let instructors write the text on the student download page\n\nThe settings page gains a rich text card, and the student page renders the saved\ntext above the certificate status through a local sanitizing renderer. A Module\nFederation remote cannot import core''s FormDescriptionHTML, so this is a local\nequivalent; it registers its DOMPurify hook once instead of per render, scopes it\nto anchors and forces rel=noopener noreferrer. Its long-term home is\n@tumaet/prompt-ui-components.\n\n* Certificate: Cover the instructor download-page text end to end\n\nThe spec owns its own fixture phase, since it writes the text and spec files run\nin parallel workers. The seeded value carries a script tag, an inline event\nhandler and a javascript: URL, so the sanitizer is exercised with markup an\nattacker would use rather than only with a benign paragraph, and the lecturer\njourney checks the student''s real view from a second browser context.\n\nAlso asserts that a student can no longer read the config payload.\n\n* Certificate: Address review findings on the student download-page text\n\nThe settings card moves into its own component, mounted only once the config has\nloaded, so the editor starts from the stored text without an effect that could\noverwrite an unsaved draft when the config refetches. The editor re-serializes on\ncreate, so its first emission is taken as the comparison baseline rather than as\nan edit, and a lone line break no longer counts as content.\n\nThe text write no longer stamps updated_at/updated_by: the settings page presents\nthose as the template''s provenance, so editing the text claimed the template had\njust been reconfigured, and an unattributed write nulled the previous editor.\n\nThe sanitizer registers its DOMPurify hook lazily rather than at import, which\nwould throw where there is no DOM, and save failures now surface the server''s\nreason instead of a fixed message.\n\n* Certificate: Decide the editor is empty by parsing, not by stripping tags\n\nA regex tag-strip reads like a sanitizer and is flagged as an incomplete one,\neven though this only decides whether the editor holds anything; the HTML is\nsanitized where it is rendered.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlop7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeMUQABaOFkiRabkAmiHJo7OgN2pZ\nBpHC+R1BRAc8ImdkVtLJuqSn1Tvyqwy1LptDw/qOjy8ZaGeTqkANTNHcRd8EvHeh\nTb60lQJTcHceSPnC3bDsLgkpXRyqXk99lksuOIu57i0Kay36k3dQPf4Uti992JDF\n41EiDsND2Vzx6zOuOjPwivO5/sgNKPUqvptL3si2VFOBQceiJZ03i5fd1ZQ0nhOu\nSUclsGibvcAUgF2IkZ6C58bjPVCgTGD47wDrtRQqbtuefCjTb5cgHVx4F1yfvZ0v\nGfvguyE74kZzHPFSQ7hUqDwEplmDk93y2QJHJa8pClX0v/7ltGWuiBL5F3HKMXD1\naJMLV0HOcsXyeT2BwrMCSUFqDfzIfsOdqkA8A2GGUqW6cch01zoMcrqlvp36MNwr\nNODd33Z44mY9QreN4kz5ZrIPemfDQo3K5PSyfaNCVS/y62QiB5gZFpkITjS9Ime5\nHwmAannmcTqO/NjzAIYadpSDjwxeA/vphhScj80kC0TkDV+Wbz8Ih10m2F+yL92O\nNKCd/QSNhtRxVFEeFK48duVTyFMKmIneWegFmKKpLtkKLkwaBXZEWEuAqbDViyHA\n+d2TqdlJlqbzAdFAUoUHhME5cOMd++Z6QFZ+Jjg7oFb39dU9B6D1yNHRK0QCslMd\nEIcPjcHj624YeA9B0reF\n=nPu6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T08:19:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_