,"gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/renovate","id":29139614,"login":"renovate[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjkxMzk2MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/e6f5dbd981e97a9aaabe4c4822604d80695c01a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:55:14Z","email":"29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"renovate[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:55:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Dependencies: Update traefik Docker tag to v3 (#2118)\n\n* Dependencies: Update traefik Docker tag to v3\n\n* General: Remove the unused Traefik JWT plugin from the compose files\n\nNo middleware referenced the jwt plugin in either production compose\nfile, so it was dead configuration. Loading it made every reverse-proxy\nstart depend on egress to plugins.traefik.io, and pinned v0.7.1 predated\nTraefik v3.\n\nVerified that Traefik 3.6.25 starts on the remaining static\nconfiguration with the Let''s Encrypt resolver intact.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maximilian Rapp <maximilian.rapp@tum.de>\nCo-authored-by: Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d812fb9f93496854879899e77ddd1832d73b1d31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/d812fb9f93496854879899e77ddd1832d73b1d31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/e6f5dbd981e97a9aaabe4c4822604d80695c01a4","verification":{"payload":"tree d812fb9f93496854879899e77ddd1832d73b1d31\nparent 570d3c5f979bb1e156f54cf25f31d4c7afa60cab\nauthor renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1788180914 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788180914 +0200\n\nDependencies: Update traefik Docker tag to v3 (#2118)\n\n* Dependencies: Update traefik Docker tag to v3\n\n* General: Remove the unused Traefik JWT plugin from the compose files\n\nNo middleware referenced the jwt plugin in either production compose\nfile, so it was dead configuration. Loading it made every reverse-proxy\nstart depend on egress to plugins.traefik.io, and pinned v0.7.1 predated\nTraefik v3.\n\nVerified that Traefik 3.6.25 starts on the remaining static\nconfiguration with the Let''s Encrypt resolver intact.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maximilian Rapp <maximilian.rapp@tum.de>\nCo-authored-by: Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlXmyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApTEQAD4wCYclyzGjh17mi2QRwX9a\nyreSyQ2yZ+8574gpOdvhfoBsdtWMLmSFw8URhUxemJJO4BJzTEAqkjIcbB7jih4e\nIXktGaia+dLKAZZdQqKNcNipjsiF1Q0rp02VMmofuDP4ipWlVAgeCLwnKmM9ossh\nbCbVIJxRanPa6NQWZ/v6+hxMl9aL+krlyym3S1+54qeS7C4AQYpbpAlJ1W1OZbzl\nMFqadBtVfsTEp13W09sZG1zmvIzd8RAX399kQ/CbnEWfXUFRaZ/EnyIklnS8wPlI\nC0AoPFRLEQl2+/Fc8lHISBMipD8QCZztUlIFFjIDHEhfxZTJ8kyfD7pLpcSoW3Kv\nPYGsiPqiOscLqnr24+tq+EqhTgzUI/neHSeuDBPOxGUkOtidHfGx04ez4uJSndUD\nv6fE3GCk51l9ANKhlS10C/SXIBDMApzvhwrubq93gTuKHxjNQOEuRlFNBxsedEyV\nm16EA5WIPKtAQqfgOqKqyfqrkJf0aww1Jf/4Xi4dBut92Gas+torHJRxfZoqXEsv\n9ps60Hkqc2iSfhY5JXl9RJx0oW/c3Jm8eulLY+oBb4eV9wBfY+88+Lh74qnPzDUZ\nyBErULpp3drGe59asmqOOrxya0D0dkTSSkOIqfo4ecUGx5LGU6SGmQzcczRhKJAA\n08CyzkuttDmuyYAVft40\n=pDgQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T12:55:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/e6f5dbd981e97a9aaabe4c4822604d80695c01a4","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKGU2ZjVkYmQ5ODFlOTdhOWFhYWJlNGM0ODIyNjA0ZDgwNjk1YzAxYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/570d3c5f979bb1e156f54cf25f31d4c7afa60cab","sha":"570d3c5f979bb1e156f54cf25f31d4c7afa60cab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/570d3c5f979bb1e156f54cf25f31d4c7afa60cab"}],"sha":"e6f5dbd981e97a9aaabe4c4822604d80695c01a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/e6f5dbd981e97a9aaabe4c4822604d80695c01a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/570d3c5f979bb1e156f54cf25f31d4c7afa60cab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:48:12Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T12:48:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Interview: Replace service singletons with constructors (#2136)\n\n* Interview: Replace the interview slot singleton with a constructor\n\n`InitInterviewSlotModule` built the service, assigned it to a package variable\nand registered the routes in one call that returned nothing. It is now\n`NewInterviewSlotService(queries, conn)` plus `RegisterRoutes(group, service,\nauthMiddleware)`, so a caller can obtain the service without a router.\n\nThe package-level service functions and gin handlers that read\n`InterviewSlotServiceSingleton` became methods using the receiver''s fields.\n`fetchAllStudentsForCoursePhase` stays a package function: it talks to core\nover HTTP and holds no state. Route paths, methods, middleware and role lists\nare unchanged.\n\nBoth test suites now build the service with the constructor instead of\nassigning the global.\n\n* Interview: Replace the interview assignment singleton with a constructor\n\nSame split as the interview slot module: `NewInterviewAssignmentService(queries,\nconn)` builds the service and `RegisterRoutes(group, service, authMiddleware)`\nregisters the routes. The service functions and gin handlers that read\n`InterviewAssignmentServiceSingleton` became methods on the service.\n\nRoute paths, methods, middleware and role lists are unchanged, including the\nstudent-facing ownership check on the delete route.\n\n* Interview: Replace the interview review singleton with a constructor\n\n`NewInterviewReviewService(queries)` builds the service and `RegisterRoutes`\nregisters the routes. This module never held a connection pool, so the\nconstructor takes queries alone.\n\n`errScoreOutOfRange` moves from the deleted module file to `service.go`, next\nto the rest of the module''s state.\n\n* Interview: Replace the privacy singleton with a constructor\n\n`InitPrivacyModule` assigned the singleton and registered the two SDK privacy\nendpoints. The module now has a `router.go` with `RegisterRoutes` like every\nother module, and the two package-level handlers became `DataExportHandler` /\n`DataDeletionHandler` methods on the service.\n\nThe SDK takes these two as function types rather than through an interface, so\nthe method values are passed directly and no adapter type is needed.\n\n* Interview: Drop the unused config and copy services\n\n`ConfigService` and `CopyService` each held a `db.Queries` and a `*pgxpool.Pool`\nthat nothing ever read. The interview phase has nothing to configure and copies\nnothing between phases, so both handlers return a constant. The services, their\nsingletons and their module files are gone; the two handlers are stateless\npackage-private structs and `RegisterRoutes` takes only the auth middleware.\n\nThe four test suites spun up a Postgres testcontainer solely to fill those\nunread singletons. Without them the suites need no database at all and run as\nplain tests.\n\nThe copy handler was named `SelfTeamCopyHandler`, a copy-paste from the self\nteam allocation service. It is now `interviewCopyHandler`.\n\n* Interview: Group the service construction in main\n\nEvery service is constructed first, then every route group is registered, so\nthe wiring order is visible in one block rather than interleaved with the\nregistrations. Registration order itself is unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"8ae05fe4065964c8d1fc138c7603fa7526736ac4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/8ae05fe4065964c8d1fc138c7603fa7526736ac4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/570d3c5f979bb1e156f54cf25f31d4c7afa60cab","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ae05fe4065964c8d1fc138c7603fa7526736ac4\nparent 13199299043b62711f8bf9965597fb7b657fda0b\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788180492 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788180492 +0200\n\nInterview: Replace service singletons with constructors (#2136)\n\n* Interview: Replace the interview slot singleton with a constructor\n\n`InitInterviewSlotModule` built the service, assigned it to a package variable\nand registered the routes in one call that returned nothing. It is now\n`NewInterviewSlotService(queries, conn)` plus `RegisterRoutes(group, service,\nauthMiddleware)`, so a caller can obtain the service without a router.\n\nThe package-level service functions and gin handlers that read\n`InterviewSlotServiceSingleton` became methods using the receiver''s fields.\n`fetchAllStudentsForCoursePhase` stays a package function: it talks to core\nover HTTP and holds no state. Route paths, methods, middleware and role lists\nare unchanged.\n\nBoth test suites now build the service with the constructor instead of\nassigning the global.\n\n* Interview: Replace the interview assignment singleton with a constructor\n\nSame split as the interview slot module: `NewInterviewAssignmentService(queries,\nconn)` builds the service and `RegisterRoutes(group, service, authMiddleware)`\nregisters the routes. The service functions and gin handlers that read\n`InterviewAssignmentServiceSingleton` became methods on the service.\n\nRoute paths, methods, middleware and role lists are unchanged, including the\nstudent-facing ownership check on the delete route.\n\n* Interview: Replace the interview review singleton with a constructor\n\n`NewInterviewReviewService(queries)` builds the service and `RegisterRoutes`\nregisters the routes. This module never held a connection pool, so the\nconstructor takes queries alone.\n\n`errScoreOutOfRange` moves from the deleted module file to `service.go`, next\nto the rest of the module''s state.\n\n* Interview: Replace the privacy singleton with a constructor\n\n`InitPrivacyModule` assigned the singleton and registered the two SDK privacy\nendpoints. The module now has a `router.go` with `RegisterRoutes` like every\nother module, and the two package-level handlers became `DataExportHandler` /\n`DataDeletionHandler` methods on the service.\n\nThe SDK takes these two as function types rather than through an interface, so\nthe method values are passed directly and no adapter type is needed.\n\n* Interview: Drop the unused config and copy services\n\n`ConfigService` and `CopyService` each held a `db.Queries` and a `*pgxpool.Pool`\nthat nothing ever read. The interview phase has nothing to configure and copies\nnothing between phases, so both handlers return a constant. The services, their\nsingletons and their module files are gone; the two handlers are stateless\npackage-private structs and `RegisterRoutes` takes only the auth middleware.\n\nThe four test suites spun up a Postgres testcontainer solely to fill those\nunread singletons. Without them the suites need no database at all and run as\nplain tests.\n\nThe copy handler was named `SelfTeamCopyHandler`, a copy-paste from the self\nteam allocation service. It is now `interviewCopyHandler`.\n\n* Interview: Group the service construction in main\n\nEvery service is constructed first, then every route group is registered, so\nthe wiring order is visible in one block rather than interleaved with the\nregistrations. Registration order itself is unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlXgMCRC1aQ