a4cd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/b8ccaa533a3502b607154b4a517c81abc53a4cd0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/81cc8c8a94e941f7815f43418629affd97a40fa6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:00:11Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:00:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Assessment: Replace service singletons with constructors (#2130)\n\n* Assessment: Construct the privacy and copy services explicitly\n\nReplaces the privacy and copy InitXModule calls with constructors and a\nRegisterRoutes each. The privacy handlers become methods behind a new\nprivacy/router.go and the service''s fields are unexported to match every\nsibling, and the copy handler becomes a package-private adapter holding its\nservice, so a zero-value handler can no longer compile and then nil-deref at\nrequest time.\n\n* Assessment: Construct the assessment services explicitly\n\nReplaces the assessments module and its four sub-modules with constructors and\na RegisterRoutes each, so every handler is now a method on the service that\nowns its queries instead of reading a package-level singleton. The calls\nbetween the five packages arrive as small consumer-side interfaces, which makes\nthe dependency direction explicit and lets a test build the graph it needs.\n\nmain.go now constructs and registers all five itself rather than having the\nassessments module nest its siblings, keeping the registration order unchanged.\nDrops the connection pool from the score level and action item services, since\nneither ever read it. Calls into coursePhaseConfig and evaluations stay\npackage-level for now; those packages follow later.\n\n* Assessment: Construct the evaluation services explicitly\n\nReplaces the evaluation module and its two sub-modules with constructors and a\nRegisterRoutes each, so every handler is a method on the service that owns its\nqueries instead of reading a package-level singleton. The evaluation and\nfeedback item services reach evaluation completion through a small consumer-side\ninterface, and the team lookup that evaluation completion used to reach through\na monkey-patchable package variable is now a constructor argument, so a test can\nsupply its own resolver without mutating shared state.\n\nmain.go constructs and registers all three itself rather than having the\nevaluation module nest its siblings, keeping the registration order unchanged.\nThe assessment service takes the evaluation lookup as another consumer-side\ninterface, which is why the evaluation services are built before it.\nAggregateEvaluations stays a package function: it reads no service state.\n\n* Assessment: Construct the category and competency services explicitly\n\nReplaces the category and competency InitXModule calls with constructors and a\nRegisterRoutes each, so both packages hand their handlers the service that owns\nthe queries instead of reading a package-level singleton. Registration order and\nevery route, middleware and role list stay as they were. Their calls into the\nassessment schema, schema modification and course phase config packages remain\npackage-level, since those three still keep singletons of their own.\n\n* Assessment: Construct the assessment schema and schema modification services explicitly\n\nReplaces the assessment schema InitXModule and singleton with a constructor and\na RegisterRoutes, turning every schema function and gin handler into a method.\nschemaModification becomes a service of its own that owns its queries, since\nevery caller already handed it the non-transactional queries value rather than a\ntransaction-scoped one. Its dependency on the schema package is now a small\nconsumer-side interface, as are the ones categories, competencies and the course\nphase config use. The course phase config keeps its singleton for now and takes\nthe schema service through InitCoursePhaseConfigModule, so its schema validation\nhelpers become methods that can reach it. Every route, middleware and role list\nstays as it was.\n\n* Assessment: Construct the course phase config service explicitly\n\nReplaces the last singleton with a constructor and a RegisterRoutes, turning\nevery course phase config function and gin handler into a method. The\nconstructor now takes the schema service, so a config service with a nil\nschemas field can no longer be built. The assessment guard becomes a method\ntoo, so the four routers that mount it take a small consumer-side guard\ninterface and still build the middleware at the same registration point, in the\nsame position, as before. Every other cross-package caller (categories,\nevaluations, evaluation completion, assessments, assessment completion, action\nitems and schema modification) gains a consumer-side interface and a\nconstructor argument instead of reaching for package state; the error sentinels\nstay package-level so callers keep using errors.Is unchanged. The two reminder\nseams the tests patched become func-typed fields on the service, so tests fake\nthem per instance rather than through a package variable, and no test builds a\nthrowaway router just to reach a service any more. Construction order now lives\nonly in main.go, which builds the schema service first so the config service\ncan take it and everything else can take the config service. Route\nregistration order and every path, method, middleware and role list are\nunchanged.\n\n* Assessment: Implement the SDK copy handler on the service\n\n`promptTypes.PhaseCopyHandler` is a structural interface, so `CopyService` can\nimplement it directly and the registration passes the service itself. The\n`assessmentCopyHandler` wrapper did not remove the zero-value hazard it was\nmeant to address: `&assessmentCopyHandler{}` still carries a nil service and\nstill dereferences at request time. Requiring a constructed service at the\nregistration call is what removes it.\n\n`CopyPhase` is split out of `HandlePhaseCopy` so the transaction takes a\n`context.Context` and typed IDs, keeping gin confined to the adapter. The four\ntest call sites construct one object less.","tree":{"sha":"d6ff9ae11864f985f14cc21fe24210a7d966a3bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/d6ff9ae11864f985f14cc21fe24210a7d966a3bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/81cc8c8a94e941f7815f43418629affd97a40fa6","verification":{"payload":"tree d6ff9ae11864f985f14cc21fe24210a7d966a3bc\nparent 038cabb0ab5b7736ce88c29ed0884b7e9f79670f\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788166811 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788166811 +0200\n\nAssessment: Replace service singletons with constructors (#2130)\n\n* Assessment: Construct the privacy and copy services explicitly\n\nReplaces the privacy and copy InitXModule calls with constructors and a\nRegisterRoutes each. The privacy handlers become methods behind a new\nprivacy/router.go and the service''s fields are unexported to match every\nsibling, and the copy handler becomes a package-private adapter holding its\nservice, so a zero-value handler can no longer compile and then nil-deref at\nrequest time.\n\n* Assessment: Construct the assessment services explicitly\n\nReplaces the assessments module and its four sub-modules with constructors and\na RegisterRoutes each, so every handler is now a method on the service that\nowns its queries instead of reading a package-level singleton. The calls\nbetween the five packages arrive as small consumer-side interfaces, which makes\nthe dependency direction explicit and lets a test build the graph it needs.\n\nmain.go now constructs and registers all five itself rather than having the\nassessments module nest its siblings, keeping the registration order unchanged.\nDrops the connection pool from the score level and action item services, since\nneither ever read it. Calls into coursePhaseConfig and evaluations stay\npackage-level for now; those packages follow later.\n\n* Assessment: Construct the evaluation services explicitly\n\nReplaces the evaluation module and its two sub-modules with constructors and a\nRegisterRoutes each, so every handler is a method on the service that owns its\nqueries instead of reading a package-level singleton. The evaluation and\nfeedback item services reach evaluation completion through a small consumer-side\ninterface, and the team lookup that evaluation completion used to reach through\na monkey-patchable package variable is now a constructor argument, so a test can\nsupply its own resolver without mutating shared state.\n\nmain.go constructs and registers all three itself rather than having the\nevaluation module nest its siblings, keeping the registration order unchanged.\nThe assessment service takes the evaluation lookup as another consumer-side\ninterface, which is why the evaluation services are built before it.\nAggregateEvaluations stays a package function: it reads no service state.\n\n* Assessment: Construct the category and competency services explicitly\n\nReplaces the category and competency InitXModule calls with constructors and a\nRegisterRoutes each, so both packages hand their handlers the service that owns\nthe queries instead of reading a package-level singleton. Registration order and\nevery route, middleware and role list stay as they were. Their calls into the\nassessment schema, schema modification and course phase config packages remain\npackage-level, since those three still keep singletons of their own.\n\n* Assessment: Construct the assessment schema and schema modification services explicitly\n\nReplaces the assessment schema InitXModule and singleton with a constructor and\na RegisterRoutes, turning every schema function and gin handler into a method.\nschemaModification becomes a service of its own that owns its queries, since\nevery caller already handed it the non-transactional queries value rather than a\ntransaction-scoped one. Its dependency on the schema package is now a small\nconsumer-side interface, as are the ones categories, competencies and the course\nphase config use. The course phase config keeps its singleton for now and takes\nthe schema service through InitCoursePhaseConfigModule, so its schema validation\nhelpers become methods that can reach it. Every route, middleware and role list\nstays as it was.\n\n* Assessment: Construct the course phase config service explicitly\n\nReplaces the last singleton with a constructor and a RegisterRoutes, turning\nevery course phase config function and gin handler into a method. The\nconstructor now takes the schema service, so a config service with a nil\nschemas field can no longer be built. The assessment guard becomes a method\ntoo, so the four routers that mount it take a small consumer-side guard\ninterface and still build the middleware at the same registration point, in the\nsame position, as before. Every other cross-package caller (categories,\nevaluations, evaluation completion, assessments, assessment completion, action\nitems and schema modification) gains a consumer-side interface and a\nconstructor argument instead of reaching for package state; the error sentinels\nstay package-level so callers keep using errors.Is unchanged. The two reminder\nseams the tests patched become func-typed fields on the service, so tests fake\nthem per instance rather than through a package variable, and no test builds a\nthrowaway router just to reach a service any more. Construction order now lives\nonly in main.go, which builds the schema service first so the config service\ncan take it and everything else can take the config service. Route\nregistration order and every path, method, middleware and role list are\nunchanged.\n\n* Assessment: Implement the SDK copy handler on the service\n\n`promptTypes.PhaseCopyHandler` is a structural interface, so `CopyService` can\nimplement it directly and the registration passes the service itself. The\n`assessmentCopyHandler` wrapper did not remove the zero-value hazard it was\nmeant to address: `&assessmentCopyHandler{}` still carries a nil service and\nstill dereferences at request time. Requiring a constructed service at the\nregistration call is what removes it.\n\n`CopyPhase` is split out of `HandlePhaseCopy` so the transaction takes a\n`context.Context` and typed IDs, keeping gin confined to the adapter. The four\ntest call sites construct one object less.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlUKbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnrsQAI1jSTSd/0hlF9Tdx+APgzdI\nuVGnNynQH9lB+YstBkXcH+CLmx9S5xvJhDBLrWCa8aAlc/eQSSnmMK/tucJ3SUiO\ntboswDldTkq1SVTPPpXHWx9MHTsJaeTxiW8AkAG33uqakXjI/IRei3WikGzFGA4I\nJTD/iDxdrL/5d+Fmc5JicbJfAWfxMzXddOm7ejA8KnRDSFn+k03SuazFgTWz5Wup\nJLsJ/EkjNED7oWS5I/mxwazn5urkou1YqrV0JqC1n/PHYvRBh1Xyk+Eh6pKL+P5D\nUqV+lOe4HBVDTzPKlqunkBnRoFvEj2x8ds7VDxT2Ib0c/B+4waVPqymKla3l+VTB\nsHfUJnwsB2xyimcsW0warqj9KcxhEDEqzvfS1SR7DVEv7U46TjVH6V7iexheONjt\nS5RHTxkr3zdZS08NKYuJFUWcenwiT6UF8E6Vposqu6TKLie6hCBzbozAB+jf+0GA\ns4WnbzyL4qgNTITEe3xW8HCjuA2mrRIc3KdWQ4ectIiS2Lw3czj/2psjCQqLhCvO\nb5jKC4B29uIndUiCo+k/oop31foybgLBc16iBPaBilTHLGPOgn0jrAirjEzFNNnD\nl/9mTjMzMLzOhVzPTW2fSz9DTTaGTkCuKsgzWgLupHvzEjHXcZEWzw+qfHOPI6jm\nXUKDIfkSrN8ObBbv2fP/\n=s8kS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T09:00:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/81cc8c8a94e941f7815f43418629affd97a40fa6","node_id":"C_kwDONRrZeNoAKDgxY2M4YzhhOTRlOTQxZjc4MTVmNDM0MTg2MjlhZmZkOTdhNDBmYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt/commit/038cabb0ab5b7736ce88c29ed0884b7e9f79670f","sha":"038cabb0ab5b7736ce88c29ed0884b7e9f79670f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/038cabb0ab5b7736ce88c29ed0884b7e9f79670f"}],"sha":"81cc8c8a94e941f7815f43418629affd97a40fa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/81cc8c8a94e941f7815f43418629affd97a40fa6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/commits/038cabb0ab5b7736ce88c29ed0884b7e9f79670f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:59:09Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T08:59:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Testing: Add end-to-end coverage for the GDPR export and deletion flows (#2135)\n\n* Core: Make the privacy status and export documents addressable in tests\n\nThe status banner exposes its presentation state, and each export document''s\nicon-only download button gains an accessible name.\n\n* Testing: Seed the two subjects the privacy journeys delete\n\nOne is Keycloak-backed and requests its own deletion, which an admin approves, so\nit really disappears; nothing else may reference it. The other has no account and\na last_modified far in the past, because the student table''s inactivity filter can\nnever match a student created during the run.\n\n* Testing: Cover the GDPR export and deletion flows end to end\n\nCovers the student export from request through async completion, the signed\ndownload and the admin archive that frees the rate limit; a deletion request\napproved by an admin, which removes its subject; a rejected request, asserted as\ndistinct from a failure; and admin-initiated deletion driven through the student\ntable''s inactivity filter.\n\nWaits poll the API against a bounded deadline and fail immediately on a failed\nrun rather than sitting out the clock, and each spec sets its own timeout so the\n60s default cannot preempt them.\n\nOnly the Core export document can succeed on this stack: prompt-sdk refuses a\npresigned upload URL that is not HTTPS unless it is localhost, and the e2e S3\nendpoint is plain HTTP, so the phase modules reject it and the export finishes as\ncompleted with issues. The spec asserts that state rather than pretending\notherwise.\n\n* Testing: Make the privacy suite survive CI retries\n\nTerminal rows are never removed from the admin console - a rejected request and\nan archived export both stay listed - so locating a row by requester name alone\nmatched the previous attempt''s row too and every retry failed on a strict-mode\nviolation. Rows are now narrowed by status.\n\nAPI contexts re-mint on 401: the prompt-client Keycloak client caps access tokens\nat 60 seconds, so a context taken once in beforeAll started failing partway\nthrough any wait that outlived a minute.\n\nThe admin-initiated dialog is asserted on its success wording, since both the\nrunning and the failed states also render a Close button, and the re-entrancy\nbranch now checks that a deletion actually succeeded rather than restating the\nguard it just evaluated. The export download resolves its signed URL through the\nAPI because the page navigates away as soon as it has one, which can outrun\nreading the response body. Wait budgets are tightened so a retried test cannot\nexhaust the shard''s global timeout.","tree":{"sha":"ea2b48eb6f06674a21de1138ffcdf53d5f123d20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/trees/ea2b48eb6f06674a21de1138ffcdf53d5f123d20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt/git/commits/038cabb0ab5b7736ce88c29ed0884b7e9f79670f","verification":{"payload":"tree ea2b48eb6f06674a21de1138ffcdf53d5f123d20\nparent 9480bf59bd9e5b23c5eb309d5103372f6fe1eac0\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1788166749 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788166749 +0200\n\nTesting: Add end-to-end coverage for the GDPR export and deletion flows (#2135)\n\n* Core: Make the privacy status and export documents addressable in tests\n\nThe status banner exposes its presentation state, and each export document''s\nicon-only download button gains an accessible name.\n\n* Testing: Seed the two subjects the privacy journeys delete\n\nOne is Keycloak-backed and requests its own deletion, which an admin approves, so\nit really disappears; nothing else may reference it. The other has no account and\na last_modified far in the past, because the student table''s inactivity filter can\nnever match a student created during the run.\n\n* Testing: Cover the GDPR export and deletion flows end to end\n\nCovers the student export from request through async completion, the signed\ndownload and the admin archive that frees the rate limit; a deletion request\napproved by an admin, which removes its subject; a rejected request, asserted as\ndistinct from a failure; and admin-initiated deletion driven through the student\ntable''s inactivity filter.\n\nWaits poll the API against a bounded deadline and fail immediately on a failed\nrun rather than sitting out the clock, and each spec sets its own timeout so the\n60s default cannot preempt them.\n\nOnly the Core export document can succeed on this stack: prompt-sdk refuses a\npresigned upload URL that is not HTTPS unless it is localhost, and the e2e S3\nendpoint is plain HTTP, so the phase modules reject it and the export finishes as\ncompleted with issues. The spec asserts that state rather than pretending\notherwise.\n\n* Testing: Make the privacy suite survive CI retries\n\nTerminal rows are never removed from the admin console - a rejected request and\nan archived export both stay listed - so locating a row by requester name alone\nmatched the previous attempt''s row too and every retry failed on a strict-mode\nviolation. Rows are now narrowed by status.\n\nAPI contexts re-mint on 401: the prompt-client Keycloak client caps access tokens\nat 60 seconds, so a context taken once in beforeAll started failing partway\nthrough any wait that outlived a minute.\n\nThe admin-initiated dialog is asserted on its success wording, since both the\nrunning and the failed states also render a Close button, and the re-entrancy\nbranch now checks that a deletion actually succeeded rather than restating the\nguard it just evaluated. The export download resolves its signed URL through the\nAPI because the page navigates away as soon as it has one, which can outrun\nreading the response body. Wait budgets are tightened so a retried test cannot\nexhaust the shard''s global timeout.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlUJdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIQwQAA5y4961M6XZFnCxUhoSEBY2\n9usYlNuByAJPXWoIE9pWxF0z850MN4A7iWG3SZNKTEDYkfGV0SSrcHfD1QbOHZu/\n9/hK/DQluztCiumQRxFTtlKc1F/pufa7YwSOiSDePsgrHypNcYrWKXmag5M4i5Lz\nKgpf7Y8JBrcz+dFhIAk3MmAh9EnoW0+gddaHplKPkbg9NxL9s3PXTLw1TtlFkvcA\nw6wxfrhlts0NpgtTVuC5Lfdw96omzg8Ufnby0zVnRTAh9UsrRk4PTYZxBWQ0vxP6\n6wjmaodLFztSqshydkhnUi0/QdS76DjuJR7YfBqT06sfea33cnja/gEG5dzV3lCc\nuKkgQqaW7glCVLktBytwdkBaNj4KPiQJ20xai7cFDF1+VP9dCT0lHNcTDUPf1W7v\nesa4TjJUDZZo7/5JObuekrY4suL59mB/a3oR6Iaf2Np/m/De4F5elYYVZmhGfsbL\nQkDYS2CYoNNqaDjTgnXizdu3bzCvU77vRS9AELguUDTwIXIdbq1wd1/vP0IBJnHP\n9yhEOUNvwHfYcH/Prelz2In73R+UlZ5gHh9W7DfuuwBXgp2Rr/K9A58eKG0qwWZJ\n+8hXdLLCE10ejE/4er2mJQERJEme7n7jVQNh4z8mnb+XsGkd+qbe/BVyHWHw0NMU\npFIQwDAdWBG89lljS8EK\n=T1Kw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T08:59:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_ur